window.FWN_YOU_PROMISED_TO_BE_AN_IDLE_SON_IN_LAW_HOW_COULD_YOU_BECOME_A_LAND_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_YOU_PROMISED_TO_BE_AN_IDLE_SON_IN_LAW_HOW_COULD_YOU_BECOME_A_LAND_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":501,"title":"Chapter 501 - 299: Today, I Draw My Sword for You","paragraphs":["At the Wu Mountain Mutual Market, the rainy night was a chaotic cacophony. Torrential rain battered the dense forest, stripping away dead leaves and sending them smashing into rocks and trees along with the mountain wind. PATTER, PATTER. The sound was endless.","Inside the Mutual Market, which was already beginning to take shape, the outlines of the structures were much clearer than before. It genuinely resembled a small town. A twenty-foot-tall wall rose from the ground on all four sides, topped with dozens of sentry forts along its narrow ridge. Bright firelight emanated from within the forts, faintly illuminating several guards clad in armor. Some belonged to the Xiao Family, while others were from the Mountain Race.","Inside the walls, most of the roads were still a mixture of dirt and gravel. Only the main avenue running north to south was paved with mountain stones. It was about fifty feet wide and polished incredibly smooth. Washed by the rain, it faintly reflected the firelight. Flanking the avenue were two hundred shops of various sizes, their heights staggered yet orderly. Behind the storefronts stood rows of square yet spacious warehouses. Some of their doors even had red paper pasted on them.","A few lines of text were written on the red paper, reading things like \"You State Red Rock Trading Company\" and \"Wumeng Mountain Old Li Race.\" This clearly indicated that these warehouses had already been claimed by certain trading companies or people from the Mountain Race.","Beyond the shops and warehouses lay several open plots of land where hundreds of uneven pits were filled with rainwater. Quite a few laborers were bent over, clearing out the crushed stones from the pits. The torrential rain cascaded down their glistening, muscular backs, sparkling like scattered crystals.","Xiao Jinghong stood on a small hill outside the Mutual Market, her face unadorned. Gazing at the bustling scene from afar, a hint of satisfaction flickered in her eyes. Several months had flown by in the blink of an eye since the Old Master’s birthday. With the Wu Mountain Mutual Market nearing completion, she couldn’t help but breathe a sigh of relief. Although they had faced difficulties along the way, her collaboration with the Mountain Race had allowed everything to progress fairly smoothly up to this point. It would be a lie to say she wasn’t happy.","At the same time, once the Mutual Market was finished, Xiao Jinghong would finally be able to step back from this project. After years of rigorous training, it was also time to test the results of the Three Towns’ New Army. Barring any major discrepancies, this branch of the Dingyuan Army could be considered to have recovered to the level it was at before the Barbarian Left King’s invasion five years ago. Her years of hard work had not been in vain.","Of course, what made Xiao Jinghong even happier was that once all this was done, she could finally rest in the Prefecture City for a while. The Old Master, her eldest sister, her uncles, the elders, and... her husband. She had to go back and see them eventually. Moreover, with the end of the year approaching, it wouldn’t be appropriate for her to be running about outside like she had during the Mid-Autumn Festival.","Xiao Jinghong thought about all this as she slipped back into the wooden cabin.","Su Zhenyue stood up and bowed, saying with a playful smile, \"Miss, you always have to take a look at the Mutual Market every single day, rain or shine.\"","\"Mhm, I won’t have peace of mind if I don’t look.\"","\"With you here, what is there to worry about?\"","In Su Zhenyue’s mind, as long as Xiao Jinghong was at the Mutual Market, let alone those blind fools who might come to cause trouble, even the unruly members of the Mountain Race would obediently do their jobs. Had it not been for this, the Wu Mountain Mutual Market wouldn’t have neared completion so quickly.","Xiao Jinghong gave a noncommittal nod. After sitting down, her eyes naturally fell on the painting hanging across from her. In the warm, soft luminescence, Xiao Fengchun, Fu Wanqing, Xiao Wan’er, Xiao Wuge, and Chen Yi were looking at her with smiles on their faces. In stark contrast, the illusionary portrait of herself stood in the corner with her arms crossed, exuding an aura that warned strangers to keep their distance. Ever since her family had sent this painting, Xiao Jinghong would glance at it from time to time.","At first, she mostly looked at Xiao Fengchun and Fu Wanqing, recalling the scarce few memories she had of living in the Marquis’s Mansion as a child. Yet, seeing the painting brought back thoughts of the people in it. Even a General like her couldn’t help but feel a tinge of melancholy. Later, Xiao Jinghong shifted her attention to Xiao Wan’er and Xiao Wuge, and finally to Chen Yi. Although Chen Yi’s appearance in the painting seemed a bit more handsome than in her memories, she could still see traces of familiarity. It was just like when she had first met him—the sunlight was just right, and he was showing off a freshly dug earthworm, a gentle and radiant smile on his face. As she gazed at him, the corners of her lips unconsciously curled into a smile.","Noticing her expression, a teasing look appeared on Su Zhenyue’s face. \"Miss, are you looking at your husband again?\"","Xiao Jinghong instantly reined in her smile and turned her head to look at her. \"Is there any news from the Commander-in-Chief?\"","Meeting her gaze, Su Zhenyue coughed to suppress her smile and handed her a memorial booklet. \"The Capital Commandery replied saying they’ve made contact with Mengshui Pass, and they haven’t found any signs of the Barbarian Race invading. General Zhang also sent word via carrier pigeon. The situation is the same along the Ancient Tea-Horse Road. Within a radius of a thousand miles, there hasn’t been a single sighting of the Peacock King Banner.\"","Xiao Jinghong looked at the memorial in her hand and gave a slight nod. \"Commander Li will continue to keep an eye on this. As for Zhu Hao...\" She paused, pulling out a letter tucked behind the memorial. After opening it and scanning the contents, she frowned. \"After the Holy Emperor issued a decree punishing grandfather, the summer grain taxes from the Three Towns have already arrived in Guangyuan?\"","Su Zhenyue hurriedly flipped open a small booklet she carried with her. Finding the right page, she said, \"It should have been delivered to Guangyuan County three days ago. Miss, did Commander Zhu mention a problem with the tax grain in his letter?\"","Xiao Jinghong shook her head. \"He must have lost his mind. He actually suspects that the Tax Officers from the Governor’s Office miscalculated.\"","\"Mis... Why would he harbor such suspicions?\"","\"Hmph, his greed knows no bounds!\" A cold glint flashed in Xiao Jinghong’s eyes. \"He has schemed against the Dingyuan Army time and time again. Sooner or later, I will settle this score with him!\"","It was no wonder she was so furious. Over the past two years, Zhu Hao had been the mastermind behind most of the incidents where the Capital Commandery had forcibly interfered. If Commander Li Fu hadn’t acted as a mediator, Xiao Jinghong would have completely fallen out with Zhu Hao a long time ago.","Just as she was about to continue asking Su Zhenyue about the recent situation in Shu State, the sharp cry of an eagle pierced the air from outside."]},{"number":502,"title":"Chapter 502 - 299: Today I Draw My Sword for You","paragraphs":["Xiao Jinghong paused, got up, and went outside, looking up at the dim night sky.","Through the pouring rain, she immediately spotted the bald eagle soaring in the sky, a small tuft of white feathers on its head.","\"An urgent report from Grandfather...\"","Xiao Jinghong frowned, placed two fingers in her mouth, and let out a loud whistle.","Hearing the sound, the bald eagle didn’t circle but instead flapped its wings, flipped, and dove straight toward her. Only when it neared the height of the wooden cabin did the bald eagle flap its wings to slow down. It landed steadily on Xiao Jinghong’s shoulder, rubbing its head against her cheek in a fawning manner.","Xiao Jinghong gently patted its head, then removed the small bamboo tube from its claws and took out a slip of paper.","[King Landu’s Grand General, the ’Jackal’ Du Cang, has captured the Eldest Miss! The ’Dragon Spear’ Liu Wu has rushed to her rescue!]","[Furthermore, there is a major matter to discuss!]","[The Marquis hopes the General will return swiftly. —Hidden Guard Xiao Jing]","Seeing the end of the message, Xiao Jinghong’s expression changed slightly. Without hesitation, she turned back into the room, took down her Long Sword, and fastened it to her waist.","As she quickly gathered her things, she instructed, \"Something major has happened at the Prefecture City. Stay here and keep a close eye on the laborers. If you encounter any trouble, immediately consult with the people of the Mountain Race!\"","Seeing her expression, Su Zhenyue didn’t bother asking further questions. She handed her the half-armor mask from the table and bowed. \"Your subordinate obeys!\"","Xiao Jinghong put on the mask, hurried out of the wooden cabin, and shot into the sky. She patted her waist, and the Long Sword inside the scabbard fell beneath her feet according to her will.","The next moment, a streak of silvery-white sword light flared in the dimness, crossing dozens of miles in the blink of an eye. It left a galaxy-like fluorescent trail stretching northward across the overcast night sky.","Just a few breaths later, as Xiao Jinghong erupted with True Essence to hurry anxiously on her way, she saw a figure transforming into a rainbow and flying toward her.","His features were dignified, his expression cold, and he was dressed in white clothes that surpassed snow. Like her, he stood upon a Long Sword. The difference was that the streak-of-light speed Xiao Jinghong could only achieve by going all out was used with effortless grace by that white-clad Swordsman.","Upon seeing the newcomer’s appearance clearly, Xiao Jinghong subconsciously raised her guard. However, the man seemed not to see her at all, brushing past her without a change in expression. He merely left behind a few words.","\"Li Wudang’s disciple? On the fifteenth of the tenth month, Gongye Bai and I will duel at the upper reaches of the Chishui River. You are qualified to come and spectate.\"","Before Xiao Jinghong could respond, the white-clad Swordsman’s voice continued to carry over. \"Could you pass a message to your master for me? After my duel with Gongye Bai this time, I hope to test my sword against his as well.\"","Immediately after, his next words echoed from afar, \"The time... and location... will be decided by the old man...\"","Hearing his voice, Xiao Jinghong’s figure stalled. Standing on her Long Sword, she turned to look back.","She only saw the retreating silhouette of the white-clad Swordsman standing with his hands behind his back as he sped away. He acted as if it were only natural that she would obediently follow his orders after hearing his words.","After observing carefully for a moment, a flash of realization crossed Xiao Jinghong’s eyes. She thought, \"It’s him. To think he has already reached the Land Immortal Realm...\"","After some thought, Xiao Jinghong silently memorized the date of the fifteenth of the tenth month, turned around, and headed toward the Shu State Prefecture City once more.","While anxious about Xiao Wan’er’s safety, some old Jianghu tales she had heard while by her master Li Wudang’s side also surfaced in her mind. Naturally, this included the several peerless Swordsmen in today’s Jianghu. Such as the \"Willow-Bending Sword\" Chen Zhitang, the \"Sword Venerable Jueyun\" Jiang Mianliu, and the swordsman whose white clothes surpassed snow just now—the \"Monarch Xue Jian,\" Lone Immortal Ye!","\"Standing alone on the snowy peak for nineteen springs, plum blossoms fall on his shoulders without staining him with dust. Today I draw my sword for you, only to realize I am also a fool.\"","\"This Lone Immortal Ye has a talent for the Sword Dao rarely seen in a thousand years. Furthermore, he devotes his entire being to the sword, allowing him to advance at godlike speed within the Sword Dao. Perhaps in a few years, he will come to challenge your master...\"","Recalling these things, a trace of worry appeared on Xiao Jinghong’s face.","She was clear about Li Wudang’s situation. Having sealed his sword and retired for several years, he was likely inferior in many ways compared to Lone Immortal Ye, who had newly advanced to the Land Immortal Realm. In a duel between Swordsmen of such Cultivation and Realm, a single misstep would result in perishing along with one’s sword.","Although out of selfishness she did not want to inform Li Wudang about this matter, she also knew that since someone like Lone Immortal Ye had spoken, Li Wudang would learn of it even if she kept silent.","A duel between the two was likely inevitable.","Xiao Jinghong felt slightly flustered. It wasn’t until the Prefecture City neared that she made a decision.","She thought, \"The fifteenth of the tenth month... I’ll ask martial uncle when the time comes.\"","Fortunately, Immortal Bai had instructed before leaving that she could seek him out if anything happened. Thus, Xiao Jinghong would be able to broach the subject. For her master’s sake, she had to be more cautious.","After all, although Lone Immortal Ye held the title of \"Monarch Xue Jian,\" he had always done as he pleased. Especially when it involved matters of the Sword Dao. It wasn’t an exaggeration to call him a \"Sword Fool.\"","Thinking of this, Xiao Jinghong restrained her Heart Spirit, put away her Long Sword, and landed directly in the front courtyard of the Xiao Family’s home.","Without waiting for the surrounding Armored Warriors to speak, she asked loudly, \"What is the situation now? Has Eldest Sister returned safely?\"","Standing nearby, Wang Lixing hurriedly stepped forward and bowed. \"Reporting to the General, the Eldest Miss returned safely two hours ago!\"","His expression slightly agitated, he added, \"We failed in our duties as guards. I beg the General for punishment!\"","Xiao Jinghong’s expression cleared up a bit, and her tone softened. \"It’s good that she’s back... Since that’s the case, let Grandfather decide the rewards and punishments for this matter.\"","After speaking, she ignored Wang Lixing and the others kneeling around her, heading straight for the Qingjing Residence.","A moment later, within a hundred feet of the Qingjing Residence, it was completely empty of people.","Xiao Jinghong sat in the hall. Elder Master Xiao, dressed in casual clothes and sitting with a straight back, smiled and said, \"The situation arose urgently. I didn’t know if the ’Dragon Spear’ Liu Wu would be able to save Wan’er, so I had Xiao Jing urgently summon you back.\""]},{"number":503,"title":"Chapter 503 - 299: Today I Draw My Sword for You","paragraphs":["\"Fortunately, Liu Wu is highly capable. He killed Du Cang and saved Wan’er. Otherwise, I fear I would have no face left to see your fa... mother.\"","Xiao Jinghong naturally breathed a sigh of relief. She nodded. \"Grandpa, I also bear responsibility for this matter.","\"If I had stayed in the mansion, Du Cang wouldn’t have dared to penetrate deep into the Prefecture City...\"","Without waiting for her to finish, Elder Master Xiao waved his hand. \"It’s not your fault. Even though I was at the Xiao Family, I failed to keep Wan’er fully safe. It’s all my fault.\"","A smile then surfaced on his face. \"However, after this incident, it can be considered a blessing in disguise.\"","\"A blessing?\"","\"I found an ideal husband for your eldest sister.\"","Xiao Jinghong’s expression shifted slightly. \"That ’Dragon Spear’ Liu Wu?","\"Grandpa, just who exactly is he?","\"During the previous incident where the summer grain of the Three Towns was burned, this person appeared outside Iron Wall Town, killed Liu Wen, and gave our Xiao Family a grand gift. And now this time...","\"Could it be that he is your arrangement, Grandpa?\"","Elder Master Xiao shook his head and chuckled. \"If only he were my man.\"","He paused for a moment and asked, \"Do you still remember the Hundred Herbs Hall?\"","Xiao Jinghong thought for a moment. \"Is it the Hundred Herbs Hall that serves tea and cooperates with our Medicine Hall?\"","The matters concerning the Hundred Herbs Hall were too trivial and only involved the silver coins within the Marquis’s Mansion, so she hadn’t paid much attention to it.","Elder Master Xiao nodded. \"Liu Wu is the boss of the Hundred Herbs Hall. His surname is Chen and his given name is Yu. He is a Saint Hand who has reached Great Success in the Medical Dao.\"","\"Chen Yu? Great Success in the Medical Dao?\" Xiao Jinghong asked with mild surprise. \"Aside from the Spear Dao, he has mastery over the Medical Dao as well?\"","\"Not only that.","\"Xiao Jing reported earlier that his ability to slay Du Cang this time revealed his attainments in the Fist Dao, in addition to the Spear Dao.\" Elder Master Xiao chuckled, \"His Fist Dao has also reached the Great Success Realm.\"","Xiao Jinghong’s beautiful eyes widened slightly. \"Fist... Great Success... Then, adding the Spear Dao and Medical Dao, wouldn’t he, wouldn’t he be...\"","Seeing this, Elder Master Xiao said rather smugly, \"Now you know why I took a liking to him, right?","\"His natural talent is more than enough to be a match for Wan’er.","\"Moreover, with his Medical Dao, there’s a good chance he might cure Wan’er in the future, not to mention...\"","Elder Master Xiao paused. He stood up tall, and the True Essence that had just recovered for the most part within his body erupted. A ferocious aura carrying a faint scent of blood enveloped the hall.","Xiao Jinghong was startled. She stood up and looked him up and down, asking with a slightly excited expression, \"Grandpa, your body... has it recovered?\"","Elder Master Xiao restrained his aura and nodded with a smile, his hands clasped behind his back. \"Thanks to that Chen Yu, the old injuries inside my body have mostly healed.","\"Although it’s impossible to return to my peak condition, holding on for another ten or twenty years shouldn’t be a problem.\"","His tone could not hide his joy. Describing it as a dying tree greeting the spring wouldn’t be an exaggeration.","Xiao Jinghong stared at him blankly for a moment before calming down. \"In that case, Chen Yu is indeed a good match for Eldest Sister.","\"Grandpa, has the wedding date for him and Eldest Sister been decided?\"","Elder Master Xiao couldn’t help but laugh. He sat back down and shook his head. \"Right now, it’s just my idea.","\"Your Third Uncle went to ask Wan’er earlier, and she doesn’t seem to want to get married. You should go persuade her later.\"","A smile appeared on Xiao Jinghong’s lips, and she agreed. \"I will.\"","In her eyes, Chen Yu, who excelled in the Medical Dao, was indeed a good match for Xiao Wan’er. Even if Xiao Wan’er couldn’t fully recover in the future, it was still better than growing old alone.","\"Does Chen Yu know about your intentions, Grandpa?\"","\"Him? He should... know, right?\"","Although Elder Master Xiao was somewhat uncertain, his tone remained forceful. \"My eldest granddaughter is so outstanding. Just let him try to refuse!\"","Hearing this, Xiao Jinghong couldn’t help but find it both funny and exasperating. \"Grandpa, the way I see it, it’s better to ask clearly first, lest good intentions lead to a bad outcome.\"","Even though she had spent years in the military and wasn’t well-versed in worldly affairs, she knew that a major event like marriage required proper preparation. Just like her and Chen Yi—hadn’t they caused a joke about a \"runaway groom\" back then?","Thinking of Chen Yu’s cold and indifferent demeanor, Elder Master Xiao ultimately couldn’t maintain his tough stance.","\"In a few days, find some time to meet him. It would be good to take the opportunity to ask for his thoughts.\"","Xiao Jinghong agreed once more.","\"But that kid needs to be knocked down a peg. You have no idea what he...\"","Elder Master Xiao went on to recount how Chen Yu had arranged for people to masquerade as the Peacock King Banner Horse Bandits and members of the Barbarian Race. He laughed out of sheer exasperation.","Xiao Jinghong frowned slightly. \"Even if he wanted to deal with the Ji State Trading Company, using such methods...\"","She paused, then nodded. \"I understand. When I see him, I will judge carefully.\"","\"Good...\"","After chatting for a while, Xiao Jinghong recalled the major event mentioned in the letter and asked, \"I wonder what it is that Grandpa wants to discuss with me?\"","Hearing this, the elder master paused, the smile on his face fading away. \"Liu Hong is colluding with the Barbarian Race and the Poshisu Country!\"","\"Who?","\"Liu Hong?\""]},{"number":504,"title":"Chapter 504 - 300: Paving a Great Dao to Heaven","paragraphs":["The night rain fell in a soft drizzle, accompanied by a cool, gentle breeze.","A freezing aura enveloped Qingjing Residence, faintly mixed with a sharp, murderous intent.","Xiao Jinghong looked at the paper in her hand, her eyes icy.","\"Liu Hong, Zhu Hao—they truly have a death wish!\"","According to the contents recorded on the paper, Liu Hong had recently done three things.","The first was sending assassins after Lin Huai’an of the Ji State Trading Company, severing his contact with Liu Hong’s second son, Liu Taofang.","Lin Huai’an had also acted as a liaison between Zhu Hao, the Deputy Commander of the Shu State Capital Commandery, and King Landu of Poshisu Country to secretly sell ironware and ores.","In addition, Mr. Lingchuan of Guiyun Academy was also involved.","The second matter was Liu Hong colluding with Academic Administrator Ma Shuhan to secretly form factions for personal gain, winning over the large and small Noble Families of Shu State.","The third matter was Liu Hong’s illicit ties with King Landu, using Lv Jiunan to rescue Asutai, son of the Barbarian Left King.","All signs indicated that Liu Hong had colluded with King Landu and the Barbarian Race a long time ago, secretly acting on their behalf on numerous occasions.","Xiao Jinghong recalled the events of the past few years and could indeed spot some suspicious details.","\"No wonder the Capital Commandery claimed a massive decrease in salt and iron tax revenues time and time again. The people I sent to investigate their account books found no errors or omissions—it turns out they had the backing of the Governor’s Office.","\"When the New Army was recruited three years ago, I suppose Liu Hong secretly orchestrated it, resulting in troops of uneven quality.","\"With this, all the doubts I couldn’t figure out before finally have answers.\"","Elder Master Xiao nodded and said with a solemn expression, \"I summoned you back hoping to discuss a foolproof plan with you.","\"Although we have now found clues of Liu Hong colluding with the enemy, we still lack a bit of evidence to take him down.","\"Furthermore, he has the Jing State Liu Family and Consort Liu backing him. I even suspect someone in the Capital Prefecture is supporting him from the shadows.\"","Xiao Jinghong pondered, \"Grandfather, do you suspect the Nine Ministers, or the Royal Family and Nobility?\"","Elder Master Xiao shook his head. \"Both are possible.\"","He then sighed. \"At this point, I won’t hide it from you.","\"Over the years, I have won every battle I fought, trampling through Poshisu Country and forcing the retreat of the Barbarian Race’s Mu Hage...","\"It may look glorious and dazzling, but in reality, during this period, I have more or less offended some people.","\"For example, when Mu Hage attacked five years ago, the Supreme Commander at the time was Zhu Chengxuan, the Minister of Rites, one of the Nine Ministers. He is now the Minister of Earth.\"","Xiao Jinghong frowned slightly. \"Zhu Chengxuan?\"","\"I remember when Father and Mother had just burned the Barbarian Race’s rations, he proposed leaving the pass to fight the Barbarian Race to the death?\"","Elder Master Xiao gave a slight nod. \"It was during that incident that a rift formed between us.","\"This man is excessively ambitious and treats human life like worthless grass. He will resort to any means necessary to advance his position.","\"Even after he returned to the Capital Prefecture and was promoted to ’Minister of Earth’ by the Holy Emperor, I believe he is still not satisfied.\"","Xiao Jinghong understood. \"No wonder he obstructed us time and time again when we petitioned the Holy Emperor to send military pay and rations for the Three Towns.\"","She looked at the elder master thoughtfully. \"Is he the one standing behind Liu Hong?\"","\"It’s not impossible, but it could also be someone else.\"","Elder Master Xiao explained, \"Zhu Chengxuan is indeed unscrupulous, but as a man who controls the Imperial Court’s purse strings, everything he does should be for the sake of profit.","\"Therefore, I actually suspect him to be the man behind the Ji State Trading Company, rather than the one behind Liu Hong.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Jinghong thought for a moment. \"I will find someone to keep an eye on him.","\"Even if it isn’t him, the fact remains that Liu Hong and Zhu Hao are secretly selling ironware through the Ji State Trading Company. We must guard against it regardless.\"","Elder Master Xiao’s expression flickered. \"You want to seek out those people?\"","Xiao Jinghong nodded and said calmly, \"Since returning to Shu State, I have not had any contact with them.","\"But the Capital Prefecture is far away. For the sake of the Xiao Family and the Dingyuan Army, I have no choice but to resort to this.\"","\"... It’s been hard on you.","\"Wandering Martial Artists belong to the Jianghu, and they have many rifts with the Imperial Court. Originally, I really didn’t want you to be distracted by Jianghu matters. Now it seems I was wrong.\"","Elder Master Xiao was very wary of Jianghu People.","Although there were many righteous individuals among them who understood the greater good, most were scoundrels who flouted moral principles and the law under the guise of chivalry.","Especially with those bloody grudges and grievances—getting involved meant an endless stream of trouble.","He didn’t want Xiao Jinghong, a General, to be deeply mired in them.","\"I understand your concerns. I will definitely be more careful,\" she reassured him.","Elder Master Xiao nodded, pausing before saying, \"Putting the Capital Prefecture aside, the most important thing right now is how to deal with Liu Hong and his cohorts.","\"As long as he is around, Shu State and the Xiao Family will never have peace. It’s time to put an end to this.\"","Xiao Jinghong hummed in agreement. After thinking for a moment, she suggested, \"Why don’t I try making a move?\"","\"Oh?\"","\"According to what the ’Dragon Spear’ said, these matters can all be traced. As long as we find conclusive evidence, Liu Hong will have no choice but to face execution.\"","Elder Master Xiao was somewhat moved but hesitated, asking, \"But your return today will inevitably alert him. I’m afraid...\"","Xiao Jinghong smiled. \"The construction of the Wu Mountain Mutual Market is nearing completion. Once I confirm that Eldest Sister is safe and sound, it will be perfectly reasonable for me to leave.\"","\"That’s true...\"","After further discussion, Xiao Jinghong stood up to leave.","\"I will head back to the Spring Lotus Garden first.\"","Elder Master Xiao walked her to the courtyard. As they walked, he said, \"Have you seriously considered the proposal I made earlier these past few days?\"","\"What...\"","Xiao Jinghong suddenly reacted, recalling how Elder Master Xiao had hinted at her consummating her marriage with Chen Yi when she last returned to the Prefecture City. With an unnatural expression, she quickened her pace.","\"Rest early, Grandfather.\"","Elder Master Xiao, completely oblivious, smiled and said, \"Your husband has now reached Perfection in the Calligraphy Dao and has gained a reputation for his talent. Marrying into our Xiao Family can be considered a fortunate event.","\"Even if he isn’t quite as outstanding as ’Dragon Tiger’ Liu Wu... or Chen Yu, he should still be worthy of your attention, right?\""]},{"number":505,"title":"Chapter 505 - 300: Paving a Great Dao to Heaven","paragraphs":["\"Grandfather, you... are acting inappropriately for your age.\"","Two faint blushes quietly surfaced on Xiao Jinghong’s face. With a light tap of her toes, she vanished from Qingjing Residence.","Elder Master Xiao was left alone behind, muttering to himself, \"Grandfather is getting old, after all. While these old bones can still move, I also want to teach my great-grandson a thing or two...\"","Xiao Jinghong moved even faster, drifting into Spring Lotus Garden in the blink of an eye. She proactively sealed her ear acupoints to block out those \"indecent\" words.","\"What great-grandson? Doesn’t he just want Chen Yi and me to... consummate our marriage?\" she thought, subconsciously looking toward the wooden building where Chen Yi stayed.","In the dim light, the quaint and elegant building with its gray tiles and red wood was faintly illuminated by several lanterns. From the corner room on the second floor closest to Jiaxing Garden, the steady, drawn-out sound of breathing could be vaguely heard. Clearly, Chen Yi was fast asleep.","Xiao Jinghong gazed at it for a moment, her mind conjuring up the Poetry and Paintings Chen Yi had made for her. Inevitably, she also recalled what Elder Master Xiao had just said: \"Chen Yi can also be considered an ideal husband.\"","\"Consummate... great-grandson...\" Before she knew it, Xiao Jinghong’s face grew even redder. She hurriedly turned around and headed to another wooden building.","With a CREAK, the door opened, and with another CREAK, it closed. Even amidst the noisy patter of raindrops, the sound carried quite far.","Once Spring Lotus Garden fell silent, Chen Yi, maintaining his steady breathing, quietly opened one eye and looked around, letting out a sigh of relief in his heart. Madam had returned much earlier than he had expected this time. Fortunately, she had made a significant amount of noise; otherwise, the aura from his Cultivation of the Four Symbols Skill earlier might not have gone unnoticed.","He wondered, \"I don’t know what she discussed with the Elder Master.","\"Liu Hong? The Peacock King Banner? The Barbarian Race?","\"Those scums have nothing to do with me anyway. But what was with her standing outside the door for so long?","\"Could she have discovered my flaws?","\"Probably not.","\"Definitely not.\"","Chen Yi muttered to himself for a bit. Still unable to figure out the reason, he rolled over and fell into a deep sleep. Having been exhausted for the past few days, he indeed needed some rest. Besides, now that Xiao Jinghong had returned, he couldn’t do anything even if he wanted to. He could only hope that Cui Qingwu, Liu Lang, Zhang Dabao, and the others would be a bit smarter and not cause any major blunders.","***","Chen Yi slept soundly, but many people in Shu State Prefecture City were destined for a sleepless night. Almost all the Wandering Martial Artists who had come to Shu State to await Immortal Bai gathered in various places across the city—taverns, teahouses, inns, and the Qin Building. Groups of these Wandering Martial Artists clustered together, discussing the night’s events.","There were even well-informed and quick-witted storytellers who dramatically reenacted the tale of \"Dragon Tiger\" Liu Wu rescuing Eldest Miss Xiao.","Inside the Spring Rain Building.","Originally, it had been filled with young masters from Noble Families and romantic scholars putting on airs of culture, reciting Poetry, drinking, and listening to music. However, once Midnight passed, the top courtesans suddenly fell out of favor.","An elderly man, over half a century old, was invited upstairs. After cupping his hands in greeting to the surroundings, he sat on the stage and slammed his wooden block down.","\"Speaking of that ’Dragon Tiger’ Liu Wu, he is without a doubt a top-tier hero in the Jianghu of Shu State recently!\"","The old man gave a thumbs-up and recounted the major deeds Liu Wu had successively accomplished. His tone was perfectly modulated, stirring up the atmosphere in the hall. Only when he sensed that many guests were growing impatient did he take a sip of tea, clear his throat, and continue.","\"As the story goes, earlier today, ’Jackal’ Du Cang of the Peacock King Banner lay in ambush outside the Xiao Family gates. Seizing the moment Eldest Miss Xiao’s carriage arrived, he abducted her using his controlled Puppet body.","\"The Xiao Family was thrown into chaos! Old Marquis Xiao was furious, and the various Government Offices in the Prefecture City... At that critical moment, ’Dragon Tiger’... At the time, Liu Wu was still known as ’Dragon Spear.’ He went to the meeting entirely alone...","\"That battle could be described as world-shaking... To know what happened next, please listen to the next installment!\"","SMACK!","Seeing this, the guests hurled a few curses, tipped him some broken pieces of silver, and were finally treated to the rest of the story.","Even though much of it was fabricated by the old man, the multitude of guests still thoroughly enjoyed listening to it.","\"That Du Cang is not someone to be trifled with. Eldest Miss Xiao’s safe return this time was truly a stroke of luck.\"","\"Indeed. If ’Dragon Tiger’ hadn’t intervened, I’m afraid no one here could have saved her.\"","\"But ’Dragon Tiger’ really played the hero saving the beauty this time. Perhaps the Old Marquis will betroth the Eldest Miss to him.\"","\"That really is a possibility...\"","Inside a Quiet Chamber upstairs.","Listening to the discussions below, Lou Yuxue couldn’t help but show a hint of disdain on her face. She muttered to herself, \"What’s so good about that sickly girl?","\"She can’t lift anything with her hands, can’t carry anything on her shoulders. She’s weak, frail, and entirely brainless... Why would Liu Wu take a fancy to her?\"","Despite saying that, Lou Yuxue had to admit that Xiao Wan’er was the most beautiful woman she had ever seen—even more beautiful than her and Cui Qingwu combined. However, she didn’t feel that Xiao Wan’er was much better than her because of this. On the contrary, she felt that if they were to stand side by side and be compared, the ultimate winner would undoubtedly be herself.","After making the comparison, Lou Yuxue revealed a faint smile. She sealed the secret letter in her hand, stuffed it into a small tube on a goshawk’s leg, and released it into the sky. Lowering her gaze slightly, she watched the rain outside the window, her smile gradually fading.","\"It’s a good thing that Liu Wu killed Du Cang, but he has ultimately caught the Pavilion Master’s eye. In the future, he’ll likely suffer some hardships,\" she thought.","This wasn’t some exaggerated fantasy of hers. In the past, there had been people similar to Liu Wu—some were unparalleled geniuses, some were brilliant masterminds, and others came from prominent Noble Families, just to name a few. Yet, most of them had ended up in miserable states.","Therefore, Lou Yuxue secretly didn’t want Liu Wu to join the White Tiger Guards, lest the Pavilion Master assign him several extremely dangerous missions. But she didn’t have any good solutions, either. She could only do her best to smooth things over. After all...","Lou Yuxue sighed. The image of Liu Wu’s half-smiling face seemed to float before her eyes, and she couldn’t resist throwing a Punch at it."]},{"number":506,"title":"Chapter 506 - 300: Paving a Heaven-Reaching Great Dao","paragraphs":["\"Bastard! Go to hell!\"","Right then, the door to the Quiet Chamber opened.","Seeing her state, Cui Qingwu couldn’t help but ask with a smile, \"Who upset our Lord Lady Tiger?","\"A bastard? Was it Liu Wu?\"","Lou Yuxue paused, a hint of displeasure appearing on her face as she turned to look at her. \"What are you doing here?","\"Aren’t you following that Young Master Chen? How do you have the free time to come here?\"","The smile on Cui Qingwu’s face mostly dissipated. She tossed a stack of contracts onto the table and said, \"As previously discussed, I’ve obtained the contracts for several major grain stores, including Lin’s Grain Store.","\"Guess how much silver we made this time?\"","Lou Yuxue’s expression shifted slightly as she picked up the contracts and began to read them.","After flipping through a few pages, a look of surprise crossed her face. \"Fourteen taels of silver per stone? They agreed to this?\"","Cui Qingwu snorted. \"Did they really think they could take advantage of the Cui Family?","\"Buying and selling as they please—how could there be such a good deal in this world?\"","\"I remember you bought it for ten taels of silver and then sold it for fourteen, which equals a profit of four taels per stone of grain. A million stones...","\"Four million silver coins!?\"","Lou Yuxue couldn’t help but be shocked. It was simply because this was too much money, and it had been earned far too easily.","In just a single day, Lin Zhenghong and the others had lost four million taels of silver for nothing.","Even with the Ji State Trading Company behind them, this was still a very considerable amount of silver.","If something were to go wrong...","There were no \"ifs.\" Lou Yuxue was almost certain that Liu Wu had backup plans prepared.","Cui Qingwu sat down at the table, casually picking up a teacup and pouring herself a cup of tea before speaking. \"Why are you so surprised? After hearing Liu Wu’s plan the day before yesterday, I already figured out what would happen to those grain stores.","\"If I hadn’t been worried about scaring them off by raising the price too high, I wouldn’t have even sold it to them for twenty taels of silver.\"","Pausing for a moment, a cold sneer appeared on Cui Qingwu’s face. \"I reckon they’re calling me a fool right now.","\"But there will come a time for them to cry. Just wait and enjoy the show.\"","Although she didn’t know what Liu Wu was going to do next, she was well aware that after setting up such a massive scheme, he would never let Lin Zhenghong and the others off easily.","Perhaps this time, they could really make the Ji State Trading Company suffer a massive fall.","Hearing this, Lou Yuxue steadied her Heart Spirit. Gripping the contracts, she asked, \"With such a large sum of silver, how much do you plan to give Liu Wu?\"","\"Give it to him?\"","Cui Qingwu snorted. \"Of course, we’re going to split it between the two of us. I’m not giving him a single penny.\"","\"Not giving him any?","\"Did you forget how he treated you earlier?\"","\"But... but once that bastard finds out, I’m afraid he won’t just let it go...\"","\"Then let him come find me. Now that it’s in this lady’s hands, I’d like to see how he plans to take it back.\"","Lou Yuxue watched as she drank the tea in one gulp. Sizing her up, she asked, \"Are you in a bad mood?\"","Cui Qingwu shot her a sidelong glance and turned her head away. \"No.\"","\"...Does it have something to do with Young Master Chen?\"","\"No...\"","In truth, Cui Qingwu was indeed in a bad mood.","Originally, after following Chen Yunfan back to Tingyu Pavilion, she had wanted to take the opportunity to mention the matter regarding Commander-in-Chief Zhu Hao to him, so he could make some preparations.","But before she could even enter the middle courtyard, she was stopped by Chun Ying, who was guarding the door.","She even said, \"My young master specifically instructed that he is going into secluded Cultivation and will not be seeing guests for the time being.\"","Was she, Cui Qingwu, just a guest?","Besides, she had clearly heard Chen Yunfan talking with someone; he wasn’t practicing Cultivation at all.","By saying that, Chun Ying was obviously brushing her off.","Seeing this, Lou Yuxue naturally realized that she was indeed in a bad mood, so she reined in her temper and offered a few words of comfort.","Unexpectedly, Cui Qingwu retorted, \"You’re trying so hard to persuade me to give Liu Wu a share of the silver. Do you really consider yourself his fiancée who hasn’t even crossed the threshold yet?\"","\"You... you’re talking nonsense...\"","...","Inside Tingyu Pavilion.","Chen Yunfan sat behind the desk, looking at the corpse on the floor in the center of the hall.","Standing to the side was impressively the middle-aged man in short clothes who had met with Chun Ying.","At this moment, he had taken off his bamboo hat. His messy hair was tied behind his head with a straw rope, and Fang Zheng’s face was covered in a full beard, leaving a large portion of his chest exposed through his open robes.","\"Eldest Young Master, I wouldn’t dare disobey the orders of the Master and the Second Master. Please don’t make things difficult for me.\"","Chen Yunfan remained silent for a moment before frowning. \"Uncle Zhong, what exactly are my father and Second Uncle trying to do?","\"When the Holy Emperor previously appointed me as the Assistant Governor of the Governor’s Office in Shu State, I found it strange. I suppose... that was Second Uncle’s idea?","\"Coupled with the fact that you’ve come looking for me with Lv Jiunan’s corpse this time, it’s hard not to overthink things.","\"Are they planning to pave a heaven-reaching Dao for me?\""]},{"number":507,"title":"Chapter 507 - 301: Not Even My Own Father Will Do","paragraphs":["When Chen Yunfan first arrived in Shu State, he didn’t think much of it. Even though he hadn’t undergone the three years of experiential learning in the Capital Prefecture and was directly promoted to the Junior Fourth Grade Assistant Governor under the Governor of Shu State, he merely thought it was a sign of the Holy Emperor’s high regard. After all, that Emperor had practically forced the title of Imperial Top Scholar onto his head. What did an exceptional promotion matter in comparison?","However, since coming to Shu State, experiencing certain events, and meeting certain people, he began to feel increasingly that something was amiss. The government affairs assigned to him were always simple, easy to execute, and yielded significant achievements. From time to time, inexplicable merits would also be delivered to his doorstep. For instance, Xiao Dongchen had handed over a task he had almost finished himself for him to complete. For example, tax grain collections were always assigned in villages and towns closest to the Prefecture City, requiring minimal effort and worry. Furthermore, whenever there was evidence of corruption involving officials from the Governor’s Office, it would always end up in his hands in the most \"reasonable\" manner.","It felt as though an unseen hand was secretly orchestrating all of this specifically for him. Although Chen Yunfan found it strange, he saw no reason to reject the achievements that landed in his lap. Moreover, assuming it was the assistance of the White-robed Minister where Chun Ying belonged, he naturally didn’t overthink it.","Today, however, Uncle Zhong, also known as Lin Zhong—a loyal servant whose ancestors had served the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family for generations—brought over Lv Jiunan’s corpse. This made him realize that the implications behind all this were vast. The mastermind wasn’t the White-robed Minister... Or more accurately, those orchestrating this from the shadows were the White-robed Minister and the Chen family themselves. Only he, the Eldest Young Master of the Chen family, was kept entirely in the dark.","Lin Zhong looked at the cold-faced Chen Yunfan, subconsciously scratched his head, and let out a dry laugh.","\"Eldest Young Master, you know how it is. Regarding the orders from the Master and the Second Master, I merely follow them. I wouldn’t dare ask for the reasons.","\"How about you write them a letter to ask?\"","Chen Yunfan knew he was making excuses to avoid speaking. \"I will write the letter, but as for this so-called ’achievement’ in the form of Lv Jiunan, send it right back where it came from.\"","Lin Zhong’s face turned bitter. \"Eldest Young Master, this Lv Jiunan is a horse bandit under King Landu of Poshisu Country. Anyone who claims his corpse would be credited with a tremendous achievement. Why are you refusing it?\"","Chen Yunfan scoffed. \"I don’t want it. Throw him out quickly before he dirties my carpet.\"","If it were anyone else’s corpse, he might have accepted it. But he knew exactly why Lv Jiunan had appeared here. And it wasn’t just him. The entire Shu State knew that Lv Jiunan had been killed by the Dragon Spear Liu Wu. If he took the corpse to the Government Office to claim the reward, the merits and the strange smiles from his colleagues aside, what about Liu Wu? Or rather, Chen Yi. If Chen Yi found out about this, wouldn’t he laugh his head off? How wonderful. A Lv Jiunan discarded like trash by Chen Yi was picked up by him and added to his record of achievements. What would that make him, Chen Yunfan? How would he ever hold his head high as an elder brother in front of Brother Yi in the future? In short, even if beaten to death, Chen Yunfan would never accept this achievement concerning Lv Jiunan!","Seeing his resolute expression, Lin Zhong could only concede. \"Since Eldest Young Master has made a decision, I will take the person back.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yunfan’s expression softened slightly, and he waved his hand. \"Take him away quickly. It annoys me to look at him.\"","Inwardly feeling helpless, Lin Zhong stepped forward and hoisted Lv Jiunan’s corpse onto his shoulder. Just as he was about to leave, he heard Chen Yunfan tell him to wait.","\"I almost forgot to ask. When did you arrive in Shu State?","\"And what is your purpose for coming this time?\"","\"To answer Eldest Young Master, after you wrote a letter to the Master previously, he also wrote a letter to the family when replying to you,\" Lin Zhong replied.","Chen Yunfan raised an eyebrow. \"Father sent you here?\"","Lin Zhong nodded. \"The Master is worried about your safety in Shu State, so he asked me to come and guard you.\"","\"What else did he say?\"","\"Nothing... Are you referring to the matter regarding Young Master Yi?\"","Chen Yunfan turned his head away, feigning ignorance while clearly knowing the answer.","Lin Zhong’s heart stirred. The Eldest Young Master was indeed exactly as Chun Ying had said—he cared a great deal about Young Master Yi.","\"In his letter, the Master reprimanded the Madam and asked your Fourth Granduncle to temporarily manage the clan’s affairs.\"","\"Reprimanded... Is this to make Mother reflect on her actions?\"","\"Most likely... Eldest Young Master, there is something I’m not sure if I should say.\"","Chen Yunfan cast a sidelong glance at him. \"Since when did Uncle Zhong become so coy?\"","Lin Zhong chuckled. \"I wonder if, during your time in Shu State, Eldest Young Master has formed any opinions about Young Master Yi’s current situation?\"","\"Opinions?","\"I have no opinions.","\"Brother Yi has now achieved success in his Calligraphy Dao, and his reputation for talent has spread across the Great Wei Nine State and Three Prefectures. He is also highly regarded by the Xiao Family. His days are boundlessly carefree.\"","Chen Yunfan said with a hint of jealousy, \"If you’re asking for my opinion... it’s just that he completely disregards me as his elder brother. Whatever happens...","\"Forget it, let’s not talk about him.\"","Recalling what he had seen and heard at Puyin Temple earlier, Chen Yunfan waved his hand in displeasure, signaling that the man could leave.","\"Since Father has already arranged for you to come, just stay here properly. While you’re at it, teach Ning Yu and Niu Mountain Martial Arts.","\"Those two lazy bums are still hovering at the Sixth Grade in their Cultivation. Urge them on for me.\"","Lin Zhong smilingly agreed, bowed respectfully, and left the study carrying Lv Jiunan’s corpse.","For some reason, he felt that the Eldest Young Master paid far too much attention to Young Master Yi, even harboring a hint of competitiveness. He really didn’t know what there was to compare between the Eldest Young Master and Young Master Yi.","With this thought, he walked out of the middle courtyard and glanced at Ning Yu and Niu Mountain, who were standing not too far away. He grinned broadly.","\"You two boys are in luck.","\"Eldest Young Master has given the word. From now on, you two will train in Martial Arts with me.\"","\"Huh?\"","Ning Yu’s expression changed. He exchanged a glance with Niu Mountain, and both couldn’t help but shrink their necks back.","\"What do you mean, ’huh’?","\"Back in the Chen family, I gave you two plenty of extra training. Don’t be ungrateful.\""]},{"number":508,"title":"Chapter 508 - 301: Even My Own Father Won’t Do","paragraphs":["Left with no other choice, Ning Yu and Niu Mountain could only nod with apologetic smiles.","Lin Zhong ignored the two buffoons. He shot Chun Ying a meaningful look before hoisting Lv Jiunan’s corpse over his shoulder and darting away.","Chun Ying understood his unspoken message. After a moment of hesitation, she instructed Ning Yu and Niu Mountain to continue standing guard, then turned and walked to the study.","Taking a moment to calm her Heart Spirit, she raised a hand and knocked on the door. \"Young Master.\"","\"Come in.\"","Chun Ying pushed the door open and stepped inside, catching from the corner of her eye that Chen Yunfan was bent over his desk, writing something. She turned to close the door behind her.","\"Young Master, Uncle Zhong came to see you about...\"","Before she could finish, Chen Yunfan interrupted her in a flat tone. \"Do you truly not know why he came here carrying Lv Jiunan’s corpse?","\"Chun Ying, don’t think that just because you are a White-robed Minister and slightly smarter than others, you can secretly interfere in my affairs.\"","Though his tone was indifferent, the words struck fear into Chun Ying’s heart. Having served Chen Yunfan for many years, she was intimately familiar with his temperament. The calmer Chen Yunfan appeared, the greater his internal displeasure. Conversely, if he scolded her outright, it usually meant the matter wasn’t too serious.","With these thoughts in mind, Chun Ying knelt down and bowed. \"Please forgive me, Young Master. I... I...\"","\"Are you also going to claim that you were just following orders? That you didn’t intentionally hide it from me?\"","\"Yes...\"","Chen Yunfan briefly raised his head, his expression as calm as still water, before looking back down to continue writing. \"Stand up and speak. I don’t care for all this kneeling and bowing here.\"","Once Chun Ying hesitantly got to her feet, he continued, \"Tell me, what exactly are my father and you White-robed Ministers scheming?","\"Sending me to Shu State—am I really supposed to take over Yang Ye’s position as the Right Governor?\"","He had completely dismissed Chen Yi’s earlier joking remark about this. But thinking about it now, there was actually a damn good chance it was true.","Chun Ying asked hesitantly, \"Young Master, you... you know everything?\"","Chen Yunfan paused, his brows furrowing slightly, but he simply gestured without looking up. \"Continue.\"","\"I... I don’t know the specific plans of the Master and the Lord White-robed Minister either. I only have my suspicions. The position of Right Governor that you mentioned... is not impossible.\"","\"Are there other positions? Let me guess.","\"The two Commanders of the Capital Commandery are in the prime of their lives, so there shouldn’t be any vacancies there for the time being.","\"The Inspectorate Office? That’s possible. Tang Zixing, the Inspector General, won’t be moved, but the Vice Envoy... it’s a possibility.","\"Next would be the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office. Liu Si is a two-faced backstabber, so I presume he won’t win Shangguan Huan’s favor; nine times out of ten, he’ll be replaced as well.","\"As for the remaining positions, they are even lower than my current rank as a Fourth-grade Assistant Governor, so there is nothing worth discussing.\"","As Chen Yunfan finished speaking, he also wrote the last character. He picked up the piece of paper from the desk and blew on it to dry the ink. \"I’m guessing it’s the Capital Commandery, isn’t it?\"","Hearing this, Chun Ying’s expression changed slightly. \"How... how did you guess that?\"","Chen Yunfan finished drying the ink on the paper, folded it neatly, and slipped it into an envelope with a snort. \"Other than the Commander-in-Chief, what other official position can influence the Dingyuan Army?","\"Even the Governor’s Office cannot openly interfere with the military affairs of the Three Towns, let alone a Government Office like the Inspectorate Office, which can only file petty complaints.\"","He set down the envelope, leaned back in his chair, and looked at Chun Ying with an indifferent expression. \"Chen Yi marrying into the Xiao Family is probably part of your scheme as well, isn’t it?\"","Chun Ying’s eyes widened slightly. She knelt down again, lowering her head and not daring to speak. Although it was just his speculation, it wasn’t far from the truth. Naturally, she didn’t dare to say anything more, lest Chen Yunfan figure out even more.","Seeing her reaction, Chen Yunfan chuckled self-deprecatingly. \"It seems I am right.","\"I knew it. Although Mother has some of the arrogance that comes from being born into the Cui Family, she has always treated us brothers equally since we were young.","\"Why would she deliberately target Brother Yi for no reason? So this is why.","\"Thinking about it now, before Father went to the Western Regions, he probably finalized everything with you White-robed Ministers, Second Uncle, and even the clan elders.","\"We brothers genuinely thought that Brother Yi had made some terrible mistake to incur Mother’s fury.\"","SMACK!","Chen Yunfan slammed his palm onto the desk, glaring icily at the kneeling Chun Ying. \"What exactly are you all scheming?!\"","Chun Ying’s body flinched. Biting her lip, she shook her head. \"Young Master, please forgive me. I truly do not know...\"","\"You don’t know? Heh, fine! Very well!\" Chen Yunfan’s lips twitched, forming a peculiar smile. \"Since that is the case, I won’t make things difficult for you.\"","He hadn’t expected that his earlier speculations would be so close to the truth. Even less did he expect that both he and Chen Yi had been played by their own family. Back then, he had even felt that his situation was better than Chen Yi’s and wanted to show off in front of him. Little did he know, both of them were just meat on someone else’s chopping block.","And the crucial point was that this \"someone else\" was his own biological father!","After venting his anger, Chen Yunfan seemed to have figured things out. He let out a long breath and said, \"I’d really like to see what tricks my father, Second Uncle, and you White-robed Ministers have up your sleeves.\"","He then tossed the envelope forward. \"It’s for my father. Send it to him.","\"Don’t give me any excuses about how long the journey takes. I know you have the means.\"","Chun Ying looked at the letter by her knees. After a moment of hesitation, she reached out, picked it up, and bowed. \"I will get it done right away.\"","Chen Yunfan waved his hand, his interest entirely depleted. \"Get out.\"","After Chun Ying left the study with her head bowed, Chen Yunfan’s expression immediately turned into one of distress. He began to grumble to himself, \"Has my father gone senile?","\"With Brother Yi’s exceptional talent, what was he thinking, sending him to marry into the Xiao Family?","\"If it were someone else... Fourth Brother... no, that glutton would eat the Xiao Family into poverty.","\"Old Liu... would be even worse. He spends all day traveling and enjoying the scenery. If he really became Xiao Jinghong’s husband, wouldn’t he be strung up and whipped?","\"Second Sister and Third Sister are girls...\""]},{"number":509,"title":"Chapter 509 - 301: Not Even My Own Father","paragraphs":["Thinking it over, Chen Yunfan finally realized that besides himself, Chen Yi was indeed the only one suitable to marry into the Xiao family as a live-in son-in-law. It was just that the price to pay was simply too great. At this thought, Chen Yunfan’s previous righteous indignation inexplicably gave way to a hint of schadenfreude.","\"Brother Yi has now achieved success in the Martial Arts, Medical Dao, and Calligraphy Dao. If Father learns of this... With his temperament, ahem... Even if he knows he was wrong, he probably won’t admit it.\"","No one knew a father better than his son. Chen Yunfan understood Chen Xuanji fairly well and knew that he was a man who would never bow his head. But Chen Yunfan couldn’t help laughing anyway.","\"My dad might just double down on his mistakes, but Second Uncle won’t. Neither will Second Grandpa, Fourth Great-Uncle, or the others. My dad is going to have a massive headache soon, haha...\"","As he laughed, Chen Yunfan recalled the rumors he had heard about Chen Yi when he first arrived in Shu State, and his smile faded slightly.","\"To dare scheme against us brothers... Even our own flesh-and-blood father can’t get away with it!\"","The following day.","The rain had cleared, leaving behind a bright sky. However, the atmosphere within the Prefecture City was rather heavy. It was as if after a night of chaos, everyone had become weighed down by their own worries, their voices softening as they conversed.","\"The grain prices in the East and West Markets have gone up again! Overnight, they skyrocketed to fifteen taels of silver per stone. Is... is this an attempt to starve us commoners to death?\"","\"Did something happen?\"","\"I heard... I heard something happened on the Ancient Tea-Horse Road.\"","\"The vanguard of the Peacock King Banner’s army appeared on the Ancient Tea-Horse Road. Many merchant caravans fell victim to them.\"","\"And I also heard that ’Jackal’ Du Cang kidnapped Eldest Miss Xiao last night to force the Old Marquis to serve the Peacock King Banner.\"","\"Does that mean... are we really going to war?\"","\"If not, how would those grain shops dare to hike up their prices on the spot?\"","\"GASP... Heavens above...\"","As the news spread, an atmosphere of panic began to permeate the Shu State Prefecture City. They couldn’t be blamed for their fear. The great war from five years ago was still fresh in many people’s memories, especially for the elderly. They still remembered how severely Shu State lacked grain during the Barbarian Race’s invasion. Although the streets hadn’t been littered with the starved dead, many families had been forced to sell their children just for a few mouthfuls of food.","Therefore, as soon as the sky began to lighten, long lines formed outside the grain shops in the East and West Markets. Those Noble Families who had initially thought about taking advantage of the situation to sell grain also reined in their greed, sealing their granaries in preparation for unforeseen contingencies. Even the Xiao family was no exception.","However, when Elder Master Xiao handed down the orders, the expression on his face was extremely complicated. In his heart, he cursed Chen Yu half to death. He could understand Chen Yu’s intention behind using such a scheme to deal with the Ji State Trading Company, but he could not accept that it implicated the common people. Let alone lasting for days; even just a single day of this would cause the commoners to suffer immensely. At the very least, they would lose a fair bit of silver.","However, after pondering for a moment, Elder Master Xiao’s furrowed brows relaxed. \"Perhaps this old man misjudged him... So that’s how it is.\"","He suddenly recalled that \"Chen Yu\" had previously mentioned needing him to step forward and resolve a matter. Wasn’t right now the exact time for him to do so?","\"Damn it all, what a clever brat. If this old man hadn’t caught on, wouldn’t he have died laughing at me?\"","Having figured it out, Elder Master Xiao summoned the Third Steward, Lu Guan, and instructed him, \"Deliver a visiting card to the Governor’s Office on my behalf. Tell Liu Hong that I have an important matter to discuss with him.\"","Since he knew that the army outside the pass was fake, he naturally couldn’t let those grain shops run amok like this. The Governor’s Office would either have to step forward and order the grain shops to lower their prices, or open the official granaries to stabilize the market. Regardless, they couldn’t let those grain shops have it easy.","After Lu Guan left, Elder Master Xiao stood up and stretched his limbs, allowing his True Essence to flow along with his movements. The surrounding sounds then transmitted to him with crystal clarity. The bustling of numerous guests coming and going in the front courtyard, the shouts of Xiao Wuge practicing Martial Arts in the middle courtyard’s Martial Arts Arena, and the backyard...","Elder Master Xiao revealed a smile. \"That girl Jinghong, it seems she actually took my words to heart...\""]},{"number":510,"title":"Chapter 510 - 302: Big Sister, How About Chen Yu?","paragraphs":["Whether he would listen or not, Xiao Jinghong would inevitably have to interact with Chen Yi now that she had returned to the Marquis’s Mansion.","She couldn’t avoid it.","And she didn’t want to.","Early the next morning, after washing up and changing into casual clothes, Xiao Jinghong stepped outside the building.","In the courtyard, Xiaodie was sweeping fallen leaves with a broom. She had even set up a ladder to sweep the roof of the pavilion. Perhaps because the courtyard was so quiet and secluded, Xiaodie’s humming drifted through the cool, slightly damp breeze. The melody was cheerful, but the lyrics did not sound like the style of the Great Wei Dynasty.","\"The cool wind brings tidings. The autumn moon knows no bounds. My lovesickness makes every day feel like a year. Although I am not a handsome gentleman standing tall as a jade tree in the wind...\"","Straightforward and novel.","Xiao Jinghong subconsciously looked toward the wooden building on the other side, inexplicably feeling that this was her husband’s masterpiece. Recalling those few lyrics, a smile inevitably tugged at the corners of her mouth. \"He is indeed a handsome gentleman.\"","In Xiao Jinghong’s heart, Chen Yi’s temperament was gentle and composed, not something that could be described by superficial words like \"a handsome gentleman standing tall as a jade tree.\" Moreover, he was a scholar who was highly likely to break through to the Saint Realm in the Calligraphy Dao before the age of thirty, enough to stand at the pinnacle of the Great Wei Dynasty’s younger generation.","What did his appearance matter?","\"Ah!\"","While Xiao Jinghong was staring blankly at the wooden building where Chen Yi was, Xiaodie inadvertently caught sight of her figure as she climbed down the ladder and couldn’t help but say joyfully, \"Second Miss, when did you get back?\"","Xiao Jinghong snapped back to reality, her smile fading as she said in a flat tone, \"Last night.\"","Xiaodie didn’t even bother putting away the ladder and hurried over. \"Did you come back because of the First Miss? Last night, the First Miss was saved by that so-called ’Dragon Spear.’ It was a blessing in disguise.","\"Second Miss, have you gone to see the First Miss yet?\"","Xiao Jinghong nodded slightly. \"I am already aware of the matter. I will go to Jiaxing Garden to visit her in a bit.\" She glanced at the sky and asked casually, \"Did my husband go to bed late last night?\"","Xiaodie nodded. \"Yes. After the First Miss was rescued and brought back last night, she sent the Young Master over here. The First Miss was quite frightened and looked a bit pale. Fortunately, Master Chen comforted her a bit, and she went back to rest after Midnight.\"","\"Midnight...\"","Xiao Jinghong thought to herself that it was no wonder; Chen Yi’s breathing was still steady, so he was obviously sleeping soundly. She thought for a moment, then waved at Xiaodie and turned back into the wooden building. \"Tell me about the interesting things that have happened in the mansion recently.\"","Suspecting nothing, Xiaodie followed her inside, feeling a little nervous.","Their questions and answers flowed harmoniously.","However, what interesting things could possibly happen in the Marquis’s Mansion? Or rather, what interesting things could Xiaodie possibly know? The person she interacted with the most was Chen Yi, so naturally, she talked mostly about matters related to him.","But this was exactly what Xiao Jinghong wanted to hear. Thus, Xiaodie recounted everything from the Old Marquis’s birthday banquet all the way to last night.","Although it spanned a considerable amount of time, Xiaodie managed to describe everything in meticulous detail, relying on her memory of writing *The Biography of the Marquis Wu’s Mansion’s Second Son-in-Law and His Little Maid*. She spoke of Guiyun Academy, the Medicine Hall, Poetry, calligraphy, Painting, Zither music, and more. She especially noted the origins of those few pieces of Poetry.","For instance, she shared how *Song of the Water Melody: Mid-Autumn: When Will the Bright Moon Appear?* won first place at Guiyun Academy’s Mid-Autumn Poetry Gathering. She also explained how Chen Yi revealed his Perfect Calligraphy Dao through the poem he wrote for Mr. Sun Fu, which read, \"Worry not that no soul knows you on the road ahead; who in this world has not heard of your name?\"","Xiao Jinghong was left wanting more after hearing the stories, finally getting a clear picture of Chen Yi’s recent circumstances. However, she didn’t show it and simply continued to ask about Xiao Wan’er, Elder Master Xiao, and the others.","\"Are you saying that the Cui Family is also going to participate in the Medical Dao Academy that my eldest sister founded?\" Xiao Jinghong asked.","\"Mhm, the First Miss asked Master Chen for his thoughts. Master Chen said that Miss Cui could participate as long as she doesn’t interfere with the academy’s internal affairs.\"","\"That makes sense...\" Xiao Jinghong gave a slight nod, thinking to herself that it was no wonder her eldest sister’s letters had been so protective of her husband. It seemed that her husband had helped her eldest sister quite a lot recently.","The Medical Dao Academy... It was a good thing.","As for Elder Master Xiao’s situation, Xiao Jinghong already knew quite a bit, so she only asked a few simple questions. It was mostly about the recent rumors circulating in Shu State City and how Liu Hong had visited multiple times to offer advice.","After a bit more casual chatting, seeing that it was already half past 5:00 AM, Xiao Jinghong stood up and said, \"Go check on my husband. If he’s awake, come with him to Jiaxing Garden.\"","Xiaodie agreed and followed her out of the wooden building. After watching her leave toward Jiaxing Garden, Xiaodie hurriedly went to find Chen Yi.","\"Master Chen, Master Chen, the Second Miss is back! You need to wake up!\"","\"Xiaodie? Let me sleep a little longer... The Second Miss is back... Hm? Madam is back? I need to bathe and change my clothes!\"","Hearing Chen Yi’s voice from the guest room, Xiao Jinghong smiled knowingly. With light steps, she crossed the corridor and disappeared toward Jiaxing Garden.","Chen Yi vaguely heard her footsteps fading away and let out a long sigh. Madam starting to ask about his experiences the moment she returned really put a lot of pressure on him.","It was no wonder Chen Yi felt so guilty. It was truly because the things he had done recently were fine as long as he pushed the blame onto Chen Yu and Liu Wu. If Xiao Jinghong found out that he was the one behind them, it would inevitably cause unexpected complications. When that time came, Elder Master Xiao would likely be highly guarded against him as well.","Fortunately, Xiaodie didn’t know much. Otherwise, that girl would have probably sold him out already.","Naturally unaware of his inner thoughts, Xiaodie hurriedly fetched water and ran over with a brand-new set of clothes.","\"Master Chen, the Second Miss went to Jiaxing Garden. She said that once you wake up, you should go over there for breakfast.\"","Chen Yi hummed in acknowledgment. As he washed up, he asked Xiaodie, who was waiting outside the door, \"When did Madam return?\"","\"The Second Miss said she returned last night. She also said that since you were already asleep, she went to rest as well.\"","\"Because of my eldest sister’s matter?\"","\"Yes, the Marquis sent an urgent message calling her back...\"","He had to put on a full act."]},{"number":511,"title":"Chapter 511 - 302: Eldest Sister, What About Chen Yu?","paragraphs":["Chen Yi would inevitably have to ask a few routine questions.","After washing up, he changed into a brand-new profound-colored brocade robe, fastened a jade belt around his waist, and hung a sachet from it. He checked his reflection in the copper mirror. Although he couldn’t exactly be called a breathtakingly handsome man, his looks were certainly above average. Coupled with his unhurried and elegant demeanor, describing him as \"handsome\" wouldn’t be an exaggeration.","Smoothing down the hair at his temples, Chen Yi revealed a gentle smile. \"Madam, it has been a long time. Your husband—cough, cough...\"","He had almost forgotten. With Xiao Jinghong’s Upper Three Grades cultivation, her hearing could probably cover the entire Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion.","Outside the door, Xiaodie heard the noise. \"Mr. Chen, are you ready?\"","\"I’m ready.\"","Chen Yi pushed the door open and stepped out. As he led her toward Jiaxing Garden, he checked today’s intelligence. Upon seeing the contents, his steps faltered.","[Daily Intelligence · Profound-rank Top Grade: At a quarter past noon, at the Governor’s Office, Duke Dingyuan Xiao Yuan will show up to demand an explanation from Liu Hong, the Left Governor of Shu State. A minor opportunity can be obtained.]","Demand an explanation? After a brief moment of thought, Chen Yi understood.","The fact that Xiao Jinghong hadn’t accompanied the Old Master to see Liu Hong meant that the Xiao family was not yet ready to take Liu Hong down. For the Old Master to go in person this time, it was likely to stabilize the grain prices in the Shu State Prefecture City.","\"It seems the Old Master still knows how to prioritize,\" he thought. \"Taking care of the Ji State Trading Company first is currently the best course of action.\"","Originally, Chen Yi had planned to find another opportunity to remind the Old Master to reassure the people of Shu State. He hadn’t expected the Old Master to be completely unaffected by Xiao Wan’er’s kidnapping yesterday and instead head straight to the Governor’s Office.","In that case, Chen Yi needed to speed things up as well.","At the very least, he first had to confirm whether Lin Zhenghong and the others had resold the grain to Cui Qingwu. He also had to notify Zhang Dabao as soon as possible to toss out the merchants who had been knocked out by the Immortal Drunk. And Liu Lang...","With this in mind, Chen Yi quickened his pace and hurried to Jiaxing Garden. Before he even stepped into the wooden building’s parlor, he heard Xiao Jinghong’s voice coming from inside.","\"Wan’er, what do you think of this ’Chen Yu’?\"","Chen Yi’s heart skipped a beat, and his raised foot nearly missed the step. He wondered why his wife was asking about that. She... she couldn’t be thinking what he thought she was, could she? Wasn’t the Old Master enough? Now even Xiao Jinghong was stepping in to persuade Xiao Wan’er to marry \"Chen Yu\"?","No, no, no.","Without overthinking or waiting for Xiao Wan’er to reply, Chen Yi stepped around the privacy screen, swept his gaze over the people inside, and bowed with a smile. \"Forgive me. I went to bed a bit late yesterday, so I slept in this morning.\"","As he spoke, his gaze drifted past Xiao Wan’er and landed on Xiao Jinghong. He greeted her with a smile, \"Madam, when did you get back?\"","Xiao Wan’er breathed a sigh of relief. Not waiting for Xiao Jinghong to speak, she raised a hand to motion for Chen Yi to sit down. \"Jinghong returned last night.\"","\"Husband, I came back last night,\" Xiao Jinghong echoed.","She was not wearing her half-armor mask at the moment. Even bare-faced, her beauty rivaled that of Xiao Wan’er. She had slender eyes that tilted slightly upward at the corners, a delicate nose, full lips, and skin as flawless and radiant as white jade. She was absolutely breathtaking, radiating a faint air of valiant heroism.","\"Oh,\" Chen Yi replied. He took a seat beside her and asked familiarly, \"How many days will you be staying this time, Madam?\"","Chen Yu this, Chen Yu that—he dared not steer the conversation back toward that fabricated persona.","Xiao Jinghong paused, a trace of apology appearing on her face. \"Please forgive me, Husband. I came back this time for Wan’er’s sake.","\"But now that I see she is safe and sound, I need to hurry back to the Wu Mountain Mutual Market. It will still take a few more days to complete the construction there.\"","\"So soon?\"","Chen Yi frowned inwardly, sensing that something was slightly off. He knew full well that the Old Master had recalled Xiao Jinghong not just to rescue Xiao Wan’er, but for the even more important matter concerning Liu Hong. Even if the Old Master could handle the situation alone, Xiao Jinghong shouldn’t be leaving the Prefecture City this early. At the very least, she ought to stay and investigate.","Unless... it was a ruse to slip away unnoticed? That was highly likely.","With these thoughts in mind, Chen Yi smiled and said, \"You have a lot on your plate, Madam. It’s only right that you attend to your duties first.\"","Noticing from the corner of his eye that Xiao Wan’er looked slightly nervous, he continued, \"Let’s talk while we eat. I’m getting a little hungry.\"","Xiao Jinghong naturally had no objections. In fact, she felt his relaxed, unreserved manner was exactly how he should act.","Hearing this, Xiao Wan’er breathed a sigh of relief and invited them to begin their breakfast. \"Jinghong, I didn’t know you were coming back, so I didn’t tell the kitchen to prepare your favorite cold-sliced mutton.\"","\"It’s fine. This is more than enough.\"","Chen Yi also let out a breath of relief. Picking up a steamed bun from the table and taking a bite, he began chatting about recent events. After guiding Xiao Jinghong to comfort Xiao Wan’er, he smoothly shifted the topic to the grain prices in Shu State and matters concerning Guiyun Academy.","\"The Annual Examination begins in ten days. If my results are poor, I hope you won’t laugh at me, Madam,\" Chen Yi said.","\"I wouldn’t dare.\"","Xiao Jinghong didn’t say she ’wouldn’t,’ but rather ’wouldn’t dare.’ Her tone carried absolutely no hint of treating Chen Yi as merely a live-in son-in-law of the Xiao family. Instead, her demeanor was simply that of a proper, legally wedded wife. \"Furthermore, with your talent and knowledge, Husband, passing the Annual Examination won’t be a problem at all.\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded in agreement. \"Jinghong is right. Chen Yi has been studying very hard lately.","\"Not only has he read through all the historical classics, but he also specifically asked for past Annual Examination papers to study diligently.\"","\"Is that so?\" A trace of amusement flashed in Xiao Jinghong’s beautiful eyes as she turned her head to look at Chen Yi. \"Since you are working so hard, Husband, the Annual Examination will be even less of an issue.\"","Meeting her gaze, Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"Thank you for the vote of confidence, Madam.\"","Exchanging a glance, the two of them tacitly focused on eating their steamed buns.","Taking in their expressions, Xiao Wan’er felt an inexplicable wave of complex emotions well up inside her. Bitterness, guilt, apprehension, and nervousness mingled together, prompting her to silently lower her head.","Taking small, absentminded bites of her breakfast, her thoughts drifted far away, to the point where she completely tuned out the sounds around her."]},{"number":512,"title":"Chapter 512 - 302: Big Sister, What Do You Think of Chen Yu?","paragraphs":["As the older sister, seeing how deeply in love Jinghong and Chen Yi were, she knew she shouldn’t and couldn’t possibly do something so despicable.","But the bitterness in her heart kept her from making a ruthless decision.","This wasn’t Xiao Wan’er’s first time considering cutting off contact with Chen Yi. Like when she first received *Wan God’s Ode*. Or like when Chen Yi held her hand...","She considered it over and over, but the result was always the same.","Deep in her heart, a clear figure had already taken root. Coupled with what she had experienced yesterday—when she was so close to death, it was Chen Yi who gave her hope. No, not just hope. He had personally saved her and brought her back into a world full of color.","She didn’t want to, nor was she willing to be so absolute.","After a moment of silence, Xiao Jinghong put down her bowl and chopsticks. Not noticing anything unusual about Xiao Wan’er, she followed her grandfather’s instructions.","\"Wan’er, last night Grandfather told me to come and ask you,\" she said. \"Do you have any feelings for ’Chen Yu’ from Hundred Herbs Hall?\"","Xiao Wan’er looked up blankly. Chen Yu?","She looked at Chen Yi and subconsciously almost nodded, but once she realized what was being said, panic flashed across her face.","\"N-no, I have no feelings for him.\"","Chen Yi nearly shoved his bowl into his mouth. Not waiting for Xiao Jinghong to press further, he put down his bowl and chopsticks.","\"Madam, is Grandfather planning to have Wan’er marry ’Chen Yu’?\"","Xiao Jinghong paused. Looking at Xiao Wan’er, who had shrunk half her face into the collar of her cloak, she nodded.","\"Grandfather does indeed have that idea.","\"That ’Chen Yu’ is young and promising, with extraordinary talent. He has achieved success in both Martial Arts and the Medical Dao, making him truly a rare find.","\"If you’re interested, Wan’er, I’ll go see him personally later.\"","Xiao Wan’er hurriedly shook her head. \"Jinghong, there’s no need. I-I have no feelings for that Chen Yu, and I w-would never m-marry him...\"","By the end of her sentence, a bitter smile tugged at the corners of her mouth, hidden behind her collar. It was as if she wasn’t talking about \"Chen Yu,\" but rather Chen Yi.","Chen Yi looked at her, then at Xiao Jinghong, whose expression remained normal. Placing both hands on his knees and suppressing the urge to curl his toes in awkwardness, he braced himself and asked, \"Madam, ’Brother Chen Yu’ has extraordinary talent in Martial Arts?\"","\"Yes, Grandfather told me.\"","Out of caution, Xiao Jinghong did not reveal that Chen Yu was actually \"Dragon Tiger\" Liu Wu. After a brief explanation, she asked, \"Chen Yi, I heard you have some personal ties with ’Chen Yu’?\"","Chen Yi forced a calm smile and said, \"As for personal ties... I suppose you could say we are quite close.","\"I have met him a few times and know he has extraordinary achievements in the Medical Dao. It’s just that...\"","\"Just what?\"","\"It’s just that ’Chen Yu’ has his heart set on the Jianghu. I’m afraid it would be very difficult for him to settle down in Shu State.\"","Xiao Jinghong frowned slightly. \"Are you saying he’ll leave and never come back?\"","Chen Yi nodded. \"He came to Shu State to repay Grandfather. In the future, he still has to follow his master’s orders to travel the world and treat the common people.","\"That’s what he told me, so I reckon he won’t stay in Shu State forever.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Jinghong’s brow relaxed. \"Such a person is indeed unsuitable,\" she said thoughtfully.","Because of the Wu Mountain Mutual Market and the Dingyuan Army, Xiao Jinghong naturally knew what it felt like to be separated from Chen Yi more often than they were together.","If \"Chen Yu\" turned out to be like her in the future, wouldn’t Wan’er be left alone in an empty house all the time? After all, Xiao Wan’er’s body was completely unsuited for long journeys.","Xiao Wan’er breathed a sigh of relief. \"Jinghong, you are already busy enough with your own affairs. You really shouldn’t worry about mine.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded, shooting her a reassuring glance. \"Wan’er is right... In my opinion, we should wait until Madam has met him before discussing this further.\"","He thought, \"Meet him? If you actually manage to meet ’Chen Yu,’ I’ll eat my hat!\""]},{"number":513,"title":"Chapter 513 - 303: Silence Speaks Louder Than Words","paragraphs":["Chen Yi had likely forgotten that, according to the laws of the Great Wei Dynasty, as a live-in son-in-law of the Xiao Family, he should have changed his surname to \"Xiao.\" However, the Xiao Family hadn’t enforced this out of respect for the reputation of the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family.","Xiao Jinghong naturally didn’t know the reason behind this. She made up her mind to ask \"Chen Yu\" about it in detail once they met. She certainly didn’t want Xiao Wan’er to repeat the same mistakes she and Chen Yi had made. If \"Chen Yu\" truly intended to roam the world in the future and rarely return home, she would never agree to this marriage, no matter what.","Once the topic of \"Chen Yu\" was brushed aside, the atmosphere in the room softened. Xiao Wan’er raised her head; though her expression remained slightly unnatural, she could now look Xiao Jinghong in the eye.","Chen Yi breathed a sigh of relief and lightened the mood with some witty banter, recounting amusing rumors he had heard.","Xiao Jinghong mostly spoke about the Wu Mountain Mutual Market, detailing matters such as recruiting laborers and resolving issues with timber and stone supplies. She explained everything thoroughly and in great detail.","Initially, Xiao Wan’er only chimed in with polite agreement, but as she realized the value of the information, she began to memorize it earnestly. In a while, she would also be heading to Tonglin Town to inspect the construction progress of the Medical Dao Academy, and this knowledge might come in handy.","Chen Yi naturally guessed Xiao Jinghong’s intentions and silently marveled at their deep sisterly bond. Xiao Jinghong had clearly taken Xiaodie’s words to heart. While she appeared to be simply recounting her recent tasks, she was actually guiding Xiao Wan’er on potential pitfalls in construction projects.","Crucially, she didn’t bring these points up bluntly or preach; rather, her guidance was subtly woven into the conversation. This was a stark contrast to her usual persona as a cold-faced General, as she meticulously looked after her older sister, Xiao Wan’er.","Just as Chen Yi was about to ask Xiao Jinghong for her thoughts on several rumors circulating in the Prefecture City, she turned her head and asked, \"Husband, a few days ago, did you happen to see two strange people in the Prefecture City?\"","\"Strange people?\" Chen Yi was slightly taken aback.","\"An older man and a young man. The elder had snow-white hair but a youthful complexion, while the younger one was breathtakingly handsome, almost otherworldly.\"","Chen Yi immediately realized she was talking about Immortal Bai and Shui Hetong. Meeting her gaze, he pretended to ponder for a moment before shaking his head, then nodding.","\"I did see two strange people. A few days ago, when I was heading to the Jishi Medicine Hall, I spotted them in the East Market.","\"But they weren’t an old man and a young man. They were two people who looked exactly alike, and their appearances... were indeed otherworldly handsome.","\"They, um...\"","He hesitated for a half-beat before changing the subject. \"Madam, do you know those two?\"","Shui Hetong was one thing, but Immortal Bai had seen through his identity and his hidden Cultivation. Xiao Jinghong’s question made him suspect that Immortal Bai and Shui Hetong had gone to the Wu Mountain Mutual Market after leaving the Prefecture City. However, judging from Xiao Jinghong’s demeanor just now, Immortal Bai probably hadn’t revealed his identity to anyone.","It made sense when he thought about it. Immortal Bai had been living in seclusion for thirty years; it was unlikely that he had a close relationship with Xiao Jinghong.","But just as Chen Yi was counting his lucky stars, Xiao Jinghong said, \"That elderly man is my martial uncle, and the younger one is his disciple.\"","\"Martial... martial uncle? Disciple?\"","\"Then your master is...\"","\"Sword Master Li Wudang.\"","\"Li Wudang...\" Chen Yi had naturally heard of this name. Rumor had it that thirty years ago, before Immortal Bai went into seclusion, he had dueled with the Sword Master and emerged victorious. Yet he had never heard anyone mention that Xiao Jinghong was Sword Master Li Wudang’s disciple. Even more unimaginably, Immortal Bai was actually her martial uncle.","Seeing his surprised expression, the corners of Xiao Jinghong’s mouth curled up. \"Forgive me, Husband. Ever since I returned to the Xiao Family, I have been considered to have completed my apprenticeship.","\"At that time, my master specifically instructed me not to reveal the Swordsmanship he taught me unless absolutely necessary, so as to avoid bringing trouble upon myself.\"","\"I see...\" Chen Yi frowned inwardly. For a moment, he couldn’t be sure whether Immortal Bai had told Xiao Jinghong about his identity or not.","He paused for a few breaths to force himself to calm down, then asked, \"I heard that Immortal Bai is most skilled at Divination? What a pity. My older brother was also there at the time, and since I was in a hurry to take him to a nearby tavern for a meal, I didn’t have time to ask for a reading.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Jinghong seemed to breathe a sigh of relief. \"It’s a good thing you didn’t ask him for a reading.\"","\"Why? Are those rumors in the Jianghu true? Are Immortal Bai’s fortune-readings truly a Life-Ending Talisman?\"","\"Most of them are.\"","Chen Yi continued to press the issue. \"Then after your martial uncle left the Prefecture City, did he go to the Mutual Market to look for you? Did he do a Divination for you?\"","Xiao Jinghong shook her head. \"No. Granny Shan had already warned me beforehand to stay far away when I saw my martial uncle.","\"Therefore, this time, my martial uncle and I merely exchanged greetings. I only heard him mention you, and I asked a few more questions out of curiosity.\"","\"Why would he mention me?\"","\"It must be because of your accomplishments in the Calligraphy Dao. It made him view you in a new light.\"","He’d rather that not be the case. Chen Yi had absolutely no desire to be targeted by an old geezer reputed to be the \"number one Martial Arts expert in the Jianghu.\"","Xiao Wan’er listened to their exchange in utter confusion, but she understood that Chen Yi had caught the attention of a Jianghu expert. She said with a smile, \"Chen Yi’s achievements are extraordinary now. Let alone the Shu State, which of the Noble Families in the Nine State and Three Prefectures of our Great Wei Dynasty wouldn’t treat him as an honored guest?\"","Xiao Jinghong smiled and shook her head. \"Not necessarily.\" Seeing Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er look over, she continued, \"The Jing State Liu Family probably doesn’t favor him much.\"","\"That’s true, haha...\" Chen Yi laughed, but inwardly he breathed a sigh of relief. He could now be certain that Immortal Bai hadn’t revealed too much to Xiao Jinghong, though he had no idea what the old man was thinking.","Was he just waiting to watch a good show? He reckoned that shameless old man probably had exactly that intention.","After breakfast.","Xiao Wan’er made an excuse about being tired and returned to her room to rest. Ultimately, she was still somewhat worried that they would bring up her marriage again."]},{"number":514,"title":"Chapter 514 - 303: Silence Speaks Louder Than Words","paragraphs":["Xiao Jinghong suspected nothing and took her leave.","Chen Yi originally thought she would go out or head straight back to the Wu Mountain Mutual Market. To his surprise, she followed him back to the Spring Lotus Garden. Although he found it strange, he didn’t show it at all.","The two walked shoulder to shoulder in silence, passing through the moon gate set in the white walls beneath black tiles, and strolled down the pear wood corridor.","The warm sunlight dispelled the chill in the wind, stretching their shadows as it bathed them in its glow. The chirping of the birds ceased, and a leaping fish landed with a SPLASH. Rainwater pooled on the flowers and trees dripped down, creating occasional PATTERING sounds. It was as if nature was accompanying the footsteps of Chen Yi, Xiao Jinghong, and Xiaodie.","Feeling she ought to say something, Xiao Jinghong placed one hand behind her back and pointed at the pavilion with the other. \"Husband, why don’t we sit over there?\"","Chen Yi turned his head to glance at her, smiling as he nodded. \"Since Madam commands, I wouldn’t dare refuse.\"","Xiao Jinghong’s footsteps faltered. She discreetly lowered the hand behind her back and quickened her pace, her head slightly bowed.","Observing her expression, Chen Yi thought for a moment and realized his earlier words could be interpreted ambiguously. However, seeing Xiao Jinghong’s reaction, a faint smile couldn’t help but surface on his face. Madam and Husband—their relationship had long been established. Even though Xiao Jinghong was the esteemed Commander-in-Chief of the Dingyuan Army, she still revealed the demeanor of an ordinary young woman in front of him. This was a good thing.","Chen Yi followed her with a smile, waving a hand to signal Xiaodie to prepare some tea and pastries.","Xiaodie quietly walked away, occasionally glancing back to see Chen Yi and Xiao Jinghong take their seats in the pavilion. Her ears twitched, straining to listen. She was clearly curious about what her young miss and the master were going to talk about.","But even as she walked far away, neither of the two spoke. The atmosphere carried a distinct sense of \"silence speaking louder than words.\"","Chen Yi sat casually on the stone bench, looking directly at Xiao Jinghong opposite him.","Xiao Jinghong, however, sat with rigid posture. Her gaze swept past him, lingered on the pond, and then flicked back to him.","After a moment of silence, Xiao Jinghong lowered her eyes slightly. \"Thank you, Husband, for the painting you made of my father and mother.\"","Chen Yi chuckled softly. She had held it in all this time just to say this?","\"As long as Madam likes it.\"","\"Mhm, I do.\" Xiao Jinghong softly agreed, but she enunciated the words \"I do\" with utmost clarity.","\"I followed my master to practice Martial Arts since childhood,\" she said. \"I was gone for over ten years. By the time I returned, my father and mother had already perished deep in the territory of the Barbarian Race.","\"So much time had passed that I couldn’t even clearly remember what they looked like.","\"Fortunately, the portrait you gave me a few days ago allowed me to recover my memories of their voices and faces.\"","Chen Yi’s smile faded, and he fell silent. He had heard about this from Xiao Wan’er. Back then, Xiao Jinghong only returned to the Xiao Family after the news of Xiao Fengchun and Fu Wanqing’s deaths in battle reached them. Following that, she stepped onto the battlefield and became the Commander-in-Chief of the Dingyuan Army. He figured that during those days, she must have been just as grief-stricken as Xiao Wan’er.","But despite his thoughts, Chen Yi couldn’t bring himself to voice words of comfort. He knew very well that the past five years, along with the years she spent in Cultivation under the Sword Master, Li Wudang, had long tempered her mind and spirit to be unyielding. Offering words of comfort now would feel somewhat out of place.","Xiao Jinghong wasn’t seeking his consolation anyway. She continued on her own, \"Over the years, whenever I encountered a problem I couldn’t solve, I would think of my father and wonder how he would handle it.","\"Over time, I became accustomed to carrying myself as the ’Commander-in-Chief,’ whether I was at home or in the Dingyuan Army.\"","She looked at Chen Yi. Her stunning face retained its usual heroic spirit, but a hint of apology inadvertently slipped through.","\"Please forgive me, Husband. I... couldn’t help it.\"","Chen Yi’s expression froze slightly. He met her gaze for a long time before smiling and shaking his head. \"Madam, there’s no need to apologize.","\"Do you remember what I told you during the Old Master’s birthday celebration?\"","Xiao Jinghong nodded. \"You said you had no desire to enter officialdom or join the military. You only wanted to stay in the Marquis’s Mansion and be an idle... husband.\"","\"Exactly. My ambitions aren’t high. I’m satisfied with a tranquil and carefree daily life—just fishing, drinking tea, and playing chess is enough.\"","Seeing that she didn’t quite understand, Chen Yi simply threw his hands up in a shrug. \"If Madam can let me live an Immortal-like life such as this, you are more than welcome to continue being your ’Commander-in-Chief’.\"","Xiao Jinghong was momentarily stunned, but soon a smile blossomed on her face. It was as radiant as the sunshine, like ice melting to usher in the revival of all things.","\"Does my husband truly not mind?\"","\"I don’t mind,\" Chen Yi said with a smile. \"If love between both sides can last for aye, why need they stay together night and day? That was the poem I wrote back then, wasn’t it?\"","Xiao Jinghong hummed in agreement. Her gaze drifted toward the wooden building behind him, a barely perceptible trace of sweetness playing at the corners of her lips.","\"After coming back last night, I saw the poems you rewrote. I really like the... Calligraphy Dao Realm in them.\"","Whether it was \"Thoughts of a Summer Night\", \"Two Thoughts on a Summer Night\", or \"Autumn Letter to My Wife\", she liked them all.","Perhaps feeling that her words were a bit too direct, Xiao Jinghong sped up her speech. \"I also like the other two pieces you wrote, ’Post-rain Reflections’ and ’Song of the Water Melody: Mid-Autumn’.","\"I wonder if you still have the manuscripts? I’d like to take them with me and read them... from time to time.\"","Naturally, Chen Yi wouldn’t refuse. He nodded and instructed Xiaodie, who was approaching with the tea, \"Go to the study and bring the two poems I hung on the wall.\"","Xiaodie set the tea down and hurried back to the wooden building, her curiosity about their conversation growing even stronger.","However, thanks to this interruption, Xiao Jinghong relaxed. She picked up her teacup, took a sip, and asked, \"Husband, I wonder what you think of the situation here at the border in Shu State?\"","Chen Yi also took a sip of his tea, vaguely feeling that this question sounded rather familiar."]},{"number":515,"title":"Chapter 515 - 303: Silence Speaks Louder Than Words","paragraphs":["Recalling for a moment, he suddenly remembered the words Elder Master Xiao had said to Xiao Jinghong during his birthday banquet—build high walls, delay claiming the throne, and amass abundant provisions.","\"The current situation in Shu State... is somewhat chaotic.\"","Xiao Jinghong waited for a moment. Seeing that he had stopped talking, she couldn’t help but ask, \"Is that it?\"","\"That’s it.\"","Chen Yi set down his teacup, looking at her with a half-smile. \"Since it’s so chaotic, it naturally falls to you, Madam, to pacify everything.","\"Otherwise, how could I peacefully remain an idle man?\"","Xiao Jinghong was left speechless. She looked at him for a moment before replying, \"Jinghong will certainly do her utmost.\"","Chen Yi picked up the kettle and poured her a full cup of tea. \"There is no need for you to rush, Madam.","\"These past few days, I read a saying in a book: ’He who commits many injustices is doomed to ruin.’","\"Those harboring evil intentions will face disaster sooner or later.","\"Take that ’Jackal’ who kidnapped Eldest Sister yesterday, for instance. Didn’t he die in the barren wilderness?\"","Xiao Jinghong hummed in agreement, her expression slightly aloof. \"King Landu has long harbored rebellious intentions. I’m certain that before he resolves the matters in Poshisu Country, he will not approach the borders of the Great Wei.\"","Hearing this, realization dawned on Chen Yi. So that was it. Her words had awakened him.","No wonder the White Tiger Guard General dared to contact King Landu. He was certain that King Landu’s target was Poshisu Country. If so, were King Landu’s transactions with Liu Hong and the Ji State Trading Company all in preparation for his rebellion?","Having figured this out, Chen Yi marveled at how many formidable figures there were within the Great Wei Dynasty while cursing the shortsightedness of the Ji State Trading Company. For the sake of some silver, they actually disregarded such crucial intelligence. They probably wouldn’t realize their folly until Cui Qingwu sold the grain back to the various grain stores, causing them massive losses.","\"Madam sees things clearly.\"","Xiao Jinghong gave a slight nod. \"It is the same for the Barbarian Race. Internal strife has already broken out, so they will not lightly start another war.","\"However, the appearance of Asutai, the son of the Left King, in Shu State was indeed beyond my expectations.","\"Was he truly captured by those horse bandits, brought to Shu State, and turned into a barbarian slave?\"","\"Yes, Grandfather told me...\"","They chatted casually for a bit longer until Xiaodie walked over, carrying two paintings. Xiao Jinghong unrolled them and took a look.","A thousand miles to Jiangling, a lone boat passing by, and the ethereal imagery of an Immortal Palace appeared before her eyes.","She couldn’t help but reveal a look of profound amazement. \"Husband’s poetry is truly... unparalleled in this world.\"","There were many in the Great Wei Dynasty who could write poetry, and many who wrote it well. But there were very few who possessed Perfect Calligraphy Dao and could also compose poetry. Combining the two naturally made one exceptionally rare.","\"As long as you like them, Madam...\"","Seeing the two of them talking and laughing, Xiaodie quietly committed their words to memory, planning to pick a few lines to write in the \"Biography of the Second Son-in-Law of the Marquis’s Mansion\". She had even thought of the Chapter title. It would be called \"September Sixteenth: The Son-in-Law Curries the Young Miss’s Favor\".","It was fortunate that Chen Yi didn’t know her thoughts, or else he would have definitely strung her up and beaten her.","How could marital harmony have anything to do with currying favor? It was clearly... clearly... a wife leading and her husband following in perfect harmony.","Unfortunately, warm moments were always fleeting.","Not long after, an Armored Warrior came to report, \"Reporting to the Second Young Miss, the Marquis has asked you to accompany him to the Governor’s Office.\"","Xiao Jinghong waved her hand without turning around. \"Understood.\"","Once the Armored Warrior left, she sighed inwardly and said, \"Forgive me, Husband. Since Grandfather has summoned me, I must take my leave.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"Do as you must, Madam. We still have long days ahead of us.\"","Though he said that, he was laughing much more wildly in his heart. Elder Master Xiao was actually taking Xiao Jinghong along to the Governor’s Office. It seemed he was determined to embarrass Liu Hong this time.","With these thoughts in mind, Chen Yi watched Xiao Jinghong leave. He waited a moment longer before changing into casual clothes.","\"I’m heading to Guiyun Academy and the Medicine Hall. I’ll bring you some tea on my way back,\" he instructed Xiaodie.","\"Take care, Son-in-Law...\"","Chen Yi did indeed walk very slowly, as he was somewhat wary of the acute hearing Xiao Jinghong possessed with her Upper Three Grades Cultivation. He unhurriedly made a trip to the academy, dallying for half an hour before finally arriving at Jishi Medicine Hall. Finding Ma Liangcai, he wrote a few words on the table:","\"Quickly notify Wang Ji. Tell him to recall Zhang Dabao and the others.\"","With the Elder Master mobilizing such a formidable force, the time left for him was running out!"]},{"number":516,"title":"Chapter 516 - 304: Unparalleled Talent!","paragraphs":["Ma Liangcai dared not delay. After seeing the water mark on the table, he nodded heavily and turned to leave Jishi Medicine Hall.","Chen Yi watched him walk away and let out a light breath. He would absolutely never be this cautious unless it was necessary. However, Xiao Jinghong was currently less than five miles away from his location in the East Market. Even if she did not use True Essence, relying solely on her hearing, she could still hear the sounds here. Therefore, Chen Yi had to let Ma Liangcai make the trip on his behalf.","As for confirming whether those people from the grain merchants had bought back that batch of grain from Cui Qingwu... that was simple.","Chen Yi turned his head to listen and heard the clamor and commotion outside the nearby grain merchants. Most people were complaining about the rising grain prices, cursing those reckless horse bandits from Poshisu Country. But there were also a few gleeful laughs.","\"Mr. Lin truly predicts things like a God. After receiving the news yesterday afternoon, he immediately determined that grain prices would skyrocket today.\"","\"You can say that again.\"","\"If he hadn’t notified us in time, all this silver probably would have been pocketed by that Miss Cui.\"","\"Actually, Miss Cui didn’t lose out either. The day before yesterday, she bought our grain for ten taels of silver, yet yesterday she transferred and sold it for fourteen taels of silver. Sigh.\"","\"In just one day, she made four million taels of silver... She earns money much easier than we do.\"","\"Who says otherwise?\"","\"If we had known earlier, we shouldn’t have listened to Mr. Lin a few days ago.\"","\"We can’t entirely blame Mr. Lin. Who could have imagined that King Nalandu and his Peacock King Banner would be so audacious?\"","\"Not only did they send men to intercept and kill passing merchants on the Ancient Tea-Horse Road, but last night, ’Jackal’ Du Cang even kidnapped Eldest Miss Xiao. They are truly courting death!\"","\"If it weren’t for a Steward working under Mr. Lin risking his life to send back the news, why would we have rushed to find Miss Cui?\"","\"Yeah, fourteen taels of silver. Her price gouging is even more ruthless than ours...\"","\"That Miss Cui may be beautiful, but her heart is black...\"","The voices inside the grain store rose and fell. Having caught the general gist of it, Chen Yi set his mind at ease. Four million taels of silver was neither too much nor too little; at most, it made a few grain merchants cough up the silver they had previously earned. As long as the grain prices didn’t fall, they would sooner or later earn the silver back using the grain they had on hand.","However, having laid out such a massive scheme, how could Chen Yi let the grain prices continue to rise?","Through the faint light, he watched the noisy scurrying of the commoners outside the Medicine Hall, his expression growing ever calmer. The scene of Yuan Liu’er selling herself to bury her father that day was still vivid in his mind. Crushed beneath the weight of the general trend, the commoners were like straw dogs; someone had to stand up for them. Now, it was indeed time to put an end to this farce.","At this moment, Yuan Liu’er blocked the light.","Compared to her emaciated and filthy state a few days ago, she had now changed into the uniform of a Physician apprentice. Wearing blue clothes and black boots, with a white linen belt wrapped around her waist, her thin face was clean and tenderly white, and her large eyes held a hint of gratitude.","Chen Yi snapped out of his reverie. Seeing her clinging to the doorframe and peeking at him, too afraid to enter, he smiled and waved her over. \"Come in and talk.\"","Hearing this, Yuan Liu’er instantly shrank back. A moment later, she finally walked in with her head lowered, stuttering slightly. \"Apprentice... Apprentice Yuan Liu’er greets you, Shopkeeper.\"","Chen Yi looked her up and down, smiling and nodding. \"Sit down and let’s talk.\"","\"Yes.\"","Yuan Liu’er carefully sat in the seat farthest away from him, her body occupying only a corner of the chair. Her head was lowered, and she occasionally lifted her eyes to peek at him, only to hurriedly lower her head again before meeting his gaze. Looking at her like this, it was hard to imagine that she had such a resolute side when selling herself to bury her father.","Chen Yi sighed inwardly. His smile faded slightly as he asked in a gentle voice, \"Are you getting used to staying at the Medicine Hall?\"","Yuan Liu’er quickly glanced at him and replied in a low voice, \"I-I’m used to it.\"","\"That’s good. From now on, just peacefully follow Ma Liangcai to learn Medical Skills. If there’s anything you don’t understand, feel free to ask him. If he doesn’t teach you, I’ll teach him a lesson for you.\"","\"N-no, he hasn’t refused to teach me. Shopkeeper, Master treats me very well. P-please don’t punish him...\"","Chen Yi couldn’t help but laugh. Seeing her acting like a startled bird, he waved his hand and said, \"I figure he wouldn’t dare anyway.\" Pausing for a moment, he changed the subject and asked, \"What has your master taught you these past few days?\"","Previously, he had told Ma Liangcai to take Yuan Liu’er as an apprentice, claiming she was a genius in the Medical Dao. Thinking about it carefully, he ultimately needed to test her.","Yuan Liu’er glanced at him again and said submissively, \"Master had me memorize the Pharmacopoeia, and also told me to commit the Yin Yang Five Elements Theory to memory. B-but I’m too stupid. Master had to teach me word by word.\"","\"Which page are you on?\"","\"Today, I barely... barely finished reading them.\"","Chen Yi gave a slight nod and continued asking, \"How much do you remember?\"","\"Remember...\" Yuan Liu’er looked slightly bewildered. Gathering her courage, she raised her head to look at him. \"I remembered all of it.\"","Her expression seemed to say, \"I can’t forget it after reading it. What do you mean by ’remember’?\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. \"All of it?\"","Perhaps worried that he would punish Ma Liangcai, Yuan Liu’er hurriedly said, \"Shopkeeper, I-I’m not lying to you. I really remembered all of it. If you don’t believe me, y-you can test me!\"","Feeling slightly odd, Chen Yi didn’t decline and asked directly, \"Heaven and earth have the Yin Yang Five Elements, and so does the human body. What is the Five Elements cycle within the human body?\"","\"The heart is fire, the kidneys are water, the liver is... Yin and Yang are also divided into deficiency and excess...\"","\"Astragalus?\"","\"Astragalus is sweet in taste and slightly warm in nature. It belongs to the spleen and lung meridians, and can replenish Qi, elevate Yang, consolidate the exterior, and stop sweating...\"","Chen Yi asked a few more questions, covering the contents of various pages from the Pharmacopoeia and the Yin Yang Five Elements Theory. Yuan Liu’er answered fluently. Even for some Profound Mysteries regarding the entry-level Medical Dao that were not in the books, she managed to offer some shallow insights."]},{"number":517,"title":"Chapter 517 - 304: Unparalleled Talent!","paragraphs":["Chen Yi looked at the still-ignorant Yuan Liu’er and couldn’t help but ask, \"Have you ever studied?\"","Yuan Liu’er shook her head, her expression dimming. \"Private schools are too expensive. My father wouldn’t allow it. I... I only memorized some words and sentences when my younger brother was reading.\"","Saying this, she raised her head again, her small face tense. \"Shopkeeper, Master is really good to me.\"","\"Teaching you how to read is considered treating you well?\"","\"Is... is it not?\"","Chen Yi smiled and shook his head. \"What a waste of natural talent.\"","He truly hadn’t expected that a momentary bout of compassion would actually result in picking up someone with unparalleled aptitude for the Medical Dao.","No, not just the Medical Dao.","With her photographic memory, Yuan Liu’er also had an extremely high talent for studying and pursuing academics.","As for everything else...","Chen Yi thought for a moment, then called Liu Quan over and ordered, \"Go fetch the brush, ink, paper, and inkstone.\"","Without overthinking, Liu Quan hurriedly placed the items on the table. He thoughtfully spread out the paper and secured it with a paperweight.","Just as he was about to stay and see what was happening, Chen Yi waved his hand. \"Wait outside.\"","Liu Quan shot a glance at Yuan Liu’er and awkwardly backed out of the room.","Chen Yi then beckoned to Yuan Liu’er, \"Write a few words for me to see.\"","Yuan Liu’er paused, shaking her head repeatedly. \"Shopkeeper, Master hasn’t... hasn’t taught me how to write yet. I...\"","Chen Yi interrupted her with a smile, \"It’s fine. I’ll teach you. Watch me.\"","He then picked up the brush and wrote a few characters on the paper: \"Medicine, Canon, Yellow, Astragalus.\"","\"Come, you try.\"","Yuan Liu’er looked at the wolf hair brush he handed her. She accepted it hesitantly, recalled his earlier posture, and lifted the brush.","First, she adjusted her grip on the wolf hair brush. Then, she dipped it in the ink, raised the brush, and lowered it onto the paper.","A blob of ink immediately spread across the page.","Yuan Liu’er’s face paled. She turned her head, about to apologize, when she heard Chen Yi encourage her, \"Continue.","\"This time, focus on using your wrist more. Press down firmly when you start, and lift gently at the end...\"","Hearing this, Yuan Liu’er tensed her small face. Gripping the wolf hair brush with great discomfort, she wrote the character for \"Medicine.\"","Although the character was still terribly written—with scattered force and unpracticed brush control—Chen Yi noticed something.","This little girl had actually memorized his movements and was mimicking them quite decently.","As Chen Yi watched, a brilliant light flashed through his eyes, and he used his Qi Observation Skill to examine her body.","\"Hiss!\"","Even though Chen Yi had previously used his Qi Observation Skill to inspect the internal conditions of many people, and had seen quite a few rare meridians and auras—such as Xiao Wan’er’s extremely cold Physique or the Old Master’s heavily ill body—upon seeing Yuan Liu’er’s aura, he still couldn’t help but reveal a hint of awe.","\"Truly an unparalleled, heaven-sent talent.\"","He saw that the Twelve Main Meridians within Yuan Liu’er’s body were completely unobstructed. She actually possessed an Innate Clear Physique. In other words, if she were to practice Martial Arts, she could shoot straight into the Middle Three Grades in an extremely short amount of time.","However, to achieve greatness in both Martial Arts and the Medical Dao, one needed comprehension; one had to enter the Dao.","Chen Yi took a few more glances and muttered \"what a waste of natural talent\" to himself once again.","Leaving a genius like this in Ma Liangcai’s hands was a complete waste of her potential. Especially after seeing the visible increase in proficiency once Yuan Liu’er finished writing a few characters, it truly made him feel a sense of, \"If Liu’er was born, why must Yi be born as well?\"","If he didn’t have his own Opportunity and excellent comprehension, his lifelong achievements probably wouldn’t even amount to a fraction of Yuan Liu’er’s.","Pondering for a moment, Chen Yi made a decision.","It was too late to have Yuan Liu’er switch masters now. There was only one viable solution—he would take Ma Liangcai in as his disciple! Only then would he be able to openly and properly teach Yuan Liu’er.","However...","That dull-witted fool Ma Liangcai was truly unworthy of his attention. If he became his first founding disciple, wouldn’t people question his judgment when word got out?","Fortunately, there was still Yuan Liu’er. Thank goodness there was still Yuan Liu’er.","Chen Yi consoled himself. His gaze toward Yuan Liu’er grew increasingly amiable as he smiled and said, \"Not bad.","\"Your master has indeed taught you quite a bit.\"","Yuan Liu’er’s face relaxed, and much of the anxiety in her heart faded. She had truly felt that the characters she just wrote were too terrible, and she had worried it would implicate Ma Liangcai.","\"Shopkeeper, if... if you have no other matters, I... Liu’er will go busy herself in the outer hall first.\"","Chen Yi hummed in acknowledgment. Before she could turn around, he spoke up, \"Don’t call me Shopkeeper in the future.","\"Call me Grandmaster.\"","\"Grandmaster?\"","Meeting Yuan Liu’er’s confused gaze, Chen Yi smiled and said, \"That’s right.","\"Your master, Ma Liangcai, is my first founding disciple. As his apprentice, you naturally have to call me Grandmaster.\"","Yuan Liu’er blankly thought about it for a moment, then hurriedly bowed in greeting. \"Grandmaster.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"Go get busy.","\"When your master returns, tell him to come find me immediately.\"","Yuan Liu’er let out an \"oh\" and meekly walked out of the inner hall.","Who would have thought that a moment later, she would return. \"Grand... Grandmaster. Thank you for letting Master take me in as a disciple.","\"I... I know it was also you who provided the silver to bury my father. Please... accept a bow from this disciple!\"","Chen Yi looked at Yuan Liu’er kneeling on the ground. The smile on his face receded for a moment, and he let out a soft sigh. \"Actually, I should be thanking you.\"","\"Wh-what?\"","\"It’s nothing. You’ll know in the future. Go out and get to work for now.\"","Yuan Liu’er looked at his expression, bowed once more, and then got up and walked out of the inner hall, looking much more relaxed.","Watching her back disappear out the door, a bitter smile tugged at the corners of Chen Yi’s lips.","\"Every drink and every peck is preordained by heaven.","\"So be it.","\"Since I’ve entangled myself in this karma, I won’t think about running away from it. Whatever happens in the future, it’ll be up to her to decide for herself.\"","Even though Yuan Liu’er’s father hadn’t died by his hands, his death was still connected to him to some extent. When Yuan Liu’er completed her studies in the future, he would eventually reveal the whole truth to her."]},{"number":518,"title":"Chapter 518 - 304: Peerless Talent!","paragraphs":["By then, whether Yuan Liu’er blamed him or not would no longer matter.","\"In this world, many things do not go as one wishes. Seeking peace of mind is enough.\"","Not long after, Ma Liangcai returned, looking as usual. Upon receiving Yuan Liu’er’s message, he hurried to the inner hall. Just as he was about to bow in greeting, he heard Chen Yi say in a stern tone, \"Kneel!\"","Ma Liangcai froze. Seeing his expression, he quickly fell to his knees. \"S-Shopkeeper, you...\"","\"What, even now, are you unwilling to call me Master?\"","\"M-Master?\" Ma Liangcai looked at him in astonishment. Upon seeing a somewhat helpless smile appear on Chen Yi’s face, he finally realized what was happening and loudly cried out, \"Master above, please accept your disciple’s bow!\"","Chen Yi frowned. \"Keep your voice down. Are you afraid the people outside won’t hear you?\"","\"Shopkeeper—no, Master, your disciple knows his mistake, hehe...\"","\"Hmph, wipe that damn grin off your face. Letting you be my founding disciple is already a huge bargain for you.\"","\"Yes, yes... Master is right...\"","Spotting Yuan Liu’er looking their way from outside, Chen Yi waved his hand, signaling Ma Liangcai to rise. Then, he used water to write a few lines on the table: \"Go to the house next to the Locust Tree in Lin Village on the East City Outskirts and find Liu Lang. Tell him that grain distribution begins tomorrow.\"","Suppressing his excitement, Ma Liangcai memorized every word without missing a single detail, then knelt on the ground to bow again.","\"Get out of here. Teach Liu’er well from now on, and remember to pass down everything you have learned to her.\"","\"Yes, Master!\"","\"Get out.\"","\"Yes, Master...\"","Ma Liangcai did not feel the slightest bit offended. On the contrary, his face was brimming with joy. He had been by Chen Yi’s side for a considerable amount of time, so he naturally knew of his capabilities and identity. Setting aside his Medical Dao, the title of \"Mr. Qingzhou\" and his Perfection Realm Calligraphy Dao alone were enough to make Ma Liangcai bow his head in reverence.","Now that he had become the disciple of such a prominent figure, his future...","Thinking of this, Ma Liangcai patted Yuan Liu’er and said sneakily, \"Hehe, my good disciple, we’ve struck it rich.\"","\"Huh?\"","\"Just keep it to yourself and don’t spread it around. Your master is now the Shopkeeper’s disciple.\"","Yuan Liu’er let out an sound of understanding. \"Grand-master already told me just now.\"","\"Grand-master?\" Ma Liangcai stared at her blankly for a moment before it suddenly dawned on him—he had likely stumbled into this colossal stroke of luck entirely because of Yuan Liu’er.","\"My dear disciple... if your master is ever in trouble in the future, you can’t just ignore me...\"","Yuan Liu’er took his words seriously and said with a stern expression, \"Master, a teacher for a day is a father for a lifetime.","\"If you are ever in trouble, your disciple will definitely save you.\"","\"What I’m afraid of is that the person causing me trouble will be...\"","...your grand-master.","Recalling Chen Yi’s earth-shattering capabilities, Ma Liangcai shivered involuntarily. After leaving Yuan Liu’er with a few more instructions, he hastily headed out of the city, clearly not wanting to experience Chen Yi’s methods firsthand.","Once he left, Chen Yi also walked out of the inner hall. He smiled and greeted the people around him before unhurriedly making his way back to the Xiao Family. Having notified Wang Ji and Liu Lang, and having learned that the grain merchants had bought back the grain from Cui Qingwu, he could finally relax for a few days. The rest would be up to the will of heaven.","By sheer coincidence, just as Chen Yi reached the corner of South Street, he saw Elder Master Xiao and Xiao Jinghong walking out of the Governor’s Office. Behind them, Liu Hong was seeing them off with his usual smile.","\"Marquis Xiao, General Jinghong, take care. I have official duties to attend to, so forgive me for not seeing you further.\"","\"Please stay, Lord Liu.\" Elder Master Xiao turned his head and replied indifferently before stepping into the carriage first.","Xiao Jinghong gave a slight nod. Just as she was about to follow, she caught sight of Chen Yi not far away. Excusing herself to the elder master, she walked over.","\"Husband, let’s head back together.\"","\"Alright. I just took a trip to the Jishi Medicine Hall...\"","\"I know. Husband even took in a disciple.\"","Chen Yi paused, then said with a smile, \"Actually, I took in a grand-disciple. That Ma Liangcai’s Medical Skill is decent, but his Calligraphy Dao talent is too poor.\"","\"That Yuan Liu’er?\"","\"Yes, her aptitude is quite good...\"","Sure enough, Xiao Jinghong had been keeping an eye on him all along. However, since Xiao Jinghong was not at the Medicine Hall, she did not know the exact extent of Yuan Liu’er’s aptitude. She simply assumed that Chen Yi was moved by his love for talent. Besides, in her mind, it was a good thing that Chen Yi could take in a disciple. The deeper her husband’s bonds with Shu State became, the less likely it was that an incident like \"fleeing from the wedding\" would happen again in the future.","After testing the waters with a few more sentences, Chen Yi set his mind at ease. Just as he was about to ask about her and the elder master’s visit to the Governor’s Office, a flash of golden light crossed his vision:","[Opportunity: +22.]","[At four quarters past Noon, Duke Dingyuan Xiao Yuan...]"]},{"number":519,"title":"Chapter 519 - 305: Palace Murder!","paragraphs":["[At exactly noon, Duke Dingyuan Xiao Yuan, accompanied by Xiao Jinghong, Commander-in-Chief of the Dingyuan Army, visited the Governor’s Office to suggest that Liu Hong stabilize the grain prices in Shu State. They had a very pleasant conversation.]","[Target not present, sound unheard, scene unseen. Failing to claim a heaven-sent Opportunity marks one as a naturally indolent person.]","*A very pleasant conversation?*","Chen Yi glanced at the golden words on the light screen and chuckled inwardly. It was truly hard for him to imagine a scene where Elder Master Xiao and Xiao Jinghong sat with Liu Hong, conversing pleasantly as host and guests. It wouldn’t be an exaggeration to describe it as coercion and intimidation.","However, recalling how Liu Hong had just seen them off with a smiling face, Chen Yi couldn’t help but mutter, \"The old fox is such a good actor. Maybe they really did have a ’very pleasant conversation.’\"","Liu Hong was a man of profound shrewdness, the absolute epitome of someone whose outer appearance belied his true thoughts. His ability to steer with the wind was likely just as formidable. Had Elder Master Xiao not brought Xiao Jinghong along this time, Liu Hong probably would have found a way to brush him off. Now, even if he were unwilling, he had no choice but to take some action to stabilize the grain prices in Shu State Prefecture City.","This actually worked out perfectly.","Beside him, oblivious to his thoughts, Xiao Jinghong chatted casually with him. Yet, the two got along harmoniously. Even the physical distance between them gradually narrowed as they wove through the passing pedestrians. Chen Yi noticed this and turned to glance at her. Seeing that her eyes beneath her half-armor were as calm as water, he didn’t pay it much mind.","\"Madam, did you and the Elder Master go to the Governor’s Office today for the grain prices?\"","Xiao Jinghong tilted her head slightly. \"Husband, how did you know?\"","Chen Yi smiled. \"I guessed. Ever since rumors began swirling in Shu State City a few days ago, the price of grain has surged. By today, it has multiplied by more than ten times. If this continues, the city’s commoners won’t be able to afford food. Given the kind-heartedness of the Elder Master and yourself, it’s only natural that you wouldn’t stand idly by.\"","Xiao Jinghong hummed in agreement. \"Grandpa indeed doesn’t want a repeat of what happened five years ago.\"","\"Did Governor Liu agree?\"","\"He agreed.\"","\"That’s good. Now I can give my grand-disciple a proper explanation.\"","\"An explanation?\"","Meeting Xiao Jinghong’s puzzled gaze, Chen Yi recounted the story of Yuan Liu’er selling herself to bury her father. \"If not for the drastic increase in the prices of food and medicine in the city, she wouldn’t have been reduced to such dire straits.\"","Xiao Jinghong’s eyes flickered slightly. She turned her head to look ahead and said in an inscrutable tone, \"Yuan... Liu’er is a pitiful girl.\" After a pause, she shifted the topic. \"Husband, do you think Grandpa should have gone to the Governor’s Office earlier?\"","\"You’re overthinking it, Madam,\" Chen Yi replied. \"Despite being gravely ill, the Elder Master still cares for the people of Shu State. It is truly admirable. How could I ever speak ill of him?\"","\"It’s good that you think so. Now...\"","Seeing her hesitate to speak, Chen Yi roughly guessed what she wanted to say and quickly changed the subject. \"Now that I’m getting more used to Shu State, I really don’t want to see this place turned into a chaotic mess. Just like yesterday, when that ’Jackal’ suddenly showed up and kidnapped Eldest Sister. It was very worrying.\"","Xiao Jinghong paused upon hearing this. \"Does my husband think the Guards in the Marquis’s Mansion... have too low of a Cultivation?\"","\"Did I... imply that?\"","\"You did. But you need not worry, Husband. Later, Jinghong will arrange for several experts with profound Cultivation to come and guard the Marquis’s Mansion.\"","Chen Yi secretly rolled his eyes. He had only mentioned it casually and never actually wanted experts guarding the Marquis’s Mansion. Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang alone made it hard enough for him to sneak out. If a few more of the experts Xiao Jinghong spoke of arrived, it would be almost impossible for him to go out after nightfall in the future.","However, thoughts were just thoughts. Chen Yi could only play along and say, \"Whatever you arrange, Madam...\"","He had no choice; the situation was out of his control. With his puny arms and legs, he was simply no match for Xiao Jinghong.","Before long, the two of them returned to the Xiao Mansion.","However, Xiao Jinghong did not step over the threshold with him. Meeting Chen Yi’s slightly puzzled gaze, she bowed slightly. \"Please forgive me, Husband. Jinghong must take her leave now.\"","Chen Yi was taken aback and looked up at the sky. \"It’s not past noon yet. Won’t you stay for lunch before leaving?\"","Xiao Jinghong shook her head slightly. \"The Mutual Market is nearing completion, and Jinghong needs to guard it for a few more days. Moreover, the New Army in the Three Towns has been training for quite some time, and it is time to test their strength... Please forgive me, Husband.\"","Chen Yi smiled and waved his hand. \"Since you have urgent matters to attend to, Madam, go on and busy yourself.\"","A trace of apology flashed through Xiao Jinghong’s eyes. \"Jinghong has already spoken to Grandpa in advance. I shall only escort my husband this far.\"","\"Alright...\"","After the deep Autumn Rain, the sunlight grew brighter, yet a lingering chill remained in the air. But on Xiao Jinghong, it cast a radiant glow that highlighted her sharp, commanding aura. Chen Yi watched her soar away until she disappeared into the southern horizon before he turned back and entered the Marquis’s Mansion.","Having a wife with such supreme martial prowess who could come and go like the wind, he was largely pleased. At the very least, whenever he wanted to slack off, Shu State had this formidable presence—a towering mountain in her own right—capable of suppressing all manner of scoundrels.","\"How cozy...\"","Chen Yi couldn’t have been anything but cozy even if he tried.","According to his guess, Xiao Jinghong would quietly return from the Wu Mountain Mutual Market in half a day at most. Her target would undoubtedly be the evidence of the crimes committed by Liu Hong and the others. As such, even if he wanted to go out and do something, he had to consider the risk of his tracks being discovered by her.","Fortunately, everything he needed to do had already been done. For the rest, he only needed to wait quietly.","That same afternoon, news that Elder Master Xiao and Xiao Jinghong had joined forces to pressure the Governor’s Office quickly spread.","Although Liu Hong had not yet taken any action to stabilize the grain prices, the commoners of Shu State City felt a glimmer of hope. Consequently, the number of people rushing to the East and West Markets to buy grain decreased significantly.","This situation was naturally not what the various grain merchants wanted to see. They had just bought back grain from Cui Qingwu yesterday at the exorbitant price of fourteen taels of silver per picul of fine grain, bringing their total cost close to fourteen million taels of silver."]},{"number":520,"title":"Chapter 520 - 305: Palace Assassination!","paragraphs":["If the Governor’s Office were allowed to open the granaries and stabilize grain prices, forget about recovering their capital—nearly a million piculs of grain would be left rotting in their hands.","Therefore, upon receiving the news, Lin Zhenghong and the others—at the suggestion of the Ji State Trading Company’s Wind Patrol Envoy, Li Sanyuan—rushed frantically to the Governor’s Office.","After learning from Liu Hong that they had three days at most, Lin Zhenghong and his peers, no matter how reluctant they were, could only scurry back to their grain shops to figure out another countermeasure.","\"Three days. Even if we lower our prices, there’s no way we can sell off all the grain,\" a pot-bellied merchant in brocade garments wailed as if he were at a funeral. \"Furthermore, now that the word from the Government Office has spread, most of the city’s commoners are planning to just tough it out. We... we’re going to suffer a massive loss this time.\"","Lin Zhenghong’s expression was even uglier.","Originally, their schemes in Shu State had gone smoothly, and every single one of them had raked in massive profits.","But now, with the price suppressed at fourteen taels of silver per picul, all their money had been converted into grain.","If the grain price fell back to one tael of silver—no, even if it dropped by just ten percent—their collective losses would exceed a million taels of silver.","Under these circumstances... under these circumstances...","Lin Zhenghong’s eyes turned bloodshot. He stood up abruptly and stormed off in a rage.","\"Mr. Lin, where are you going?\"","\"I’m going to find the main culprit!\"","The person Lin Zhenghong was looking for was none other than Li Sanyuan.","So what if he was the Wind Patrol Envoy of the Ji State Trading Company? So what if he had overseen several highly profitable transactions? At this moment, it was all a joke in his eyes.","Later, at the Lin Mansion.","Lin Zhenghong marched straight into the backyard, shoved open the wooden door of the guest room where Li Sanyuan was resting, and roared, \"You’ve completely ruined me!\"","Li Sanyuan froze slightly, his expression instantly turning ugly. \"Lord Liu didn’t agree to our request?\"","\"Agree?","\"Old Marquis Xiao and General Jinghong went there together today! No matter how reluctant Liu Hong might be, he wouldn’t dare protect us from losses at a time like this.\"","\"Then what did he say?\"","\"Lord Liu gave us a final three days!","\"After three days, either the grain shops voluntarily lower their prices, or the Government Office will open the granaries to stabilize the market!\" Lin Zhenghong fumed. \"Are you satisfied now?!\"","Li Sanyuan’s expression shifted. Ignoring the man’s attitude, he furrowed his brows and pondered a countermeasure.","But no matter how hard he thought, he couldn’t come up with a better plan.","The crux of the issue lay in one thing: the cost of the grain was too high!","If no one else took this batch of grain off their hands, not only would they suffer heavy losses, but they would also be punished by the Trading Company.","That kind of outcome...","Li Sanyuan shuddered, a trace of fear flashing across his face. \"Don’t panic. Don’t be hasty. We still have three days left.","\"I... you and I will definitely think of a way.\"","\"A way?\" Lin Zhenghong laughed out of extreme anger. \"What kind of way can you possibly think of?","\"Now that the news has spread, the commoners are all waiting for the grain prices to drop. Who would be stupid enough to buy grain at a time like this?\"","\"Buy?\" A flash of inspiration struck Li Sanyuan. \"Someone will buy it!\"","Lin Zhenghong’s angry expression faltered. \"Who?\"","\"Just because there’s no one in Shu State doesn’t mean there’s no one on the outside.\" Li Sanyuan looked toward the west, a faint smile actually surfacing on his face. \"The men under the Peacock King Banner are currently launching a massive invasion.","\"Based on what I know about them, that cavalry of rebel forces must be traveling light, bringing very little rations and fodder.","\"If we can sell the grain to them, not only will we recover all our losses, but we might also make a huge... well, a small profit.\"","Hearing this, Lin Zhenghong’s anger dissipated considerably. \"Would King Nalandu agree to this price?\"","Li Sanyuan chuckled. \"He’ll have to agree, whether he wants to or not.","\"Actually, before your father died, he secretly contacted King Landu to sell them a batch of Weapons, Armor, and Refined Iron.","\"That’s a transaction worth hundreds of thousands of taels of Gold.","\"As long as we bundle that batch of ironware with this grain, he’ll have no choice but to agree.\"","Hearing this, Lin Zhenghong pondered for a moment. \"Will this work?\"","\"Of course! Besides the Trading Company, who else in the entire Great Wei Dynasty would dare to sell ironware and blocks of Refined Iron to them?\"","\"Then... what should I do?\"","\"You? You can’t. Since this mistake was caused by me, how can I let you take the risk?\" Li Sanyuan revealed a cold sneer. \"Besides, since Liu Hong has shown no respect for the Trading Company, there’s naturally no need for us to be polite to him either.\"","Lin Zhenghong was taken aback. \"You... you want to do something to Liu Hong...\"","\"Watch your words!","\"No matter how foolish I am, I’d never be stupid enough to make a move against Liu Hong!\"","\"Then...\"","\"Do you remember who your father saw in the mansion on the night he died?\"","\"You... you mean... Liu Taofang?\"","\"Exactly.","\"Later, take a trip to the Liu Family. Seek out Liu Taofang to negotiate, and make sure you get your hands on the grain he has.","\"The price will be the same as what Miss Cui got—fourteen taels.\" A flash of ruthlessness crossed Li Sanyuan’s face. \"Since Liu Hong is being heartless, he can’t blame us for being unjust!","\"No matter what, the grain sold to King Landu this time must include a portion from the Liu Family!\"","Lin Zhenghong opened his mouth, but upon seeing the look in Li Sanyuan’s eyes, he didn’t dare say anything more and nodded in agreement.","He had already been forced to the edge of a cliff. Since he was doomed either way, he might as well gamble alongside Li Sanyuan.","Especially after the two parted ways and Lin Zhenghong heard another rumor circulating outside, he became even more determined to drag Liu Hong down with him.","The news was none other than this: at Lin Village in the East City Outskirts, someone was selling grain for the price of one tael of silver per picul.","As the news spread, the commoners of the entire Prefecture City scrambled out the East City Gate, rushing toward Lin Village.","Under such circumstances, no matter how weak-willed Lin Zhenghong was, it was impossible for him not to harden his heart.","He went straight to the Liu Family. Taking advantage of the time while Liu Hong was still at the Government Office, he sought out Liu Taofang, who had been confined for many days.","Li Sanyuan also swung into action."]},{"number":521,"title":"Chapter 521 - 305: Palace Massacre!","paragraphs":["Almost immediately after receiving news that someone was forcibly slashing prices, he couldn’t wait to head out through the West City Gate, rushing all the way along the official road straight toward the Ancient Tea-Horse Road.","He was not stupid. On the contrary, he was very smart; otherwise, he wouldn’t have been able to climb to the position of Wind Patrol Envoy in the Ji State Trading Company’s Pingzheng Hall.","Obviously—they had been set up this time. Although he still didn’t know who was orchestrating all this behind the scenes, there was absolutely no way he would just let it go.","\"After this, I will definitely send a message to the Trading Company to dispatch experts to thoroughly investigate this matter. Even if I have to dig three feet into the ground, I will find that bastard!\"","...","Meanwhile, on the other side.","In Lin Village.","Liu Lang, who was in disguise, was up to his neck in work. He was just short of dragging Boss Chen over to give him a piece of his mind.","Although he had been busy from start to finish this time—purchasing grain, Transferring grain, and taking charge of guarding it—the whole process had gone fairly smoothly.","But when it came to this final selling step, he truly couldn’t understand Boss Chen’s intentions.","\"We bought this grain for eight, nine, and ten taels, and now... now we’re selling it all for one tael of silver?","\"Did the boss get kicked in the head by a donkey, or does he just have money burning a hole in his pocket?\" he muttered.","Even though Liu Lang wasn’t good at arithmetic, he knew this would result in a massive loss.","One had to know that the grain in his hands had cost nearly five hundred thousand taels of silver for about one hundred thousand piculs.","If they were all sold at the price of one tael per picul, they would lose at least four hundred thousand taels.","Throwing that much shining white silver into the water would at least make a splash, but with Boss Chen, it didn’t even make a sound.","However, regardless of what Liu Lang thought, he didn’t dare not follow orders.","In the past, he could still hold his head high in front of Chen Yi by relying on his identity as the \"Sword Madman,\" his Cultivation, and his Technique Realm.","But ever since the duel that night, he was completely subdued.","Chen Yi wasn’t just far superior to him in intelligence; he was also vastly superior in martial prowess.","Even if he had the mind to disobey orders, he had to weigh whether he could withstand that spear strike.","\"Motherfucker, it’s not my silver that’s being lost anyway, so what the hell am I afraid of!\"","Steeling his resolve, Liu Lang naturally became more and more efficient at his task.","With the help of Xue Duanyun and the others, it only took them half a day to sell fifty thousand piculs.","Broken silver and copper coins piled up in several bamboo baskets.","Even so, there were still quite a few people rushing over from the Prefecture City. Upon hearing that there was no more grain today, they immediately caused a ruckus.","It wasn’t until Liu Lang raised his voice and announced that there would be another fifty thousand piculs tomorrow that they quieted down.","The sky had just darkened.","Liu Lang and the others closed the gates of the compound. Looking at the silver and copper coins in front of them, none of them showed any joy on their faces.","\"What do you guys think the boss has up his sleeve?\" one of them asked.","Liu Lang snorted. \"You’re asking me, but who am I supposed to ask?","\"Either way, they can’t blame us for the silver lost this time.\"","Xue Duanyun and the other two exchanged glances and shook their heads as well. \"They can’t blame us either...\"","Four hundred thousand taels of silver! They wouldn’t be able to come up with that much even if they sold their Celestial Sect.","...","After nightfall.","After having dinner, Chen Yi, Xiao Wuge, and Xiaodie sat in the pavilion, reading and playing Go.","It was a leisurely and carefree evening.","Chen Yi had naturally heard a thing or two about what was happening outside the estate. But this was exactly the result he wanted.","He thought, \"The Old Master took this Step neither too early nor too late; it was just right.","\"With him applying pressure, even if Liu Hong had the mind to resist, he wouldn’t be able to delay for too long.","\"But regardless of whether he takes action or not, the news has to be released eventually.","\"This way, Liu Lang can take the opportunity to make his move without it seeming too conspicuous.\"","Grain prices were bound to plummet!","Thinking about this, Chen Yi was in a good mood and played Go with Xiao Wuge with a chuckle.","On the other hand, Xiao Wuge was pouting and sulking. \"Brother-in-law, Second Sister coming back is such a big deal, so why didn’t anyone come to notify me?\"","\"Why would they notify you?\" Chen Yi replied. \"Your second sister came back because she has things to do. How could she stay in the estate all the time? Besides, your most important task right now is Cultivating Martial Arts. You don’t need to worry about anything else.\"","\"You say that, but it’s been a long time since I last saw Second Sister.\"","\"I’ve already seen her on your behalf...\"","Xiao Wuge was left speechless for a moment and casually placed a white piece on a corner of the chessboard.","\"Palace Kill.\"","Chen Yi looked at the board, where the white pieces had formed a dominant position and were faintly surrounding the large dragon of Heizi. Smiling, he placed down a Heizi.","\"You’re too impatient.\"","In an instant, the white pieces’ encirclement was completely dismantled.","With Chen Yi’s Go skills, he had seen this Step coming a long time ago and had already set a trap, waiting for Xiao Wuge to place his piece at this exact moment.","Just like the Ji State Trading Company.","No matter what moves they made, there would only be a dead end waiting for them.","Xiao Wuge’s small face looked as if he wanted to cry but had no tears. He could only stare blankly as Chen Yi unhurriedly picked up the captured white pieces one by one.","\"It doesn’t count, Brother-in-law. This game doesn’t count.\"","\"Why doesn’t it count? A true gentleman never takes back a move once it’s made. Haven’t you heard of that?\"","\"No...\"","Talking and laughing, as 7:00 PM approached, Xiaodie took Xiao Wuge to rest first.","Chen Yi originally planned to wash up as well, but then he heard a burst of footsteps coming from outside the Spring Lotus Garden.","\"Sir, Shopkeeper Wang of Hundred Herbs Hall is here to visit.\"","Chen Yi furrowed his brows slightly. \"Wang Ji? It’s so late... Did something happen over at the Ancient Tea-Horse Road?\"","\"Invite him in.\""]},{"number":522,"title":"Chapter 522 - 306: Ambition, Gift","paragraphs":["Unless absolutely necessary, Wang Ji would never have dared to visit late at night. Not only was it presumptuous, but it would also draw unwanted scrutiny from Elder Master Xiao and the others.","Chen Yi thought it over and concluded that there could only be one reason: something had gone wrong on the Ancient Tea-Horse Road.","In an instant, the chessboard in his mind began to shift. One by one, Heizi were placed on the Ancient Tea-Horse Road.","First, King Landu. Because of the death of the \"Jackal\" Du Cang, that Grandmaster might have sent someone to Shu State to investigate the situation.","Second, the Barbarian Race. Asutai had previously left with the envoy from the Barbarian Race, and they should have already escaped the borders of Shu State by now. Perhaps they had taken a detour via the Ancient Tea-Horse Road and consequently bumped into the retreating Zhang Dabao and his men.","Third, the people dispatched from Shu State. Be it the military, the Government Office, or even the Jianghu, someone would undoubtedly head to the Ancient Tea-Horse Road to confirm the location of the Peacock King Banner.","And the last possibility... was the people from the Ji State Trading Company.","Today, the situation in the Shu State Prefecture City had taken a sudden turn. Various rumors were spreading like wildfire. Outside the Governor’s Office and Lin Village, Liu Lang and others were slashing grain prices, resulting in more than half the commoners preferring to go hungry rather than buy grain from the merchants. The several grain companies and the Ji State Trading Company behind them were bound to be overwhelmed with panic. It made perfect sense for them to send someone to the Ancient Tea-Horse Road.","If they confirmed that the main force of the Peacock King Banner was attacking, those grain companies would likely be willing to take a loss of some silver coins and endure the current hardship. As long as they held onto their grain, they would have a chance to stage a comeback. But how could Chen Yi not have anticipated this? After all, those grain companies were currently just coughing up the silver they had earned over the past few days; they were far from suffering a devastating blow.","It didn’t take long before Wang Ji was led into the Spring Lotus Garden by the Marquis’s Mansion’s Armored Warriors.","\"Mr. Qingzhou, please forgive my intrusion for visiting so late at night.\"","Chen Yi nodded slightly, gesturing for the man to follow as he smiled and replied, \"You are too polite, Shopkeeper Wang.\"","After exchanging a few pleasantries, the two arrived at the study. Without waiting for Chen Yi to prompt him, Wang Ji impatiently took a letter from his robe and placed it on the desk.","\"This is—\"","Before he could finish, Chen Yi took the letter and interrupted, \"Did your boss send you to find me?\"","Wang Ji immediately swallowed his original words and played along. \"Yes, yes, my boss dispatched me to see Mr. Qingzhou...\"","He paused, unable to come up with a good excuse, his face flushing slightly. He had come in such a hurry that he hadn’t prepared a proper reason.","Fortunately, Chen Yi leisurely opened the letter. As he read the contents, he spoke with a slightly questioning tone, \"Has your boss finally figured it out?\"","\"I-I suppose so?\" As for what had been figured out, Wang Ji had no idea. He stammered, unable to speak coherently.","Chen Yi, however, fell silent as he read the words on the paper:","\"A man claiming to be from the Ji State Trading Company came looking for us. His name is Li Sanyuan. He wants to meet King Landu, saying he has a major business deal to discuss with him.","\"I am momentarily at a loss for what to do. Please give me clear instructions, Sir.\"","Li Sanyuan?","That should be the same person who forced Lin Zhenghong to sell grain to Cui Qingwu. And now he was running to King Landu to discuss a major business deal... it must be regarding that batch of grain, right?","Having figured everything out, Chen Yi couldn’t help but chuckle inwardly. \"Sure enough, the people from the Ji State Trading Company have gone looking for them.\"","Truth be told, he liked this kind of smart person. The type who thought they had seen through everything and had everything under control, always staying one step ahead. If there were more of these \"smart\" fools around, why would he ever worry about trouble brewing in Shu State?","Chen Yi looked at the troubled Wang Ji and smiled. \"Your boss wants me to write an inscription for Hundred Herbs Hall? What’s so difficult about that?\"","Wang Ji’s expression relaxed. He agreed repeatedly and flattered, \"My boss was just worried about inconveniencing you, Mr. Qingzhou.\"","Chen Yi put away the letter. \"It merely costs a bit of ink and effort.\"","He then walked over to the desk. While pondering his reply to Zhang Dabao and the others, he spread out a sheet of blank Yunsong Paper and secured it with a paperweight. Knowing his place, Wang Ji stepped forward to pour water and grind the ink. \"Mr. Wang thanks you on behalf of my boss.\"","\"You are treating me like an outsider, Shopkeeper Wang. Compared to the help Hundred Herbs Hall has provided to the Marquis’s Mansion’s Medicine Halls, a piece of Calligraphy is nothing.\"","\"No, no, no, you simply don’t have a clear understanding of the value of your calligraphy. Most of the works you’ve left at Guiyun Academy recently have been collected by the teachers for their exhibition hall, but a few have been bought at high prices.\"","Chen Yi paused. \"How high?\"","\"I heard it’s ’one thousand gold pieces for a single character,’ and for your Cursive Script copybooks, some have even offered up to ’two thousand gold pieces a character.’ It’s a pity that Mr. Yue Ming and the others refuse to sell.\" Wang Ji smacked his lips in regret and continued on the topic. \"Furthermore, your inscription will bring numerous benefits to Hundred Herbs Hall. Take Xinglin Hall, which has recently made quite a name for itself in Shu State, for example. Their signboard was inscribed by a Calligraphy Dao master who had only reached Minor Success, yet it attracts many scholars to observe it every day, bringing a lot of business to Xinglin Hall. If Hundred Herbs Hall could obtain your calligraphy, it would truly be... truly be like being blessed by God.\"","Wang Ji’s words were exaggerated, but they could still be considered sincere. He had been wanting Chen Yi to write an inscription for Hundred Herbs Hall for a long time but had never found a suitable opportunity to bring it up. He hadn’t expected that taking a rash trip to the Marquis’s Mansion today would yield such an unexpected harvest. It was foreseeable that in the future, Hundred Herbs Hall would definitely become like Xinglin Hall—no, the sensation it would cause would inevitably surpass Xinglin Hall.","Chen Yi smiled and didn’t say anything more. He picked up his brush, dipped it in ink, and wrote three large characters on the paper: Hundred Herbs Hall.","His strokes were bold and sweeping, flowing with unconstrained elegance.","When the characters were completed, a blinding flash of Jin Guang dazzled the eyes, and swirling mist rose into the air. A vast and majestic illusion of mountains, rivers, lakes, and seas emerged, within which lay the prosperous sights of numerous cities. There were many figures dressed in linen clothes whose faces could not be seen clearly, but it was evident that everyone wore a smile."]},{"number":523,"title":"Chapter 523 - 306: Ambition, Gift","paragraphs":["As people walked through the cities, stopping now and then, most would pause to gaze at a certain wooden building within the walls. Inside the mahogany building, rows of tea jars and counters filled with medicinal herbs were on display, with several uniformly dressed Physicians sitting upright behind them. Above the entrance, a prominent plaque displayed three large, gold-stamped characters: \"Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","The scene in the calligraphy painting ended there, yet the grandeur of its Mental Realm made its underlying ambition clear to anyone who saw it. It carried a profound meaning—Hundred Herbs Hall would spread across the Nine State and Three Prefectures of the Great Wei Dynasty!","Wang Ji stared blankly at the scene, completely mesmerized for a moment. This was exactly the future he hoped for—the future of Hundred Herbs Hall. And naturally, it would include his own contributions.","After a long while, Wang Ji snapped back to reality. With a look of excitement, he cupped his hands and said, \"Sir... Sir, I, Mr. Wang, thank you for your gift on behalf of Boss Chen!\"","Chen Yi gave a nod of acknowledgment. The brush in his hand never stopped as he deliberately mimicked Liu Lang’s handwriting to write a reply. In less than three breaths, he set his brush aside, folded the letter, and waited for the ink on the Hundred Herbs Hall calligraphy painting to dry before handing both to Wang Ji.","\"Take this back, and give my regards to Boss Chen.\"","Wang Ji took the items and was about to nod in compliance when he saw Chen Yi write a few more lines on a brand new sheet of paper:","[General Jinghong is currently in the Prefecture City. She must have noticed your arrival and will likely keep an eye on Hundred Herbs Hall.]","[Pretend you know nothing. Just say that Boss Chen had urgent matters to handle and has already left Shu State.]","Wang Ji’s heart skipped a beat as he read the words. He hurriedly replied, \"Please forgive me, sir, but my boss has already left Shu State. Once he returns, I, Mr. Wang, will definitely report this to him.\"","Chen Yi continued writing as he answered, \"Brother Yu is truly an extraordinary man, as elusive as a divine dragon.\"","Watching the words appear on the paper, Wang Ji responded, \"To be honest with you, sir, my boss’s ambition is to treat and diagnose the common people of the world.","\"If there are no major events in Shu State, he usually sets off for other places.\"","\"When will he be back?\"","\"As short as three to five days, or as long as one or two months,\" Wang Ji said. \"Sir, you should know that Hundred Herbs Hall is opening a branch over in Guangyuan.\"","\"Oh,\" Chen Yi said, his tone carrying a hint of regret. \"I wonder when I’ll be able to see him next. I really enjoyed our conversation on the Painted Boat.\"","\"Sir...\"","A moment later, they finished acting out this little play. Chen Yi wrote one last reminder: \"After you leave here, return to Hundred Herbs Hall, then send someone to Lin Village outside the East City Gate to find Liu Lang. Have him deliver a letter to Zhang Dabao.","\"Remember to also inform him that General Jinghong is in the Prefecture City.\"","Wang Ji nodded heavily and gave a formal bow. \"Then I, Mr. Wang, won’t disturb you any longer, sir. I’ll take my leave.\"","Chen Yi rested his brush on the inkstone. \"I’ll see you out.\"","Wang Ji did not decline.","The two of them exchanged casual remarks as they walked out of Spring Lotus Garden. Chen Yi watched him walk away. His gaze drifted, seemingly by chance, toward the southeast—the direction of Liu Hong’s residence. Even though he hadn’t deactivated the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique, he was absolutely certain that Xiao Jinghong was over there right now.","He knew exactly why she was keeping an eye on Liu Hong. It was nothing more than an attempt to dig up concrete evidence of that old coot’s crimes. However, at this moment, with Lv Jiunan and Du Cang dead and Asutai having fled the Great Wei, the only people left who could prove Liu Hong’s guilt were his closest confidants.","If he were Liu Hong, he definitely wouldn’t make any moves during this period. At the very least, he would wait until it was confirmed that King Landu wouldn’t invade, and until the turmoil within the Shu State Prefecture City had completely settled down.","Under these circumstances, Li Sanyuan of the Ji State Trading Company became especially important. At the very least, he could reveal some information about Liu Hong. But to get him to cooperate obediently, Chen Yi still needed to make some preparations.","\"The matter concerning Li Sanyuan is of great importance. Leaving it to Madam is just perfect,\" Chen Yi thought to himself.","Thinking of this, he stretched lazily, glanced around, and leisurely returned to the guest room to rest. Having a Madam with profound Cultivation standing guard was truly wonderful; he could sleep much more soundly. However, whenever he entertained crooked thoughts or wanted to do some private things, it was a bit inconvenient.","\"Ah, whatever. Time to sleep, time to sleep...\" he muttered.","The reality was exactly as Chen Yi had guessed.","At this moment, Xiao Jinghong was sitting cross-legged on a bed in a courtyard not far from Liu Hong’s residence. Her aura was completely concealed, kept from leaking out. Even though she hadn’t practiced a Pile Skill like the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique, her level of Cultivation already allowed her to perfectly control her body’s aura.","By doing so, she couldn’t use her True Essence to amplify her senses and eavesdrop on the entire Prefecture City. However, relying solely on her natural hearing, she could act just like Chen Yi had earlier, picking up on all movements within a five-mile radius and hearing a pin drop with crystal clarity.","Naturally, the activities inside Spring Lotus Garden could not be hidden from Xiao Jinghong either. It was just that she couldn’t hear it as clearly as she had during the day at the Governor’s Office. She only knew that Wang Ji had visited to deliver a letter to Chen Yi and request a calligraphy painting for Hundred Herbs Hall. Aside from that, she had also caught wind of the fact that the boss of Hundred Herbs Hall had embarked on another long journey.","Xiao Jinghong frowned slightly, thinking, \"That ’Dragon Tiger’ is truly someone who can’t sit still.","\"If my eldest sister marries him in the future, even if it extends her lifespan, I’m afraid she won’t be happy.","\"Three to five days is fine, and three to five months is acceptable too. But if ’Dragon Tiger’ is away all year round and never returns, wouldn’t my sister be living like a widow?\"","After all, Xiao Wan’er wasn’t Chen Yi; she didn’t have such a calm and detached temperament. Xiao Jinghong made up her mind to ask \"Dragon Tiger\" clearly once she met him. If \"Dragon Tiger\" still insisted on going his own way, there was absolutely no way she would agree to Xiao Wan’er marrying him.","Thinking up to this point, Xiao Jinghong refocused her attention on her surroundings.","About an hour passed. It was nearing Midnight. There was no movement from Liu Hong’s residence. Instead, someone was sneaking over from the West Market.","Xiao Jinghong listened carefully for a moment before rising silently to peer through a crack in the window."]},{"number":524,"title":"Chapter 524 - 306: Ambition, Gift","paragraphs":["\"A disciple of the Celestial Sect? From the Hundred Herbs Hall?\"","Xiao Jinghong had learned from several letters from home that Xie Tingyun had arranged for a group of Celestial Sect disciples to join the Hundred Herbs Hall. She also guessed that the ones Dragon Tiger had sent to the Ancient Tea-Horse Road to pose as horse bandits were most likely these very same Celestial Sect disciples. Bumping into one now couldn’t help but pique her curiosity.","However, after watching the Celestial Sect disciple head all the way out of the East City Gate, Xiao Jinghong withdrew her gaze and returned to her bed. Right now, her most important task was finding evidence of Liu Hong’s crimes. Everything else could wait.","Half an hour passed.","At the faint sound of movement, Xiao Jinghong’s ears twitched. She turned her head toward Liu Hong’s residence. From the inner rear courtyard, a series of unsteady, meandering footsteps echoed, clearly belonging to someone navigating the corridors and winding paths.","Then, the person called out, \"Father.\"","Liu Hong’s voice followed. \"Fang’er? What urgent matter brings you here so late?\"","It was Liu Taofang. Recognizing the visitor’s voice, Xiao Jinghong remained completely calm and continued to eavesdrop.","\"Father, your son has great news to tell you,\" Liu Taofang said.","\"Great news? You’ve been stuck at home all this time—what great news could there be?\"","\"It’s true! Today, Lin Zhenghong from Lin’s Grain Store came looking for us and bought all the grain we had on hand! Fourteen taels of silver per stone, haha—\"","\"Nonsense!\"","\"Father, you...\"","SMACK!","\"You bastard! You’re good for nothing but ruining things! At a critical time like this, how dare you give our grain to Lin Zhenghong?\"","\"Father, I sold it to him, I didn’t just give it away. I got silver for it!\"","\"Fool! Do you have any idea what has been happening in Shu State lately? Today, Xiao Yuan and Xiao Jinghong came to see me, pressuring me to stabilize the grain prices here. Coupled with other recent events, a drop in Shu State’s grain prices is already a foregone conclusion! Lin Zhenghong and his lot can’t even save themselves right now. If they came looking for you at a time like this, they definitely harbor ill intentions!\"","\"Ah? Then... then I’ll go find him right now—\"","\"It’s too late! From now on, you’re not going anywhere. You will stay right here in the manor.\"","\"But Lin Zhenghong...\"","\"They only did this because they want to drag me down with them! Hmph. What could you possibly resolve by showing your face? Hurry up and scram back to your room!\"","\"Y-yes... your son will take his leave...\"","Soon, Liu Hong’s residence fell silent. Even Liu Hong merely cursed a few more times before quieting down.","Hearing this, Xiao Jinghong withdrew her gaze, her eyes beneath the mask revealing a hint of deep thought. \"The grain store... selling grain at high prices... this counts as one crime. But it’s not enough to bring down Liu Hong.\"","Although the laws of the Great Wei Dynasty were strict, Liu Hong was not the mastermind behind this matter. At most, he would face a minor punishment, but it wouldn’t affect his Official’s Hat. Evidence of colluding with the enemy was the real key.","Meanwhile, in Lin Village.","On night watch, Xue Duanyun caught sight of a figure sprinting toward them in the distance. He quickly coughed to draw the person’s attention, then gestured for him to climb over the wall. The new arrival understood and vaulted over the wall into the courtyard.","\"Senior Brother, there’s a door right there, why not let me use it?\"","\"Keep your voice down,\" Xue Duanyun warned. \"The commoners keeping vigil outside just fell asleep. Don’t wake them.\"","Perhaps afraid that Guard Liu and the others would stop selling grain at low prices, the commoners who had rushed over from Prefecture City had all decided to sleep on the ground outside. Faced with such a spectacle, even the usually brash Liu Lang didn’t dare make any sudden moves, let alone Xue Duanyun. They were terrified that the slightest misunderstanding might turn the desperate civilians into a mob of bandits charging in to loot the grain.","Having traveled far and wide for many years, Liu Lang intimately understood the temperament of such crowds. The possibility of someone raising a rallying cry and inciting a riotous mob was not out of the question.","After a brief explanation, Xue Duanyun asked, \"Why are you here?\"","The visitor pulled a letter from his chest and handed it over. \"The Shopkeeper told me to deliver this to Guard Liu.\"","Xue Duanyun took the letter. \"Did he say anything else?\"","\"He also said that General Jinghong is currently in the city.\"","\"General Jinghong?\" Utterly baffled, Xue Duanyun was just about to reply when he heard the rush of wind behind his head, followed by Liu Lang’s deliberately lowered voice.","\"General Jinghong is back? Damn it, why didn’t you say so earlier?\" Not waiting for Xue Duanyun to respond, Liu Lang snatched the letter and began to read it.","He knew very well that Xiao Jinghong had been looking for him and the boss. He understood that if Wang Ji had sent someone here, it must be to pass on a message from the boss.","Sure enough, after reading the contents of the letter, Liu Lang silently memorized it. With a flick of his wrist, he shattered the Yunsong Paper into dust and cautiously tossed the remains into the brazier.","\"I have an urgent matter to attend to and must leave. I’m leaving this place in your hands tomorrow.\"","Xue Duanyun was momentarily stunned. \"Is this... about the boss?\"","\"Don’t ask what you shouldn’t know, lest word gets out.\"","Saying this, Liu Lang changed into a set of Night Clothes, strapped on his long blade, and after giving them a few brief instructions, silently slipped out of the manor.","Watching him vanish into the night, Xue Duanyun rubbed his messy hair and muttered to himself. \"Does General Jinghong have a grudge against our... um, against the boss? Why else would Senior Liu run away the second he heard she was in Prefecture City?\""]},{"number":525,"title":"Chapter 525 - 307: Your Boss is Truly as Elusive as a God Dragon!","paragraphs":["Run?","How could Liu Lang run away just because Xiao Jinghong was in the Prefecture City?","Not only would he not run, but he would also deliver himself right to her doorstep.","It wasn’t that he was particularly brave; rather, the letter he had just received explicitly stated a few instructions:","[Zhang Dabao has Li Sanyuan of the Ji State Trading Company in his custody. This person is the puppet master behind several grain trading companies in Shu State.]","[You and Dabao must conspire to extract information from him using the name of King Landu to discern his intentions. Afterward, take Xiao Jinghong to see him.]","[As for Xiao Jinghong’s whereabouts... you only need to go outside Liu Hong’s residence on South Street and reveal your true face.]","[Remember to answer Xiao Jinghong truthfully when you see her. She already knows my identity.]","[Additionally, relay to her that there is one other person who might know something, and that person is—Mr. Lingchuan of Guiyun Academy!]","After reading this, Liu Lang felt immensely relieved.","Since Xiao Jinghong already knew the boss’s identity, what did he have to panic about?","The things he and the boss had done previously carried no intention of harming the Xiao Family.","With this in mind, Liu Lang briskly skirted the Prefecture City and headed west toward the Ancient Tea-Horse Road. Now, he only needed to pry the truth from this Li Sanyuan of the Ji State Trading Company, and then he could openly go and meet Grand General Xiao.","\"That works out well,\" Liu Lang muttered to himself. \"You spared my life last time. One Liu Jing wasn’t enough, so I’ll repay you with Li Sanyuan.","\"If that’s still not enough, there will always be opportunities to pay off the debt in the future.\"","Liu Lang had likely forgotten that he was ordered by Chen Yi to bring the man to Xiao Jinghong; it wasn’t his own merit. Even if he hadn’t forgotten, he would probably just shamelessly declare, \"What’s the boss’s is mine.\"","Before dawn, hurrying along without pause, Liu Lang bypassed a watchtower and traveled three hundred miles to reach Zhang Dabao and the others.","As the morning light gradually brightened and the eastern sky turned the color of a fish’s belly, deep within the lush, forested mountains, several figures dressed in coarse Poshisu Country clothing crouched in the trees, looking entirely cautious.","Liu Lang scanned the area and blew a whistle.","At the sound, the foliage rustled. Dozens of figures emerged one after another. Like the sentries from earlier, they were all dressed as Poshisu Country horse bandits.","One of them, a short and stocky man with brown curly hair and brown eyes, asked in the Poshisu Country language, \"Who goes there?\"","\"One of your own,\" Liu Lang replied with a smile. \"Where’s Dabao? The boss sent me.\"","Hearing this, the \"Poshisu Country horse bandits\" in the trees visibly relaxed. \"Is that Guard Liu?\"","\"It’s me. Cut the chatter and take me to see him,\" Liu Lang said, following a Celestial Sect disciple disguised as a Poshisu Country horse bandit deeper into their hideout.","Several ancient trees, so thick it would take five men to embrace them, had been hollowed out, their interiors extending all the way underground.","\"You’ve been hiding in this cramped little hole all these days?\" Liu Lang asked.","\"Please don’t laugh,\" the disciple replied. \"We had to improvise. We were truly worried about being discovered, so we dug out a secret chamber right here on the spot.\"","\"I have to admit, it’s quite exquisite.\"","\"Small but perfectly formed...\"","Descending about a thousand feet underground, Liu Lang finally saw Zhang Dabao. Zhang Dabao was similarly dressed as a Poshisu Country horse bandit. His youthful face was intentionally smeared pitch-black with mud, and a fake mustache was stuck above his lip.","\"Dabao?\"","\"Brother Liu, did the boss send you?\"","Liu Lang grunted in affirmation. \"Where is he?\"","Zhang Dabao pointed behind him and lowered his voice. \"He just fell asleep. If you hadn’t come, I was planning to take him back first thing tomorrow morning.\"","Previously, Chen Yi had sent a messenger with a letter ordering him to depart immediately. If Li Sanyuan hadn’t happened to stumble upon them, he would have already led the Celestial Sect disciples back to the Hundred Herbs Hall by now.","Liu Lang nodded and also lowered his voice to explain, \"The boss wants you to help me put on an act...\"","After a brief exchange, Zhang Dabao nodded and smiled. \"That’s easy. I’ll give you a disguise first.\"","\"Alright.\"","Zhang Dabao led Liu Lang to change into a horse bandit outfit, though it was slightly different from the others. Aside from the coarse cloth tunic underneath, it included an outer robe tailored from silk, with iron armor plates on the shoulders, elbows, and other areas.","\"This is the attire of a commander among the Peacock King Banner horse bandits.\"","Hearing Zhang Dabao’s words, Liu Lang twirled his small mustache in the Copper Mirror and grinned. \"Good craftsmanship.\"","After the disguise, not only had his hair and facial structure changed, but even the color of his eyes was different. According to Zhang Dabao, this was achieved using a special alchemical dye.","Confirming his appearance was flawless, Liu Lang thought of a problem. \"I don’t know the Poshisu Country language. What should I do?\"","Zhang Dabao smiled. \"That’s easy. The commanders of the Peacock King Banner all know a bit of the Wei Language. Just speak as stiffly as possible and add a touch of a Poshisu Country accent to your tone.","\"That man firmly believes in our identities; he shouldn’t be able to spot any flaws.\"","Liu Lang nodded, strapped on his long Blade, and motioned for Dabao to lead the way. Zhang Dabao didn’t waste any words, calling over a man who spoke the Poshisu Country language to follow them.","\"This is...\"","\"Da Shan. He spends his time mingling in the East Market, dealing with those human traffickers.\"","\"Is that so?\"","The man named Da Shan flashed a mouth full of yellow teeth, bowing and scraping. \"Sir, if you need anything, just give the order.\"","Liu Lang didn’t doubt him and walked ahead. After turning down a narrow passage, he paused, looking at the people scattered haphazardly on the ground inside. Suspicious, he asked, \"Who are they?\"","\"The boss ordered me to intercept all passing merchants without killing them,\" Zhang Dabao chuckled. \"I had quite a headache over it at the time.","\"Later, the boss sent over some medicinal powder. It’s incredibly effective! Even a Middle Three Grades Martial Artist will pass out within three breaths of inhaling it.\""]},{"number":526,"title":"Chapter 526 - 307: Your Boss Is Truly Elusive!","paragraphs":["\"I see...\" Having followed Boss Chen for so long, Liu Lang had naturally heard the name Immortal Drunk.","\"He didn’t suspect anything?\"","\"He went through another alley. I didn’t dare let him come this way.\"","Liu Lang hummed in acknowledgment and asked no more questions. Bypassing the others, he headed straight for the pit deep within.","Seeing that everything was ready, Zhang Dabao cleared away the bricks and stones stacked against the earthen wall, revealing a room made of wooden logs inside. A dim oil lamp hung from the ceiling beam, illuminating Li Sanyuan, who lay on a wooden bed.","Liu Lang took one look, cleared his throat, forced a ferocious smile onto his face, and walked in first.","\"Li Sanyuan...\"","About half an hour later.","Liu Lang looked at the yellow paper in his hand, bearing a signature and a fingerprint. He cracked his neck, squeezed out of the wooden cabin, and muttered, \"I talked nicely to you, but you just had to force me to get rough.\"","Even though he had been careful enough, Li Sanyuan still saw through his disguise. Fortunately, he had already investigated the purpose of Li Sanyuan’s visit beforehand. Otherwise, the ensuing matters would have been troublesome.","Zhang Dabao followed behind him. He looked back at Li Sanyuan, who was tied up tightly and gagged, and asked, \"Brother Liu, what should we do now?\"","\"Keep an eye on him here. I need to return to the Prefecture City. I’ll bring someone over before nightfall.\"","\"Who?\"","\"General Xiao... Jinghong.\"","\"Ah?\"","\"Relax, the boss has his own arrangements.\"","Zhang Dabao watched Liu Lang leave with half-belief and half-doubt. After thinking for a moment, he gathered the others to pass on the news.","\"General Jinghong will be here shortly...\"","\"Don’t worry, she’s coming for Li Sanyuan. We’ll just wait here for another half day.\"","Zhang Dabao could choose not to trust Liu Lang, but he believed in Chen Yi. During the time he had followed Chen Yi, he had long sincerely admired this figure outwardly known as \"Mr. Qingzhou.\"","Even if General Jinghong came, he had nothing to fear. After all, the boss and the General were husband and wife...","Meanwhile.","Liu Lang rode non-stop back to Shu State Prefecture City and headed straight for South Street.","When he arrived outside Liu Hong’s residence, he looked around. Seeing very few people about, he took off his mask to reveal his true face. However, after waiting for a moment, there was still no sign of Xiao Jinghong.","Liu Lang couldn’t help but mutter, \"Did the boss get the location wrong? Is General Jinghong not here?\"","Before he even finished speaking, he heard a voice ring in his ear. \"Are you looking for me?\"","Startled, Liu Lang scanned his surroundings but still saw nothing. He lowered his voice and said, \"Boss Chen sent me to find you.\"","\"Come up.\"","Immediately after, Liu Lang sensed a sharp Sword Intent land right in front of him, guiding his gaze toward a nearby courtyard.","Over there?","Liu Lang put his mask back on and flashed over.","As soon as he landed in the courtyard, he saw a figure standing outside the main hall with her hands behind her back. She wore that silver half-armor mask on her face.","He grinned, cupped his fists, and said, \"We meet again, General.\"","Xiao Jinghong looked at him calmly. \"How did you know I was here?\"","\"Uh, Boss Chen wrote to tell me.\"","\"Your boss? Chen Yu?\"","\"Yes...\"","\"Where is he? How did he know I was here?\"","\"I don’t know either...\" Seeing that she didn’t believe him, Liu Lang shook his head. \"After Boss Chen ordered me to go to Lin Village a few days ago, I haven’t seen him since.\"","\"Lin Village?\" Xiao Jinghong pondered. \"Are you the ones selling the grain outside the city?\"","Liu Lang smiled and nodded. \"So you already know. Yes, it was indeed Boss Chen’s arrangement. But honestly, I really don’t know what he’s thinking. That batch of grain cost about five hundred thousand taels of silver to purchase, yet it’s only being sold for one tael per shi. What a loss...\"","Liu Lang rambled on, complaining about how his boss wouldn’t tell him anything.","Xiao Jinghong listened patiently. \"Your boss truly is as elusive as a divine dragon.\"","Not only was he elusive, but what surprised her even more was that the man could actually deduce that she would return and hide outside Liu Hong’s house.","How did he do it?","Even someone as powerful as Immortal Bai couldn’t compare to the wariness Xiao Jinghong felt toward \"Chen Yu\" right now. Was there truly a Divine Calculator in this world who could deduce every response of others?","Unaware of her inner thoughts, Liu Lang chuckled dryly. \"Forgive him, General. Boss Chen is just like that. He does everything secretively.\"","Xiao Jinghong gave him a deep look and asked, \"Tell me, what did he send you to find me for?\"","\"Boss Chen asked me to take you to see someone. He said that person can help you bring down...\" Liu Lang pointed at the nearby Liu family residence. \"And it’s true. That person knows a lot about their affairs.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Jinghong’s eyes flickered slightly, but she was no longer as surprised as before. Since \"Chen Yu\" could calculate that she would be here, it was perfectly normal for him to know her intentions.","\"Where is this person?\"","\"The Ancient Tea-Horse Road...\"","\"Lead the way!\"","Xiao Jinghong swept her robes and waved her hand, summoning a black cloak from the inner hall to drape over herself.","Seeing this, Liu Lang said no more and led the way out of the courtyard. The two traversed through the West Market and the West City Gate, heading straight for the Ancient Tea-Horse Road.","\"Oh right, Boss Chen also asked me to pass on a message. Mr. Lingchuan from Guiyun Academy might have what you need as well.\"","\"Mr. Lingchuan from Guiyun Academy? Zhu Lingchuan?\" she mused. \"It seems your boss possesses even vaster Divine Skills than I previously understood.\"","\"Just average, haha, just average...\"","While leading the way, Liu Lang wiped the sweat from his forehead, cursing his boss in his heart for being disloyal. Even though he was certain Xiao Jinghong wouldn’t hold a grudge against him for what happened earlier, the pressure at this moment was still overwhelming.","The two traveled west, conversing in low voices along the way.","As Xiao Jinghong listened to him recount Li Sanyuan’s identity and deeds, a strong killing intent surged in her heart. It wasn’t just directed at Li Sanyuan, but also at Zhu Hao from the Capital Commandery.","No wonder \"Chen Yu\" reminded her that Mr. Lingchuan might know something.","So that was it!","Inside the Spring Lotus Garden.","Sensing something, Chen Yi stood up and looked toward the west. Holding a book in his hand, he thought, \"Calculating the hour, Xiao Jinghong should have already been led to the Ancient Tea-Horse Road by Liu Lang. By Midnight tonight at the latest, she will bring the person back to the Prefecture City.\"","With this in mind, Chen Yi put down the book, called for Xiaodie, and instructed, \"I’m taking a trip to Guiyun Academy. Prepare some ink and paper in the study for me this afternoon. I have a few policy essays to write when I return.\"","\"Yes, Mr. Chen.\"","Unexpectedly, before Chen Yi could even step out of the Spring Lotus Garden, he saw Xiao Wan’er approaching with Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang.","Upon seeing him, Xiao Wan’er’s breathtakingly beautiful face was filled with confusion. Hesitating for a moment, she asked, \"Chen Yi, are you heading out?\"","Chen Yi guessed her purpose and smiled, nodding. \"I previously agreed to visit Mr. Yue Ming today. Wan’er, are you... also heading out?\"","\"Yes, Little Sister Qingwu invited me to meet at the Yunqing Building to discuss the Medical Dao Academy.\"","\"Oh?\"","Chen Yi frowned inwardly. He had been planning to find Cui Qingwu under the guise of \"Liu Wu.\" After all, he had spent so much silver this time, and he had to make Cui Qingwu cough up the silver she owed him.","Moreover, the incident with the \"Jackal\" Du Cang had sounded a wake-up call for him.","He needed to prepare for a rainy day.","He had to leverage the power of the White Tiger Guard to make some preparations, preventing anyone else from getting desperate and biting back.","With these thoughts in mind, Chen Yi made a decision.","\"Are you in a hurry, Wan’er? If not, could I hitch a ride?\"","Xiao Wan’er hesitated for a moment before nodding in agreement.","A short while later.","The four of them boarded the carriage and left the Marquis’s Mansion.","Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er sat inside the cabin, and the atmosphere inexplicably turned a bit strange.","Xiao Wan’er kept her head lowered, half her face hidden in her cloak, her eyes stealing occasional glances at Chen Yi. In contrast, Chen Yi’s expression remained perfectly calm.","It was just that...","His hand wasn’t behaving. He held onto Xiao Wan’er’s hand the whole time, even opening her palm to trace his fingers over it.","Xiao Wan’er tried to pull away, but seeing that he wouldn’t let go, the ticklish sensation in her palm made her blush. \"Chen Yi...\"","Chen Yi gave a helpless smile. While remarking about how lively it looked outside, he gestured for her to look at her palm.","Then, he wrote a few more words: [Ask whatever you want to ask.]","Xiao Wan’er understood the invisible writing, and her face immediately grew even redder. She had just thought Chen Yi was taking liberties with her. Now that she realized what he was doing, she only wanted to shrink completely into her cloak.","Seeing this, Chen Yi patted her gently. He smiled, extending his own palm, and signaled with his eyes for her to write.","Xiao Wan’er understood. She tried her best to calm her Heart Spirit, raised her hand, and traced on his palm:","[Are you \"Chen Yu\"?]","[Yes, I am.]","[So, did you establish the Hundred Herbs Hall with Wang Ji just to help me?]","[You could say that.]","Chen Yi traced those few words, his mind recalling how Xiao Wan’er had once pawned her gold and silver jewelry to subsidize the monthly allowances for the various households.","[It wasn’t right to let you bear the burden all alone, Wan’er. Besides, the mansion gives me an allowance of silver every month anyway, so I came up with a Method.]","[You know the Medical Dao?]","[I do.]","Receiving his answer, the blush on Xiao Wan’er’s face deepened noticeably. It took her a long while before she haltingly traced a few words on Chen Yi’s palm:","[So when I had my previous illness attacks, w-was it you who treated me?]"]},{"number":527,"title":"Chapter 527 - 308: Leave Everything to Me!","paragraphs":["Xiao Wan’er hadn’t thought of this at first.","But after learning that Chen Yi was both \"Liu Wu\" and \"Chen Yu,\" she couldn’t help but recall that embarrassing incident as she looked back on all that had happened. Back then, Chen Yi clearly hadn’t just been lifting her blanket; he was treating her illness.","So... so... Not only had he seen her in her undergarments, but Chen Yi might have even touched her body...","Xiao Wan’er didn’t dare to think any further. Her face flushed as red as fire, and she shrank into her cloak, only willing to reveal her eyes.","[You... that prescription from Physician Ma Liangcai, was that you too?]","Reading the words traced on his hand, Chen Yi couldn’t help but turn his head to look at her in stunned silence. Their eyes met, and Xiao Wan’er hastily turned her head away, not daring to meet his gaze. A rosy blush had already spread around her eyes, looking exceedingly beautiful.","Chen Yi smiled. He pulled her hand back, opened her palm, and traced the word [Yes].","The simplest response would have been a nod, but at this moment, Xiao Wan’er didn’t dare to look at him at all. If not for the inconvenience of her long hair and the golden jade phoenix hairpin adorning it, she probably would have tucked her entire head into the cloak by now.","After waiting for a moment, Chen Yi saw that she still had no intention of poking her head out. He simply held her hand and continued tracing on it.","[Initially, I had Wang Ji establish Hundred Herbs Hall just to earn some silver and help relieve some of your burden.]","[Later, because of the provisions issue for the Three Towns, the estate’s silver coins became tight, which was why I started expanding Hundred Herbs Hall...]","At this point, Xiao Wan’er suddenly pulled her hand back. A smile, seemingly half-reproachful and half-delighted, bloomed on her face hidden beneath the cloak.","No wonder she had felt a sense of familiarity when she first met \"Chen Yu.\" She had thought it was because the roots of love had planted deep within her. She realized this bad man had even deceived her just to keep up his act. Yet, everything this bad man did was for her sake...","Chen Yi stopped moving and watched her with a faint smile.","A long while later, Xiao Wan’er finally peeked out half of her face. Her eyes instantly met Chen Yi’s gaze, and her heart, which had just calmed down a bit, began to THUMP THUMP once more. Holding back her shyness, she reached out, grasped Chen Yi’s palm, and traced:","[I... I didn’t know you did so many things. I thought... I thought you were just studying in the estate.]","[If I had known this earlier, I... I wouldn’t have let you come to the estate.]","[And Grandfather wouldn’t have made me marry you... Chen Yu.]","Words like \"marry\" were somewhat embarrassing for Xiao Wan’er to use. But she knew in her heart that it was impossible for her to truly marry Chen Yi, not even under the identity of \"Chen Yu.\"","Chen Yi understood this and replied with a few words: [For the time being, I will no longer travel around Shu State under the identities of ’Chen Yu’ or ’Liu Wu.’]","[Whether it’s the Old Master or... Madam, since they won’t be able to see me, they naturally won’t have any way to bring this matter up.]","Before he could think of a proper solution, Chen Yi could only resort to a stalling tactic.","But Xiao Wan’er still didn’t relax. As if she had thought of something, the rosy blush on her face gradually faded. Her eyes shifted away from Chen Yi’s gaze and lowered slightly as her fingers subconsciously stroked his palm.","A moment later, seemingly having figured something out, she let out a breath and wrote a few more words:","[When Second Sister questioned me yesterday, I... I didn’t know what to say... I felt terrified, panicked, and a bit...]","Bitter. Xiao Wan’er tried several times but couldn’t manage to completely trace the word.","Chen Yi, however, had already understood her feelings. He flipped his hand over to grasp hers and gently patted it.","\"I’ll handle everything.\"","These words were no longer written; they were spoken from his own mouth. His tone carried a gentle smile, but it was also laced with firmness.","It made Xiao Wan’er’s inexplicably fluttering heart instantly relax. Meeting his gaze, she nodded softly.","\"Mhm.\"","At this moment, Xiao Wan’er felt that she was probably going crazy. From childhood to adulthood, she had never been as bold as she was now. Even though neither of them had spoken of love, nor had they made any lifelong promises, a voice in her heart was telling her—this was a private betrothal.","Apart from that uncontrollable burst of joy, what Xiao Wan’er thought about more were the words \"sister’s husband.\" Neither secular society nor the Xiao Family would find it easy to accept such a thing. If word got out, she, Chen Yi, and even the entire Xiao Family would be mocked by the whole world.","Xiao Wan’er knew all this clearly, yet she still pressed on without turning back. In her fragile heart—tormented by physical illness and the grief of her parents’ deaths—she only hoped to preserve this affection. She wasn’t asking to be with Chen Yi or to marry him. She would even be content just silently watching over him for the rest of her life.","She didn’t want too much, did she?","Chen Yi, on the other hand, didn’t think that far ahead. We’ll cross that bridge when we come to it; surely a living man wouldn’t let himself be boxed into a corner. However, he also knew that his relationship with Xiao Wan’er could only go this far. Obviously, outsiders could not be allowed to know about it.","There was no other way. Setting aside whether the Old Master would agree, just getting past his Madam, Xiao Jinghong, would be difficult enough. Put his foot down as the husband? What a joke. Chen Yi had no desire to cross swords with Xiao Jinghong, so he needed to play the long game.","But all of that was for the future. Right now, he just wanted to enjoy this moment of tranquility.","The small carriage was filled with warmth. His hand held hers, as if their hearts were beating as one.","Meanwhile, just outside the carriage, separated by a single curtain, a smile suddenly appeared on Xie Tingyun’s face, and she let out a soft chuckle.","Shen Huatang was still pondering the meaning behind that brief exchange of \"I’ll handle everything\" and \"Mhm.\" Hearing Xie Tingyun’s sudden noise, she cast a dissatisfied glance over.","Xie Tingyun didn’t mind. She shrank her neck and gestured something to her. Coupled with her smile, her whole demeanor appeared somewhat sleazy."]},{"number":528,"title":"Chapter 528 - 308: Leave Everything to Me!","paragraphs":["But Shen Huatang understood.","\"Junior Sister, in what context do you think someone would say, ’Don’t worry, I’ll take care of everything’?\"","Shen Huatang pondered the question, mouthing wordlessly, \"When Miss encounters a difficulty... is the young master comforting her?\"","\"Yes, but also no.\"","\"I’m guessing it went like this...\"","Xie Tingyun’s small mouth opened and closed repeatedly as she mouthed a scripted conversation:","\"Second Sister is back. I’m afraid she will discover our affair. If she finds out, you and I...\"","\"Don’t worry, Eldest Sister. I’ll take care of everything.\"","\"Mhm...\"","Truth be told, Xie Tingyun’s speculation about such matters was remarkably accurate. Even Shen Huatang subconsciously believed that was exactly how it happened. However, after thinking it over, she felt it didn’t quite make sense.","\"Eldest Miss isn’t that bold, not when you and I are still right here.\"","\"Miss might not be, but the young master certainly is! He... Tell you what, if you don’t believe me, I’ll lift the curtain, and you look back.\"","\"Based on your senior sister’s experience wandering the Jianghu, when a noble family’s daughter privately pledges herself to someone, she’s either resting in his arms or holding his hand.\"","Shen Huatang hesitated for a moment before nodding as if possessed.","Xie Tingyun instantly chuckled mischievously, quietly reaching out to rest her hand on the edge of the curtain.","\"Junior Sister, are you ready?\"","\"Mhm!\"","\"Three, two, one, look!\"","SWISH.","The curtain was suddenly lifted by a corner.","Shen Huatang cooperatively turned her head to look inside the carriage. Once she saw clearly, she whipped her head back around.","Watching her reaction, Xie Tingyun had intended to drop the curtain, but she couldn’t resist sneaking a peek herself. She froze on the spot.","Inside, Chen Yi was sitting closest to the curtain, his hand suspended in mid-air—he had clearly been preparing to lift it himself. Xiao Wan’er was sitting behind him. Although her face bore a faint blush, everything else appeared perfectly normal.","The three of them stared at each other for a moment.","Chen Yi retracted his hand and asked with a half-smile, \"Fairy Tingyun, did you have something to say?\"","Xie Tingyun stammered, \"N-no... Ah, no, I think I wanted to say...\"","\"Senior Sister wanted to say that we’ve arrived at Guiyun Academy,\" Shen Huatang quickly interjected.","\"Right, right, right! Young Master, we are almost at Guiyun Academy.\"","Chen Yi looked at her, then glanced at Shen Huatang, who didn’t even dare to turn her head back, and said with a smile, \"I was just about to get off.\"","He then turned back to Xiao Wan’er and winked. \"Eldest Sister, dropping me off here is fine. Don’t let me delay your business.\"","Xiao Wan’er gave him a reproachful glare. Noticing Xie Tingyun’s gaze, she merely murmured an acknowledgment and said, \"Come back home early once you’re done.\"","\"I’ll remember.\"","With that, Chen Yi stepped out of the carriage. He greeted Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang, then motioned for them to drive away.","Amidst the clattering of hooves, the carriage turned around.","Chen Yi stood by the roadside, watching as Xiao Wan’er shifted from one window to the other, and waved with a smile. Xiao Wan’er returned his smile, her eyes brimming with tenderness, before drawing the curtain closed as the carriage moved forward.","The Noon sun was shining perfectly. As the carriage drifted further away, a woman remained radiant, her captivating gaze bright and dazzling.","Chen Yi thought that he would remember a scene like this for the rest of his life. But really, what right did he have to deserve such affection?","At this thought, Chen Yi let out a self-deprecating smile. Straightening his posture, he strolled unhurriedly into Guiyun Academy. If he wasn’t worthy, who else in this world could deserve such affection?","An hour later.","Accompanied by Ma Guan, Chen Yi left Guiyun Academy. His mind had never been fully on the academy anyway, so he had merely chatted briefly with Mr. Yue Ming and Mr. Zhuo Ying. Mostly, their conversation revolved around the Annual Examination.","According to the notices issued by the government office, the scholars within Shu State Prefecture City were to participate in the Annual Examination on the twenty-eighth of this month. The venue was set in a small courtyard next to the Governor’s Office.","Having committed this to memory, Chen Yi brought up another matter—the rumor that his calligraphy was worth its weight in gold.","Mr. Yue Ming and Mr. Zhuo Ying’s aged faces immediately flushed red. They stammered out that some individuals in the academy were going through difficult times. Like Ma Guan, for instance, whose family lacked money and struggled to make ends meet when grain prices skyrocketed. Left with no other choice, the academy had sold a few of the calligraphy pieces Chen Yi had written during his lectures. They exchanged the money for grain to distribute among students from impoverished families, and even a few financially strapped instructors had benefited from this kindness.","Seeing that this was the reason, Chen Yi naturally didn’t voice any objections. In fact, he was highly supportive of Mr. Yue Ming’s approach.","\"Sir, I thank you on behalf of Brother Feihong and the others,\" Ma Guan said.","\"It was the dean’s idea. It has nothing to do with me.\" Chen Yi patted his shoulder and added, \"If you truly want to thank me, then perform exceptionally well in the upcoming Annual Examination.\"","Ma Guan nodded solemnly. \"I will surely etch your teachings into my heart, Sir.\"","\"You are always so... Just go back. I’m leaving.\"","Chen Yi had wanted to call him stubborn, but after thinking it over, he felt it was inappropriate. When Ma Guan achieved Minor Success in the Calligraphy Dao, his Dao Intent had been crystal clear—he was a scholar steadfastly adhering to the path of the \"ancient gentleman.\" Having outsiders say too much would only cause harm, not good.","\"I bid you farewell, Sir.\"","Chen Yi waved without looking back. Out of the corner of his eye, he caught sight of A Wonton Shop not far from the academy. Seeing its desolate storefront, he understood the reason. At a time when prices for grain, meat, and vegetables were surging, even small eateries that solely sold wontons struggled to attract customers. Beyond that, he figured it also had something to do with Lou Yuxue’s prolonged absence.","He thought, \"It really isn’t appropriate for a Silver Banner Officer of the White Tiger Guard to run a private business...\"","With these thoughts in mind, Chen Yi’s pace didn’t slow. Exiting Kangning Street, he quickly made his way toward the residence on Chuansi Street. To conceal his whereabouts, he stopped and started along the way, ensuring no one noticed his tracks.","Even the wandering martial artists gathered in the Prefecture City, anxiously waiting for Immortal Bai, were mostly busy chatting and laughing. There was nothing new. No matter how much he listened, it boiled down to a few sentences:","\"’Dragon Tiger’ Liu Wu killed ’Jackal’ Du Cang! This calls for a toast. Cheers, everyone!\"","\"I wonder how King Landu will react when he finds out.\"","\"First Lv Jiunan died, and now Du Cang. It’s no different from severing his left and right arms.\"","\"If I were him, even if I didn’t lead an army to invade the borders, I would definitely send someone to exact revenge.\"","\"You can say that again...\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi felt it was dull. Just as he was about to speed up, he abruptly overheard another sentence that made him slow his steps.","\"Didn’t we see ’Dragon Tiger’ leading Lv Jiunan to Puyin Temple that night?\"","\"But when we rushed over later, we only saw Du Cang’s corpse. We didn’t find any trace of Lv Jiunan.\"","\"Maybe he was beaten into ash by ’Liu Wu’?\"","\"Even so, shouldn’t there be some traces left behind?\"","\"That...\"","Lv Jiunan’s corpse was gone?","Chen Yi frowned inwardly. He was certain that his spear strike that night had completely shattered Lv Jiunan’s heart meridians. The man was undoubtedly dead. Yet now his corpse was missing... What was going on?","Could it be that, aside from the strange swordsman flying in the sky, there were other experts hiding nearby?","No, there shouldn’t have been. At least, not before Chen Yi had left. Otherwise, given how terrifying that swordsman was, he would have definitely sensed anyone else spying on them. Therefore, it had to be a latecomer who deliberately took Lv Jiunan’s corpse away.","After pondering for a moment, Chen Yi formed a few hypotheses, though they were merely guesses rather than concrete deductions.","The first possibility was Liu Hong’s men. Lv Jiunan was connected to him and King Landu. If Liu Hong or his subordinates stumbled upon the corpse, they had every reason to take it. It was far better than letting it fall into the hands of the various government offices in Shu State.","The second possibility was the White Tiger Guard. Setting aside the fact that they were lying low in Shu State, they likely had numerous internal schemes. Taking Lv Jiunan’s body might give them leverage to negotiate with King Landu.","The third—and least likely—possibility was someone from Poshisu Country. Aside from these three, Chen Yi couldn’t think of anyone else in Shu State who would go out of their way to take Lv Jiunan’s corpse.","It couldn’t possibly be someone trying to fraudulently claim the credit for killing him, right? That would simply be too despicable.","Having reached this point in his thoughts, Chen Yi made up his mind to question the White Tiger Guard. Regardless, he needed to figure out where Lv Jiunan’s corpse had gone.","A moment later.","Taking advantage of the deserted surroundings, Chen Yi flipped over the wall into the residence. He dug out two masks to complete his disguise, then headed straight for the Spring Rain Building.","By this time, Noon had just passed. The Yanhua Lane in the South City was relatively deserted. Aside from a few hungover, philandering gentlemen and young masters who had just woken up, there were very few people walking about.","Chen Yi didn’t bother to hide his movements much, heading straight for the quiet chambers on the top floor of the Spring Rain Building. Just as he was about to look for Lou Yuxue, he spotted a figure standing at the end of the quiet, dimly lit corridor, watching him silently.","It was none other than the Golden Banner Officer of the White Tiger Guard—General!","\"’Dragon Tiger’ Liu Wu?\"","\"Seeing you in person surpasses your reputation. I am General.\""]},{"number":529,"title":"Chapter 529 - 309: A Conversation Across Space with the Pavilion Master!","paragraphs":["General?","It was indeed General’s appearance, yet his aura was vastly different from before. He wore black brocade robes and black boots etched with purple floral patterns. A long blade hung at his waist, its hilt and scabbard boasting an archaic and elegant design. His hair was combed into a neat bun and tied with a headband, revealing a cleanly shaven face. Above all, his eyes carried a faint smile but harbored an intense, predatory aggressiveness.","His imposing presence as a Golden Banner Officer of the White Tiger Guard was on full display.","Chen Yi scrutinized him up and down with a calm expression. Meanwhile, his ears caught a faint murmur. It sounded like Lou Yuxue muttering something about how they could have been discovered. Clearly, General waiting here was no coincidence.","Chen Yi thought for a moment before tipping his bamboo hat back to reveal his handsome face. \"General of the White Tiger Guard? Your reputation precedes you.\"","General chuckled, his face flickering in and out of the shadows cast by the lanterns hanging from the corridor ceiling. \"You must be joking, Mr. Dragon Tiger. I am but a nameless man selling my life for the Imperial Court, incomparable to a peerless genius like yourself.\" He paused, cupped his fists, and pointed to his right. \"I know you are here to discuss matters of importance. Why don’t we have a chat in a Quiet Chamber?\"","Chen Yi’s expression remained unchanged as he looked at him. He gave a slight nod. \"I shall respectfully accept.\"","The Quiet Chamber over there was not the one Lou Yuxue was currently occupying. It seemed General had indeed waited here specifically because he had something to say.","Chen Yi was acutely aware of this, yet he followed along regardless. It just so happened that his own reason for coming to the Spring Rain Building also involved the White Tiger Guard. He could easily weigh the difference in importance between a Golden Banner Officer and a Silver Banner Officer.","Inside the Quiet Chamber, there were no windows on any of the four walls, and candlelight illuminated the space. There was a black wooden desk flanked by two Grandmaster’s Chairs. A pristine white tea cloth covered the desk, upon which sat two steaming cups of tea with clear, bright liquid.","Chen Yi glanced at it, a faint smile curling the corners of his mouth. \"How thoughtful.\"","General could only guess that he would come, but he couldn’t possibly know exactly when. Therefore, for these two cups of perfectly brewed tea to be ready, he must have replaced them with fresh tea and boiling water every fifteen minutes. It was indeed thoughtful, or rather, a show of sincerity.","\"It is only right for me to extend my hospitality to grace the presence of the esteemed Mr. Dragon Tiger.\" General sat in the inner chair and waved with a smile. \"Please, have a seat.\"","Chen Yi graciously complied, taking the seat opposite him. Resting his hands naturally on the desk, he merely looked at the man calmly, quietly waiting for him to continue.","With General showing such exceptional courtesy—dismissing his subordinates and constantly brewing fresh tea—whatever he was about to ask for had to be quite significant. Chen Yi couldn’t help but feel a twinge of curiosity.","The smile on General’s face faded slightly. He raised his teacup and offered a simple, \"Please.\"","Chen Yi noncommittally took a sip, set the cup down, and remained entirely silent.","Seeing this, General smiled and shook his head. \"Mr. Dragon Tiger, you truly live up to your reputation as the figure who has recently stirred up storms in Shu State. Your composure alone is enough to put me to shame.\"","This time, he didn’t wait for Chen Yi to speak. Setting down his teacup, he continued, \"Additionally, I should first offer you an apology.\"","\"Oh?\" Chen Yi was slightly surprised.","General smiled. \"Earlier, when you ’killed’ Lv Jiunan in Heiyu Lane, I happened to be right outside the West Market. Out of curiosity, I followed you.\"","\"That is human nature,\" Chen Yi said with understanding.","General shook his head. \"If I hadn’t done that, I wouldn’t have been reprimanded by Lord Pavilion Master.\"","Truthfully, he hadn’t been wronged. That time, he had followed \"Liu Wu\" to Kangning Street and bumped into Liu Zhaoxue, leading him to mistakenly believe that \"Liu Wu\" was a member of the Liu Family. Because of this, he even specially wrote a letter to send back to the White Tiger Guard.","He originally thought Lord Pavilion Master would give him instructions on how to deal with the Jing State Liu Family. To his surprise, Lord Pavilion Master’s recent reply contained no such instructions. Instead, his wording was razor-sharp: \"Fool! ’Liu Wu’ is a member of the Xiao Family!\"","The letter conveyed a profound sense of anger at his Non-Struggle. Fortunately, there were a few more sentences at the end that helped ease General’s mood amidst his shame and trepidation. Otherwise, his tenure as a Golden Banner Officer would likely have come to an abrupt end.","Naturally, Chen Yi was unaware of these details. He asked, \"The White Tiger Guard Pavilion Master... reprimanded you?\"","He was asking a question to which he already knew the answer. If the mysterious Pavilion Master of the White Tiger Guard had reprimanded General, it could only be because he had made a misjudgment or committed a mistake. Combining this with what was just said, it wasn’t hard for Chen Yi to deduce that General must have assumed he was a member of the Liu Family and relayed that information back to the White Tiger Guard.","At the same time, he made an even deeper deduction: the Pavilion Master of the White Tiger Guard was absolutely certain he was not a member of the Liu Family. Or perhaps, that Pavilion Master knew his true identity?","It was impossible! Currently, the only people who knew his identity were Pei Guanli, Xiao Wan’er, Wang Ji, Zhang Dabao, and Yan Sea. Apart from those five, there was only Immortal Bai—the number one figure in Martial Arts who had seen through his Martial Arts Cultivation and true appearance with a single glance. As for anyone else, not even Liu Lang, who interacted with him closely, knew he was the live-in son-in-law of the Xiao Family. The White Tiger Guard Pavilion Master wasn’t even in Shu State, so how could he possibly know his identity?","Chen Yi recalled the few past incidents where his identity might have been leaked. Suppressing and killing Liu Jing, defeating Yan Fusha with a spear, and his recent slaying of Du Cang... Of the very few times he had revealed his true face or displayed his real strength, the most likely source of the leak was... Yan Fusha...","Who could it be?","Unaware that his casual, unintentional remark had led Chen Yi to deduce so much, General chuckled. \"Indeed. Lord Pavilion Master possesses immense Divine Skills. The esteemed elder can know the affairs of the world without ever stepping foot outside his door.\"","Suppressing the doubts in his heart, Chen Yi asked, \"Does this have anything to do with me?\"","\"Of course it does,\" General replied. \"Lord Pavilion Master has ordered me to formally invite you to join the White Tiger Guard.\"","At this point, General shook his head. \"However, I’m guessing that you won’t agree, Mr. Dragon Tiger. Just like how you rejected Lady Tiger last time—why would an exceptional talent like yourself ever stoop to serve under others?\"","Chen Yi looked at him noncommittally. \"How would you know if you don’t try?\"","\"Try?\" General picked up his teacup and took a sip. He looked at Chen Yi and said, \"You are a smart man, sir. I wouldn’t dare make a fool of myself in front of you.\""]},{"number":530,"title":"Chapter 530 - 309: A Conversation Across Space with the Pavilion Master!","paragraphs":["Whether it was the matter of the summer grain in the Three Towns or everything that had recently happened in Shu State, all signs pointed to \"Liu Wu\" possessing an intellect bordering on the demonic.","To some extent, General’s wariness of his scheming far outweighed his fear of Liu Wu’s Martial Arts aptitude and Cultivation.","However, the reason General was certain that Chen Yi would not join the White Tiger Guard was due to a specific line in the Lord Pavilion Master’s letter:","[’Liu Wu’ is a once-in-a-century monster. The Banner Officers of Shu State are not worthy of his attention. Set aside the matter of inviting him to join the White Tiger Guard for now.]","Although General was unconvinced, after his probing just now, he indeed couldn’t see anything unusual in Chen Yi’s expression.","Even when he brought up the \"Lord Pavilion Master,\" it was the same.","Such a monster truly could not be swayed by his petty tricks.","\"I have come to wait for you this time not only to meet with you, but also to ask for a favor,\" General said.","Seeing that General was being so tactful, Chen Yi naturally wouldn’t keep him at arm’s length. \"Let’s hear it.\"","\"Since you can navigate Shu State with such ease and even took action to eliminate Liu Wen, Lv Jiunan, Du Cang, and the others, you must be very familiar with the situation here.\"","\"I’ve heard a little.\"","\"Then you should also know some of the background of the Ji State Trading Company, their profit-driven nature, and their collusion with Zhu Hao of the Capital Commandery.\"","\"Zhu Hao?\" Chen Yi thought. Seeing the man beat around the bush only to point the spearhead at the Ji State Trading Company and Zhu Hao, he frowned inwardly.","He was the one who had passed the information about the collusion between Zhu Hao and the Ji State Trading Company to Lou Yuxue; he understood the connection better than anyone.","But what did this have to do with him?","That Zhu Hao was far away in Guangyuan, well beyond his reach.","Moreover, he had already eliminated the malignant tumor that was the Ji State Trading Company. A powerful regional official like Zhu Hao should naturally be dealt with by the Court Officials.","General seemed to see his confusion. \"Don’t be hasty.","\"The favor I am asking for is related to them, but they are not the target. It is someone else.\"","General paused for a moment, then said sternly, \"This matter is of great importance. It is something our White Tiger Guard has been planning in Shu State for many years.","\"I hope that after you hear it today, whether you agree or not, you will not reveal a single word of it to anyone.\"","In truth, his original intention was to never let an outsider interfere with his mission.","But with the Lord Pavilion Master’s orders pressing down on him, he had to obey. He didn’t dare not to.","Seeing him speak so solemnly, Chen Yi picked up his teacup and took a sip.","After a moment of thought, he put down the cup and shook his head. \"If that’s the case, you should save your breath.\"","It was better not to listen.","He had no interest in risking his life for the White Tiger Guard. Even if he was curious about the White Tiger Guard Pavilion Master, he didn’t want to get involved.","If he really did this, what difference would there be from him joining the White Tiger Guard?","Unexpectedly, after hearing this, General wasn’t worried but amused. He said with a face full of smiles, \"The Lord Pavilion Master possesses divine foresight. He guessed that you would definitely refuse.\"","Chen Yi’s gaze shifted slightly. He said flatly, \"Since your Pavilion Master knew I would refuse, why did he order you to do this?\"","\"I don’t know.\"","General paused, then continued, \"I am just following orders. I hope you can forgive me.","\"But the Lord Pavilion Master said that if you knew who the target of this endeavor was, you would definitely be interested.\"","Chen Yi stared at him intently. A moment later, he spat out a single word: \"Speak.\"","\"Chen Yunfan!\"","\"Chen... Yunfan?\"","Chen Yi originally thought he would hear his own name from General’s mouth, but he hadn’t expected it to be his older brother—Chen Yunfan.","This was indeed beyond his expectations.","It also genuinely piqued his interest.","But because of this, he grew even more wary of the White Tiger Guard’s Pavilion Master.","It felt like a dark cloud looming over his head, seeing through everything about him.","—His identity, aptitude, Cultivation, background, and even his very thoughts.","General’s attention had been on him the entire time, so he naturally noticed the subtle changes in his expression. The admiration he felt for the Lord Pavilion Master in his heart surged like a torrential river.","No matter how mysterious and incredibly talented this \"Liu Wu\" was, he still couldn’t escape the Lord Pavilion Master’s grasp, could he?","However, General was also confused about one thing—this \"Liu Wu\" was a member of the Xiao Family, so why would he care about Chen Yunfan?","It had to be known that in the Xiao Family, there weren’t many people related to Chen Yunfan. There was only one—the live-in son-in-law of the Xiao Family and the White Tiger Guard’s \"Fledgling,\" Chen Yi.","Could \"Liu Wu\" be related to Chen Yi?","Or could they be...","General carefully and thoroughly looked \"Liu Wu\" up and down, secretly denying the guess in his heart.","Whether it was their appearance, aura, Cultivation, or aptitude, these two people didn’t have a single similarity.","On top of that, one was skilled in Poetry and songs, as well as Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting, while the other practiced both the Martial Arts and Medical Dao.","If these two were the same person, how could the word \"monster\" even begin to describe him?","At the very least, they would have to add \"peerless\" in front of it, or simply call him \"the person with the highest aptitude throughout the ages.\"","General obviously didn’t believe it. Going back thousands or even tens of thousands of years, such a figure had never appeared.","Therefore, he leaned more toward the idea that \"Liu Wu\" and the \"Fledgling\" had a connection.","That was why \"Liu Wu\" had rescued the \"Fledgling\" outside the Prefecture City with Liu Lang on the night of the Mid-Autumn Festival.","He had heard Simurgh Phoenix mention this matter before.","After a long silence, Chen Yi tapped the table, a smile appearing on his face for the first time. \"Lord General, why don’t you tell me exactly what you need my help with.\"","Since it involved Chen Yunfan, no matter how wary he was of the White Tiger Guard Pavilion Master, he would give it a try.","He wanted to see exactly what this White Tiger Guard was up to.","Hearing this, General clapped his hands and said, \"Your straightforwardness is truly admirable.","\"Actually, the matter is very simple...\"","After listening, a trace of oddity flashed through Chen Yi’s eyes. \"It’s... just that?\"","General nodded and smiled. \"It’s just that simple.","\"You only need to make a trip on behalf of our White Tiger Guard and deliver the evidence of Zhu Hao’s crimes into Assistant Governor Chen’s hands.\""]},{"number":531,"title":"Chapter 531 - 309: A Conversation Across Space with the Pavilion Master!","paragraphs":["\"Why don’t you do it yourselves?\"","\"There is something you don’t know, sir. Due to a few previous incidents, Assistant Governor Chen harbors quite a few misunderstandings toward our White Tiger Guard.","\"If we were to come forward, it would only incur his displeasure.\"","\"And it’ll be fine if I go?\"","\"At the very least, Assistant Governor Chen has heard of your recent actions in Shu State. He will merely assume that you have come on behalf of the Xiao family.\"","General lifted the teapot, filling both their cups more than halfway, and continued,","\"You can rest assured, sir.","\"Assistant Governor Chen is not only the eldest son of the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen family but also the Imperial Top Scholar appointed by the Holy Emperor himself. No matter how ruthless we might be, we could never scheme against him.","\"Asking you to go this time is truly a helpless move on our part.","\"After all, Assistant Governor Chen... well, his ambitions do not lie in the Imperial Court.\"","Chen Yi did not respond immediately upon hearing this. He stared at the man for a moment before slowly nodding. \"Alright.\"","He understood.","The White Tiger Guard Pavilion Master wanted to use the Xiao family—no, he wanted to use the relationship between him, Chen Yi, and Chen Yunfan—to have an outsider like \"Liu Wu\" deliver a great merit to Chen Yunfan.","It seemed a bit convoluted, but Chen Yi was already certain that the White Tiger Guard was scheming around both him and Chen Yunfan.","If he was the \"Fledgling,\" then what was Chen Yunfan?","A mythical roc soaring ninety thousand miles into the highest heavens?","However, there was one thing Chen Yi believed—Chen Yunfan’s ambitions truly did not lie in Shu State, nor in an official career. He also believed that Chen Yunfan absolutely did not care about the White Tiger Guard. How could someone who constantly talked about the Emperor on his lips ever obey the arrangements of the White Tiger Guard?","They exchanged a few more words of idle chatter.","Before Chen Yi could rise to take his leave, General took two items from his chest pocket and placed them on the table.","\"This one on the left is the secret missive you previously handed over to Lady Tiger, as well as the ’evidence’ of Zhu Hao colluding with the enemy that our White Tiger Guard gathered in Shu State.","\"As for this one on the right...\"","General patted it and said meaningfully, \"This is the share of the silver coins you rightfully earned from scheming against the Ji State Trading Company.\"","Chen Yi glanced at him, then looked at the two items covered in brocade cloth on the table. \"Did Lou Yuxue tell you?\"","\"No.\"","General continued, \"Lady Tiger cares... quite deeply about you, sir. Naturally, she was unwilling to leak the details of your cooperation.\"","\"Simurgh Phoenix?\"","General shook his head again.","\"Neither of them said anything. It was only after receiving orders from the Lord Pavilion Master that I sent someone to investigate their recent actions.","\"This silver was also prepared by Lady Tiger well in advance. I am merely taking the credit for her generosity.\"","At this point, a suggestive smile appeared on General’s face as he looked at Chen Yi.","\"Did you know, sir, that Simurgh Phoenix originally intended to split this sum of silver equally only with Lady Tiger?","\"But Lady Tiger couldn’t bear it and specifically diverted one million taels of silver from her own share to give to you.\"","Chen Yi shot him a look. The fingers resting on the table twitched slightly, and True Essence circulated, pulling the two items into his grasp. He then uncovered them one by one to inspect.","A stack of evidence.","Silver coins... two million taels?","Not waiting for him to speak, General smiled and explained, \"The other one million taels is your remuneration for running this errand for the White Tiger Guard.\"","Chen Yi gave a noncommittal hum, tucking the items into his sleeve. He downed the rest of his tea in one gulp, then stood up.","\"Say ’thank you’ to Lady Tiger for me.\"","General was slightly taken aback. \"You aren’t going to go see her?\"","Chen Yi turned and walked outside. \"The purpose of this trip has already been achieved. What difference does it make whether I see her or not?\"","He understood the underlying meaning in General’s words, and naturally, he also understood Lou Yuxue’s feelings. But his heart was only so big; it could no longer hold too many people. Moreover, this was between him and Lou Yuxue. How could he tolerate an outsider pointing fingers?","As for the purpose of his visit today—the silver coins, as well as preventing Liu Hong, Zhu Hao, and the others from lashing out like cornered beasts—it had indeed been accomplished.","The quiet chamber’s door opened with a CLICK and closed with another CLICK.","General opened his mouth, then broke into a bitter smile. \"Did I just do a bad deed with good intentions?","\"Sigh, the Lord Pavilion Master possesses unparalleled foresight. As a Golden Banner Officer, I truly cannot enter his eyes.\"","He naturally had some selfish motives for acting the way he just did. After all, Lou Yuxue was a spy for the White Tiger Guard and a core member about to be promoted to Golden Banner Officer. If she could form a marital tie with someone like \"Dragon Tiger,\" it would be entirely beneficial and harmless to the White Tiger Guard.","Even if \"Dragon Tiger\" didn’t join the White Tiger Guard, if Lou Yuxue encountered danger in the future, could he possibly stand by and watch her die?","But it seemed this little trick had been seen through by \"Dragon Tiger.\"","\"I hope Lady Tiger doesn’t blame me for being a busybody.","\"Yeah, it’s best if she knows nothing... I really don’t want to make an enemy of another Golden Banner Officer...\"","General shook his head with a bitter smile. After calming down slightly, he took a secret missive from his chest pocket and began to read it. Upon it were clearly written a few lines:","[If he is unwilling, use the name ’Chen Yunfan’ to entice him.]","[If he is still unwilling, then this person cannot be used. I permit you to mobilize everything and kill him!]","General looked at those last two words with a helpless expression.","\"Lord Pavilion Master, you say it so lightly, but do you know that ’Liu Wu’ can already fight those in the Upper Three Grades?","\"And against ’Jackal’ Du Cang, no less...\"","A reputation preceded a man like a shadow preceded a tree.","General considered himself to be merely on par with Du Cang. In a life-and-death struggle, it was hard to say who would win and who would lose. Coupled with the fact that on that night, \"Liu Wu\" not only killed Du Cang but also brought Xiao Wan’er back to the Xiao family completely unscathed. Adding those two feats together, General knew he was inferior. Even if he mobilized everything to kill \"Liu Wu,\" he was afraid it would come at a grievous cost.","Fortunately, \"Liu Wu\" had agreed.","Thinking this, General stood up and made his way to the quiet chamber where Lou Yuxue was. Seeing her forcing a facade of calm, a smile appeared on his face.","\"’Dragon Tiger’ was very satisfied. He took the money and left.\"","Lou Yuxue felt a wave of relief wash over her heart, but her face remained impassive. \"Everything is up to your discretion, sir...\"","...","Capital Prefecture.","In mid-September, the chill in the Northern Territory was much more pronounced than in the southern Shu State. As the fine, misty rain drifted down, it cast a dark sheen over the rows of blue-tiled roofs.","Only the Imperial City, with its red roofs, golden pillars, and exquisitely carved and painted beams, stood majestic and sweeping. Even in this dreary, rainy weather, it remained dazzlingly resplendent.","At this moment, within a study deep inside the Imperial City.","Mist curled up from the incense burner, filling the air with the rich scent of agarwood. Charcoal burned in the heating stove against the wall—smokeless, radiating steady waves of warmth.","Chen Xuanji, wearing a pale mask, sat upright before a Go board, holding a black piece between his fingers and hesitating to place it. Opposite him sat a middle-aged man dressed in dark brocade robes and wearing a Dragon Crown. He had a fair complexion and piercing eyes.","Stroking the beard at the corner of his mouth, the man spoke with a half-smile, \"Xuanji, resign.\"","Chen Xuanji paused at his words, then firmly placed the black piece onto the board. \"Your Majesty declares victory too soon.\"","The middle-aged man glanced at the board. His smile faded slightly as he shook his head.","\"It’s always like this. Xuanji, with your level of skill in Go, I’m afraid you are close to breaking through to the Saint Realm, aren’t you?\"","\"I still need a bit more time.\"","\"Heh. Break through as soon as possible. I am still waiting for you to decide for me whether that blade should swing south or strike north.\"","\"Please be patient, Your Majesty. Within five years, I will ensure that your blade falls exactly where it should!\"","From the corner of his eye, Chen Xuanji swept a glance toward the south. His gaze held neither sorrow nor joy, remaining completely tranquil.","He thought, \"Qingzhou, let your father see what choice you will make.\""]},{"number":532,"title":"Chapter 532 - 310: Brother Is Too Hardworking","paragraphs":["Chen Xuanji’s eyes were calm. Preoccupied with his thoughts, he gathered the Go pieces and the board, arranging them neatly.","Opposite him, a middle-aged man wearing a Dragon Crown simply smiled as he watched his movements without saying a word.","This was Emperor Wei, Wei Kai, also known as Emperor Anhe.","Once Chen Xuanji had finished putting the board away, Emperor Anhe gently waved his hand. Two cups of hot tea instantly materialized on the table.","\"Tell me, when do you plan to ’return’ to Great Wei?\"","Chen Xuanji glanced at his teacup and did not raise his eyes again, as if profound mysteries were hidden within the clear tea.","Five years ago, under the guise of an \"ambassadorial mission to the Western Buddha Country,\" he had hidden himself in the Capital Prefecture to secretly command the White Tiger Guard.","He truly hadn’t gone to the Western Buddha Country, but someone else had gone in his stead.","Now that the situation in the Western Buddha Country had been thoroughly investigated, that person was about to return. This meant Chen Xuanji would have to reappear in the Great Wei Dynasty as well.","\"The sooner, the better,\" Chen Xuanji replied.","\"Oh? I thought you would delay it for a few more days. Why the rush?\"","\"A person who has been away from home for years is always eager to return. If I delay on the road, it will only allow those with ulterior motives to notice something.\"","\"Those with ulterior motives...\" Emperor Anhe scoffed. He picked up his teacup, twisting the lid twice with his other hand, and said, \"Among the Court Officials, there are countless individuals who think highly of themselves, but how many can actually stand shoulder to shoulder with you, Xuanji?\"","Chen Xuanji lowered his head further. On the white tiger pattern mask covering his face, only the faint outline of the character for \"king\" remained visible on its forehead.","\"Your Majesty flatters me.\"","Emperor Anhe glanced at him, took a sip of tea, and smiled. \"You deserve my praise.","\"In the twenty-one years since I ascended the throne, you have schemed and plotted for me, roping in the northern nobility, filling the state treasury, and strengthening Ji State...","\"You are so much better than those useless officials who occupy positions without doing any work.","\"If the Court Officials had even a tenth of your ability, why would I ever worry about my grand ambitions not coming to fruition?\"","Chen Xuanji respectfully raised his teacup with both hands and bowed. \"This subject was merely fulfilling his duty.\"","He then took a small sip of tea to show his gratitude for the Holy Emperor’s reward.","\"Heh, Xuanji, we have known each other as sovereign and subject for many years. Why must you be so reserved in my presence?\"","\"This subject would not dare overstep his bounds.\"","\"Overstep your bounds?\" Emperor Anhe shook his head with a smile. \"You... you.","\"Do as you please. It’s a trivial matter; I simply won’t pay it any mind.\"","Setting down his teacup, Emperor Anhe looked at Chen Xuanji, his smile unwavering as he continued, \"I’ve heard that your son, who married into the Xiao Family, has gained quite a reputation lately. He’s being hailed as the modern ’Poetry Immortal’ of the Great Wei Dynasty, standing alongside the two Poetry Immortals of the previous dynasty, Zhou and Sun.\"","Chen Xuanji paused, then set down his teacup. \"Your Majesty praises him too highly.","\"My son merely possesses a little talent for poetry. It was nothing but good luck that he managed to write that ’Song of the Water Melody’ during the Mid-Autumn Festival.\"","\"Then could his luck be even better, perhaps enough to pass the next imperial examination?\"","\"This subject does not dare speak out of turn.\"","\"Haha... I simply have an appreciation for talent. A grand Calligraphy master who has reached Perfection in the Calligraphy Dao becoming a matrilocal son-in-law for the Xiao Family... his reputation will inevitably suffer a bit.","\"If you are willing, help me persuade him. Serving the Imperial Court is always better than hiding away in an academy as an Instructor.\"","\"This...\"","\"What? As his father, can you not even discipline him?\"","Chen Xuanji hummed softly in agreement. \"There is something Your Majesty does not know. Ever since my son went to Shu State, his temperament has changed significantly. He has become idle.\"","\"Idle? Heh, haha... Then, wouldn’t that mean he’s unable to wield the Xiao Family as a Blade for me?\"","\"Your Majesty, please forgive me. This subject has failed to teach his son properly...\"","Before he could finish, Emperor Anhe waved his hand dismissively. \"Don’t try to brush me off with the same formalities others use on me.","\"If he is unwilling, I have other candidates in mind. It matters not.\"","Chen Xuanji bowed respectfully and said no more. He certainly did not ask about the identities of those other candidates.","Emperor Anhe didn’t elaborate either. Instead, he shifted the topic, \"I summoned you to the palace this time because there is another matter I cannot decide on.","\"The Jing State Liu Family has repeatedly disregarded the law. Do you have a solution, Xuanji?\"","Chen Xuanji raised his head slightly to meet his gaze and pondered for a moment. \"I do have a solution.\"","\"Tell me.\"","\"If Your Majesty can punish Consort Liu, the Jing State Liu Family will naturally not dare to overstep the rules any further.\"","\"Liu... Pick another.\"","\"Then there is only one path left—eliminate them.\"","\"Good. I will leave this matter to you.\"","\"This subject obeys.\"","A short while later.","Chen Xuanji transformed into a streak of rainbow light. In the blink of an eye, he drifted down into the five-story wooden building closest to the Imperial City, heading straight into a dim Quiet Chamber deep on the fourth floor.","Inside this wooden building controlled by the White Tiger Guard, there was a Quiet Chamber belonging to him on every floor. Sometimes he would be on the second floor, sometimes on the fourth. It varied. Let alone the insiders of the White Tiger Guard, even he himself wouldn’t decide beforehand which Quiet Chamber he would use. Was it troublesome? Yes. But Chen Xuanji had long since grown accustomed to such caution.","As soon as his feet touched the ground, Chen Xuanji waved his hand to obscure the windowsill, and the oil lamp on the wall lit up on cue.","The dim yellow flame flickered wildly in the sudden draft, casting shifting, indistinct shadows over his figure. He scanned his surroundings, then slowly walked over to sit behind the desk in the center of the room.","Hidden beneath his mask, his expression was unreadable. Only a steady, measured breath escaped his lips.","\"Phew...\"","He thought, \"Accompanying a sovereign is like accompanying a tiger... The Holy Emperor’s temperament has indeed undergone a drastic change in recent years.\"","Recalling his previous audience with the emperor, a flicker of contemplation crossed Chen Xuanji’s eyes.","The Xiao Family had deeply rooted themselves in Shu State for two hundred years. Even if they were gradually declining, they were not some weak pushovers to be manipulated at will.","He pondered, \"If the ’Fledgling’ fails, who else can take command of the Xiao Family and the Dingyuan Army?","\"The Commander-in-Chief, the Governor, the Inspector General... They have stayed in Shu State for many years and know full well how formidable the Xiao Family is. They will either go all out or do nothing at all.","\"As for the others... The Vermilion Bird?\"","Chen Xuanji had a vague inkling but didn’t delve deeper into the thought. He raised his hand and rang the Bell on the desk."]},{"number":533,"title":"Chapter 533 - 310: Elder Brother Is Too Hardworking","paragraphs":["RING, RING, RING.","Three crisp chimes echoed in the Quiet Chamber. Soon, a figure dressed in a large red robe and wearing a white mask hurried in.","\"Xuan Xing greets the Pavilion Master.\"","\"Is there a reply from Shu State?\"","\"Yes.\"","Xuan Xing rose, kept his posture low, and presented a secret letter with both hands.","Chen Xuanji took it, his gaze narrowing slightly as he read:","[’Dragon Spear’ Liu Wu killed ’Jackal’ Du Cang of the Peacock King Banner and rescued Miss Xiao Wan’er of the Xiao family.]","[In this battle, Liu Wu displayed a Perfect Realm Gun Dao and a Great Success Realm Fist Dao. His aptitude parallels that of Xiao Jinghong, known for his ’Spear and Sword Dual Mastery’, earning him the title of ’Dragon Tiger’.]","[The plot of the Ji State Trading Company was defeated, entirely due to ’Dragon Tiger’s’ intervention. With the help of Miss Cui Qingwu of the Cui family...]","Reaching the end, Chen Xuanji laughed. \"Good, good, good!\"","Although the red-robed Xuan Xing wanted to ask what was so good, he felt as if a massive mountain was pressing down on him, rendering him entirely immobile. Cold sweat instantly soaked his robe.","After a long silence, Chen Xuanji crushed the secret letter he had read multiple times into ash. His voice still carried a smile as he instructed, \"Pass the order to General. Tell him to pull the net in as soon as possible.\"","\"Yes, sir!\"","Feeling as if he had been granted amnesty, Xuan Xing hastily bowed and retreated from the Quiet Chamber.","Once everything quieted down, the amusement in Chen Xuanji’s eyes slowly dissipated. He rested his hands on the desk and tapped lightly.","TAP, TAP, TAP...","The interval between each tap was identical, as was the volume. Before the echo of one tap faded, the next began.","Suddenly, the tapping stopped.","\"My son, don’t let your father down...\"","...","Mid-afternoon. Shu State Prefecture City.","The sun shone brightly in a cloudless sky. The streets and alleys of the prefecture city remained bustling and noisy. This was due to both the death of \"Jackal\" Du Cang and the continuing rise in grain prices at the grain stores.","The price of one stone of refined grain had soared to twenty-one taels of silver. As a result, the commoners who had heard that the Governor’s Office was about to stabilize grain prices couldn’t help but grow anxious.","\"Didn’t they say Lord Liu Hong summoned the people from Lin’s Grain Store and others to discuss matters and order them to lower the grain prices?\"","\"Why did it rise instead of falling today?\"","\"It’s only the first day. Those grain stores probably want to make one last massive profit.\"","\"Just a dying struggle.\"","\"I heard they’ve hoarded no less than half a million stones of grain. Once the prices are stabilized, they’ll likely lose everything.\"","\"Every single one of these unscrupulous merchants deserves to die!\"","While some comforted others and reassured themselves, others were quick to dampen their spirits. A sudden rumor began spreading, sweeping through the streets and alleys of the prefecture city in an incredibly short amount of time.","\"You all shouldn’t celebrate too early.","\"’Jackal’ Du Cang died in Shu State, and so did Lv Jiunan. Do you really think King Landu of the Peacock King Banner will act as if nothing happened?\"","\"Are you saying he’ll actually lead an army here?\"","\"Not ’he will’—he’s already here. I heard something went wrong over at the Ancient Tea-Horse Road.\"","\"How could this be?\"","\"Then... then doesn’t that mean the government’s price stabilization is only temporary? Once the old grain is exhausted, we will still...\"","What would happen to them went without saying.","Chen Yi listened to the surrounding discussions as he calmly walked through the crowd. He had long known that the Ji State Trading Company wouldn’t just sit still and await their doom. Even with Elder Master Xiao and Xiao Jinghong stepping in, they could only temporarily force the grain stores to bow their heads.","As long as they still held the grain, they could eventually sell it, and whatever silver they lost wouldn’t be enough to cripple them. Just like now. By spreading rumors in the streets to fool the commoners, they could drive up the grain prices again and sell off as much as possible.","As for the rest... they were presumably waiting for Li Sanyuan’s reply. However, with Madam stepping in, how could Li Sanyuan possibly escape?","Chen Yi’s thoughts briefly touched upon this before returning to his recent meeting with General. The White Tiger Guard’s renewed invitation. The unfathomable Pavilion Master’s schemes against him and his older brother, Chen Yunfan. And Zhu Hao!","Chen Yi remembered the hint he had received when he first met Chen Yunfan—his brother desired to walk a grand and righteous path of rapid promotion. Since it was a path of rapid promotion, based on his brother’s position in the Governor’s Office, eliminating Liu Hong was clearly the most suitable way to advance further.","Yet, the White Tiger Guard had produced evidence of the crimes committed by Zhu Hao, the Deputy Commander of the Shu State Capital Commandery. Was there a deeper meaning to this?","The chessboard in Chen Yi’s mind trembled. Chen Yunfan, this half-black, half-white chess piece, made him hesitant about his next move. If placed in the corner representing the Governor’s Office, Chen Yunfan could succeed Yang Ye as the Right Governor of Shu State. He would hold greater power, a higher rank, and be able to fully showcase his abilities.","But if the piece were placed in the Capital Commandery... to check and balance the Xiao family? Or perhaps...","After pondering for a moment, the chess piece held by the giant hand in Chen Yi’s mind turned white and landed precisely in the center among several pieces belonging to the Shu State Capital Commandery.","\"The White Tiger Guard’s plot is traceable. Whether it’s me or Chen Yunfan, the ultimate target points straight at the Xiao family, or rather, the Dingyuan Army under their control.","\"However, the current situation has changed. Behind Zhu Hao stands another giant Buddha—Liu Hong.","\"Presumably, Liu Hong wasn’t part of the White Tiger Guard’s original plan. It’s just that he and the Jing State Liu Family have been interfering too much in Shu State recently, so... the Liu family is doomed.\"","Although Chen Yi couldn’t foresee the entirety of the White Tiger Guard’s schemes, understanding one corner allowed him to grasp the general direction. At least within Shu State, he could deduce the approximate outcome.","Therefore, whether it was the Jing State Liu Family or the Shu State Liu Family, anyone who dared to lay hands on the Xiao family would become a thorn in the White Tiger Guard’s side. Even if Chen Yi didn’t inform Elder Master Xiao of everything, the Liu family would still perish.","\"In half a month at the earliest, or two months at the latest, the Liu family will undoubtedly fall.","\"As for my brother... estimating at the fastest pace, he might skyrocket up the ranks within a year. Third Grade? Even Junior Second Grade is possible...\"","It was nothing short of an exaggeration. Such a speed of promotion was rare not only in the Great Wei Dynasty but likely unseen even looking back a thousand or eight hundred years.","Having figured this out, Chen Yi knew how to handle the hot potato in his hands. His brother takes down Zhu Hao, and the Xiao family destroys Liu Hong—fair and just.","\"Let’s hope the White Tiger Guard doesn’t come out to be an eyesore...\"","Chen Yi glanced back before swiftly heading toward Tingyu Pavilion. With his current hearing, since he hadn’t heard Chen Yunfan’s voice at the Governor’s Office, the only remaining possibility was Tingyu Pavilion.","Fifteen minutes later.","Chen Yi arrived outside Tingyu Pavilion. Tilting his bamboo hat slightly to observe his surroundings, he caught the faint sounds coming from inside. Xiao Wan’er, Cui Qingwu, Xie Tingyun, Shen Huatang, Huan’er... Chen Yunfan, Ning Yu, Niu Shan, and... huh?","Chen Yi turned his head toward the eaves of another courtyard at the alley’s entrance. There, a man sat leaning carelessly against the flying eaves, staring straight at him. The man was dressed in a short tunic, appearing to be middle-aged with a face full of thick beard. Seeing Chen Yi appear here, he asked in mild surprise, \"’Dragon Tiger’ Liu Wu?\"","Chen Yi didn’t respond; he simply activated his Qi Observation Skill and looked at him. He felt like he had seen that face somewhere before. Where... The Chen family! He was the Guard Commander of the Chen family—Lin Zhong!","Realizing this, Chen Yi had a sudden epiphany. \"The Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family truly hides crouching tigers and hidden dragons. A mere guard commander possesses an Upper Three Grades Cultivation...\"","With his thoughts spinning rapidly, Chen Yi calmly cupped his hands and said, \"Excuse me, I have urgent matters and request an audience with Assistant Governor Chen.\"","\"You wish to see my young master?\" Lin Zhong looked him up and down, his expression slightly guarded. He wondered inwardly, \"Did he discover that I picked up Lv Jiunan’s corpse?\"","\"May I ask what business Your Excellency ’Dragon Tiger’ has with my young master?\"","\"I have been entrusted by someone. Forgive me, but I cannot disclose the details.\"","\"Oh?\"","Hearing this, Lin Zhong relaxed slightly. As long as it wasn’t about Lv Jiunan, everything was fine. After a moment of thought, he stood up and said, \"Please wait a moment, Your Excellency. I will go and inform my young master.\"","Chen Yi nodded, calmly watching his figure vanish, but raised an eyebrow inwardly. \"A Great Success level of Martial Arts·Step? Or perhaps... Perfection? Tsk, not to be underestimated.\"","As the saying goes, \"All martial arts in the world can be broken, except for speed.\" If a Body Technique was cultivated to the Perfection Realm, its power would be no less formidable than Du Cang’s Black Magic Secret Skill. If one lacked a method to overcome the enemy, defeat and death would only be a matter of time.","While Chen Yi muttered to himself, his Heart Spirit followed Lin Zhong into the middle courtyard of Tingyu Pavilion.","Amidst the SWISH SWISH of ringing swords, it felt as though wisps of sharp Sword Intent were tearing through the air. Looking at the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism being stirred up around him, a small smile touched the corners of Chen Yi’s mouth.","\"My brother is truly hardworking. He didn’t go to the Government Office to work today, choosing instead to stay in Tingyu Pavilion to practice Martial Arts.\"","However, before his smile could fade, a crystalline, shining light suddenly materialized before his eyes, accompanied by a frantic, urgent voice shouting, \"Young Master, don’t!\"","The light coalesced into a delicate short sword, shooting fiercely toward Chen Yi. Wherever it passed, its brilliance shone like a rainbow. It wasn’t blindingly bright, yet it carried an awe-inspiring might.","Chen Yi chuckled in exasperation. Facing the incoming sword light, he pointed out with One Finger.","A flash of Jin Guang appeared and vanished. Along with it, the sword light dissipated entirely, as if it had never existed at all.","\"Assistant Governor Chen, what magnificent Swordsmanship...\""]},{"number":534,"title":"Chapter 534 - 311: Your Brother Will Play Along with Your Act","paragraphs":["\"Assistant Governor Chen, good Swordsmanship?\"","The slightly mocking tone displeased Chen Yunfan. He almost blurted out, \"Is this how you treat your older brother?\" Fortunately, his rationality prevailed. His Sword Dao had not yet broken through to the Realm of Perfection, so it was completely normal that it couldn’t compare to Chen Yi’s Spear Dao. Furthermore, with Lin Zhong, Cui Qingwu, Xiao Wan’er, and the others currently in the estate, it was highly inconvenient for him to reveal Liu Wu’s true identity.","But doing nothing left him feeling extremely frustrated. Just as Chen Yunfan was about to thrust his sword again, Lin Zhong finally made a move. He grabbed Chen Yunfan’s arm and urged, \"Young Master, don’t! Please don’t attack again!\"","After all, that was \"Dragon Tiger\" Liu Wu, a ruthless character who had just slain \"Jackal\" Du Cang, a Third Grade Realm expert, with only a Fifth Grade Realm Cultivation. Coupled with his Perfect Realm Gun Dao and Great Success Fist Dao, even two Chen Yunfans wouldn’t be his match!","Chen Yunfan cast him a sidelong glance, snorted, and sheathed his Long Sword. \"Invite him in to talk.\"","He thought, \"Brother Yi, once I achieve Sword Dao Perfection, I will definitely seek you out for a duel.\"","Seeing this, Chun Ying hurried forward. \"Young Master, I will go prepare hot water for you to bathe and change clothes.\"","Only then did Chen Yunfan realize he was shirtless. He nodded in agreement, turning to lead Chun Ying back to the guest room.","Ning Yu and Niu Mountain consciously stood guard outside the door. Although they hadn’t heard the visitor’s identity, anyone who could block Chen Yunfan’s strike, Silent and Unnoticed, was certainly not to be underestimated.","At this moment, Cui Qingwu, having heard the commotion, flew over. When she saw Lin Zhong, she was visibly taken aback. \"Commander Lin?\"","Lin Zhong naturally recognized her as well. He smiled and cupped his fist in greeting. \"Lin Zhong pays his respects to Miss Cui.\"","Cui Qingwu’s anxious expression softened. Scanning the area and seeing Chen Yunfan disappearing into the guest room, she couldn’t help but ask, \"Who was Brother Yunfan fighting just now?\"","Remembering that Liu Wu had mentioned having important matters to discuss outside the gates, Lin Zhong hesitated slightly. \"A good friend of the Young Master came to visit. I hope you can forgive us for startling you, Miss Cui.\"","\"A good friend? Do I know him?\"","\"You should know him. The visitor is ’Dragon Tiger’ Liu Wu, who is currently famous throughout Shu State.\"","\"Liu Wu?\" Cui Qingwu blurted out. \"What is that bastard doing here?\"","Without realizing it, she had adopted Lou Yuxue’s \"honorific\" for Liu Wu. It wasn’t that she held a grudge over the Poisoning incident where Liu Wu knocked her out. Rather, it was out of wariness after interacting with him recently. Especially over the past few days, seeing how the Ji State Trading Company and several grain merchant companies were being schemed against without even realizing it, she felt that Liu Wu’s mind was truly terrifying.","Lin Zhong’s eyes flickered. \"Bastard?\"","\"I...\" Before she could answer, Cui Qingwu suddenly recalled his previous words. \"Commander Lin, did you just say that bas... that ’Dragon Tiger’ came looking for Brother Yunfan?\"","Seeing her anxious and irritable expression, Lin Zhong grew curious. \"Miss Cui, do you know Liu Wu?\"","\"He... I’ve dealt with him a few times before.\" Thinking of Liu Wu’s Cultivation and a belly full of schemes, Cui Qingwu inevitably felt somewhat annoyed. She really wanted to know why he was looking for Chen Yunfan.","She wondered, \"Could it be that he realized I’m not going to give him the silver, so he came knocking on the door?\"","Before Cui Qingwu could continue probing, Chen Yunfan’s voice rang out from inside the guest room. \"Don’t worry, Qingwu. ’Dragon Tiger’ coming here should mean he has an urgent matter that requires my help.\"","Cui Qingwu froze. \"Brother Yunfan, is he really your good friend?\"","\"Of course. We are old friends who have known each other for many years.\"","\"This... Alright.","\"But please be careful, Brother Yunfan. That... that ’Dragon Tiger’ is extremely deceitful. Be careful not to fall into his trap.\"","Looking at Cui Qingwu through the window, Chen Yunfan guessed she must have had contact with Chen Yi. Or rather, she had contact with Chen Yi under his alias, \"Liu Wu.\"","He wondered, \"Did they meet through the White Tiger Guard? Brother Yi is truly daring. To think he actually dared to provoke that bunch of Living Yamas from the White Tiger Guard.\"","Out loud, Chen Yunfan reassured her, \"Relax, I know what I’m doing. Besides, with Uncle Zhong standing guard here, I doubt he’d dare to try anything funny.\" After a pause, he continued, \"You head back first and continue discussing the Medical Dao Academy with the Eldest Miss of the Xiao Family. We can talk about this in detail later.\"","In truth, he needed to ask Cui Qingwu exactly how Brother Yi had gotten mixed up with the White Tiger Guard.","Hearing this, Cui Qingwu glanced at Lin Zhong and felt slightly more at ease. \"In that case, I will take my leave first.\"","\"Uncle Zhong, please invite that ’Dragon Tiger’ to have a seat for a moment...\" Chen Yunfan’s voice drifted out.","Listening to the voice fading behind her, Cui Qingwu returned to the backyard, weighed down by her thoughts.","Xiao Wan’er was standing outside the guest room door, accompanied by Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang. Seeing Cui Qingwu’s expression, her heart tightened. \"Little Sister Qingwu, nothing happened, right?\"","Having survived a calamity, Xiao Wan’er was much more cautious than before. Although she wasn’t exactly at the point of being once bitten, twice shy, this was Tingyu Pavilion after all, and she didn’t want to implicate others because of herself.","Cui Qingwu forced a smile. \"Brother Yunfan’s good friend came to visit...\" Before she could finish, she saw Xiao Wan’er’s eyes light up, so she shifted her words. \"Sister Wan’er, you know him too.\"","\"I know him too... Is it Qingzhou?\"","\"No, it’s the man who rescued you the night before last.\"","\"He... he came here?\"","Xiao Wan’er’s beautiful eyes widened. She and Chen Yi had been apart for barely over an hour, yet she never expected him to come here. Moreover, he came to see Chen Yunfan under the identity of \"Dragon Tiger\" Liu Wu. Fortunately, she had a frank discussion with Chen Yi today and learned a few things. So, even though she was puzzled at the moment, she didn’t let it show.","Cui Qingwu smiled and nodded. \"It is indeed him. Sister Wan’er, I presume you must have a rather close relationship with him?\"","\"Ah, I... no, not at all. It was my first time meeting him too.\""]},{"number":535,"title":"Chapter 535 - 311: I, Your Brother, Will Play Along With Your Act","paragraphs":["That wasn’t wrong.","Strictly speaking about \"Liu Wu,\" it truly was Xiao Wan’er’s first time meeting him.","\"Oh, come on! Regardless of how many times you’ve met, the fact that he risked his life to save you means you two must have some kind of connection.","\"Sister Wan’er, how about... how about we go over there to see him later?\"","\"No, we can’t.\"","Xiao Wan’er shook her head repeatedly. She knew Chen Yi was here for a specific purpose, so it was naturally out of the question to visit him rashly.","\"Oh, but he’s your savior after all! Sister Wan’er, don’t you want to meet him at least?\"","\"No...\"","After being relentlessly pestered by Cui Qingwu, Xiao Wan’er said helplessly, \"Actually, the reason I don’t want to see him is because... because my grandfather wants me to marry him...\"","\"Huh?\"","\"Sister Wan’er, then what are your feelings for...\"","\"None. It won’t happen. I won’t marry him.\"","Hearing this, Cui Qingwu understood her thoughts. She stepped forward, took her hand, and playfully apologized. However, she didn’t feel too disappointed despite failing to achieve her goal. With Xiao Wan’er here, if that Liu Wu dared to harbor any crooked thoughts, he couldn’t blame Cui Qingwu for being ruthless.","As they spoke, they entered the wing room one after another. However, because of this little interlude, both Xiao Wan’er and Cui Qingwu were somewhat absent-minded. One was distracted because of Chen Yi, and the other because of Chen Yunfan.","\"Sister Wan’er, the Medical Dao Academy has already started construction. Do you know when it will be finished?\"","\"At most a year, at least two years...\"","\"Huh?\"","\"...Forgive me, Little Sister Qingwu. It should be completed within two months...\"","\"Do you have any leads on the Physicians you mentioned earlier, Little Sister Qingwu?\"","\"You can count on me for the medicinal herbs...\"","Seeing how distracted they both were, Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang exchanged a glance.","\"Junior Sister, do you think we guessed wrong? The person the Eldest Miss fancies isn’t the Second Son-in-law, but that ’Dragon Tiger’?\"","\"It’s possible...\"","Meanwhile, sitting quietly in the parlor, Chen Yi naturally overheard the conversation coming from the inner courtyard. He felt a sudden urge to laugh. Cui Qingwu aside, he hadn’t expected the usually gentle and dignified Xiao Wan’er to have such a cute side. However, Chen Yi knew that his sudden arrival would inevitably cause Xiao Wan’er to overthink. He was already used to it.","In another room, Chen Yunfan changed into a fresh set of brocade clothes, letting Chun Ying arrange his accessories and hairpieces. He paid no attention to the conversation between Cui Qingwu and the others; all his focus was on Chen Yi in the outer room.","Even after racking his brain, he couldn’t figure out why Chen Yi had come to find him. He couldn’t possibly be here specifically to reveal his true identity, could he?","He thought, \"It better not be. Otherwise, how will I get my revenge on you for keeping secrets?\"","Chen Yunfan was probably getting a bit obsessed. Whenever he thought about how miserably and how long Chen Yi had deceived him—and how he had even wasted his energy running over to help—he was furious. Therefore, he made up his mind to give Chen Yi a taste of his own medicine.","Especially now that their positions were reversed—he was the one hiding in the shadows, while Chen Yi was out in the open. He knew Chen Yi’s identity, but Chen Yi didn’t know that he had already found out. This was his chance.","In the future, when he defeated Chen Yi in martial arts, he would definitely laugh out loud three times and declare, \"Brother Yi, oh Brother Yi, I already knew everything you were doing.","\"You thought you were hiding it so well! Hahaha! I was just playing along with your little act all this time.\"","Only then would Chen Yunfan be able to \"avenge his great grievance,\" and he could enjoy the spectacular expression on Chen Yi’s face while he was at it. Just thinking about it put him in an excellent mood.","Chun Ying naturally had no idea about any of this. She only felt that his changing expressions were very bizarre at the moment. One moment he was frowning, the next he was grinning foolishly, and then he would suddenly gnash his teeth. She didn’t know who he was directing it all at.","\"Young Master, when did you meet ’Dragon Tiger’?\"","Chen Yunfan paused at her words. His expression smoothed over as he adjusted his cuffs and said, \"A busy man like me wouldn’t know a Jianghu ruffian like him.\"","\"Then...\"","\"No ’thens.’ Go brew some tea.\"","Not waiting for Chun Ying to ask anything else, Chen Yunfan adjusted his sleeves once more, left the wing room, and headed straight for the outer parlor. Helpless, Chun Ying could only go and brew the tea.","A short while later, Chen Yunfan arrived in the parlor. Without even glancing at Chen Yi, he walked straight over and sat down on the Grandmaster’s Chair in the seat of honor. Lin Zhong naturally took his place standing behind him.","Chen Yi watched the two of them. His gaze landed on Chen Yunfan as he clasped his fists and said in a flat tone, \"Jianghu ruffian ’Liu Wu’ greets Assistant Governor Chen.\"","He thought, \"Jianghu ruffian?\"","Chen Yunfan secretly curled his lip, realizing that his earlier conversation with Chun Ying had been overheard.","He thought, \"So what if he knows?\"","Seeing Chen Yi’s calm and indifferent demeanor, a wave of fury immediately boiled within him.","\"Brother... Liu, you’re too polite.\"","The word \"Brother\" almost made Chen Yunfan shatter his teeth from gritting them so hard. Yet, he couldn’t lash out.","He thought, \"Brother Yi, just you wait!\"","Seeing him with his chin held high, Chen Yi thought that his older brother hadn’t changed a bit; he always put on a proud front in front of anyone.","\"That sword strike from earlier was incredibly powerful, Assistant Governor Chen. I hadn’t expected you to possess such impressive Martial Arts Cultivation.\"","\"It doesn’t compare to yours, Brother Liu. I merely practice this Swordsmanship in my spare time.","\"Just to keep fit! Haha, just to keep fit.\"","Let alone Chen Yi, even Chen Yunfan himself didn’t believe those words.","Seeing the atmosphere turn inexplicably awkward, Lin Zhong spoke up from the side to remind him, \"Lord Dragon Tiger, you mentioned earlier that you had urgent business to discuss with my young master. Please speak plainly.\"","Chen Yi gave an affirmative grunt. Without any nonsense, he took the cloth bag containing Zhu Hao’s criminal evidence from his chest pocket and placed it on the table.","\"Someone entrusted me to deliver these to Assistant Governor Chen.\"","Chen Yunfan raised an eyebrow. \"You’re delivering something?\"","\"Assistant Governor Chen will know once he takes a look.\"","With that, Chen Yi lightly tapped the table. The cloth bag immediately flew toward Chen Yunfan. Catching sight of a faint trace of golden spear aura hidden within it, Chen Yunfan secretly grimaced.","He thought, \"Damn it, Brother Yi is as vindictive as ever.\"","Despite his thoughts, Chen Yunfan’s movements weren’t slow. He slowly raised his palm, gathering his True Essence and Sword Intent as he grasped the flying cloth bag."]},{"number":536,"title":"Chapter 536 - 311: Your Brother Will Play Along With Your Act","paragraphs":["CRACK. A crisp sound rang out.","Chen Yunfan’s figure remained motionless, but the Grandmaster’s Chair beneath him was pushed back half a step by the Power radiating from the cloth bag.","Lin Zhong frowned. \"Lord Dragon Tiger, what are you doing?\"","Before Chen Yi could reply, Chen Yunfan waved the cloth bag in his hand and smiled. \"Uncle Zhong, there’s no need to say more. Brother Liu is just exchanging martial arts pointers with me.\"","His expression was relaxed, without the slightest abnormality. However, his feet had already gripped the ground tightly; it was just hidden by his boots so others couldn’t see.","Chen Yi nodded slightly. \"It is impolite not to reciprocate. Assistant Governor Chen has indeed practiced excellent Swordsmanship.\"","\"You flatter me...\" Chen Yunfan made a mental note of this offense from Chen Yi while opening the cloth bag to take a look.","After flipping through a few pages, his brows instantly furrowed, and he shot a sharp glare at Chen Yi. \"Is... is this for me? From whom?\"","Chen Yi lightly uttered three words, \"White Tiger Guard.\"","He naturally wouldn’t hide it, as he already disliked the White Tiger Guard secretly plotting against him and Chen Yunfan. At the same time, he wanted to see Chen Yunfan’s reaction upon hearing this.","\"The White Tiger Guard?\" Chen Yunfan subconsciously looked toward the inner residence, inevitably guessing that it was Cui Qingwu’s doing.","But after a moment of thought, he decided it wasn’t. Although Cui Qingwu cared about his future, she should know his temperament and wouldn’t do something so underhanded. Therefore, there was only one answer—the White Tiger Guard was placing a bet on him!","Beside him, Lin Zhong’s expression remained unchanged.","Observing their expressions, Chen Yi understood clearly. His older brother likely didn’t know the inside story either. It was Lin Zhong who seemed to know something.","After sitting in silence for a moment, a cold sneer appeared on Chen Yunfan’s face. \"I wonder which Banner Officer of the White Tiger Guard Brother Liu might be?\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"None of them. I came here merely because I made a deal with the White Tiger Guard, nothing more.\"","\"What kind of deal?\"","\"Forgive me, Assistant Governor Chen, but I have no comment on that.\"","Chen Yunfan tossed the cloth bag onto the table and snorted. \"Let me guess. You rescued the eldest young miss of the Xiao Family from Du Cang the other day, so you must know the Xiao Family’s situation. Approaching the White Tiger Guard is likely for the Xiao Family’s sake, isn’t it? Is it about the Poshisu Country’s Peacock King Banner, or those petty schemers in Shu State?\"","Seeing him guess the general situation in just a few words, Chen Yi inwardly praised his older brother’s extraordinary intellect while replying aloud, \"I won’t trouble Assistant Governor Chen with the details. I only came here to hand this over to you. How you handle it is entirely up to you.\"","\"Now that this is in my hands, it’s naturally up to me. However... if I were to burn all of this, how would Brother Liu respond?\"","\"It has nothing to do with me.\"","The ones who should be having a headache were the White Tiger Guard. Thinking this, Chen Yi stood up, cupped his fists, and said, \"The items have been delivered. I will take my leave now.\"","Chen Yunfan paused but didn’t stop him, simply waving his hand as a farewell. Seeing this, Chen Yi turned and left decisively.","Only Lin Zhong followed to keep an eye on him, returning only after he was certain the man had gone far away.","\"Young Master, what he gave you...\"","Before he could finish, Chen Yunfan said indifferently, \"Good things that you were hoping to see.\"","Lin Zhong had roughly guessed what it was and didn’t dare say more. The last time he had brought Lv Jiunan’s corpse here, he was severely scolded by Chen Yunfan. Naturally, he knew exactly how Chen Yunfan felt upon discovering the White Tiger Guard’s scheme.","To his surprise, after a brief moment, Chen Yunfan suddenly burst into laughter.","\"It seems everyone is hoping for me to climb higher. Good, very good! Then I shall fulfill your wishes!\"","After his laughter subsided, he looked at Lin Zhong. \"Uncle Zhong, is Lv Jiunan’s corpse still here?\"","Lin Zhong’s heart skipped a beat. \"It is...\"","\"Bring it along. I’m going to take him to the Government Office to claim the reward!\""]},{"number":537,"title":"Chapter 537 - 312: Madam Is Too Kind","paragraphs":["How would Chen Yunfan choose?","Chen Yi didn’t calculate it carefully; there were only two possible outcomes.","Either he would take the evidence of the Capital Commandery’s Zhu Hao’s crimes and report it to the Imperial Court in exchange for a meteoric rise in his career. Or he would turn a blind eye and remain an Imperial Top Scholar who treated power and influence like dirt.","Regardless of the outcome, Chen Yi could accept it.","It just meant he would have to work a little harder in the future—if Chen Yunfan became the blade the Imperial Court swung at the Xiao Family, then Chen Yi would simply cut down the one wielding that blade.","As for who that person might be... Chen Yi had his guesses. It was none other than the White Tiger Guard Pavilion Master, the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family, or perhaps the Holy Emperor seated upon the throne.","Fortunately, there was still time, and he was still in Shu State.","Once the chessboard in his mind fully took shape and gained momentum, the lands of Shu State might not become an impenetrable fortress, but they would certainly leave anyone trying to meddle with it nowhere to hide.","After wandering about until dusk, Chen Yi finally strolled leisurely back to the Xiao Family’s home.","Just as he reached the entrance, Xiao Wan’er’s carriage also drove through the estate gates. Seeing that Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang were driving the carriage, Chen Yi stopped and stood to the side.","While waiting to return to the inner courtyard with Xiao Wan’er, he looked toward the porter’s lodge and asked Third Steward Lu Guan, Wang Lixing, and the others, feigning ignorance, \"I haven’t seen Uncle Gui for several days. Is he no longer in the estate?\"","Lu Guan smiled bitterly and replied, \"Mr. Chen, you might not know this, but on the day the Eldest Miss had her accident, Uncle Gui returned to the estate and then disappeared.\"","Wang Lixing added with a nod, \"We’ve searched every corner of the estate but similarly found no trace of him. We only know that after he returned that day, he went to the backyard...\"","Liu Si’er, who was standing to the side, looked at the group before letting his gaze fall on Chen Yi. He chimed in, \"Because of this, we even went to his home to look for him, but there was still no sign of him. Who knows where he went.","\"Perhaps... perhaps he also ran into Du Cang...\"","Liu Si’er considered himself the one who best understood Uncle Gui’s true identity among them, so he inevitably guessed that the White Tiger Guard had made new arrangements for Uncle Gui. Thus, saying this was his way of covering for him.","Chen Yi shook his head with pity. \"Uncle Gui... he was also a pitiful man.\"","But a pitiful person always had something detestable about them. Not to mention disregarding the Old Master’s kindness, Uncle Gui had also become Du Cang’s puppet and ended up having his corpse blasted to pieces by Chen Yi’s spear. He died a truly tragic death.","Hearing this, Liu Si’er felt a sense of sorrow, lamenting the feeling that \"when the hare dies, the hound is boiled.\" Thinking back to a few months ago, the Xiao Family still had two Silver Banner Officers and several Iron Banner Officers. But now, those who hadn’t died had left. He didn’t know when he might follow in their footsteps.","After a few words of idle chatter, once Xiao Wan’er stepped down from the carriage, Chen Yi greeted Lu Guan and the others before taking a few quick steps to the front of the carriage.","\"Wan’er, did the discussion with Miss Cui go smoothly today?\"","Seeing him smiling as gently as usual, Xiao Wan’er gave him a reproachful glare. She wanted to ask him, \"You were also at Tingyu Pavilion this afternoon, so you should know, right?\"","Fortunately, Xiao Wan’er only thought this in her heart; after all, she had to cover for Chen Yi.","\"It went quite smoothly,\" she said. \"Little Sister Qingwu will find several Physicians in a few days. Right now, aside from the fact that a candidate for the academy dean hasn’t been decided yet, we can already start pushing forward with the other matters.\"","Chen Yi understood her look and smiled with a tacit understanding. \"With Uncle Kang keeping an eye on the academy, all that’s left is to start drafting the academy’s ’Medical Canon,’ ’Regulations,’ and the like.\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded lightly and walked ahead. \"According to what Little Sister Qingwu said, the character of those Physicians is excellent, but it’ll be difficult for them to take the lead. Compiling the ’Medical Canon’ might be...\"","Chen Yi naturally understood this point.","The Medical Dao, after all, wasn’t like Martial Arts or Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting. Its purpose was to cure illnesses and save lives, allowing for not a shred of carelessness.","The academy’s \"Medical Canon\" was the same. Rigor was of the utmost importance. Only after that could they consider integrating the strengths of various schools of thought, and organizing prescriptions, medicinal materials, pharmacology, and medical cases. Even a Medical Saint Hand in the Minor Success Realm would probably find it difficult to take on the role of the academy’s dean.","Thinking of all this, Chen Yi muttered inwardly, \"In the end, I’ll likely have to do it myself.\"","He then said, \"I’ve asked Ma Liangcai previously; once the academy is built, he can also go there to serve as an Instructor.\"","\"Divine Doctor... Ma?\" Xiao Wan’er smiled winsomely, tilted her head to look at him, and voiced her approval. \"It would naturally be for the best if Divine Doctor Ma can come.\"","She knew that Chen Yi stood behind Ma Liangcai. Ma Liangcai going to the Medical Dao Academy meant that Chen Yi would also involve himself in the academy’s affairs.","In all fairness, in Xiao Wan’er’s heart, the best candidate for the academy’s dean was Chen Yi. But she knew that Chen Yi didn’t plan to reveal his true talents and knowledge anytime soon. A secret was a secret, after all. Settling for the next best thing, Ma Liangcai serving as an Instructor at the academy was already the best outcome.","However, Xiao Wan’er couldn’t help but feel somewhat embarrassed in her heart. For her sake, Chen Yi had first established Hundred Herbs Hall, and then offered strategies to propose the Medical Dao Academy. Now, under the circumstances where the candidate for dean hadn’t been decided, they still needed Chen Yi to lend a helping hand in secret.","Feeling An Xin, Xiao Wan’er was also very grateful to Chen Yi.","\"Thank you... Chen Yi.\"","Chen Yi tilted his head to look at her. Guessing her thoughts, he smiled and shook his head. \"We are family; there’s no need for such formalities.","\"Besides, Ma Liangcai is a Physician at the Medicine Hall to begin with. The fact that you agreed to let him serve as an Instructor at the Medical Dao Academy is truly a stroke of good fortune for him.\"","Xiao Wan’er knew she had lost her composure. She murmured a response and buried half of her face into her cloak. Warmth flowed from her chest throughout her entire body, not only dispelling the bitter cold but also bringing two rosy clouds to her cheeks.","Finally meeting the right person—it was probably exactly like this.","Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang followed behind them. No matter how suspicious they were, they didn’t discover anything at this moment. How could they have imagined that the matter of a Medical Dao Academy could hide so many twists and turns?","Before long, the four of them crossed the garden in the middle courtyard and passed in front of Qingjing Residence.","Xiao Wan’er was just hesitating over whether she should go pay her respects to the Old Master when she saw Chen Yi stop by her side."]},{"number":538,"title":"Chapter 538 - 312: Madam is Too Kind-Hearted","paragraphs":["She paused. \"Chen Yi, are you coming to see Grandfather with me...\"","Before she could finish, Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang suddenly looked up at the sky and whispered a warning, \"Miss Wan’er, Miss Jinghong has returned.\"","\"Jinghong?\" Xiao Wan’er was slightly stunned. Both she and Chen Yi looked up.","Xiao Jinghong descended directly into the central courtyard, standing atop a flying longsword while carrying a man with a cloth sack over his head in one hand.","She had spotted them earlier. Upon landing, she nodded in greeting. \"Wan’er, Chen Yi.\"","Xiao Wan’er asked in surprise, \"Jinghong?\"","Chen Yi feigned surprise. \"Jinghong, how did you get back so quickly?\"","As he spoke, his gaze swept over the hooded captive, seemingly by chance. He did not need to guess; this man was undoubtedly Li Sanyuan of the Ji State Trading Company.","Xiao Jinghong replied, \"I need to make a trip to the Guangyuan Capital Commandery. I’m just stopping by to rest on the way.\"","She then tossed the captive to Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang, issuing her orders. \"Take him to the Punishment Hall’s inner prison and keep a strict watch over him. No one is allowed to visit or interrogate him without my or Grandfather’s orders.\"","\"Yes, Ma’am.\"","After Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang left, a slight smile appeared beneath Xiao Jinghong’s half-armor mask. She looked at Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er. \"Wan’er, Chen Yi, I’m going to see Grandfather. Would you like to come along?\"","Hearing this, Xiao Wan’er suppressed the ripples of emotion in her heart and smiled gently. \"Business comes first. I will come pay my respects to Grandfather tomorrow.\"","Chen Yi did the same. \"Jinghong, I still need to read a bit and prepare for the Annual Examination.\"","Xiao Jinghong glanced at them and did not insist. After a brief exchange of pleasantries, she headed to the Qingjing Residence alone.","Seeing her disappear from sight, Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er exchanged a look and silently returned to the backyard.","Xiao Wan’er felt a bit guilty. If her body were not already as cold as ice, the deathly pallor of her face earlier would have given her away.","Chen Yi, however, remained completely composed. He first escorted Xiao Wan’er back to Jiaxing Garden before returning to Spring Lotus Garden.","It was much as he had expected. Xiao Jinghong had successfully met Li Sanyuan and had likely already obtained evidence of the illicit trade between the Ji State Trading Company and King Landu. As for whether that evidence could implicate Liu Hong, that would depend on Xiao Jinghong and Elder Master Xiao’s abilities.","However, two things had caught Chen Yi off guard.","First, Xiao Jinghong had just mentioned Guangyuan County. Her target could only be Zhu Hao, the Deputy Commander of the Capital Commandery. This aligned perfectly with the target of the \"evidence\" Chen Yunfan had obtained. If Xiao Jinghong went directly to Guangyuan County and captured Zhu Hao, the White Tiger Guard’s plan to let Chen Yunfan climb the ranks by stepping on Zhu Hao would likely fail. The outcome would simply depend on who struck first.","As for the second discrepancy...","Chen Yi turned his head toward the Punishment Hall and sighed inwardly. He thought, \"Jinghong is still too kind-hearted. For someone like Li Sanyuan, how could it be enough just to make him confess the inner workings of the Ji State Trading Company and lock onto Liu Hong or Zhu Hao? It would be good to put this trash to use. Those few grain merchants don’t have many silver coins, but they have plenty of grain. It would be a pity to let such a good opportunity go to waste.\"","After a moment of thought, a smile crept onto Chen Yi’s face. He thought, \"You don’t know the cost of firewood and rice until you run a household. Jinghong is kind-hearted, but I am not.\"","Having made his decision, Chen Yi gave Xiaodie a few instructions to prepare dinner, while he took Xiao Wuge to the study to read.","\"Chen Yi, is Jinghong back?\"","\"Yes, she’s back.\"","\"Then she won’t leave again, will she?\"","\"Probably not... I think?\" Chen Yi couldn’t say for sure.","Knowing Xiao Jinghong’s temperament, it was entirely possible she would leave the Prefecture City that very night and rush to Guangyuan County. \"Just wait patiently...\"","...","Inside the Qingjing Residence.","Elder Master Xiao, Xiao Jinghong, and Xiao Jing sat formally in the main hall.","Sitting at the head of the room, Elder Master Xiao listened to Xiao Jinghong’s report. Even though he already knew what Liu Hong and Zhu Hao had done, he still couldn’t help but burn with rage.","\"How dare they commit such treasonous acts? How can they face the millions of citizens in Shu State, and how can they justify the official robes they wear?\"","Elder Master Xiao growled in uncontrollable fury. \"That Liu Gongmo... he nearly died at Mengshui Pass all those years ago. It was the soldiers at the pass who risked their lives to save him! Is this how he repays the people of Shu State?","\"And Zhu Hao! That bastard! Embezzling the Dingyuan Army’s funds and provisions, while secretly... secretly... he deserves a thousand deaths!\"","Xiao Jinghong lowered her eyes, listening silently as he vented his anger. Xiao Jing did the same.","A long while later, Elder Master Xiao finally stopped shouting. He smashed the table beside him with a single slap and sat panting heavily, looking at Xiao Jinghong with bloodshot eyes. \"What do you plan to do next?\"","Xiao Jinghong had come prepared and spoke calmly. \"Liu Hong has hidden himself very well. Even if Li Sanyuan is confident he can implicate the second son of the Liu family, I’m afraid it will still be very difficult to find direct evidence to bring down Liu Hong.","\"That is, unless the information passed on by ’Dragon Tiger’ is true, and Zhu Lingchuan really does possess evidence of Liu Hong’s treason. Therefore, I plan to go to Guangyuan first to prevent Zhu Hao from doing something desperate when cornered.\"","Hearing this, Elder Master Xiao’s expression softened slightly. He pondered for a moment before instructing Xiao Jing, \"In the near future, have the Hidden Guards keep a close eye on the Noble Families and Government Office officials who are on good terms with Liu Hong.\"","Xiao Jing bowed in acknowledgment. \"Recently, due to the Annual Examination, all the Noble Families and officials close to Liu Hong have already been recorded.\" He paused, then asked, \"What about Liu Hong himself?\"","A hint of sorrow appeared on Elder Master Xiao’s face as he shook his head. \"He is an extremely shrewd man and will definitely be on guard. With Jinghong absent, it is inconvenient for the Hidden Guards to make a move.\"","Xiao Jinghong nodded. \"My decision to leave Zhu Lingchuan alone for now is also to avoid alerting the enemy.\"","Elder Master Xiao sighed, his emotions finally settling down. \"Once Jinghong returns, I will submit a memorial to the Imperial Court. This time... even if it turns Shu State upside down, I will see Liu Hong dead!\"","Xiao Jinghong understood what he meant by turning Shu State \"upside down.\" Once Liu Hong was convicted, the position of Governor of Shu State would be left vacant, and the Imperial Court would naturally make new arrangements. It was still unknown whether the situation then would be for better or worse.","\"Grandfather, I’ve been thinking. What ’Dragon Tiger’ said earlier is correct—one can be a thief for a thousand days, but one cannot guard against a thief for a thousand days. If our Xiao family is too weak outwardly, those people will only think we are easy targets.\"","Elder Master Xiao paused upon hearing this. \"What do you intend to do?\"","\"The strength of the Hidden Guards in the estate is ultimately a bit too low, especially considering what happened to Wan’er the other day. I have considered it carefully and wish to recruit some new people.\"","Xiao Jinghong glanced at the visibly embarrassed Xiao Jing, her tone unwavering. \"I am not targeting the Hidden Guards specifically. The same goes for the Personal Guards in the estate.\"","She had been pondering this matter ever since Chen Yi mentioned the inadequate security of the estate to her. After much thought, there were only two ways to quickly fill the shortage of experts in the estate. The first was to select elites from the Dingyuan Army. The second was to recruit people from the Jianghu. For instance, the Celestial Sect or the Wind and Rain Tower. Or perhaps the former servants of her master, Li Wudang.","Elder Master Xiao pondered for a moment. Though feeling somewhat despondent inwardly, he still nodded. \"Since that is the case, then do as you say.\"","Xiao Jinghong stood up and bowed. \"I understand the gravity of the situation. I will now hurry to Guangyuan County.\"","\"What? You finally managed to come back, and you aren’t going to have a simple meal with Qingzhou before you leave?\"","\"This...\"","Elder Master Xiao waved his hand, brokering no argument. \"Half a day or a day won’t make a difference. Go on back.\"","Xiao Jinghong hesitated, then nodded. \"I will go right away.\"","After she left the Qingjing Residence, Elder Master Xiao looked at Xiao Jing. \"You may go and make the arrangements as well. Remember to be careful.\"","\"Yes, Marquis!\"","Before long, the Qingjing Residence fell completely silent. Elder Master Xiao sat quietly for a moment, glanced at the shattered table beside him, and stood up with a sigh.","\"Shu State... Shu State... The Holy Emperor is very wary of our Xiao family...\"","...","Xiao Jinghong’s return to Spring Lotus Garden overjoyed Xiao Wuge, who pulled her aside and chattered endlessly. One moment he talked about amusing anecdotes from his Martial Arts practice, and the next he asked Xiao Jinghong to guide him on his recent progress.","The atmosphere was lively and filled with cheerful laughter. Although Xiao Jinghong didn’t show it, Chen Yi could tell that she was in a good mood.","However, happy times were always short-lived. After finishing dinner, Xiao Jinghong had Xiaodie help her change into a set of light clothes and packed her bags.","Seeing this, Chen Yi naturally understood her intentions. \"Jinghong, remember to stay safe while traveling.\"","Xiao Jinghong looked up at him, hesitated for a moment, and removed the half-armor mask from her face, revealing her stunningly beautiful face without a trace of makeup. \"Thank you for your concern, Chen Yi.\"","Chen Yi met her gaze with a gentle smile on his face. \"It’s no trouble. As the Commander-in-Chief of the Dingyuan Army, it’s only right that you are busy.\"","\"Mhm...\"","They stopped at that. After a brief exchange, Xiao Jinghong put her mask back on, said she was leaving, and truly departed.","Chen Yi watched as she vanished into the night sky. He thought, \"Jinghong... days like this must be exhausting, right? As your husband, I ought to share some of the burden.\"","Chen Yi chuckled inwardly, glanced at the sky, stretched lazily, and turned back to his wing room. \"It’s time to cultivate...\""]},{"number":539,"title":"Chapter 539 - 313: Fourth Grade!","paragraphs":["For the past two days, Xiao Jinghong had been hiding in Shu State Prefecture City, so Chen Yi naturally couldn’t cultivate the Four Symbols Skill.","However, keeping the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique active allowed him to continuously absorb the Profound Mysteries of [Martial Arts·Body]. By integrating them, he enhanced his comprehension of his three major cultivation techniques: the Four Symbols Skill, the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique, and the Big Spear Pile Skill.","Specifically, the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique and the Four Symbols Skill had already reached the absolute peak of the Perfect Level. The effect of concealing his cultivation was even better. Although Chen Yi wasn’t sure if it could withstand the prying eyes of someone like Immortal Bai, it should be enough to fool ordinary Upper Three Grades martial artists.","Next was the Four Symbols Skill. Just as Chen Yi had estimated, at the absolute peak of the Perfect Level, the cultivation speed of the Four Symbols Skill was more than twice as fast as before. Even now as he cultivated, the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism poured into his body, rapidly filling his Sea of Qi with True Essence and faintly allowing him to sense an opportunity for a breakthrough.","Then there was the Big Spear Pile Skill. Even though Chen Yi hadn’t cultivated it for a few days, his physique continued to grow. Not only had his strength reached Six Symbols Power, but his defense was also astonishing. He estimated that relying solely on his physical strength, he could withstand a strike from a Middle Three Grades martial artist. Of course, the premise was that the opponent’s technique realm did not exceed Minor Success and lacked the enhancement of the Heaven and Earth Spiritual Mechanism Realm.","Aside from the most direct improvements in his three major cultivation techniques, the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique’s effects on nourishing the body and cultivating essence had also seen considerable progress. Enhanced by the Gold Spirit, the Dragon-slaying Spear’s sharp power was over twenty percent stronger than before. His other techniques, such as the Mountain Shattering Fist, Brocade Spring Saber Technique, Hundred Flowers Palm, and Wandering Dragon and Phoenix, had improved by a roughly similar margin. Only the power of their Spiritual Essence differed.","As Chen Yi cultivated, he utilized the flow of True Essence through his Sea of Qi, meridians, and the connection to his Divine Position to sort through his gains.","Time passed unknowingly. About an hour and a half later, Chen Yi suddenly opened his eyes, a sharp glint flashing through them. The \"God\" within his Forehead Acupoint immediately connected with the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism.","In an instant, the guest room he was in completely transformed. The bed, table, chairs, and the stone floor expanded and morphed, turning into continuous mountains, rivers, and forests. Rushing rivers surged down through the mountain valleys. Immediately after, a massive chessboard rotated and rose, blotting out the sky and the sun, covering everything.","Above the chessboard, Chen Yi sat upright in the clouds, looking down at the board’s setup, holding a chess piece in each hand. One black, one white. He looked just like a holy sovereign looking down upon all living beings.","Chen Yi swept his gaze over his surroundings and threw the pieces in his hands, landing them on two diagonally opposite star points. Plumes of smoke began to rise from the chessboard, spreading like a mist across the mountains and rivers. A moment later, even Chen Yi’s figure faded away significantly.","—This was the power of Chess Dao at the Perfection Realm.","Before this, Chen Yi already knew that cultivating the \"God\" in Chess Dao wasn’t referring to the Divine Position mentioned in the Four Symbols Skill, but rather his own \"Divine Intent.\" It was also the \"God\" within the essence, qi, and god spoken of in the Medical Dao. In fact, once Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting were cultivated to the Perfection Realm, they all possessed different powers.","For instance, Calligraphy Dao evolved \"words\" into \"intent,\" pointing directly to the calligrapher’s original heart. Painting Dao could \"turn drawings into reality,\" making painted objects indistinguishable from the real thing, capable of confusing, evoking emotions, bringing back memories, and intimidating...","As for Zither Dao, Chen Yi hadn’t cultivated it much. It was still at Minor Success, so he couldn’t yet see any Divine Intent power. Perhaps it could kill people with melodies, much like the Evil Demonic Dao practitioners of the Illusory Sound Sect.","Meanwhile, the power of Chess Dao was to cultivate the \"God.\"","Originally, Chen Yi only used Chess Dao for deduction, at most expanding the scope—from the Prefecture City to Shu State, and eventually to the whole world. But after encountering Du Cang and falling into his Black Magic Secret Skill, Chen Yi had extracted this particular usage from the Profound Mysteries of the Chess Dao. He could use his \"God\" to manifest a heaven and earth chessboard, using the pieces on the board to form momentum and aura to conceal himself or injure enemies.","Enveloped by the chessboard, he was the \"God\" here, controlling and isolating everything. It was majestic, Zhong Zheng, and grand. It was far more domineering than the so-called Black Magic Secret Skill of the \"Jackal,\" Du Cang.","\"I really should thank him...\" Chen Yi smiled as he looked at his surroundings. Feeling that he no longer needed to worry about outside prying, he released the cover of the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique.","The True Essence within his three major Seas of Qi and twelve meridians surged and flowed like the rivers below. His cultivation was fully revealed, yet the people outside didn’t notice a thing.","Xiao Wuge and Xiaodie, who were close by, lacked the strength to notice. Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang, who had sufficient cultivation, noticed a trace of abnormal movement in the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, but upon careful inspection, they found absolutely nothing. What they didn’t know was that right under their noses, Chen Yi was going all out to break through.","\"Four Symbols Practitioner, Cyan Dragon...\" He drew the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism into his body, converting it into True Essence through the two Seas of Qi in his Dantian and Chest. However, in his Forehead Acupoint Sea of Qi, it wasn’t as simple as merely refining the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism to enhance his True Essence cultivation. At the same time, there was the Refining Spirit and Shaping Form. Namely, the four Divine Positions of the Cyan Dragon, White Tiger, Black Tortoise, and Vermilion Bird.","Each Divine Intent corresponded to a different Spiritual Essence, which was used to enhance various techniques, such as the Sharp Power of the Dragon-slaying Spear and the explosive power of the Mountain Shattering Fist. Therefore, in the Middle Three Grades Realm, apart from increasing one’s True Essence cultivation, the most important thing was to temper the \"Divine Positions\" to make them take form.","With Chen Yi comprehending this, his breakthrough naturally fell into place. The True Essence within his three major Seas of Qi surged and circulated, gradually solidifying and becoming as thick as mercury. The images of the Cyan Dragon, White Tiger, Vermilion Bird, and Black Tortoise on the four major Divine Positions flickered into view, the details of their whiskers and fur already visible.","[Cultivation successful. Cultivation: Lower Fourth Grade.]","[Four Symbols Skill (Earth Tier) Divine Position Spiritual Essence has advanced. The enhancement power of Wood, Water, Fire, and Gold Spiritual Essence has doubled.]","In the blink of an eye, the difference in Chen Yi’s strength compared to before was like night and day. Not only had his True Essence cultivation grown twofold, but the Spiritual Essence enhanced by his Divine Positions had also made significant progress."]},{"number":540,"title":"Chapter 540 - 313: Fourth Grade!","paragraphs":["This doubled the power and effectiveness of Cultivation Techniques and Techniques like his Four Symbols Skill, Dragon-slaying Spear, and Mountain Shattering Fist.","To put it bluntly, if the current Chen Yi were to fight Du Cang again, he wouldn’t even need the Chess Dao. He could forcefully shatter Du Cang’s Black Magic Secret Skill using only the Spear Dao. Without his Black Magic Secret Skill, Du Cang wouldn’t even be able to withstand a single thrust of his spear!","Chen Yi felt the True Essence surging within his body. After stabilizing it for a moment, he slowly ceased his cultivation and used the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique to rein in his aura.","However, advancing in his Cultivation wasn’t entirely without drawbacks. Even though the power of his Four Symbols Skill had doubled, it was impossible for him to break through a minor realm in just four days like he did in the Fifth Grade Realm. As for an exact estimate... it was hard to say. It all depended on how much time he could spare for cultivation.","Chen Yi stood up and casually dispelled the mountains and rivers conjured by his Chess Dao. Looking around the guest room, which remained clearly visible despite the dim lighting, a slight smile appeared on his face.","Now that his Cultivation had reached the Fourth Grade Realm, the combined might of his various Techniques was enough to rival a Martial Artist in the Upper Three Grades Realm. This meant he had achieved the goal he set when he first arrived in this world: to have the ability to protect himself. As long as he didn’t provoke people like Immortal Bai, he could go anywhere in this vast world.","Then again, at this point, Chen Yi didn’t want to go anywhere at all.","\"Staying here in Shu State is pretty nice,\" he murmured. \"Stunning scenery, pristine waters, beauties by my side... But more importantly, the Emperor is far away, so I can actually enjoy some rare peace and quiet.\"","Looking at the full moon outside the window, Chen Yi felt completely at peace. He was used to everything here. He had formed attachments to people and matters that were hard to let go of, making it difficult for him to ever wander far away. Besides, for someone as lazy as him, leaving meant finding some obscure corner to hide in. He wouldn’t have Xiaodie to take care of him, Xiao Wan’er to fret over him, or Madam Xiao Jinghong to constantly spur him on.","He might as well just stay here in the Spring Lotus Garden.","Just as he was thinking this, a golden light flashed before his eyes.","[Daily Intelligence · Yellow-level Top Grade: At 9:00 PM in Kangle Lane, Yuan Liu’er will diagnose and treat her younger brother. A minuscule Opportunity can be obtained.]","After reading it, Chen Yi couldn’t help but gasp softly. \"That girl, Liu’er, has only studied the Medical Dao for a few days, yet she already dares to treat patients? And it’s her own brother?\"","After thinking it over, Chen Yi silently noted the time, planning to go take a look after nightfall tomorrow. Yuan Liu’er was a disciple he valued highly. Given her outstanding aptitude, he had to look out for her. Moreover, the Medical Dao was different from other paths; rashly prescribing medicine and treating ailments could easily backfire.","\"It’s good to go check on her. It’s my duty as her grandmaster, after all.\"","Chen Yi couldn’t help but think of his disappointing eldest disciple, Ma Liangcai, and curled his lips in disdain. \"He’s studied under me for so long but is still only at the entry-level of the Medical Dao. Truly a lost cause. Ah, well, whatever.\"","Ma Liangcai had started out as a quack doctor, so managing to hold down the fort at the Jishi Medicine Hall decently well was proof of his hard work. Plus, his character was commendable, and he worked efficiently, barely qualifying him to be a trusted aide.","Chen Yi checked the sky outside, then pulled out the travel bag from under his bed. He changed into black clothes, donned a mask, and left the Spring Lotus Garden, silent and unnoticed. He first visited the residence on Chuansi Street. Seeing no movement inside, he headed straight for the Hundred Herbs Hall.","The night was hazy, and a cool breeze blew gently. There weren’t many pedestrians on the streets. Only a few Jianghu People were sleeping under the open sky. Occasional laughter echoed as they chatted about recent amusing events.","In the gloomy alleys, there were even fewer people. Fortunately, the few lanes connecting the East and West Markets were mostly inhabited by people of status, so shady activities rarely occurred there. Chen Yi navigated his way through, avoiding the servants guarding the residences, as well as the patrolling City Guard Army and Imprisonment Officers, until he arrived at the Hundred Herbs Hall.","As soon as he approached, he heard the slightly hushed voices of Liu Lang and the others coming from inside. It sounded like they were in the Quiet Chamber.","\"...And that’s pretty much what happened,\" one voice said. \"General Jinghong truly lives up to her reputation as a top-tier expert in Shu State. When I went looking for her, before I even got close, a sliver of Sword Intent was already pressed against my neck.\"","\"Hiss, she’s that formidable?\"","\"You bet. Did you think I was lying? If she wasn’t that powerful, why would I have obeyed her every command? Dabao, you have the nerve to judge me? Back in the pit, you were too scared to even breathe a word!\"","\"Hehe... With you taking the lead, Mr. Liu, how could I dare steal the spotlight...\"","During the lull in their banter, Wang Ji asked from the side, \"Since you guys are back in the Prefecture City, what’s the plan next?\"","Liu Lang replied that he would head to Lin Village to sell off the remaining grain.","Zhang Dabao thought for a moment before saying, \"Since the lord hasn’t given any further instructions, I’ll just take the members of the Celestial Sect into hiding for a while.\"","Liu Lang nodded in agreement. \"Makes sense. You really pulled off something huge this time, kid. I originally thought the boss just sent you to pull some underhanded tricks, but I never expected it was actually to...\"","Before he could finish, Chen Yi pushed the door open and walked in. \"Actually to what?\"","\"Boss?\" Liu Lang snapped to attention, quickly standing up with a smile. \"I’ve taken care of everything you asked for.\"","Ever since he lost his duel with Chen Yi and nearly died, no matter how arrogant he was, he didn’t dare cross the line anymore.","Wang Ji and Zhang Dabao bowed successively, greeting him as \"Lord.\"","Chen Yi closed the door, took the seat of honor, and waved his hand, signaling them to sit down and talk. \"Dabao, you did an excellent job this time.\"","A hint of shyness appeared on Zhang Dabao’s youthful face. \"It’s all thanks to your guidance, my lord. To be honest, there were a few slip-ups along the way. Thankfully, the guys from the Celestial Sect were quick-witted and salvaged the situation in time, preventing anyone from escaping.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"As long as the outcome was Perfection, that’s what matters.\"","It was, in fact, a very perfect outcome. Zhang Dabao and the others had disguised themselves as horse bandits from the Poshisu Country and Scouts from the Barbarian Race. This not only caused the capital Lin Zhenghong and his group needed to buy grain to skyrocket, but they had also unexpectedly captured Li Sanyuan from the Ji State Trading Company.","\"Tell me, what was Li Sanyuan trying to do?\" Chen Yi asked. Guesses were just guesses; he wanted to know exactly what the Ji State Trading Company was scheming.","Zhang Dabao quickly recounted the entire sequence of events. \"That guy is incredibly sly. Even under Liu Lang’s interrogation, he only spilled part of his plan. If General Jinghong hadn’t arrived later and forced the rest of the plan out of him, I wouldn’t have known he actually sent people to get dirt on Liu Taofang.\"","\"Liu Taofang...\" Chen Yi lowered his head slightly, his fingers tapping rhythmically against the back of his chair.","Things were roughly as he had deduced—Li Sanyuan wanted to take a risk and make a deal with King Landu to secure the silver coins they had earned from the grain trade. However, he hadn’t expected—or rather, he had underestimated—Li Sanyuan’s decisiveness. Realizing he couldn’t drag Liu Hong down with him, the man immediately targeted Liu Taofang.","\"If things really go according to his plan, then there will be a massive flaw on Liu Hong’s end,\" Chen Yi mused. His gaze shifted north. No wonder Madam Xiao Jinghong was in such a hurry to head to Guangyuan.","Li Sanyuan only held the evidence of Zhu Hao’s transactions with King Landu through the Ji State Trading Company, which didn’t implicate Liu Hong. At most, it would just lead to some suspicion. Under these circumstances, Xiao Jinghong had no choice but to go to Guangyuan County to avoid alerting Liu Hong here in the Prefecture City.","\"If that’s the case, Madam probably won’t apprehend Zhu Hao right away,\" Chen Yi thought. He wouldn’t have either.","The best countermeasure was to keep a close eye on Zhu Hao and see if he could be tied to Liu Hong. \"This gives her older brother a chance to claim this merit...\" However, at this thought, Chen Yi secretly frowned.","\"I shouldn’t have killed Lv Jiunan,\" he realized. \"Judging by the caution the Old Master and Madam have shown towards Liu Hong, he must be hiding some secrets, or perhaps he has a powerful backer. To the point where they can’t act rashly without making foolproof preparations. If Lv Jiunan were still alive, the outcome would be different. He could have served as a witness to pin Asutai’s escape from Shu State entirely on Liu Hong.\"","After pondering for a moment, Chen Yi formed a plan. He then gave out instructions to Liu Lang and Zhang Dabao one by one.","After hearing them, Zhang Dabao’s jaw dropped as he pointed at himself. \"L-Lord, you want me to disguise myself as Li Sanyuan?\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. \"What, you can’t do it?\"","\"I can do it, it’s j-just... I’m afraid I’ll mess it up and delay your plans, my lord. After all, that grain...\"","A million bushels of grain! The mere thought of that number made Zhang Dabao’s heart tremble. Even setting aside current prices, it was worth a million silver coins based on the rates before the grain price surged. If he screwed this up, he wouldn’t be able to pay off the debt in a lifetime.","Chen Yi chuckled softly. \"It’s best if you succeed, but even if you fail, we can still force them to transport the grain out of the city. When that time comes...\"","Liu Lang’s face lit up with excitement. He gripped the hilt of his Blade and snickered, \"Then it’ll be my time to shine.\"","Back when he was in the Northern Desert, he had pulled off quite a few robbery jobs through the Bright Moon Building. It would be a walk in the park. This time, there was just more loot and more manpower needed. But at its core, it was still about killing everyone, snatching the goods, and storing them safely. Very simple.","Chen Yi nodded. \"Remember to hide the grain well. If it comes down to it, take it to Tonglin Town.\"","\"Tonglin? The Xiao Family’s fief?\" Liu Lang grinned. \"The boss really thinks of everything.\"","Seeing that Liu Lang and Zhang Dabao understood their tasks, Chen Yi turned his attention to Wang Ji and instructed, \"I need you to do something for me as well.\"","\"Please give your orders, my lord.\"","\"Tomorrow, go to the Xiao Family’s estate. The Hundred Herbs Hall in Guangyuan County is about to open, and it needs some backing from the Xiao Family...\""]},{"number":541,"title":"Chapter 541 - 314: Deserves to Die!","paragraphs":["With silver—and a whopping two million taels of it at that—Chen Yi naturally wouldn’t hide it at the bottom of a chest to gather dust.","It had to be spent.","Calculating the time, more than half a month had passed since Yan Sea and the others went to Guangyuan to investigate the situation. It was time to take the first Step in expanding Hundred Herbs Hall.","The Marquis’s Mansion, with its two-hundred-year legacy, was living so frugally that it was truly unbearable to watch. Even if not for himself, for the sake of the Xiao Family which was bleeding money like a sieve, expanding Hundred Herbs Hall was imperative. He couldn’t let the Xiao Family worry about silver anymore. It would be a joke.","After giving his instructions, Chen Yi took out one hundred silver notes from his robes, each worth ten thousand taels, and placed them on the table.","\"Five hundred thousand taels of this will make up for the money spent buying grain a few days ago. The silver coins Xue Duanyun and the others made from selling grain will also be entered into Hundred Herbs Hall’s accounts.","\"As for the remaining five hundred thousand taels...\"","Tapping on the silver notes, Chen Yi looked at Wang Ji and said, \"The Xinglin Hall incident this time has reminded me. We can’t rely entirely on those merchants for raw medicinal materials. It’s best if we open up our own channels.\"","Wang Ji lowered his head. \"You are right, my Lord.\"","\"Although Old Jia had bad luck over there, in the end, it’s still because we couldn’t find another alternative,\" Chen Yi continued. \"Running into a wealthy and overbearing entity like Xinglin Hall that monopolizes all medicinal materials, Hundred Herbs Hall’s business will inevitably be affected.\"","Wang Ji looked up and glanced at the silver notes on the table, his eyes burning with desire. \"Rest assured, my Lord. With this silver, I will forge a path even if I have to wade through fire and water. I will absolutely not let Hundred Herbs Hall experience another shortage of medicinal materials.\"","Chen Yi nodded noncommittally. \"Tomorrow, when you go to the Xiao Family, ask the Eldest Miss to step forward and negotiate with the Mountain Race.","\"The medicinal materials from Wumeng Mountain will be given away regardless of whether it’s to others or to us. Remember to let them save face; it doesn’t matter if we spend a bit more silver.\"","That being said, the medicinal herbs the Mountain Race harvested from Wumeng Mountain every month were limited. If they gave them to Hundred Herbs Hall, they couldn’t give them to other merchants. Those merchants who had dealt with the Mountain Race for so many years to secure their channels would naturally be unwilling to have them snatched away.","Even if the Xiao Family stepped forward and the Mountain Race couldn’t refuse, it would still damage their reputation and old friendships, especially for conservative people like the Mountain Race. Therefore, Chen Yi was willing to spend more silver. It would preserve the Mountain Race’s dignity, prevent the Xiao Family from owing a favor, and gag those merchants.","It was killing three birds with one stone.","A short while later, Chen Yi stood up and was about to leave when he caught sight of Zhang Dabao and Liu Lang. After some thought, he instructed, \"You all have worked hard this time. Later, Wang Ji will distribute some silver to everyone as a reward.\"","Wang Ji, having just put away the silver notes, looked at Zhang Dabao and Liu Lang upon hearing this. \"My Lord, how much... would be appropriate?\"","\"One hundred silver coins for every participant, an extra hundred for those with outstanding performance, and an extra three hundred for Dabao, Liu Lang, and the others.\"","\"Understood.\"","Liu Lang and Zhang Dabao bowed joyfully in thanks. Chen Yi nodded, then slipped out of the Quiet Chamber and headed back to the Xiao Family.","After he left, Wang Ji muttered, his heart aching for the money, \"Those who don’t manage the household don’t know the cost of firewood and rice. Who gives out silver as rewards like this?\"","Liu Lang glared at him in displeasure. \"Shopkeeper, the few of us risked our necks this time, and you’re already heartbroken over a hundred-odd taels of silver?\"","\"I wouldn’t dare, I wouldn’t dare. Please don’t take offense, Guard Liu.\"","\"I’d reckon you wouldn’t.\"","Zhang Dabao looked at the awkwardly smiling Wang Ji and then at the unhappy Liu Lang, stepping in to smooth things over. \"Brother Liu, let’s go too. We still need to make some preparations for the tasks the Lord assigned.\"","Liu Lang immediately stood up and walked out. \"See you later, Shopkeeper.\"","Zhang Dabao smiled at Wang Ji and turned to follow him out.","Watching them walk away, Wang Ji first lightly slapped his own mouth and muttered something about how it wasn’t his money anyway. Then, he took out the stack of silver notes and started counting, looking exactly like a miser.","Stepping outside Hundred Herbs Hall, Chen Yi listened to the conversation behind him and shook his head with a smile.","Wang Ji was too short-sighted; otherwise, he wouldn’t have engaged in crooked practices at Jishi Medicine Hall. Even though he had become the Shopkeeper of Hundred Herbs Hall and broadened his horizons a bit, some bad habits were still hard to change, such as being stingy with his subordinates. Fortunately, Wang Ji was obedient, efficient, and fully dedicated to Hundred Herbs Hall, so he was somewhat useful. Otherwise, Chen Yi absolutely wouldn’t have let him take the helm in expanding Hundred Herbs Hall.","He sighed, \"Good talents are hard to come by.\"","Wang Ji and Ma Liangcai, these two latecomers, could barely keep up for now. Their future would depend on their own fortunes. In contrast, Liu Lang, Zhang Dabao, the disciples of the Celestial Sect, and most importantly, Yuan Liu’er, had promising futures.","\"Grow up quickly, all of you. It’s truly ridiculous that I can’t even be a hands-off boss...\" he mumbled to himself.","Moving like a phantom, Chen Yi slipped into an adjacent alleyway and disappeared into the night.","A short while later, he arrived on Chuansi Street. Just as he was about to head into a nearby residence to remove his disguise, he caught a familiar figure out of the corner of his eye.","Fang Hongxiu.","However, at this moment, Fang Hongxiu looked slightly anxious and stern. Leading a few Imprisonment Officers, she was hurrying from west to east. It seemed something had happened.","After thinking for a moment, Chen Yi snapped his fingers and asked with a hint of a smile, \"Hundred Households Fang, where are you rushing to in such a hurry?\"","Fang Hongxiu paused at the sound. Turning her head, she spotted Chen Yi’s figure, a hint of surprise flashing across her stern eyes.","\"Dragon Tiger?\"","Over the past few days, the name of \"Dragon Tiger\" Liu Wu had resounded throughout Shu State, so Fang Hongxiu was naturally aware of it. Furthermore, she had personally led her people to Puyin Temple and brought Du Cang’s corpse back to the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office.","Seeing Liu Wu appear at this moment, her expression became somewhat complicated. First, Liu Wu had evolved from \"Dragon Spear\" to \"Dragon Tiger,\" his strength even greater than before. Second, the person Liu Wu had saved was the Eldest Miss of the Xiao Family. Even if he wasn’t part of the Xiao family, he was someone connected to them."]},{"number":542,"title":"Chapter 542 - 314: Even Death Is Not Enough!","paragraphs":["Any past \"grudges\" between them were a moot point now. Combined with the fact that it was Liu Wu who had relayed the news of the East Market barbarian slave girl’s disappearance and death to her, and their even earlier transaction...","At this moment, Fang Hongxiu didn’t know what attitude she should adopt when facing \"Liu Wu.\" Behind her, the Imprisonment Officers exchanged glances, somewhat flustered, and their expressions grew wary.","Chen Yi slightly tipped up his bamboo hat, revealing his handsome face. He looked at Fang Hongxiu, who was leading the group, and asked with a light chuckle, \"May I have a word?\"","Fang Hongxiu hesitated for a moment. After nodding, she ordered the rest of the Imprisonment Officers to continue on their way. Once they had left, she took a few steps closer and asked in a low voice, \"You came looking for me specifically. Is it about that matter?\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. \"What? Did Hundred Households Fang find something?\"","After taking Asutai away that day, he had indeed had someone pass a message to Fang Hongxiu, just to cause some frustration for Liu Hong. He hadn’t actually expected the Imprisonment Department to find anything useful.","Hearing this, Fang Hongxiu understood that he hadn’t caught wind of anything. She shook her head and said, \"I didn’t find anything.\"","Chen Yi naturally didn’t believe her. He smiled and said, \"If it’s about the Liu family, just hand it over to me. I promise not to implicate anyone.\"","He had been figuring out how to force Liu Hong to show his true colors, but lacked some necessary conditions.","Seeing that he had seen through her thoughts, Fang Hongxiu fell silent for a moment. She then unfastened the sachet she carried at her waist and handed it to him.","\"I did find some things, but... exercise your own discretion.\"","Chen Yi looked at the sachet, then at her expression, and reached out to take it.","\"I know. No matter the result, this matter has nothing to do with your Imprisonment Department.\"","Since Fang Hongxiu had been cautiously keeping it on her person, the contents of the sachet must be extraordinary. Chen Yi could even imagine the heavy heart she had been bearing these past few days, likely worried that leaking the information would bring fatal disaster upon her.","Fang Hongxiu nodded gently, her expression relaxing. \"If there’s nothing else, I’ll take my leave first.\"","Chen Yi pocketed the sachet and asked casually, \"Seeing you all in such a hurry, did a major case occur?\"","Fang Hongxiu glanced around. Seeing that there was no one nearby, she leaned closer and whispered a few words.","Chen Yi’s smile faded as he listened. \"It’s that serious? There are actually refugees on the move?\"","Fang Hongxiu nodded. \"Several county cities have suffered natural disasters. Even if the Prefecture City has distributed relief grain, there are still many starving people. News arrived two days ago that tens of thousands of refugees are heading toward the Prefecture City. The faster ones have already reached Lin Village outside the city.\"","\"Lin Village...\"","Chen Yi looked toward the East City Gate and asked, \"What do the Governor’s Office and the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office say?\"","Although he had heard a few days ago that several counties downstream of the Chishui River had suffered floods and extremely low grain yields, given the overall harvest in Shu State this year, the government offices should have the ability to allocate grain. Now it seemed he had underestimated the Governor’s Office—or rather, Liu Hong’s viciousness.","To allow the citizens of several counties to reach the point of exchanging their children for food, causing the refugees to be displaced, all while sealing off all information...","It wasn’t hard for Chen Yi to deduce that Liu Hong must have a profound ulterior motive for doing this. However, time was pressing, and he couldn’t see through Liu Hong’s intentions right away. It couldn’t possibly be to cooperate with the Ji State Trading Company to continue driving up grain prices, could it?","Fang Hongxiu spoke frankly, \"After Lord Liu learned of this, he ordered the Lord Prefect to open the granaries and distribute food. But because...\"","Seeing her hesitate, Chen Yi thought of what had happened two days ago and said, his expression shifting slightly, \"Because Old Marquis Xiao and General Jinghong proposed that he stabilize the grain prices?\"","Fang Hongxiu nodded and said helplessly, \"The Lord Prefect’s meaning is that the Prefecture City is more important.\"","Chen Yi frowned inwardly. Such an excuse might work for Liu Si, but for Liu Hong, the Governor, it was quite unjustifiable. Whether it was the Prefecture City or the county cities, they were all within Shu State. With such a major incident occurring, how could he not treat them equally? Once a problem arose with the disaster relief, there was no guarantee the refugees wouldn’t cause chaos.","However, Chen Yi had already guessed Liu Hong’s countermeasure—using the excuse that Old Marquis Xiao had shown up at his door to \"force\" him to stabilize grain prices, he would report to the Imperial Court and humbly apologize for his failure.","After pondering for a moment, he said in a deep voice, \"This matter is of great consequence. Focus on pacifying them as much as possible.\"","Fang Hongxiu nodded. \"I understand.\"","Seeing that Chen Yi had nothing more to say, she cupped her fists together and said, \"There were many misunderstandings between us before; let us leave them in the past.\"","With that, without waiting for Chen Yi to speak, she turned and left.","Chen Yi watched her run off, then flipped his hand and took out the sachet. He knew clearly that the Imprisonment Department’s deployment out of the city was mostly for defense, to prevent any troublemakers among the refugees. They had no way to intervene in the disaster relief efforts.","But right now, the remaining grain in his hands was merely a drop in the bucket for tens of thousands of refugees. If this matter couldn’t be resolved in a short time, there was no telling what other backup plans Liu Hong and the others had waiting.","With this thought, Chen Yi turned and slipped into an alleyway, heading back to the West Market, as he took out the items inside the sachet to examine them. Now that he knew about this, it was impossible for him to turn a blind eye. The sooner the better; he had to make some countermeasures regardless.","Before taking more than a few steps, Chen Yi halted as he read the contents of the slips of paper in his hand. The papers contained several clues pointing directly to Zhao Shichang and others by Liu Hong’s side:","[September 1: Borrowing the Government Office’s power, Zeng Zhifeng ordered the Cao Gang to prepare several boats heading south.]","[September 3: A residence outside the East Market was rented by Zeng Zhifeng. The man has disappeared without a trace, suspected to have been abducted by the \"Dragon Spear.\"]","[September 4: Horse bandits from Poshisu Country went to the Liu family’s estate outside the city.]","[September 9: Several suspicious individuals entered and exited the Liu Mansion. One of them is currently at Xinglin Hall...]","Chen Yi’s eyes narrowed slightly after reading. The other clues about Zeng Zhifeng were one thing, but the final note about a person from Xinglin Hall appearing at the Liu family...","When it came to suspicious individuals, Chen Yi couldn’t think of anyone else besides the members of the Five Poison Sect. His mind raced as the situations of the first, second, and third branches of the Jing State Liu Family flashed through his thoughts one by one.","Liu Jing was dead.","Liu Wen was dead.","Liu Zhaoxue was colluding with the Five Poison Sect in an attempt to control the first branch of the Jing State Liu Family...","The Five Poison Sect...","\"Could it be that Liu Hong is also connected to the Five Poison Sect?\" he wondered. \"If that’s the case, then he truly deserves to die!\"","Thinking of this, Chen Yi put away the slips of paper. His pace quickened involuntarily as he darted toward the West Market.","It didn’t take long for him to find Liu Lang and Zhang Dabao. Meeting their surprised gazes, he instructed in a serious tone, \"Tonight, you two will go to the Lin family. You must finalize the trade for that one million shi of grain.\"","Liu Lang pinched the full beard he had just glued to his face and asked in confusion, \"Why the rush? Did something happen?\"","Chen Yi nodded. \"A matter of life and death. Do as I say. Additionally, once you’ve confirmed the transaction time with Lin Zhenghong, go to Lin Village before dawn tomorrow and suspend the sale of grain.\"","\"S-Suspend it?\" Liu Lang was startled, nearly ripping off his fake beard. \"Boss, it’s not that I disagree, but Lin Village is currently surrounded by the city’s commoners. If we really stop selling grain, I reckon those people might even start looting.\"","Chen Yi waved his hand and said, \"The refugees have arrived.\"","With the sheer number of those refugees, once the Prefecture City’s citizens saw them, they probably wouldn’t have the mind to stay outside the city anymore. Naturally, it would also be impossible for them to clash with Xue Duanyun and the others.","Liu Lang was utterly confused. \"Refugees? What refugees?\"","\"Refugees from several counties downstream of the Chishui River. Quite a few of them have already arrived at Lin Village...\" Chen Yi gave a brief explanation, not forgetting to remind them, \"Dabao, later on, you can use this as an excuse to make Lin Zhenghong transport the grain out of the city as quickly as possible.\"","Zhang Dabao and Liu Lang understood and repeatedly voiced their agreement.","\"After you arrive at Lin Village, you must guard that grain well. I have a major use for it.\"","\"Rest assured, my Lord...\"","Although there wasn’t much grain left, it would at least last a day or two, leaving some room to maneuver. Once Zhang Dabao finished disguising the two of them, they bid farewell to Chen Yi and concealed their tracks as they headed toward the East Market.","Chen Yi watched their retreating backs. After a moment of thought, he fetched a brush and ink and wrote a few lines. This matter was of grave importance; he had to notify the Xiao family as soon as possible.","Well past the Hour of the Ox.","Chen Yi made a detour and completed a few tasks before returning to Spring Lotus Garden. He changed into casual clothes and went to the window, looking at the scattering of starlight that had appeared in the middle courtyard not far away.","\"I hope the Old Master can come up with a countermeasure,\" he thought. \"Otherwise, with Liu Hong’s tactics, the longer those refugees stay outside the Prefecture City, the worse the outcome will be...\""]},{"number":543,"title":"Chapter 543 - 315: Frail Scholar Chen Qingzhou","paragraphs":["Displaced refugees were a constant threat.","If mishandled, they could easily rise up in rebellion armed with nothing but clubs and bricks.","As the saying went: they were dead either way, so why not risk it all for the chance to achieve something great?","If Chen Yi could realize this, Elder Master Xiao and the others naturally understood it as well.","\"Number Three, go find Liu Si. Ask him how he plans to settle those disaster victims.","\"Xuanshuo, take the Punishment Hall’s men and head just outside the East City Gate immediately. Assess the situation there. If any evildoers are committing crimes, you know what to do.","\"Lixing...\"","\"Understood!\"","Before dawn had even broken, the Xiao family estate was already bustling with activity.","Armored warriors of the personal guard strictly patrolled the front and rear courtyards, while men from the Punishment Hall darted back and forth, delivering stream after stream of intelligence.","Even Xiao Wan’er, who had just woken up early in the morning, was summoned by the Elder Master.","Walking through the estate, Xiao Wan’er naturally noticed the solemn expressions on the armored warriors’ faces. Upon arriving at the Qingjing Residence, she asked, \"Grandfather, you sent for me? Has something happened?\"","Elder Master Xiao rested both hands on his walking cane, sitting upright in his grandmaster’s chair. He gave a slight nod and said, \"The commoners of Guang’an, Le Jiang, Xingwen, and other counties had an abysmal summer harvest. A famine has broken out, forcing many to flee all the way here to the Prefecture City.\"","\"Famine refugees...\" Xiao Wan’er’s eyes widened. \"There are refugees outside the city?\"","Elder Master Xiao sighed. He was extremely reluctant to use the word \"refugees,\" but it was the undeniable truth.","\"Those commoners arrived last night, and in no small numbers.\"","\"Then... why did you send for me...?\"","\"How much silver does our mansion currently have left?\"","Xiao Wan’er looked at him in confusion. \"We have less than forty thousand taels remaining.\"","Elder Master Xiao quickly weighed his options. \"Take it all out. Later, I will send someone to deliver it to the Wan family.\"","\"The Wan family?\"","\"I have already reached an agreement with Old Wan. At a rate of two taels of silver per stone of grain, we will buy enough provisions to provide relief to the commoners outside the city.\"","Xiao Wan’er understood his intentions. After a moment of thought, she offered, \"Grandfather, let me handle the delivery.\"","\"You? Out of the question.\"","\"The crowds outside the city are a chaotic mix of people right now. What if...\"","The incident with Du Cang had just recently passed, so Elder Master Xiao was naturally unwilling to let his granddaughter put herself in harm’s way again.","Besides, handing out porridge to refugees was inherently a thankless and exhausting task; whether Xiao Wan’er’s frail body could even endure it was highly doubtful.","Xiao Wan’er shook her head. \"Grandfather, it is precisely for that reason that I should be the one to lead our people there.","\"Although the Xiao family’s legacy is built on martial prowess, our roots are firmly planted in Shu State. We ought to lead by example in times like these.\"","It was true that she rarely left the Marquis’s Mansion, but she had read her fair share of books and understood what needed to be done and what did not.","Aiding the refugees was an absolute necessity. Furthermore, given the Xiao family’s current predicament, having her step up was the only way to properly demonstrate the family’s firm stance.","Elder Master Xiao was still hesitant. \"It’s not that your grandfather is being unreasonable, but with your health...\"","\"Please rest assured, Grandfather. My health is no longer a major issue, and I’ll also have Chen Yi with me...\"","\"Chen Yi? What use could a frail scholar like him possibly be?\"","Realizing her slip of the tongue, Xiao Wan’er hurriedly explained, \"It’s precisely because Chen Yi is an educated scholar that he can help me navigate the complicated situation outside the city.\"","\"I suppose that makes sense...\" Elder Master Xiao muttered to himself for a moment. After glancing at Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang standing guard outside the residence, he finally nodded.","\"Since you insist, you may lead the group.","\"But remember, if anything unexpected happens, you must have the guards escort you back into the city immediately.\"","\"I will...\"","As Elder Master Xiao watched Xiao Wan’er hurry away, his expression was unavoidably conflicted. He felt a mixture of gratification and heartache.","If Xiao Fengchun and the others were still around, there was no way the prestigious Xiao family would force a terminally ill girl like Xiao Wan’er to show her face in public.","\"Alas, such is our fate.\"","Elder Master Xiao let out a heavy sigh and turned his gaze toward the southeast—in the direction of the Governor’s Office. His eyes turned ice-cold.","\"Liu Hong!\"","The previous night, Elder Master Xiao had sent people to assess the situation at the government offices. The results were far from optimistic.","The Prefectural Magistrate’s Office shirked responsibility, claiming the Governor’s Office had not issued any explicit orders. Meanwhile, the Governor’s Office claimed they had a shortage of grain.","They insisted that until the grain merchants in the East and West Markets lowered their prices, the reserves in the official granaries could not be touched.","Upon hearing this, how could Elder Master Xiao not see right through Liu Hong’s scheming?","He had been so furious he was trembling.","If Xiao Jinghong hadn’t reasoned with him before leaving—arguing that the time wasn’t quite ripe to deal with Liu Hong—he would have long since donned his armor and led his men to slaughter their way into the Liu family estate.","But given the current crisis, he still had to find a way to placate the refugees outside the city to prevent any further chaos from breaking out.","\"That son of a bitch Zhang Xuan... Where did he send the grain and silver coins I lent him?\"","While Elder Master Xiao was burning with anxiety, Chen Yi was completely unhurried.","By the time he was informed that he needed to accompany the group to distribute porridge outside the city, it was already 7:00 AM.","He had just finished breakfast and was preparing to stay in the Spring Lotus Garden, intending to cultivate the Four Symbols Skill while waiting for news from the outside.","Since Xiao Jinghong hadn’t returned yet, he figured he should put in some extra effort so his Cultivation wouldn’t fall too far behind hers in the future.","Besides, he had already taken countermeasures the previous night.","With the grain from Lin Village, those refugees would at least have enough to make do for a few days.","However, when Xiao Wan’er came over with her attendants and explained the situation, Chen Yi simply acted as if he had done nothing and readily agreed to go.","After he changed into everyday clothes, the group boarded a carriage and hurried toward the city outskirts.","Aside from Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang, the three maids—Juan’er, Cui’er, and Xiaodie—naturally tagged along as well.","Prior to their arrival, however, Wang Lixing, Liu Si’er, and the other armored warriors of the Marquis’s Mansion had already transported the estate’s grain outside the city and set up a porridge distribution station. This had done much to put the minds of the people outside the city at ease.","Even so, the Prefecture City was still heavily impacted by the sudden influx.","Although the refugees weren’t nearly as terrifying as the Peacock King banner or the Barbarian Race scouts, the city’s residents were still filled with unease.","With tens of thousands of extra mouths to feed appearing out of thin air, people couldn’t help but wonder: Was there enough grain in the Prefecture City? What was the government office’s stance? And would grain prices ever drop again?"]},{"number":544,"title":"Chapter 544 - 315: Frail Scholar Chen Qingzhou","paragraphs":["Questions were thrown out one after another, but no one could provide a clear answer. Even the public notices issued by the Governor’s Office and the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office offered no specific countermeasures. They only stated that the city gates were restricted to entry only and advised residents to minimize going out.","\"Why has our Shu State been in such chaos lately?\"","\"Countless merchants have died or been injured over by the Ancient Tea-Horse Road. Everyone says the Peacock King Banner has launched an attack.\"","\"There’s still no accurate news from over there, yet the refugees from Guang’an County and its neighbors have already fled here.\"","\"It’s a troubled time, indeed.\"","\"Compared to all that, aren’t those grain shops even more detestable?\"","\"Today’s grain price has skyrocketed to thirty silver coins. At this rate, let alone people like us, even those Noble Families won’t be able to afford to eat.\"","\"Them?\"","\"They all have reserves of old grain. They don’t need us worrying about them...\"","Looking out the window at the hurried commoners, Chen Yi could naturally hear the noisy discussions around him.","\"Ultimately, it’s due to the influx of refugees. The city gates are half-sealed,\" he noted.","Xiao Wan’er didn’t hear him clearly, but she knew the current situation was urgent. A touch of worry surfaced on her pale face. \"Chen Yi, can we hold out by distributing porridge like this?\"","Chen Yi didn’t pour cold water on her hopes. \"We should be able to.\"","He knew very well that the crux of the problem wasn’t the refugees themselves, but the main culprit who caused the people of Guang’an County to swarm the Prefecture City. If that person were a bit more ruthless, they could incite the refugees to riot in an instant. When that happened, no amount of grain would be of any use.","After a moment of thought, Chen Yi suggested, \"We might as well set up a few more distribution points. After all, there are tens of thousands of refugees. Just the few of us won’t be enough for even a single day.\"","Xiao Wan’er hesitated slightly. \"We don’t have enough people.\"","\"I have a way.\"","Taking advantage of the carriage passing by the Jishi Medicine Hall, Chen Yi stepped off and found Liu Quan and the others, telling them to come along. Now was not the time to worry about the meager earnings of the Medicine Hall; placating the refugees outside the city as quickly as possible was the top priority.","Just then, Ma Liangcai approached with Yuan Liu’er and a well-featured young boy. He bowed and said, \"Master.\"","Chen Yi glanced at him and grunted in acknowledgment, reluctantly accepting the title of \"Master.\"","\"Liu’er greets Grandmaster.\"","\"Ah, it’s still my good grand-disciple who knows her manners. Grandmaster will take you there in the carriage.\"","\"...\" Ma Liangcai opened his mouth but couldn’t utter a single word.","Yuan Liu’er looked at him, then at the boy beside her, and stammered, \"Grandmaster, this is my brother, Yuan Hao. Could he... could he come along with you...\"","\"He’s your brother?\"","Chen Yi sized up the young boy. Inevitably recalling those large golden characters, he cast a glance at him using his Qi Observation Skill.","\"Huh, he isn’t sick?\" Chen Yi thought. He pondered for a moment, his eyes drifting toward the East City Gate. Could it be related to the refugees outside the city?","Seeing him fall silent while staring intently at Yuan Hao, Yuan Liu’er tangled her fingers together and said anxiously, \"Grandmaster, please forgive me if I misspoke just now. Please... please don’t take offense...\"","Even Yuan Hao, who was shrinking back behind her, looked at Chen Yi with a hint of fear.","Chen Yi snapped back to reality and waved his hand with a smile. \"Relax. I wouldn’t mind such a trivial matter. Come, come with me.\"","Without giving them a chance to argue, Chen Yi brought both Yuan Liu’er and Yuan Hao onto the carriage. Of course, Yuan Hao only managed to snag a spot on the driving box, sitting alongside Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang. Yuan Liu’er followed Chen Yi into the carriage cabin. Liu Quan, Ma Liangcai, and the others carried their medicine chests and followed behind the carriage, just in case.","When the carriage arrived at the East City Gate, Xie Tingyun negotiated with the City Guard Army, allowing the group to exit the city.","Outside the gate, hundreds of City Guard Army soldiers were lined up longitudinally on both sides. They wore long blades at their waists, carried wooden shields on their backs, and bore solemn expressions. In the distance on the official road, a sparse smattering of people could be seen. Most were in rags, their faces so covered in mud and ash that their original appearances were indiscernible. Only their pairs of eyes stood out.","Regardless of age or gender, they all gazed longingly in the direction of the Prefecture City. Most weakly muttered the same few words.","\"Water... food.\"","\"Save my child...\"","\"My lord, please...\"","Through the gap in the window curtains, Chen Yi watched these refugees with a calm expression. With his superior eyesight, he could naturally see much further. He knew that the condition of these refugees near the Prefecture City was actually considered relatively good. Further away, there were commoners so emaciated from hunger that they were too weak to walk. Leaning against trees or lying on the side of the official road, they could only let out weak groans, begging for something to eat or drink.","Seeing this, Xiao Wan’er’s face revealed a look of unbearable pity. \"Chen Yi, there are quite a few commoners here. Should we just distribute the porridge right here?\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"We’re going to Lin Village. Other people will come to help the folks here.\"","He believed there were many ruthless people like Liu Hong, but he also believed there were even more people in the Prefecture City willing to perform good deeds like the Xiao family. Let alone later, even right at this moment, he could hear the sound of horse hooves and reprimands echoing from inside the city gate behind them.","\"Can’t you see that our Sun family is going out to provide relief to the refugees? Hurry up and let us through!\"","\"If the Xiao family can do it, why can’t we?\"","\"Get out of the way quickly, or you’ll lose your official posts.\"","Instances like this were numerous. Chen Yi directly instructed, \"Fairy Tingyun, please hurry to Lin Village.\"","\"Rest assured, Mr. Chen...\"","Xiao Wan’er said no more; as long as these refugees were saved, it was fine. However, as she observed the conditions along the way, her face grew increasingly pale. She had only ever read about the miserable state of commoners during natural disasters and man-made calamities in books, mostly summed up by the phrase, \"exchanging children for food.\" But she had never been able to truly imagine it, nor did she want to believe it.","Now, seeing it with her own eyes—those bloodshot-eyed, starving refugees staring at the children beside them with the gaze of wild beasts... Xiao Wan’er had no choice but to believe it.","Chen Yi noticed her distress. He patted her shoulder and said softly, \"Once we start distributing the porridge, these people will be saved.\"","Xiao Wan’er didn’t care that Xiaodie and the others were still present. She leaned lightly against his shoulder and murmured an acknowledgment, unable to bear looking any longer. The three maids—Xiaodie, Cui’er, and Juan’er—felt the same, their eyes brimming with tears.","Only Yuan Liu’er stared outside in deep trance.","After a long while, Yuan Liu’er spoke in a low voice, \"Grandmaster, can Medicinal Stone cure these people?\"","Chen Yi looked at her in slight surprise. \"Medicinal Stone?\" He paused, then shook his head and said, \"It would be difficult. Although hunger is agonizing, it is not a disease. Moreover, they are too weak. Feeding them ordinary medicines wouldn’t be as effective as a piping hot bowl of rice soup.\"","Yuan Liu’er uttered an \"oh,\" her small face serious as she gazed out the window, lost in her own thoughts.","Chen Yi, on the other hand, could guess a little. Strictly speaking, Yuan Liu’er’s father had also died of \"starvation.\" She was likely struck by the scene and moved by compassion.","Stopping and starting along the way, the carriage eventually arrived outside Lin Village. Just as Chen Yi had guessed, the commoners from the Prefecture City who had previously gathered here were nowhere to be seen. They had been replaced by starving refugees with sallow faces, forcing their weak bodies to stand in a long line, waiting to drink a bowl of rice soup.","At the front of the line, Wang Lixing, Liu Si’er, and the others were busy cooking porridge. There were a total of four porridge distribution stations, each guarded by four Armored Warriors. Further out, Xiao Xuanshuo was leading men from the Xiao Family Punishment Hall to maintain order. And even further away were the disguised Liu Lang, Xue Duanyun, and the others. They were guarding a residence while observing the situation outside.","Chen Yi scanned the area and gained a general understanding of the situation before joining Xiao Xuanshuo alongside Xiao Wan’er.","Without pausing to look closer, Xiao Wan’er said, \"Uncle Xuanshuo, let’s set up a few more stoves and get them something to eat and drink as quickly as possible.\"","Xiao Xuanshuo glanced at her, his gaze then landing on Chen Yi and the others. He mused, \"It’s not that I don’t want to, but the grain...\"","Despite Elder Master Xiao taking out all their silver coins to purchase grain this time, compared to the sheer number of refugees, it was still a drop in the bucket.","Before Xiao Wan’er could speak, Chen Yi chimed in, \"Uncle Xuanshuo, we only need to hold out for today. I see that other Noble Families from the Prefecture City are also sending people.\"","\"Really?\"","Seeing his certainty, Xiao Xuanshuo hesitated no longer. He took some men and built a few more earthen stoves nearby. He then ordered people to bring over large iron cauldrons, light the fires, and start cooking.","Not long after, outside Lin Village, the refugees held their bowls and drank the rice soup, calling out \"Benefactors!\" with every mouthful.","Liu Lang crossed his arms and watched the busy Chen Yi, Xiao Wan’er, and the rest. Clicking his tongue, he said, \"As expected of the Xiao family, they are indeed charitable and generous. Dabao, do you think our boss also wants to do this?\"","Zhang Dabao looked at Chen Yi in the crowd and carefully replied, \"Probably... I suppose.\"","\"Hard to say,\" Liu Lang continued. \"The boss is incredibly calculating. He rarely does anything that puts him at a disadvantage.\"","\"...Brother Liu, I advise you not to speak ill of the boss.\"","\"What’s there to be afraid of? He’s not even here. Don’t worry...\"","Zhang Dabao opened his mouth to speak but stopped. Out of the corner of his eye, he caught Chen Yi calmly looking over in their direction. Frightened, he shuddered and quickly lowered his head.","\"Brother Liu, I did warn you,\" he thought. \"You just wouldn’t listen...\"","Liu Lang remained completely oblivious. Upon seeing Chen Yi looking over, he even tilted his head up, raised an eyebrow, and muttered, \"The Xiao family’s live-in son-in-law... What are you looking at Master Liu for? Whatever, out of respect for General Jinghong... why should I bicker with a frail scholar?\""]},{"number":545,"title":"Chapter 545 - 316: A Family That Accumulates Good Deeds Will Surely Have Abundant Blessings","paragraphs":["Chen Yi was already used to Liu Lang’s lack of filter. Scolding him was useless. Only a good beating would teach him a lesson.","Retracting his gaze, Chen Yi looked at the frail boy standing before him, holding a bowl with both hands. He smiled gently and said, \"Hold it steady.\"","He poured a ladle of rice gruel—half soup, half grains—into the bowl. The boy cast a fleeting glance at him, bowed low, and mumbled a soft, \"Thank you, benefactor,\" before carefully carrying the bowl away.","Beside him, Xiao Wan’er was doing the same, her eyes lowered as she doled out the gruel to the refugees. She couldn’t bear to look closely, nor could she clearly make out the mud-caked, emaciated faces of these people, but their continuous chorus of gratitude filled her ears. Some voices were deep, some clear, some genial, and others muffled. Without exception, almost all were weak and feeble. It was only after they took a sip of the gruel that their SLURP finally carried a hint of vitality.","Whenever Xiao Wan’er raised her head, she would meet pairs of hopeful eyes, and an inevitable pang of sorrow would wash over her.","\"Chen Yi, I’m afraid we won’t last much longer on our own,\" she murmured. \"If the family’s grain runs out in a few days, they...\"","Though her voice was soft, Chen Yi heard her clearly. He turned his head to look at Xiao Wan’er. Understanding how she felt, he said with a faint smile, \"Families that accumulate good deeds will surely be blessed with abundance. Just do our best.\"","Chen Yi was well aware that relying solely on the Xiao Family’s grain to aid tens of thousands of refugees was completely impossible. It wasn’t realistic. Even if all the other Noble Families pitched in, they would eventually eat through their reserves; it would still be a drop in the bucket. Only if the Government Office stepped in to properly disperse and settle the refugees, and manage the food supply, could this crisis be thoroughly resolved.","Xiao Wan’er lifted her head slightly to meet his gaze. The distress on her pale face faded a little as the corners of her lips curved upward in a breathtaking smile.","\"Mhm, just doing our best is enough.\"","On the other side of the encampment.","Ma Liangcai was leading Yuan Liu’er, Yuan Hao, and a few others to treat the severely ill refugees. He checked their pulses and diagnosed their conditions, teaching Yuan Liu’er along the way.","\"This elderly man is old and frail. After stumbling all the way here, his vitality has been drained, and exhaustion has turned into illness...","\"Ma’am, rest and don’t move. The wound on your leg is too severe, and the infection is spreading upwards. I will administer acupuncture first...","\"And also...\"","Yuan Liu’er watched carefully and listened attentively, silently committing everything to memory. Unknowingly, she grew more familiar with the *Treatise on Cold Pathogenic Diseases* she had been studying over the past few days.","Although Yuan Hao heard some of it, he couldn’t remember or understand a thing. After a short while, he felt bored. Catching sight of a few boys nearby who had just finished their gruel, he wandered over to join them. They murmured in hushed voices, mostly exchanging questions like where they were from, how old they were, and what their names were.","Yuan Hao grinned, told them his name, and asked how they had managed the journey.","\"We just followed wherever the adults went, crossing mountains and rivers,\" a relatively sturdy boy with tanned skin replied, looking at Yuan Hao with envy.","\"Then what did you eat?\" Yuan Hao asked.","\"In the beginning, everyone had dry rations. When those ran out, we scavenged for food everywhere,\" the boy answered. \"Have you ever eaten Black Bear?\"","\"Bear?\" Yuan Hao asked, surprised.","\"Yeah! My dad and the others hunted a Black Bear. It was massive, and it fed a lot of people a full meal.\"","Seeing the tanned boy thump his chest proudly as if he had hunted the bear himself, Yuan Hao glanced around enviously. \"Your dad is so amazing! Is he here?\"","For ordinary commoners, studying or practicing martial arts was an unreachable luxury. Therefore, the strongest among ordinary people naturally became their idols.","The tanned boy’s smile froze. He turned his head away, his expression turning sorrowful. \"He’s gone.","\"It was raining heavily that day. My dad took some people up the mountain to hunt, but they ran into Grandpa Mountain God’s fury and got buried in a mudslide.\"","Yuan Hao was just about to apologize when the tanned boy took a deep breath and continued.","\"My dad said that a man has to live on his feet in this life. No matter how hard or bitter it gets, you have to grit your teeth and endure it.","\"I survived, so I have to keep living for my dad.\"","Yuan Hao looked at him, at a loss for words. After a long while, he finally said, \"Good man.\"","Hearing this, all traces of sorrow vanished from the tanned boy’s face. \"I think my dad was a good man, too. Along the way, he and a few older men saved a lot of people...\"","As they chatted, the boys grew more acquainted and began playing simple games together. It was straightforward: tossing a copper plate and guessing heads or tails. The loser had to carry the winner on his back for a lap. Before long, the lively, playful laughter of the youngsters echoed through the otherwise lifeless crowd of refugees. Simple and pure.","Yuan Liu’er turned her head to look. Seeing Yuan Hao having fun, she smiled softly and continued assisting her master, Ma Liangcai, with the free clinic. Chen Yi noticed them too. Seeing nothing out of the ordinary, he went back to serving gruel to the refugees.","Everyone remained busy.","It was past Noon before nearly fifty thousand refugees had all received a bowl of gruel. Taking a brief moment to rest, Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er pulled Xiao Xuanshuo, Liu Si’er, and the others aside to discuss the upcoming arrangements.","\"With twenty thousand bushels of grain, if we use it sparingly, it should last us ten days.\"","\"We can’t calculate it like that,\" Chen Yi said.","\"Sir?\"","Chen Yi pointed toward the official road east of Lin Village and said softly, \"There are still refugees on the way.\"","This was merely the first day of the refugees’ arrival; there was no telling how many more would follow. At a conservative estimate, making it past five days would be a blessing.","Xiao Wan’er looked at him. \"Chen Yi, do you have a solution?\"","\"There is a way. If we exchange all our fine grain for coarse grain, we can stretch it for another five days. Plus...\" Chen Yi paused, his tone growing more resolute. \"Let’s use only coarse grain.\"","One bushel of fine grain could be exchanged for two bushels of coarse grain. Every extra day they could endure mattered.","They just had to hold out until...","Chen Yi’s gaze swept past Xiao Wan’er and landed outside a manor near the edge of Lin Village—under the eaves, Zhang Dabao, Liu Lang, Xue Duanyun, and the others had been continuously peering in their direction. He didn’t know if those grain merchant guilds had been successfully fooled.","After a moment of thought, Chen Yi whispered a few words to Xiao Wan’er. \"I’ll go over there and take a look.\""]},{"number":546,"title":"Chapter 546 - 316: A Family That Accumulates Good Deeds Will Surely Have Abundant Blessings","paragraphs":["Xiao Wan’er naturally wasn’t worried about his safety, but she still instructed Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang to keep an eye on his whereabouts.","Chen Yi went along with it. Bypassing the crowd, he approached Zhang Dabao and the others. Cupping his hands, he asked with a smile, \"I heard from those returning to the city that you have grain on hand. Which of you is the Steward?\"","Liu Lang slightly raised an eyebrow, about to speak, but saw Zhang Dabao rush ahead of him to bow.","\"This humble one greets Mr. Qingzhou,\" Zhang Dabao said respectfully. \"You can discuss any matters directly with me.\" As he spoke, he winked and signaled with his eyes, indicating that he was at Chen Yi’s beck and call.","Chen Yi glanced at him and nodded with a smile. \"There are too many eyes and ears here. Why don’t we find a quiet place?\"","Zhang Dabao naturally had no objections. Pushing past Liu Lang, he invited Chen Yi into the courtyard.","Watching the two of them close the wooden doors behind them, Liu Lang couldn’t help but grumble, \"He isn’t even a member of the Xiao family, yet he comes knocking to ask for grain? Am I right, guys?\"","Xue Duanyun nodded with an awkward smile, not daring to utter a single word. He only dared to peek at Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang from the corner of his eye.","Since Chen Yi and his group had arrived, Xue Duanyun, along with Zhang Sanhu and Zhang Sihu, had been acting like mice meeting a cat, completely silent. They were terrified of being discovered by their two senior martial sisters, as they wouldn’t be able to explain themselves.","Noticing their strange behavior, Liu Lang curled his lips. \"Are they really that scary? If we’re talking about scary, it has to be our boss. His Martial Arts are so domineering! I couldn’t even take a single move from him. If he hadn’t shown mercy that time, I would have died eight hundred times over.\"","Speaking of this, Liu Lang caught sight of Xiao Wan’er. He stared at her carefully for a moment before suddenly bursting into laughter. Lowering his voice, he asked, \"Say, do you think the boss fancies her?\"","Xue Duanyun and the other two looked over. Realizing what he meant, their faces revealed a hint of ambiguous understanding. It went without saying.","Liu Lang lightly slapped his thigh and chuckled. \"As they say, even heroes struggle against the allure of a beauty, and the boss is no exception! Otherwise, facing dangerous people like the horse bandits, how could he dare to charge in alone? Yes, definitely. Next time I see the boss, I’ll be sure to ask him—\"","Inside the gates, Zhang Dabao heard his voice and shook his head inwardly. \"Brother Liu is a lost cause,\" he thought. \"It’s bad enough he previously called His Excellency frail, but now he dares to gossip about His Excellency and the Eldest Miss of the Xiao family. The worst part is that His Excellency is right in front of him...\"","Chen Yi had also heard Liu Lang’s words, and a faint smile appeared on his face. \"It seems one beating wasn’t enough,\" he thought.","Then, while casually asking Zhang Dabao for his surname aloud, Chen Yi traced a few characters in thin air: [Is everything going smoothly?]","Zhang Dabao nodded in understanding and traced back: [Smoothly. Lin Zhenghong will gather grain from the other families today. After Midnight tonight, they will find a way to transport it out of the city and trade it two hundred miles to the west.]","After Midnight...","Chen Yi noted the hour and gave a slight nod. [You don’t need to keep an eye on Lin Village anymore. The matter with Lin Zhenghong is more important.]","Since he had come here with Xiao Wan’er, the grain here would naturally not be lost. Besides, Xue Duanyun and the others were still present.","Once he had a clear picture of the situation, Chen Yi felt more assured. He chatted with Zhang Dabao for a few more moments before walking out of the courtyard.","Seeing the two of them come out, Liu Lang cupped his hands with a smirk. \"Is Mr. Qingzhou leaving so soon?\"","Chen Yi ignored him, walking straight toward Xiao Wan’er and the others.","Liu Lang’s smile froze. Recovering himself, he shook his Punches at Chen Yi’s retreating back. \"What Mr. Qingzhou? He’s just a fraud fishing for fame!\"","Zhang Dabao shot him a helpless look. \"Brother Liu, you should really speak less.\" The more he spoke, the more mistakes he made, and his ending would be miserable.","Liu Lang scoffed disdainfully, \"What can he do to me?\" Then he changed the subject, \"By the way, what did he want? Is he after the grain?\"","\"Yes, that’s right...\"","\"Unless the boss gives the word, who dares touch it? Not even Mr. Qingzhou!\"","\"The problem is that the boss has already given the word,\" Zhang Dabao thought. He shook his head, deciding to keep his distance from Liu Lang after tonight to avoid suffering any unprovoked disaster.","Chen Yi acted as if he hadn’t heard anything, rejoining Xiao Wan’er and the rest.","\"I’ve asked. They do have grain over there, though I don’t know which family from the Prefecture City it belongs to,\" Chen Yi said. \"However, seeing that they were selling grain at fair prices earlier, the master of that household must be a charitable and generous person.\"","Xiao Wan’er’s face lit up with joy. \"How much grain do they have?\"","\"He didn’t specify, but there should be at least ten thousand shi.\"","The incident had happened so suddenly; if Chen Yi hadn’t reacted quickly, not even these ten thousand shi of grain would have been left.","Xiao Wan’er was not disappointed. Instead, she calculated eagerly, \"Then we can hold out for another five days.\"","\"Probably...\"","After discussing the matter, the group split up. Xiao Xuanshuo took his men and the grain to exchange for coarse grain with the nearby Noble Families, while the others continued to busy themselves with distributing porridge.","It wasn’t until the sky grew dark that Chen Yi and the others took a carriage back. Passing by Jishi Medicine Hall, they saw Ma Liangcai leading Yuan Liu’er, Yuan Hao, and the others out to bid their farewells. Chen Yi purposely took another look at Yuan Hao. Seeing nothing unusual about him, he patiently followed Xiao Wan’er and the rest back to the Marquis’s Mansion.","Watching the carriage depart, Yuan Liu’er pulled Yuan Hao along as they followed Ma Liangcai. Her mind was still recalling the Methods for treating illnesses and saving lives she had learned during the day.","Yuan Hao, on the other hand, occasionally glanced at the carriage flying the Xiao family flag, his face full of envy. \"Sis, the people from the Marquis’s Mansion are all good people.\"","\"They are also highly capable people,\" he thought. \"Not only is the Eldest Miss beautiful, but she is also very kind-hearted, always treating the refugees outside the city with gentleness. The Second Son-in-Law—my sister’s grandmaster—is exactly the same. He is just as described in books, gentle and refined. Then there are the Guards, every one of them tall and burly, clad in Iron Armor and wearing long Blades at their waists, looking incredibly majestic.\"","\"Mm,\" Yuan Liu’er replied absentmindedly. \"Grandmaster and the others are our benefactors. Remember not to act recklessly when you see them in the future.\"","\"I know, Sis...\"","A short while later.","After finishing dinner at Jishi Medicine Hall, Yuan Liu’er and Yuan Hao bid farewell to Ma Liangcai and made their way back to Kangle Lane."]},{"number":547,"title":"Chapter 547 - 316: A Family That Accumulates Good Deeds Will Surely Have Abundant Blessings","paragraphs":["This was a small alley near the East City Gate.","It was home to fewer than a hundred households.","The narrow lane was deep and dimly lit. The uneven, potholed flagstone path caused Yuan Liu’er and Yuan Hao to stumble along, their footing constantly shifting.","As they walked, Yuan Hao recounted what he had seen and heard during the day.","\"Liu’er, they’re so pitiful.","\"They came all the way from Guang’an County along the Chishui River. They didn’t even dare to take the official roads, afraid of being stopped by the Government Office’s men, so they could only travel through mountain trails and waterways.","\"There was no food on the road. Many had to fight wild beasts, and some even waded into the freezing water to catch fish.","\"When there was truly nothing left, they resorted to eating tree bark and wild weeds...\"","Yuan Liu’er was more mature. Having recently experienced a tragedy in their own family, she naturally empathized with their plight.","\"Don’t mention this to Mother and the others when we get back.\"","\"I know, Liu’er.\"","Yuan Hao pulled a paper-wrapped sugar cube from his pocket and offered it to her. \"Want some?\"","Yuan Liu’er glanced at it and shook her head. \"No.\"","She then asked, \"Where did you get it?\"","\"A peddler just passed by and gave us each a piece of candy.\"","Seeing that she didn’t want it, Yuan Hao carefully took a lick and chuckled. \"So sweet.\"","Yuan Liu’er patted his head. \"Make sure you hide it well. Don’t let anyone else see it.\"","Kangle Lane was mostly populated by poor families. In a place where people couldn’t even afford meals, there would always be some who resorted to petty theft.","She was accustomed to such things, but she didn’t want Yuan Hao to experience the cruelty of human nature too early.","\"I know, I know...\"","Yuan Hao couldn’t resist licking it a few more times before carefully wrapping the candy up and tucking it securely into his clothes.","However, not long after returning home, he began to feel dizzy.","\"Mother, I’m sleepy.\"","\"Hao, go to sleep then...\"","Just after 7:00 PM.","Chen Yi moved with feather-light steps. Donning a mask and changing into his Night Clothes, he sneaked out of the Spring Lotus Garden.","Today, aside from Xiao Wuge, everyone in the inner courtyard had been exhausted from a long day and had gone to bed early.","In the quiet night, Chen Yi moved alone.","He slipped through a stretch of low-lying woods, evaded the Xiao Family’s hidden sentries, and headed straight for Kangle Lane.","By this time, it was already late at night.","Yet, there were still quite a few people on the streets.","Wandering Martial Artists mingled in various inns and taverns, while the commoners were mostly heading back to their own homes.","There was some laughter and chatting, but not much.","The atmosphere was largely solemn.","Even the out-of-town Jianghu People sensed it. Speaking in diverse accents from all over the realm—from the South Sea to the northern borders—they discussed the recent events in Shu State.","Among them were plenty of well-informed individuals detailing the hidden secrets of certain matters.","\"That ’Dragon Tiger’ Liu Wu definitely took a fancy to the Xiao Family’s eldest daughter. Otherwise, why would he take such a massive risk to mount a rescue?\"","\"Maybe he’s just highly skilled and daring?\"","\"Bullshit!","\"It has to be a hero saving the beauty!\"","Chen Yi smiled and walked past them, secretly agreeing with the \"hero saving the beauty\" sentiment.","It was just that, as the hero in question, he had been forced into it.","Before long, Chen Yi wound his way into Kangle Alley. He hadn’t even begun to search from house to house when he heard a frantic cry coming from deep within.","\"Help! Someone help! Hao... Hao is dying!\"","The startled neighbors got up one after another. Some asked what had happened, while others grumbled and cursed.","Chen Yi looked toward the source of the noise. In a flash, he slipped into the residence, hiding in a corner to observe the situation inside.","He saw that Yuan Hao, who had been full of life just during the day, now had a livid complexion, his lips and teeth tinged with a dark, sickly hue.","Yuan Liu’er was currently checking his pulse.","A few others stood by, crying out anxiously while dealing with the inquiring neighbors.","Chen Yi scanned the area. After confirming there were no suspicious individuals around, he utilized his Qi Observation Skill to inspect Yuan Hao’s body.","With just one glance, his expression grew grave.","Without a moment’s hesitation, he strode directly to Yuan Liu’er’s side. \"Step aside, let me!\"","Turning a deaf ear to him, Yuan Liu’er continued checking the pulse, muttering under her breath.","Seeing this, Chen Yi wasted no words. He pulled her away and said in a deep voice, \"This is a plague toxin. Take them and get away from him!\"","Yuan Liu’er froze. Before she could even process who this stranger was, she blurted out, \"What is a plague toxin?\"","\"The plague.\"","\"The plague?!\""]},{"number":548,"title":"Chapter 548 - 317: Hell Has No Gates","paragraphs":["Chen Yi didn’t even need to say another word.","The moment the word \"plague\" came out, the neighbors who had just wanted to step forward and watch frantically retreated from the house.","They were both panicked and terrified.","\"Mrs. Yuan, your family caught the plague! Why are you screaming blindly? Are you trying to drag us all down to the grave with Old Yuan?\"","\"To think I rushed over in a panic when I heard the Yuan family’s women crying for help. Is this how you repay us?\"","\"Damn it...\"","Yuan Liu’er’s mother, holding a girl in each hand, also retreated a few steps, turning a deaf ear to the surrounding curses. She looked at Yuan Hao, whose fate was unknown, and then at Chen Yi inside. With a heavy THUMP, she knelt on the ground and repeatedly knocked her head against the floor.","THUD, THUD, THUD...","\"I beg you, benefactor, please save my Hao’er! Please save him...\"","Chen Yi glanced sideways and ordered the bewildered Yuan Liu’er in a deep voice, \"Go help your mother up and take her away!","\"I can save your brother!\"","Looking at his unfamiliar yet somewhat familiar face, Yuan Liu’er inexplicably believed his words. Without time to overthink, she hurriedly pulled her mother and two younger sisters up, and together they retreated from the house.","\"Mother, our benefactor says he can save Hao’er. Let’s wait outside,\" Yuan Liu’er comforted her. She didn’t forget to shout to the surrounding crowd, \"Thank you all, uncles and aunts, for coming to help. Since the benefactor inside can save my brother Hao, he can surely save our lives as well.","\"I hope everyone can show some mercy with your words...\"","\"But that’s the plague! You—!?\"","Before the speaker could finish, Yuan Liu’er frowned and looked over. \"Uncle Zhao, my mother, my two younger sisters, and I were the first to touch Hao’er.","\"Don’t forget, if this plague is truly that fierce, we of the Yuan family will be the first to die!\"","Hearing this, the man choked on his words, his expression fluctuating unpredictably. Most of the nearby neighbors resentfully shut their mouths.","However, some still looked indignant and muttered, \"It’s not even certain if the guy inside can save your Haozi.","\"If the plague really spreads, your Yuan family will be the sinners of our Kangle Lane.\"","Yuan Liu’er furrowed her brows fiercely. \"I don’t even fear death, so why would I fear being a sinner?\"","The surrounding people fell completely silent, only staring helplessly through the gaps in the fence to watch the situation in the courtyard.","Yuan Liu’er did the same. Despite acting so tough moments ago, in truth, she was more anxious than anyone else and carried a deep sense of guilt. Recalling the events of the day, she roughly deduced that Yuan Hao must have contracted the plague while playing with the refugees outside the city. If it cost Yuan Hao his life, she would never be able to forgive herself.","With these thoughts in mind, Yuan Liu’er gritted her teeth and walked back into the house. Pretending to be calm, she stood beside Chen Yi and asked, \"Benefactor, if there is anything you need, just give the order, and I...\"","Chen Yi waved a hand to dismiss her, his focus entirely on examining the aura inside Yuan Hao’s body. \"Go boil some water.\"","\"Ah, oh, I’ll go right away.\" Yuan Liu’er frantically hurried off to start a fire and boil water.","Chen Yi had no time to pay her any mind. As crystalline light flickered in his eyes under the Qi Observation Skill, the aura inside Yuan Hao’s body appeared as a completely tangled mess. He couldn’t help but frown.","At this moment, aside from a stream of black Qi flowing throughout Yuan Hao’s entire body, there were also golden, red, and cyan auras invading his internal organs. It did not resemble highly toxic poison; instead, it contained the Spiritual Essence aura of Wood, Metal, Fire, Water, and Earth. However, this Five Elements Spiritual Essence did not correspond harmoniously to the attributes of the five organs. Instead, they countered them one by one.","For example, the Fire essence went to the Water-attribute kidneys, and the Water essence went to the Fire-attribute heart, completely blocking all circulation of the Qi Mechanism in Yuan Hao’s body.","And that was not all.","The most serious issue was the microscopic poisonous insects within Yuan Hao’s blood—shaped like flying ants, they reproduced at an incredibly rapid rate. In the blink of an eye, the number of these poisonous insects had doubled.","Under such circumstances, Chen Yi had no choice but to be cautious.","The profound mysteries of the Medical Dao flowed through his mind, taking the Yin Yang Five Elements as the foundation, ascending on the left and descending on the right... Soon, he formed a strategy to cure the poison.","He first needed to take out silver needles to trap the poisonous insects outside Yuan Hao’s five organs, preventing them from invading the heart meridian. Next, he would untangle the Spiritual Essence, then neutralize or expel the plague poison to cut off the source of nourishment for the poisonous insects. Finally, he would eradicate the poisonous insects altogether...","But this method was only viable for treating Yuan Hao alone. If the plague poison spread to other people and mixed with their pre-existing illnesses, the detoxification process would be far more difficult.","Understanding this, Chen Yi stopped rushing to treat Yuan Hao. Instead, he reached out with both hands and placed his fingers on Yuan Hao’s wrists to take his pulse, memorizing the condition. Then, he pulled Yuan Hao’s mouth open, examined his tongue, and revealed a thoughtful expression.","\"Fire essence violates Kidney Water; the Yang-heat evil Qi drives straight toward the kidney acupoints, and the regulation of Qi is lost.","\"Water essence attacks Heart Fire; Yin-cold water Qi rises to bully the sovereign heart, and the God within is disturbed.","\"Metal essence harms Liver Wood; the harsh Metal Qi aggressively counters Liver Wood, leaving it powerless to dredge and drain.","\"Wood essence insults Spleen Earth; the wind-wood Qi invades the central region, failing in its duty of transportation and transformation, throwing ascent and descent into chaos.","\"Earth essence suppresses Lung Metal; stagnant Earth Qi rises to shroud the canopy, obstructing dissemination and descent, completely blocking the airway.","\"The reverse countering of the Five Elements causes the Qi Mechanism of the five organs to knot and congest, severing all paths of ascent, descent, entry, and exit throughout the entire body.","\"Coupled with those poisonous insects... twelve hours... No, given the frail bodies of those refugees outside the city, I’m afraid they won’t even last that long.","\"Six hours, six hours at most...\"","If the refugees infected with the plague poison did not receive effective treatment during this period, they would turn into nests for those poisonous insects. And when the poisonous insects swarmed out, anyone nearby would become their new nests.","As Chen Yi figured this out, a frosty expression surfaced on his face.","\"The Five Poison Sect deserves to die!\"","There was no need to overthink it; those poisonous insects inside Yuan Hao’s body were undoubtedly cultivated by the Five Poison Sect. But it was a complete mystery as to why they would do such a thing.","The figure of Liu Hong suddenly flashed into Chen Yi’s mind—it could only be him!","\"That old dog has finally grown desperate, resorting to such a perilous move. His... his schemes must be massive!\""]},{"number":549,"title":"Chapter 549 - 317: Hell Has No Gates","paragraphs":["Thinking of this, Chen Yi no longer hesitated. He took out another silver needle and pierced Yuan Hao’s heart area.","True Essence flowed, guiding the silver needle to connect with Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism to sort out the oppressive Spiritual Essence aura.","Once the Five Elements Spiritual Essence returned to its rightful place and the Qi Mechanism within Yuan Hao’s body flowed smoothly, Chen Yi ordered, \"Hot water!\"","\"Coming!\"","Yuan Liu’er promptly brought over a basin of hot water and placed it next to Chen Yi.","Chen Yi sliced open Yuan Hao’s wrist to let out blood, using his True Essence to force out the poisonous insects within the boy’s body while simultaneously controlling his True Essence to seal the area around the wooden basin.","A moment later.","Chen Yi retrieved the silver needle from Yuan Hao and looked at the poisonous insects in the basin of hot water.","The venomous bugs, invisible to the naked eye of ordinary people, were flapping their wings, but under the seal of his True Essence, they were completely unable to fly out.","Chen Yi glanced at them, then used the Qi Observation Skill to examine Yuan Hao and everyone else around. \"The plague poison has not spread,\" he said calmly. \"It’s fine now. You may all return home. Remember, follow the government office’s notices and do not go out in the coming days.\"","\"Yes, yes...\"","After receiving Chen Yi’s clear diagnosis, the people outside the house finally breathed a sigh of relief and returned home one by one.","Even those who wanted to spread the news didn’t dare to go out at this time.","Yuan Liu’er’s mother and sisters also walked in, expressing their profound gratitude to Chen Yi.","Chen Yi waved his hand. Just as he was about to offer a few words of comfort, the unconscious Yuan Hao rubbed his eyes and woke up.","\"Mother, oldest sister, second sister, third sister... What’s wrong?\"","He looked around blankly. His gaze landed on Chen Yi, and he suddenly blurted out, \"Grandmaster?\"","Chen Yi looked at him carefully and shook his head. \"You’ve got the wrong person.\"","The boy had a pure spirituality, managing to catch a hint of a similar aura between Chen Yi and himself.","Yuan Hao paused for a moment and scratched his head. Before he could even get up, he was pulled into a tight embrace by his mother and sisters.","\"You scared me to death, you scared your mother to death...\"","Once Yuan Hao realized what had happened, he couldn’t help but cry in lingering fear.","Seeing this, Chen Yi looked at Yuan Liu’er and asked, \"Tell me, where did you all go today?\"","Yuan Liu’er glanced at the still-wailing Yuan Hao and recalled, \"Lin Village, outside the East City Gate. We were there all day and only came back after dark.\"","Chen Yi thought for a moment and asked, \"Did you encounter any suspicious people or come into contact with anything strange on your way back?\"","During the day, he had paid close attention to these siblings and hadn’t noticed any abnormalities.","He could only deduce that Yuan Hao was exposed to the plague poison after they had separated.","\"Suspicious...\"","Remembering something, Yuan Liu’er turned and shouted, \"Hao, that piece of candy!\"","Still crying, Yuan Hao took out the sugar-coated sugar cube from his pocket. \"Sister, this...\"","Yuan Liu’er was about to take it, but Chen Yi waved his hand to stop her. He used his True Essence to pull the candy into his own hand.","A sharp glint flashed in his eyes as he inspected it.","A moment later, a faint smile appeared on his face. \"So that’s how it is.\"","Plague poison.","It was a special poison refined from a plague using a Secret Technique.","It was far more potent and highly contagious.","Furthermore, whoever refined this poison would mix in other highly toxic substances, greatly increasing the difficulty of detoxification.","But if one had a sample of the plague poison...","All the toxic ingredients in its formula instantly surfaced in Chen Yi’s mind.","Upon this discovery, he instructed Yuan Liu’er without leaving room for argument, \"Go get a pen and paper and write down what I say.\"","Yuan Liu’er didn’t even hesitate. She agreed, ran to fetch a pen and paper, and sprawled on the ground to write.","Chen Yi detailed the pathology of the plague poison step by step, then recited three prescriptions.","Once Yuan Liu’er finished writing, Chen Yi took it and reviewed it. Then, he grabbed a few more sheets of paper and copied out three more versions, perfectly imitating Yuan Liu’er’s handwriting.","After he was done, he handed her one sheet. \"Take this to the medicine halls in the Prefecture City and tell them to prepare the medicinal ingredients listed here.\"","Yuan Liu’er carefully tucked it away. \"May I ask which medicine hall my benefactor is referring to?\"","Chen Yi glanced at her, the corners of his mouth curling up. He gave her a light smack on the back of her head and said, \"No need to test me. Just hurry and hand it over to Jishi Medicine Hall.\"","Not panicked by him seeing through her thoughts, Yuan Liu’er looked at him from under his large hand and asked, \"May I ask for my benefactor’s esteemed name? I will definitely repay this great kindness in the future.\"","Chen Yi smiled. \"Liu Wu.\"","Immediately after, he leaped into the air, taking the remaining papers with him.","Yuan Liu’er watched him disappear, then turned to Yuan Hao and asked, \"Hao, why did you call our benefactor ’Grandmaster’ just now?\"","Wiping his eyes, Yuan Hao sobbed, \"I don’t know... I, I just thought he looked like him...\"","Hearing this, Yuan Liu’er looked thoughtfully at the northern night sky. After giving a few instructions, she also left the house.","Regardless of who the person was, the appearance of a plague in Shu State Prefecture City was an earth-shattering matter, and she didn’t dare to be the slightest bit careless.","Chen Yi likewise could not afford to be careless.","Leaving Kangle Alley, he headed straight for Kangning Street in the North City.","Now that the Five Poison Sect had made their move, it was time for the Mountain Race to take action.","Otherwise, no matter how capable he was at saving lives using the Medical Dao, he couldn’t guarantee he’d be able to fend off whatever follow-up moves the Five Poison Sect had planned.","Just then:","[10:30 PM. You saved Yuan Hao’s life using the Medical Dao and provided a detoxifying prescription for the plague poison.]","[Reward: Sugar-Making Essentials, Opportunity +12.]","[Evaluation: Arrived on the scene, voice heard, presence known. Fairly good performance.]","Chen Yi glanced at it and paid it no more attention.","It was fortunate that it had been Yuan Liu’er this time. Had it been anyone else, he might have just stayed inside the Marquis’s Mansion to practice his Four Symbols Skill.","If that were the case, by the time he noticed the plague poison in the Prefecture City, many commoners would likely have already fallen victim to it.","As Chen Yi thought of this, the icy glint in his eyes grew heavier.","With his True Essence surging, wind gathered beneath his feet as his body transformed into a streak of shadow. In just a few breaths, he arrived at Kangning Street.","He tilted his head to listen carefully.","Locating where Pei Guanli, Pei Qian, and the others were, Chen Yi headed straight for that residence."]},{"number":550,"title":"Chapter 550 - 317: Hell Has No Gates","paragraphs":["Before he even landed, a hoarse voice rang in his ears. \"Who goes there?\"","Chen Yi looked toward the voice and saw a thin old man dressed in Mountain Race attire, with a dark face, black eyes, and a square mouth and nose.","\"I am Liu Wu. I have come specifically to seek the Mountain Race’s assistance.\"","\"Liu Wu? The ’Dragon Tiger’ Liu Wu?\"","\"That would be me.\"","The old man looked him up and down, a grin suddenly breaking out on his pitch-black face.","\"You truly live up to being a renowned figure in Shu State. What a dignified appearance. No wonder Miss Pei has been constantly talking about you.","\"I am Pei Ze of the Mountain Race. Come in and tell me what you need.\"","Chen Yi nodded and followed him into the residence. However, after taking just a few Steps, he noticed abnormal sounds outside the gatehouse. Hundreds of Gu Insects were actually hidden in the shadowed corners.","Seeing that he had discovered them, Pei Ze said with a chuckle, \"They are just little playthings our race uses for warning. Please forgive us, my young friend.\"","Chen Yi naturally did not say much, but what followed truly opened his eyes.","After taking ten Steps, the number of Gu Insects broke a thousand. After a hundred Steps, tens of thousands of Gu Insects all turned to look at him.","Although they posed little threat, Chen Yi’s overly sharp senses still found it somewhat uncomfortable. After all, those were tens of thousands of Gu Insects. Not to mention their emotionless gazes, just the convergence of the faint sounds they made was enough to make his hair stand on end.","It wasn’t until he entered the back residence that this feeling finally dissipated a bit.","\"Wait a moment, my young friend. I will go...\"","Before Pei Ze could finish his sentence, a series of JINGLE JINGLE sounds approached from afar.","Chen Yi looked over. No matter how much coldness he held in his heart, he couldn’t help but smile.","Pei Guanli ran over with her hair disheveled, rubbing her eyes as she ran, looking half-asleep. Upon seeing Chen Yi, her eyes lit up, and she ran over on her tender white bare feet.","\"You... My Lord, why are you here?","\"I thought Little Flower had smelled the wrong scent.\"","Chen Yi revealed a faint smile. \"There are some matters that made my visit necessary.\"","Pei Guanli’s smiling face turned into a pout. She leaned in close and muttered, \"What? You’re not here to take me back?\"","Chen Yi patted her head. \"Wait a little longer.\"","\"I know, I know. Waiting is fine. I’m not in a hurry, hehe...\"","\"Not in a hurry?\" Pei Ze observed their expressions and said with an odd look, \"Miss Pei, who was it that complained every day about how boring it is here?\"","\"Third Granduncle, don’t say it out loud! Be careful, or I’ll pull your beard...\"","As they were speaking, Pei Qian and several other Mountain Race members arrived together.","\"Senior, Se... You?\" Previously, Pei Qian had only ever seen that black iron mask. This was his first time seeing Chen Yi in this \"Liu Wu\" disguise, and he couldn’t help but open his mouth in surprise. \"How... how old are you?\"","Before Chen Yi could answer, a young girl even younger than Pei Guanli squeezed through and looked up at him.","\"You’re the ’Lord’ Sister Guanli talked about?","\"You do look quite dashing. I approve of your marriage. However, you can’t bully Sister Guanli in the future, or else...\"","Pei Guanli hurriedly covered the girl’s mouth. Blushing fiercely, she shouted, \"Lan Yanni, or else what? If you dare spout any more nonsense, be careful I don’t tear your mouth off!\"","\"Mmph... yoo... can’t beat mm...\"","Another middle-aged man and woman arrived together. They glanced at Chen Yi, their expressions largely the same as Pei Ze’s had been earlier.","Although Chen Yi found this amusing, business was more important.","After exchanging pleasantries with Pei Qian and the others, he took the sugar cube out of his pocket. His tone turned somewhat serious. \"The people from the Five Poison Sect have made their move!\"","\"Hmm?\"","Pei Qian, Pei Ze, and the others instantly wore solemn expressions. Without needing to ask, several Gu Insects flew out from their bodies and landed on the sugar cube.","A moment later, Pei Ze looked at the dead Gu Insects on the sugar cube and furrowed his brows deeply. \"It is indeed the Poison Refining Technique of those Gui’Ers from the Five Poison Sect.","\"However... the Poisonous Insects on it...\"","Pei Qian finished his sentence. \"...are very similar to our Mountain Race’s Witch Transformation Technique for Gu Insects.\"","The middle-aged man named Li Yunjun revealed murderous intent. \"Thirty years ago, several people from our race were captured by the Five Poison Sect.","\"The Five Poison Sect must have obtained the Witchcraft and Gu Skill from them.\"","He paused, then looked at Chen Yi and asked, \"May I ask where you obtained this poison, sir?\"","Chen Yi put away the sugar cube and said, \"From the refugees outside the East City Gate. The Five Poison Sect’s people hid among them at some point and spread these things out.","\"Fortunately, it hasn’t been long. As of right now, no one should have lost their lives because of it.\"","Hearing this, Pei Guanli blanked for a moment. She looked suspiciously at Pei Ze and the others. \"Third Granduncle, Brother, didn’t you say you were keeping a close eye on the people from the Five Poison Sect?","\"How did they leave the Prefecture City?\"","Pei Qian pursed his lips slightly and remained silent.","Pei Ze, who was standing beside him, wore a cold expression. \"We naturally kept a close eye on those Five Poison Sect members in Xinglin Hall. However, if they came in from the outside...\"","Li Yunjun nodded in understanding. \"This kind of Poison Refining Technique is sinister and vicious. Coupled with the Witchcraft and Gu Skill...","\"There shouldn’t be many people in the Five Poison Sect who can pull this off. Thinking about it, it could only be him.","\"The Great Elder of the Five Poison Sect—Yan Jingchen!\"","A fierce grin tugged at the corners of Pei Ze’s mouth. \"An old friend has returned to Shu State. How worthy of celebration!\"","After saying that, he looked at Pei Qian. \"Search!\"","Pei Qian grunted in agreement. With a flip of his wrist, a palm-sized piece of bamboo, as translucent as jade, appeared in his hand. Next, he bit down on one end of the bamboo and blew hard into it.","\"WOOO—\"","A shrill and piercing sound suddenly rang out. Following that, a charmingly naive, plump white caterpillar slowly crawled out from the other end of the bamboo. Once its entire body was out, it curled into a ball, and a cocoon quickly formed around it. It was like a caterpillar metamorphosing into a moth.","Seeing this, Pei Qian waved to the others and signaled, \"It will take another half an hour.\"","Pei Ze nodded and said, \"Everyone, go prepare.\"","Everyone except for Pei Guanli returned to their rooms, clearly preparing for a major battle.","Chen Yi quietly watched their actions from the side, having no intention of leaving. Since the Five Poison Sect’s people had arrived, he also wanted to meet them.","But before that, Chen Yi still had one thing to do.","Before he could even speak, however, a streak of Jin Guang flashed before his eyes:","[Daily Intelligence · Earth-level Lower Grade: At the third quarter of the Chou hour, Yan Jingchen led the Five Poison Sect to attack Lin Zhenghong, Liu Lang, and the others. Reward: Obtain a massive Opportunity.]","Hmm?","Chen Yi blanked slightly, then looked toward the west, his gaze narrowing.","\"The people from the Five Poison Sect went there?\" he thought. \"To think they actually know about the trade between the grain merchant firms and Liu Lang’s group. Is it Liu Hong? That’s right. Li Sanyuan previously mentioned wanting to drag Liu Taofang down with them. It seems that old fox Liu Hong has made his move first.\"","Thinking of this, a smile curled the corners of Chen Yi’s mouth.","\"There is a road to the Celestial Court, yet you refuse to take it; there is no door to Hell, yet you barge right in. Heh...\""]},{"number":551,"title":"Chapter 551 - 318: The Mantis Stalks the Cicada!","paragraphs":["The people of the Five Poison Sect had been in Shu State for quite some time.","Initially, it was assumed they were associating with Liu Zhaoxue to use the Jing State Liu Family against the Mountain Race. Unexpectedly, they had another motive for coming to Shu State—they were likely colluding with Liu Hong to deliberately cause disaster.","This time, if Chen Yi hadn’t been in the right place at the right time and immediately noticed the Five Poison Sect’s subtle movements, the outcome would have been dire. Given a few more days, tens of thousands of commoners inside and outside the Prefecture City would have suffered this calamity and died tragic deaths.","Even now...","Chen Yi looked at the sky, then turned to the Mountain Race people standing quietly around him. \"The Five Poison Sect’s scheme this time is not small. Even if we find their location, we still need to guard against their contingency plans.\"","Pei Ze, Pei Qian, and the others exchanged glances. \"You might as well speak plainly, young friend.\"","\"Plague poison is different from the rest; it’s extremely malicious and can cause massive casualties among the commoners in a very short time.","\"I want to notify some people now so they can prepare in advance.\"","Pei Ze nodded. \"That is how it should be. Please, go ahead.\"","Pei Qian and the others naturally had no objections.","However, Pei Guanli asked, \"Sir, aren’t you going with me?\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"You all go first. I will head over shortly.\"","Yuan Hao could hold on for that long, but those refugees could not. After a brief exchange, Chen Yi disappeared in a flash.","Pei Guanli stared at his retreating back, the smile on her face growing wider as she giggled incessantly.","Beside her, the little girl Lan Yanni looked up at her. Teasing the little white snake wrapped around her wrist, she said, \"Sister Guanli, Dragon Tiger’s real name shouldn’t be Liu Wu, right? It looks like a fake name.\"","Pei Guanli gave her a joyful look. \"Of course not.\"","\"Then what’s his real name?\"","\"I’m not telling you.\"","\"Sister Guanli, after we finish dealing with the Five Poison Sect, we have to go back to the mountains.\"","\"So what?\"","Zhu Fangling smiled mischievously. \"Lan Girl means she plans to tell your Ah Ma about this. There’s no guarantee the old lady won’t come down the mountain personally to see that ’Dragon Tiger’.\"","\"Ah?\"","Seeing Lan Yanni nod, Pei Guanli’s smile vanished. She bared her teeth, brandished her claws, and pounced on the girl, wrapping an arm around her neck and trapping her head against her chest. \"If you dare spout nonsense, I... I’ll let Little Flower bite you!\"","\"I won’t dare! I won’t dare anymore...\"","Pei Ze watched the two of them roughhouse but did not intervene. Instead, he looked up at the cloudless night sky and said unhurriedly, \"The Five Poison Sect... After this, I hope they still exist.\"","Li Yunjun glanced at Pei Qian, who was fully engrossed in incubating his insect cocoons, and asked in a low voice, \"Mr. Pei, you are the most familiar with the Five Poison Sect among us. Tell me more about that Yan Jingchen.\"","\"What? Are you scared?\"","\"It’s better to be prepared.\"","\"Heh, this time just follow Xiaoqian and charge their formations. Leave the rest to me.\"","A ferocious sneer appeared on Pei Ze’s gaunt face. A foot-long centipede crawled out of his nostril, slithering along the deep wrinkles of his skin all the way up to his shoulder. \"Old buddy, it’s been a long time since you made a move. Do you still remember the taste of killing?\"","\"HISS!\"","Two hundred miles west of the Shu State Prefecture City.","A bright moon hung high in the sky. Silvery moonlight blanketed the mountains and wilderness.","In the forest, a convoy of carriages pulled by horned horses and camels wound its way through the trees. Beside the vehicles walked guards dressed in black, wearing bamboo hats, with swords and Blades hanging at their waists and holding torches high. The scattered torchlight stretched for several miles along the winding mountain path.","Inside a carriage lagging near the back, Lin Zhenghong leaned against the wall. He peered through the window curtains at the advancing convoy from time to time, unable to conceal his delight.","\"A brilliant plan, sir. Taking the waterway out of the city to the west, then switching to the mountain paths and bypassing the official relay stations perfectly avoids any interrogations from the Prefecture City’s men.\"","Lin Zhenghong looked at \"Li Sanyuan,\" who was reclining in the innermost seat of the carriage. After offering a few compliments, he asked, \"Sir, the trading location is still within the western mountain pass. Do you think that’s somewhat inappropriate?\"","Zhang Dabao’s eyes were half-closed. Resting comfortably on the soft goose-down pillows at the back of the carriage, he hummed dismissively, \"We are only here for the silver. There’s no need to worry about anything else.\"","As he spoke, he looked over to the other side—at a man dressed in fine silk and sporting a thick beard, styled in the attire of the Poshisu Country. \"Wouldn’t you agree, Your Excellency Wolf Six?\"","Seeing his high-and-mighty, bureaucratic demeanor, Liu Lang pinched the flesh of his chin, nearly ripping off a few strands of his fake beard. Stifling a laugh, he said in a stiff tone, \"No need, for your esteemed grain company, to worry. We, naturally have, our own methods!\"","Lin Zhenghong glanced at him. Although he thought little of the man, for the sake of the silver, he nodded with a chuckle. \"Lord Wolf Six and your Peacock King Banner possess formidable strength... We were indeed overthinking it.\"","He thought, \"I really have too much free time. Once the transaction is complete and the silver is in hand, who cares how you horse bandits transport the grain out.\"","Compared to his subtle restraint, Liu Lang was much more direct. Hugging that long Blade wrapped in rags with both arms, he said disdainfully, \"Wei People, cannot be trusted.\"","Zhang Dabao shot him a glance, thinking that only he could spout such words. An ordinary person really couldn’t act out that kind of obnoxious vibe.","Liu Lang didn’t care what they were thinking. He leaned back in the carriage, his body swaying with the bumps of the mountain road.","About fifteen minutes later, the carriage came to a halt.","Zhang Dabao took a deep breath and was the first to step down from the carriage. \"We’re here.\"","Lin Zhenghong politely yielded the way, stepping down last.","Liu Lang followed them out. He scanned the surroundings, a smile breaking through his crudely disguised face. \"Dark moon, high wind. Not bad.\"","Lin Zhenghong walked up beside him and smiled. \"This matter is of grave importance, so please forgive us, Lord Wolf Six. After this transaction is over, we will welcome you to Shu State anytime. When that day comes, I will definitely treat you to the best restaurant in town.\"","\"Very good, very good...\" Liu Lang grinned and gestured for Zhang Dabao to lead the way."]},{"number":552,"title":"Chapter 552 - 318: The Mantis Stalks the Cicada!","paragraphs":["Zhang Dabao understood the cue. He straightened his robes, took a deep breath, and led the way.","Despite his composed demeanor along the journey, he still felt a surge of nervousness now that the moment had arrived. A million piculs of grain—worth tens of millions of silver coins at current market prices! If anything went wrong, selling him wouldn’t be enough to cover the loss. Even though Chen Yi had said some reassuring words to him earlier, his heart still THUMPED wildly in his chest.","Liu Lang, on the other hand, seemed completely unfazed.","Last night, to ensure the transaction went smoothly, he and Zhang Dabao had specifically instructed Lin Zhenghong and the others to bring fewer guards. The excuse was that too many people would attract unwanted attention. In reality, it was just to make it easier for them to hijack this batch of grain.","Before long, Zhang Dabao, Liu Lang, and the others arrived at the front of the convoy. Looking at the quiet mountain forest in the distance, Zhang Dabao shouted loudly, \"Guests from afar, halt your carriages at the pass!\"","His voice echoed all around. Then, from the distant woods, a voice replied in an even thicker Poshisu Country accent than Liu Lang’s, \"The mountain path is treacherous, harder than scaling the heavens.\"","Hearing this, Zhang Dabao cupped his fists in a salute. \"Li Sanyuan has come to keep the appointment! I hope the heroes of the tea route will show themselves.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, three figures walked out from the forest. Over a hundred dark shadows could also be seen darting among the branches. RUSTLE, RUSTLE. A flock of birds took flight in alarm.","The three figures quickly approached. All of them had the appearance and attire of Poshisu Country men. The leader glanced at the horse-drawn and camel-drawn carts on the mountain road, as well as the hemp sacks piled on them. In stiff, broken Wei Language, he said, \"L-let’s trade.\"","Zhang Dabao exchanged a glance with him, gave a subtle nod, and then gestured behind him invitingly. \"Come, esteemed guests. Please inspect the goods first.\"","Understanding his look, the leader stepped forward as a sampling rod slid out of his sleeve. He went from cart to cart, randomly inspecting the grain inside the sacks. He even made a show of biting a few grains of rice to check their quality.","Seeing them act so cautiously, Lin Zhenghong was pleased rather than annoyed. He leaned close to Zhang Dabao and whispered, \"Sir, it seems they take this transaction very seriously.\"","\"Naturally. It is a massive sum of silver coins, after all. If anything goes wrong, they wouldn’t have enough heads for King Landu to chop off.\"","\"You are absolutely right, sir...\"","Zhang Dabao ignored him and stealthily shifted his feet closer to Liu Lang, figuring that if things went south, he at least wouldn’t be instantly killed. Liu Lang had also dropped his earlier cynical demeanor. His left hand gripped his long blade, and his right arm hung naturally by his side, maintaining a posture ready to draw the blade at a moment’s notice.","About fifteen minutes later, the three \"Poshisu Country men\"—who were actually disguised Celestial Sect disciples—completed their rounds and returned.","\"The Trading Company is very trustworthy!\"","Zhang Dabao smiled. \"You flatter us, sir. Business is business. We certainly wouldn’t dare play tricks in front of the Peacock King Banner.\" He paused for a moment before asking, \"Shall we proceed with the trade?\"","The leading \"Poshisu Country man,\" Jin Peng of the Celestial Sect, nodded. \"Wei Dynasty, silver notes.\"","He waved to the distant forest. Another Poshisu Country man, also dressed in black, walked over carrying a large chest.","Lin Zhenghong stared eagerly at the chest, unable to suppress the joy on his face. Although this transaction was only for ten million silver coins—which still constituted a significant loss for them—compared to the pressure from the Governor’s Office, this minor loss was nothing. Furthermore, they had brought the Liu Family’s stale grain this time; sooner or later, they would make up for this deficit through Liu Hong.","There was no rush.","Seeing the Poshisu Country man approach with the chest, Lin Zhenghong was just about to step forward to inspect the silver notes when Zhang Dabao cut in diagonally, blocking his path.","\"I’ll do it,\" Zhang Dabao said.","Lin Zhenghong froze for a second. Once he recovered, he offered an awkward smile. \"Sir, this... this is against the rules.\"","According to the rules of the Ji State Trading Company, a Wind Patrol Envoy could not directly intervene in business deals. Only if the Trading Company’s Shopkeeper—namely, him, Lin Zhenghong—died could the Wind Patrol Envoy temporarily take charge. This was also the reason why he had been the one to formally visit Cui Qingwu earlier.","Zhang Dabao didn’t care about his rules. He scoffed, \"I was the one who facilitated this deal. Are you trying to steal the credit?\"","\"N-no, I wouldn’t dare...\"","\"If you know better than to dare, why haven’t you stepped back?\"","\"Yes, yes.\"","Once Lin Zhenghong retreated a few steps, Zhang Dabao inwardly sighed in relief and stepped forward to open the chest. How could he possibly let Lin Zhenghong handle this? Forget picking up the silver notes to examine their authenticity one by one—even a single glance would guarantee they’d be exposed.","Liu Lang knew exactly what was going on. He casually blocked Lin Zhenghong’s line of sight, leaned in, and said impatiently, \"Silver notes. Wei merchants. Brought them. Not fake.\"","Zhang Dabao laughed and voiced his agreement while quickly picking up and putting down the stacks, preventing the people behind him from seeing the authenticity of the silver notes. A few breaths later, he shut the chest with a loud CLACK and locked it. He picked it up and smiled.","\"The amount of silver notes is correct. We look forward to our next trade with your esteemed King’s Banner.\"","Jin Peng gave a grunt of affirmation. \"Then, we part here.\"","He waved his hand again, and nearly a hundred men in black poured out of the forest, heading toward the horse and camel carts. Playing along, Zhang Dabao turned and signaled for the guards to step back. Holding the chest, he watched as the men drove the carts away along the mountain path toward the west. Liu Lang, Jin Peng, and the others all remained standing in place.","Lin Zhenghong watched for a while before glancing at the chest. Still unwilling to give up, he shuffled over.","\"Sir, you are a man of noble status. Why don’t you let me hold on to the silver notes for safekeeping?\" As he spoke, he reached out his hands.","Zhang Dabao thought for a moment before handing the chest over to him with a warning. \"Don’t flash your wealth. It’s best if you wait until we get back before opening it.\"","Lin Zhenghong agreed profusely. He took the chest and hugged it to himself, unable to contain his wild joy. Now that the money was safely in the bag, he and \"Li Sanyuan\" would no longer have to suffer the Trading Company’s punishment."]},{"number":553,"title":"Chapter 553 - 318: The Mantis Stalks the Cicada!","paragraphs":["\"My Lord, this time we only traded grain. When will the other batch of goods you mentioned earlier...\"","Before he could finish, Zhang Dabao shot him a sideways glance. \"Keep your voice down.\"","Lin Zhenghong froze for a moment. Belatedly noticing the several \"people from Poshisu Country\" standing nearby, he nodded. \"You are right to reprimand me, My Lord.\"","About fifteen minutes later.","The horse and camel carriages had gone far; only the faint sounds of hooves and rolling wheels echoed from a distance.","Zhang Dabao gestured to Lin Zhenghong. \"Take your men and head back first. I have another deal to discuss with our esteemed guests.\"","Lin Zhenghong hesitated for a moment before nodding. He turned and led the grain store guards toward the Chishui River.","As he walked, he grumbled inwardly, \"A mere Wind Patrol Envoy really thinks he’s a Commerce House Shopkeeper. To act so inappropriately... how utterly ridiculous.\"","Despite his complaints, Lin Zhenghong knew the reality of his situation. He was not his father, Lin Huai’an, and his foundation within the Ji State Trading Company was still unstable. Moreover, with things going sideways during this transaction, he hadn’t yet found an opportunity to make contact with the Trading Company’s core personnel. He could only bide his time and plan for the future.","Just as Lin Zhenghong arrived at the Chishui Riverbank with his men, dreaming of his future success, he saw a fast boat cutting through the waves toward them.","He frowned slightly and waved his hand, signaling the guards behind him to be on high alert.","\"It’s already past Midnight. Logically, there shouldn’t be any more boats coming from the direction of the Prefecture City...\" he muttered.","He couldn’t help but worry, considering he was holding silver notes worth tens of millions of taels.","But whatever one fears the most always comes to pass.","As the fast boat approached, before Lin Zhenghong or his men could even ask a question, dozens of masked men clad in armor lunged forward.","The crossbows mounted on their arms fired with terrifying force.","Crossbow arrows whistled as they tore through the night sky.","Lin Zhenghong’s eyes widened instantly. He screamed at the top of his lungs, \"Enemy attack!\"","However, the attackers on the boat had caught them entirely off guard. Following the barrage of crossbow arrows, a flurry of porcelain bottles was hurled at Lin Zhenghong and his men, who had no time to dodge.","SWISH. SWISH.","\"Ah!\"","\"Watch out—!\"","\"You’re courting death! Kill them!\"","The chaotic shouts, the whistling crossbow arrows, and the sound of shattering porcelain mingled together, painting the night along the Chishui Riverbank with a splash of blood.","Severed limbs flew through the air as blood splattered in all directions.","The guards around Lin Zhenghong fell one after another.","Panic-stricken, he clutched the chest tightly and sprinted toward where \"Li Sanyuan\" and the others were located in the distance.","Desperate screams constantly rang in his ears.","He didn’t know how much time had passed. It could have been fifteen minutes, an hour, or perhaps just a few breaths. When the sounds finally ceased, Lin Zhenghong continued to run while suppressing his terror to glance back. But he saw absolutely nothing.","Just as he was about to slow down, his body crashed into something with a loud THUD. Caught off guard, he was sent flying and hit the ground hard.","Without time to think, Lin Zhenghong scrambled to his feet, holding onto the chest, ready to continue fleeing for his life.","But as soon as he stood up and looked ahead, he froze. His widened eyes were filled with absolute horror.","\"You... you...\"","Standing before him was a young man in brocade robes, his hands clasped behind his back, looking at him with a beaming smile. It was none other than Liu Hong’s eldest son, Liu Taoyao!","He glanced at the chest in Lin Zhenghong’s arms and asked with a smile, \"Boss Lin, where are you off to?\"","As he spoke, he slowly stepped closer.","Clutching the chest, Lin Zhenghong retreated step for step. His facial features were entirely scrunched up as he shouted, putting up a false front of bravado,","\"Do... do you know who I am?","\"I-I belong to the Ji State Trading Company! I am the Chief Shopkeeper of the Shu State Prefecture City branch!","\"How... how dare you bring people to attack us?","\"Does your Liu Family have a death wish?!\"","Liu Taoyao’s smile didn’t waver. \"And who would know it was us?","\"You? Or those horse bandits from Poshisu Country?","\"Haha, don’t be silly, Chief Shopkeeper Lin.","\"Since I’ve already appeared before you, neither you nor the silver in your hands will escape my grasp.\"","Hearing this, Lin Zhenghong’s legs gave out. He collapsed to the ground, and the chest tumbled from his grip.","He frantically crawled toward it. \"My... my silver...\"","But before he could grab the chest, a heavy foot stepped on his leg. No matter how hard he struggled, he couldn’t move an inch.","He turned his head to look back, but before he could clearly see anything, a flash of silver-white light swept past his eyes.","His vision went completely dark, followed instantly by agonizing pain.","He clutched his eyes, curling up on the ground as he wailed, \"My eyes... I... take it! I don’t want the silver anymore! Please, let me go!","\"Young Master Liu, Eldest Young Master Liu, I beg you...\"","Liu Taoyao let out a chuckle and leisurely walked up to him. He picked up the chest, weighed it in his hands, and looked down at the writhing man.","\"Wouldn’t it have been better if you had been this compliant from the start?","\"Now, it’s too late.\"","\"No... it’s not too late! I’ll... I’ll give you whatever you want! It’s not too late!\" Lin Zhenghong pleaded.","\"You? Give it to me?","\"What a joke!","\"The moment you conspired against my second brother, you chose the path to your own doom!\"","As soon as he finished speaking, Liu Taoyao coldly thrust his sword forward, piercing straight through Lin Zhenghong’s chest.","With one hand clutching his eyes and the other gripping the blade, blood poured from Lin Zhenghong as he trembled and gasped out,","\"You... I’ll wait for you... in hell...\"","\"Go down there and repent!\"","Liu Taoyao yanked the sword sideways in a horizontal slash, sending drops of blood flying. He then sheathed his blade, not bothering to spare the man another glance.","Lin Zhenghong was left lying in a pool of blood, his life slowly fading away as his bloodshot eyes stared blankly at the night sky.","\"Eldest Young Master, should we go over there and take a look?\" a subordinate asked.","\"No need,\" Liu Taoyao replied.","\"With those of the Evil Demonic Dao making a move, they will definitely erase the Peacock King Banner’s people from this world.","\"We should hurry back to the estate.","\"If we return too late, we’ll just be letting this silver gather dust for no reason.\"","\"Understood.\"","Meanwhile, Zhang Dabao and the others, who were still dressed as people from Poshisu Country, had already changed directions and were heading toward the Chishui River."]},{"number":554,"title":"Chapter 554 - 318: The Mantis Stalks the Cicada!","paragraphs":["This was the upper reaches of the Chishui River. Under the bright moonlight, the rolling mountain range in the distance could faintly be seen—it was the northern foothills of Wumeng Mountain. Among the towering peaks, the mountain path was steep. Zhang Dabao and the others had to drag and haul with all their might just to move the horse and camel carriages to the banks of the Chishui River.","Liu Lang looked around and said in surprise, \"Didn’t Wang Ji say he had already arranged the boats? Why aren’t they here?\"","Zhang Dabao shook his head, equally puzzled. Without the boats, all of them—along with the grain—would have to wait here, needlessly increasing their risks. Although this place was desolate, once dawn broke, there would still be people coming to hunt or gather medicinal herbs. If they were spotted, unexpected complications would inevitably arise.","Beside them, Jin Peng couldn’t help but tear off his fake beard, his expression betraying his anxiety. \"Could the Shopkeeper be a no-show?","\"With this much grain, if we’re discovered, we... all of us will become wanted fugitives by the Government Office.\"","\"Don’t panic, don’t panic, let’s just wait a bit...\"","Before Zhang Dabao could finish, Liu Lang pointed downstream and raised his eyebrows. \"Aren’t they here? I knew it... Huh?\"","An almost imperceptible, cold and sinister aura swept over from the boats on the distant river, cutting Liu Lang’s words off in his throat. His expression instantly turned solemn. Gripping his blade’s hilt with his right hand, he said in a deep voice, \"Everyone, be careful. Those aren’t our people!\"","\"What?!\"","Before Jin Peng and the other Celestial Sect disciples could comprehend the situation, a soft gasp of surprise drifted over from the distant boat. \"You aren’t people of Poshisu Country?","\"Wei People?","\"Interesting, how interesting. To think that the horse bandits trading with those grain merchants are actually Wei People in disguise, haha...\"","Liu Lang waved his hand, signaling the people behind him to prepare themselves, while he focused his gaze on the newcomers and asked, \"Who are you?\"","However, even without knowing their identities, he was already well aware that these newcomers were not to be trifled with. The leader’s Cultivation, along with the heavy, oppressive aura wrapped in Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, sent a profound chill through his heart. It felt just like when he had faced Xiao Jinghong at the Wu Mountain Mutual Market. But compared to that duel with Xiao Jinghong, Liu Lang’s strength had since improved. He wouldn’t be so intimidated by this arrival that he lacked even the courage to draw his blade.","\"You ask who I am?\" the leader replied. \"Little brother, didn’t your elders ever teach you that before asking such a question, you should first state your own name?\"","\"I never change my name under any circumstances,\" Liu Lang declared. \"I am Wolf Six!\"","\"Wolf Six?\"","As the boats drew closer, the newcomer’s figure gradually became clear, and the people standing behind him also revealed their true appearances. There were over a dozen individuals dressed in black, wearing Scale Armor under black cloaks, their heads covered by bamboo hats and veils. The leader sized Liu Lang up, his eyes filled with a teasing smile. \"Forgive my ignorance, but I don’t recognize the lineage of your Saber Dao.\"","Hearing this, Liu Lang held back his temper. He observed them for a moment before a look of realization dawned on his face. \"So it’s you lot—the Five Poison Sect!\"","The leading man in black was somewhat surprised. \"You actually know that we are from the Five Poison Sect?\"","\"Hmph!\" Liu Lang sneered. \"A bunch of stray dogs, disgusting bugs that only dare to hide in dark corners. Do you really think you’ve hidden yourselves well?\"","Having discerned their identity as the Five Poison Sect, Liu Lang knew there would be no peaceful resolution today, so he decided he might as well indulge in some verbal sparring. However, as he spoke, he was secretly waving his hand to signal the others behind him to get ready. Towards Zhang Dabao in particular, his hand was waving so fast it became a blur.","Zhang Dabao quickly caught on. He hurriedly pulled a bamboo tube from his sleeve and lit it with a flint. A brilliant streak of light instantly shot up into the sky.","Seeing this, the leading man in black narrowed his eyes, staring intently back and forth between him and Liu Lang. After a moment, he finally spoke in a sinister tone. \"What a sharp-tongued brat!\"","Before his voice had even faded, he transformed into a dark blur, crossing a distance of a hundred feet in the blink of an eye. \"Remember! The one who kills you is Yan Jingchen of the Five Poison Sect!\""]},{"number":555,"title":"Chapter 555 - 319: The One Who Will Kill You!","paragraphs":["Yan Jingchen! The Great Elder of the Five Poison Sect?!","Liu Lang’s heart chilled. Looking at Yan Jingchen, who had arrived in the blink of an eye, he advanced instead of retreating. His right hand drew his Blade, his left hand threw the scabbard aside, and he gripped the hilt with both hands. The Blade’s body reflected the moonlight—with a flash of brilliance, a streak of Blade light pierced the sky!","At the same time, Liu Lang did not forget to sternly warn, \"Dabao, take them and retreat! If you run into danger, remember to use that!\"","He knew very well that the Cultivation and Technique of the people behind him were absolutely no match for Yan Jingchen and the rest of the Five Poison Sect. Staying behind would only distract him and increase casualties in vain. Therefore, the best solution was for everyone to run for their lives; perhaps one or two could still survive.","Hearing this, Zhang Dabao told him to be careful, then hurriedly threw down the bamboo tube, turned around, and ran. Jin Peng and the others did the same.","A person’s reputation casts a long shadow. Even if most of them had never heard of Yan Jingchen’s name, they were not unfamiliar with the Five Poison Sect. They knew that it was an Evil Demonic Dao that had wreaked havoc in Shu State for decades. Most of these Celestial Sect disciples were only at the Lower Three Grades Realm in Cultivation, with only Jin Peng and a dozen others at the Middle Three Grades. Furthermore, their Sword Dao Realm was too low. The entry-level and Minor Success Sword Dao posed absolutely no threat to Yan Jingchen and his people. Not to mention, the people of the Five Poison Sect were truly vicious. Their Cultivation Technique and Technique were already so, not to mention the Poison and Poisonous Insects they carried with them.","If they didn’t run now, what were they waiting for?","Yan Jingchen formed claws with his hands and crushed Liu Lang’s streak of Blade light, coldly ordering, \"Kill them!\"","Four of the remaining black-clad men on the boat leapt out, flying toward Zhang Dabao and the others. Liu Lang glanced at them but paid no further attention, only staring solemnly at Yan Jingchen. Especially his hands—his five fingers were as crystal-clear as jade, and his nails shone like weapons.","\"The Five Poison Sect’s secretly passed down White Jade Skill. I have heard of it for a long time, but I didn’t expect to run into it here,\" Liu Lang stated.","The name of the White Jade Skill was elegant, but it was an out-and-out Poison Skill. Rumor in the Jianghu had it that the Five Poison Sect’s White Jade Skill was cultivated using highly toxic substances. Every day, a large amount of toxic substances had to be consumed and smeared all over the body, until it became as crystal-clear as jade.","\"I heard that every move and stance of the White Jade Skill can injure people with Evil Poisonous... You’re scaring me to death,\" he continued to mutter. In fact, Liu Lang was indeed not confident in facing Yan Jingchen, and he wanted to run for his life too. But if he didn’t make a move to block Yan Jingchen, Zhang Dabao and the others would all die.","\"You have some knowledge, but it’s a pity...\" As he spoke, Yan Jingchen’s figure moved like the wind, turning into a streak of black light. When seen again, he had already arrived by Liu Lang’s side. His hands formed claws, and several claw-shaped white blades instantly appeared one after another—dazzling and gorgeous!","Liu Lang naturally did not dare to take it head-on. His body moved with his Blade, and he gripped the long Blade with both hands to execute the Coiling Blade Style. However, it wasn’t a conventional coiling around the body, but rather, while linking with the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, he condensed streaks of illusory Sword Intent at the fastest speed. There were so many of them that they connected into a patch of pitch-black Blade light visible to the naked eye.","Black and white instantly collided together. Weirdly, the two streams of True Essence and Spiritual Mechanism dissipated silently and unnoticed, without any power leaking out.","\"Oh? Ghost Blade?\" Yan Jingchen recognized the origin of this Blade and narrowed his eyes. \"So you are the disciple of the Sword Ghost, Chu Xiudao!","\"Wolf Six? The ’Sword Madman’, Liu Lang!","\"No wonder you are so bold as to be so disrespectful to me!\"","The reason why the \"Ghost Blade\" was called the \"Ghost Blade\" was that the sharpness and overbearingness of its Saber Technique were merely superficial. The true \"Ghost Blade\" was eerie and extremely insidious. Just like the evenly matched collision just now. It seemed like there was only one Blade, but in reality, hundreds of streaks of Blade light were slashed out in that instant. Otherwise, how could an attack from Yan Jingchen, with his Upper Three Grades Cultivation and Perfect Realm Fist Dao, be blocked silently and unnoticed?","Liu Lang took a noncommittal step back, stepped into a bow stance, held the Blade at his side with both hands, and stared at him, saying, \"Old thing, since you know my identity, why don’t you hurry up and let us leave? If my master finds out about this, you and the Five Poison Sect will all be buried with me.\"","Yan Jingchen laughed when he heard this. \"I consider myself of the same generation as your master. Do you really think I would be afraid of him?\"","However, after confirming Liu Lang’s identity, Yan Jingchen was no longer in a hurry. He sized up Liu Lang, swept his peripheral vision across the Five Poison Sect members who were chasing down Zhang Dabao and the others in the distance, and then looked around. \"I heard that you and ’Dragon Tiger’ Liu Wu are best friends. I wonder where he is right now?\"","Liu Lang understood, grinning and sneering, \"Old thing, someone like you wants to fight him? I advise you to run now, or else when he comes, you won’t be able to escape even if you want to.\"","Yan Jingchen’s eyes turned cold. \"You won’t give up until staring death in the face!\"","Before his voice had even faded, he attacked again. He raised his hands, forming claws. The surrounding Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism was consequently split in two—one side as bright as daylight, the other as pitch-black as ink. Two immense forces instantly squeezed Liu Lang’s body, making his movements sluggish. He had to exert his full strength for every inch he moved.","\"Old thing, you are still far from enough!\" Naturally, Liu Lang would not surrender without a fight. With a roar, his entire being sank into that patch of pitch-black. He turned sideways and swung a Blade. The pitch-black Blade light, shrouded in darkness, howled as it slashed toward Yan Jingchen. The wind from the Blade ruffled the Chishui River, causing the boats on the river surface to sway violently.","However, Yan Jingchen cast a contemptuous glance. His figure remained motionless, neither dodging nor evading, as his clawed hands crossed up and down. The pitch-black Blade light shattered with a CRACK.","With a flick of his wrist, he lashed out a claw. Five white blades, as long as a person, drew an arc and enveloped Liu Lang.","Conversely, Liu Lang stared at him without blinking. He paused slightly on his feet, and his figure split into two. One stood in the vast white domain, and the other stood in the pitch-black domain, as if separated by yin and yang. He allowed the five claw blades to shoot past, crossing a hundred feet and carving five trenches into the rock-covered ground."]},{"number":556,"title":"Chapter 556 - 319: The One Who Kills You!","paragraphs":["Liu Lang was entirely unconcerned. The two figures brandished their long blades from the left and right, slashing toward Yan Jingchen.","\"Ghost Blade: Double Kill!\"","\"Hmph!\"","Yan Jingchen snorted coldly, reaching out with both hands to catch the two blade lights.","CRACK! CRACK!","Following two crisp sounds that rang out almost simultaneously, the blade gleams shattered.","Instead of being pleased, Yan Jingchen was infuriated. \"What audacity!\"","Before he could make another move, another blade shadow came slashing right in front of him.","The blade body was half black and half white, striking precisely at the weakest point of his Fist Dao Realm.","However, Yan Jingchen was ultimately an expert of the Upper Three Grades. His Protective True Gang erupted at just the right moment.","CLANG!","The long blade sank three inches into the bamboo hat before it was blocked by an immense force.","Liu Lang had anticipated this. In the gap where the two figures crossed paths, they unexpectedly split into two once more.","A full four figures surrounded Yan Jingchen.","Two in the front, two in the back.","Yan Jingchen didn’t even look at him. His eyes were fixed on the bamboo hat that had been cleaved into two by the Sword Intent and slid off. He laughed out of sheer fury:","\"Good, good, good!","\"It seems I’ve underestimated you, and underestimated the Ghost Blade as well!","\"Rumor has it that the ’Ghost Blade’, Chu Xiudao, can transform into thousands of incarnations—striking with one blade causes ten thousand to fall, possessing the unpredictable might of ghosts and Gods.","\"Looking at it now, the rumors are true. No wonder Chu Xiudao managed to carve out such a massive reputation!\"","Compared to his anger, Liu Lang was much calmer. \"If my master were here, you wouldn’t be able to withstand even a single strike from the old man.\"","Facing an old Jianghu monster who had been famous for decades, he had no choice but to deal with him carefully.","He no longer harbored the delusion that he could be like Chen Yi—using Fifth Grade Cultivation to overcome the Upper Three Grades and emerge victorious. He only wanted to stall for time as much as possible.","Without pausing, Liu Lang struck out with his blade once more.","The four figures moved in perfect unison, half-turning and slashing out diagonally. Looking down from above, the distinctly black and white blade lights slashed inward. Like a spinning windmill, they thrust straight toward Yan Jingchen.","—Ghost Blade: Four Kills!","But this time, Yan Jingchen didn’t just let him attack freely. Shifting his footing, he continuously thrust out his palms.","In just the blink of an eye, four palm shadows shattered Liu Lang’s four blade gleams.","The tyrannical Palm Force even penetrated right through the blade gleams.","Out of the four figures Liu Lang had transformed into, three illusory copies shattered. His true body raised his blade to block in front of him.","SMACK.","Amidst a crisp sound, Liu Lang was uncontrollably sent flying backward at an angle.","Furthermore, a slightly foul-smelling aura traveled along the long blade in his hands, invading all the way to his arms. Before he could react, that aura landed on his fingers and the back of his hands.","Immediately following, Liu Lang felt waves of agonizing, heart-piercing pain emanating from his hands.","\"Ah—!\"","Caught off guard, Liu Lang cried out.","After landing, before he could steady himself, he looked at his hands. His skin and flesh were already torn open. The blood flowing out was not dark red, but pitch-black. Moreover, streaks of blackness were tracing along his blood vessels and meridians, invading his body at a speed visible to the naked eye.","Liu Lang gritted his teeth, forcing himself to endure the intense pain. Forming his fingers into a blade, he slashed a wound onto each of his wrists. At the same time, his True Essence circulated and sealed the vital acupoints at the crooks of his arms, forcing that Poison Power out.","Gouts of pitch-black blood sprayed out. As they landed on the ground, they corroded it, forming pitted holes.","However, even though the majority of the Poison Power had been expelled, Liu Lang still felt the severe pain in his hands had not diminished in the slightest.","He was in so much pain that sweat rained down his body, and his facial features were scrunched together. But even so, Liu Lang still tightly gripped his long blade, glaring fiercely at Yan Jingchen.","\"The White Jade Skill is nothing more than this!\"","Yan Jingchen glanced at him and tore off the black cloth covering his face, revealing a face as flawless and white as jade, completely devoid of any traces of old age. Coupled with his bright, pitch-black hair, one couldn’t tell in the slightest that he was an old Jianghu monster past his fifties.","\"Your mouth is harder than your blade.","\"However, being able to cleave off my bamboo hat with just Fifth Grade Cultivation means you do have some skill.\"","Yan Jingchen shook his head after speaking. \"What a pity.","\"Chu Xiudao should have had a fine disciple capable of inheriting his mantle, but alas, you...","\"You reckless fool!\"","The killing intent on his face grew thicker. Facing Liu Lang’s direction, he brought his hands together.","Following his movement, Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism frantically compressed toward Liu Lang. At the same time, gouts of black qi drifted out from his jade-like, translucent fingers, gradually spreading into the surroundings.","\"Later, I will spread word throughout the Jianghu to deliver a message to your master—this day next year will be the anniversary of your death, and he should come here to pay tribute to you!\"","Liu Lang looked at the howling black qi but gave no response.","The White Jade Skill was domineering, its Poison Power ferocious. Combined with Yan Jingchen’s Cultivation and Technique Realm, it made it utterly impossible for him to evade.","Therefore, before that black qi could encircle him, Liu Lang fiercely took a step forward, the True Essence within his body erupting tumultuously as he condensed all of it onto the long blade in his hand.","Following that, his figure disappeared from his original spot.","In the blink of an eye, phantom-like figures materialized, completely surrounding Yan Jingchen.","His long blade quivered slightly, stirring and shattering the river-like Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism around him. Although it was only a portion of it, it was enough for Liu Lang to unleash a strike.","\"Ghost Blade: Thousand Kill!\"","Thousands of illusory figures, their faces pale and their eyes icy cold, simultaneously swung their long blades. Thousands of pitch-black blade lights shot forth, covering an area of a hundred zhang and enveloping Yan Jingchen within.","A smile crept up the corners of Yan Jingchen’s mouth. \"A foolish imbecile who overestimates his own strength!\"","Then, he lifted one hand upward.","The black qi that had surged and spread out earlier instantly formed two massive hands, guarding his body from above. No matter how the surrounding blade lights slashed against them, they couldn’t break through even the slightest bit—let alone harm his physical body.","Watching this scene, a bitter smile appeared on Liu Lang’s face. Ultimately, the gap in their strength was just too vast. It was an even more powerless feeling than when he had sparred with Chen Yi back then.","His strongest blade strike had been executed, yet it failed to stir up even the slightest ripple.","However—Liu Lang still had no intention of giving up.","Even though his figure was already swaying unsteadily under the oppression of that Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism. Even though his earlier actions had caused his body to be tainted by a trace of the Evil Poisonous black qi, leaving the flesh on his face and body torn open.","Intense pain swept through his entire body.","\"You old bastard, who the hell are you looking down on?!\"","Liu Lang clenched his jaw, wringing out the last drops of True Essence in his body, frantically connecting with Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism.","Faintly, a pitch-black blade gleam up to ten zhang long could be seen floating in mid-air. Its imposing aura spread out, unexpectedly dispersing all the surrounding black qi.","Seeing this, Yan Jingchen was slightly moved. He looked at Liu Lang in astonishment. \"You... actually have one foot in the Perfection Realm?\"","Liu Lang acted as if he hadn’t heard him. Or rather, at this moment, his eyes, ears, mouth, and nose had all lost their senses under the invasion of the Evil Poisonous aura.","Liu Lang could only rely on instinct, opening his mouth wide in a silent roar as he slashed his final blade strike at Yan Jingchen.","—Ghost Blade: Unity!","The pitch-black blade gleam fell straight down, following his movement.","It was deceptively slow but lightning-fast.","The solidified Sword Intent, wrapping around the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism within a ten-zhang radius, aggressively cleaved into the Fist Intent surrounding Yan Jingchen. Even the black hands he had condensed above himself earlier were unable to block it in the slightest.","Witnessing such a scene, Yan Jingchen retracted all his expressions, sighed, and dodged out of the way. It wasn’t that he couldn’t block it, but with his strength, he would still suffer some superficial wounds from this strike.","After he shifted laterally, the blade light landed on his original position.","HISS—","Amidst a sound so faint it was almost inaudible, the blade light sank straight into the mountain rocks.","As if slicing through a block of tofu.","Only then did a rumbling sound ring out. The mountain rocks within a ten-zhang radius were split in two, sent flying outward by that Sword Intent.","BANG! BANG!","The booming echoed endlessly.","Yan Jingchen quietly stood by and watched the Sword Intent wreak havoc, his gaze then landing on Liu Lang.","At this moment, Liu Lang was still maintaining his posture of gripping his blade with both hands. Fresh blood flowed across his body, and his aura was no longer as sharp as it had been before.","Yan Jingchen looked at him for a long while before smiling and shaking his head. \"A Swordman with decent aptitude. What a pity...\"","After speaking, he waved his hand, and a Qi Blade slashed straight toward Liu Lang.","\"From this moment on, there will be no more ’Sword Madman’ in the Jianghu.\"","Little did he know, before he could see Liu Lang beheaded, a cold snort rang out from the distance:","\"Who permitted you to say such a thing?\"","\"Hmm?\"","Before Yan Jingchen could make a move, a blurry phantom approached from afar. In the blink of an eye, it traversed a distance of several dozen miles, arriving just in time as that Qi Blade fell in front of Liu Lang.","Merely the aura radiating from his body shattered that Qi Blade. What followed was a domineering, sharp aura that frantically churned the surrounding Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism.","Even Yan Jingchen’s Fist Dao in the Perfection Realm was uncontrollably suppressed by that imposing might.","Yan Jingchen’s face turned solemn as he stared at the back of the figure blocking Liu Lang—wearing tight black martial attire, with long hair fluttering in the wind beneath a bamboo hat. His facial features couldn’t be clearly seen.","\"Who goes there!?\"","The newcomer did not make a sound. Instead, he flicked out several Silver Needles, piercing them into vital acupoints on Liu Lang’s body. As True Essence surged, he forced the black blood out of Liu Lang’s body and neutralized it.","Two breaths later, once Liu Lang’s aura had recovered slightly, the newcomer finally turned around, staring straight at Yan Jingchen with icy cold eyes.","\"The one who will kill you!\"","It was none other than Chen Yi!"]},{"number":557,"title":"Chapter 557 - 320: Liu Wu, Domineering!","paragraphs":["Seeing Liu Lang in such a state made Chen Yi feel rather guilty. He should have arrived sooner. However, with the plague about to spread inside and outside the Prefecture City tonight, he had to make sure everything was properly arranged.","In fact, after leaving Pei Qian and the others, Chen Yi had successively notified Elder Master Xiao and Wang Ji. For a matter of life and death like this, a delay of even a quarter of an hour would increase the danger for the refugees outside the city. Once those refugees infected with the plague died, the lives of all the refugees would be at risk.","When that time came, even if Chen Yi could cure the poison, the hours spent boiling medicine and treating the sick would still result in massive casualties. Furthermore, quite a few people had left the Prefecture City today. Aside from the Xiao Family and their group, members of other Noble Families had also gone out. The Government Office needed to step forward and investigate them one by one to ensure no one slipped through the cracks.","\"B-Boss...\"","The lethal poison in Liu Lang’s body had largely dissipated. Under the effects of the Silver Needles, his strength and True Essence were slowly recovering, giving him a bit of energy. Looking at the figure standing protectively in front of him, he weakly raised a hand. \"Please be careful... That old geezer practices... he practices the White Jade Skill... The Poison Power covers... his entire body...\"","Chen Yi gave a soft grunt of acknowledgment and said without looking back, \"Rest well. Leave it to me.\"","Hearing this, Liu Lang managed a relieved smile. Leaning heavily on his long Blade, he shakily closed his eyes. With his boss here, he felt much more at ease.","Yan Jingchen watched them. His gaze landed on Chen Yi, and a smile slowly squeezed onto his translucent, jade-like face before he burst into laughter.","\"So it’s you, ’Dragon Tiger’ Liu Wu!\" His laughter came to an abrupt halt as he glared at Chen Yi. \"Did you just say you were going to kill me? With just you!?\"","SWISH!","SLASH!","Almost as soon as Yan Jingchen finished speaking, the sound of several figures piercing the air rang out. The other men in black on the boat gathered at his side. Beneath their bamboo hats, which were hung with dense black threads, pairs of eyes stared fixedly at Chen Yi.","\"Sect Leader, how long has it been since we’ve seen a young man with such outstanding talent?\"","\"If I remember correctly, the last one to die by our hands was that Little Daoist from Kongtong Mountain. What was his name again?\"","\"Heh, Snake King, he’s already turned to dust. Why even bring him up?\"","\"True...\"","A tall, thin man standing next to Yan Jingchen lifted the veil on his bamboo hat, pulled down his mask, and grinned at Chen Yi. \"Just so Your Excellency ’Dragon Tiger’ knows who killed you, I am an Elder of the Five Poison Sect, Xue Chong!\"","Chen Yi glanced at him. \"An Elder? No wonder you’re so weak.\"","\"Weak?\" The corners of Xue Chong’s mouth stretched wider. \"Your Excellency ’Dragon Tiger’ clearly hasn’t grasped the situation. Right now, you are facing my Five Poison Sect. Or do you think that just because you killed a ’Jackal,’ you’re suddenly invincible in this world?\"","Chen Yi withdrew his gaze. Out of the corner of his eye, he spotted the other men in black who were chasing Zhang Dabao. Calmly, he unfastened the Five-section Spear from his wrist. \"It’s all the same to me. Whether it’s you or the rest of them, your fate will be exactly like Yan Fusha’s. It’s nothing more than...\"","Upon seeing Zhang Dabao take advantage of the men in black’s inattention to throw out several bottles of Immortal Drunk, Chen Yi furrowed his brows slightly. \"...Nothing more than a little extra effort.\"","Before his voice could fade, he had already turned around, grabbed Liu Lang, and transformed into a blurred phantom, sweeping toward Zhang Dabao and the others.","The members of the Five Poison Sect soaked themselves in Poison year-round. Ordinary Immortal Drunk or Qingfeng Drunk would have virtually no effect on them. Zhang Dabao using those Poisons against them was no different from throwing eggs at a rock.","\"Such audacity!\" Yan Jingchen frowned slightly. He shifted laterally by several paces and reached out to grab Chen Yi with one hand.","Who would have thought that the moment he planted his feet and raised his hand, Chen Yi had already vanished from his sight. No, to be precise, he watched helplessly as Chen Yi disappeared right before his eyes like a ghost. If his five senses were not still intact, and his True Essence hadn’t connected with Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism to cover the surroundings, he wouldn’t have been able to sense Chen Yi’s location at all. Xue Chong and the others beside him were even worse off; they had no way to block Chen Yi’s path.","He thought, \"Great Success in Step Dao... With such a Body Technique and speed, it’s no wonder he was able to arrive in time to block my attack. Truly terrifying!\"","But just as this thought surfaced in his mind, Yan Jingchen suddenly realized what Chen Yi was trying to do. He turned around and shouted, \"Dodge, quickly!\"","\"Too late!\" Chen Yi shouted.","After bypassing Yan Jingchen and the others using the Wandering Dragon and Phoenix Body Technique, Chen Yi took great strides forward. The Meteor Butterfly Step allowed his figure to leap with weightless grace. With every step, he dashed forward over ten meters, arriving beside Zhang Dabao and the group in just a few leaps.","After tossing Liu Lang over to Zhang Dabao, Chen Yi swept his Long Spear horizontally, forcing back three men in black. Without waiting for the last man to react, he flicked his wrist. The Long Spear tapped the man’s body as lightly and swiftly as a dragonfly skimming the water. Jin Guang flared brightly as his True Essence, carrying Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, shot out a streak of Spear Intent.","HISS—","An ear-piercing, sharp screech erupted. The man in black’s chest was pierced straight through. He stared blankly at Chen Yi for a moment before belatedly looking down.","\"You...\"","Before he could finish speaking, blood sprayed from his mouth. A large patch of blood also poured from his chest, dyeing half of his black clothes a deep crimson. Chen Yi pulled out the Long Spear and thrust it into a nearby rock with a flick. The few drops of blood staining the shaft slid down. Looking right through the bloody hole in the man in black’s chest, he stared directly at Yan Jingchen and the others in the distance and spoke with a cold, clear voice.","\"Dabao, take them and retreat further away.\"","Only then did Zhang Dabao snap out of his daze. Staring in lingering fear at the three men in black who were unaffected by the Immortal Drunk, he agreed repeatedly.","Jin Peng and the others looked at Chen Yi standing protectively in front of them, and all of them immediately breathed a sigh of relief. In the short span of just a quarter of an hour, their group of a hundred Celestial Sect disciples had been chased by four men in black from the Five Poison Sect until they fled in disarray. It was truly a humiliating sight.","But they couldn’t be blamed for being in such a wretched state. The Cultivation of their strongest member was only at the Fifth Grade Realm, and his Sword Dao had barely crossed the threshold. They were simply no match for the four Middle Third-Grade Martial Artists of the Five Poison Sect."]},{"number":558,"title":"Chapter 558 - 320: Liu Wu, Domineering!","paragraphs":["At this moment, they carefully followed Zhang Dabao, retreating several miles to reorganize the scattered horse and camel carriages that had fled in all directions.","Meanwhile, the three men in black from the Five Poison Sect who had narrowly escaped death returned to where Yan Jingchen and the others were. All of them looked at Chen Yi with solemn expressions.","In contrast, Chen Yi’s face was completely calm. Without Zhang Dabao and the others by his side, he no longer had any worries holding him back.","Yan Jingchen stared at him for a moment, the smile having long vanished from his face.","\"I haven’t been in Shu State for long, yet I have heard your name several times.","\"Jianghu People in Shu State call you a Spearman rarely seen in a century, with extraordinary talent on par with Xiao Jinghong.","\"The Bright Moon Building highly regards you; any mission involving you uniformly charges silver coins at the gold-medal standard.","\"Poshisu Country says you are a Wei Thief, and an old friend of mine hates you to the bone.","\"I originally thought you were just an ordinary rising star of the Jianghu. Now it seems I underestimated you.\"","Yan Jingchen paused. His eyes swept over the corpse of the man in black lying on the ground before looking back at Chen Yi, sighing as he spoke.","\"Spear Dao Perfection, Great Success in Fist Dao, Great Success in Step Dao... and the Medical Dao you just used to treat Sword Madman...","\"With such talent, even Gongye Bai, who has stood at the pinnacle of the Jianghu for decades, is probably no more than this, right?","\"Heh heh, but I suppose this can be considered a stroke of good fortune.\"","Xue Chong shook his head. \"Sect Leader, how is this a stroke of good fortune?","\"With such a peerless genius appearing in the world, if we cannot kill him today, the future troubles will be endless.\"","Beside him, a petite figure in black took off her bamboo hat, revealing an exceptionally soft and charming face.","\"The Sect Leader means that it is our good fortune to stumble upon ’Dragon Tiger’ before he has fully matured.","\"If we let him grow, forget about our Five Poison Sect—even if all the other Evil Demonic Dao factions in the Jianghu joined forces, I’m afraid it would be difficult to slay him.\"","\"Heh, who do you think he is? Immortal Bai?\" Xue Chong retorted.","The two of them chatted back and forth. They seemed to be bickering, but in reality, Poisonous Insects had already crawled all over the ground beneath them.","Snakes, bugs, rats, ants, centipedes, and lizards—there was no shortage of them. They densely swarmed up and down the rocks, the venom secreted from their bodies corroding tiny ravines into the stone.","Amidst HISSING sounds, dark green smoke rose, gradually forming a thick miasma that was then concealed by Yan Jingchen’s Fist Intent. Only a pungent, foul stench spread through the air.","The other men in black acted similarly, bringing out Poisonous Insects, Poison, and hidden weapons. Even Yan Jingchen, who led them, drew a pair of claw Blades from his waist, crossing them in his grip.","\"After today, there will be no more ’Dragon Tiger’ in this world.","\"But don’t worry, I will definitely make your name renowned in the Jianghu in the future.\"","A ferocious sneer appeared on Yan Jingchen’s face. Shedding the arrogance he had shown when toying with Liu Lang, killing intent wrapped around him like frigid ice.","\"The title ’Dragon Tiger’ isn’t great. How about ’Dragon Tiger Leopard’?\"","The question boomed like thunder, exploding in all directions!","A cloud of Evil Poisonous energy surged from Yan Jingchen’s body, surprisingly enveloping the miasma previously formed by the Poisonous Insects corroding the rocks. It coiled like smoke, forming long, pitch-black snakes that hovered around him.","At the same time, Xue Chong and the others struck in unison, charging and launching a coordinated assault toward Chen Yi. Their lowered bodies mimicked the Poisonous Insects below; some slithered like snakes, some crawled on all fours, while others launched themselves into the air.","Chen Yi quietly watched them, completely ignoring the gradually approaching Poisonous Insects around him.","\"Tell me, what is your purpose in spreading the plague toxin in Shu State?\"","As soon as the words left his mouth, he shook his head. \"Forget it. With the brains of people like you, even when scheming, you can only think three steps ahead.","\"Any more than that, and...\"","Chen Yi took a step forward, facing the incoming Xue Chong and the others, and said in a calm tone, \"...it would be too difficult for you.\"","A gentle halo of light suddenly appeared around his body, rippling outward like waves.","The surrounding world instantly began to transform.","The gray and gloomy miasma floated into the sky, forming a dark cloud.","With a RUMBLING sound, the mountain rocks shot up rapidly, as if an earth dragon were rolling over. Stretching for hundreds of miles, they formed a jagged, undulating mountain range.","The forest trees instantly shot up hundreds of feet high. Dangling vines and branches sprouted new shoots all around, and in the blink of an eye, they covered the newly uplifted mountainous terrain.","Even the Chishui River was caught in these changes in heaven and earth, transforming into a mighty, rushing river. It looked like a cascading milky way, suspended in the heavens.","It wasn’t until this moment that a massive chessboard, hundreds of feet wide, materialized in front of Chen Yi, hovering and pressing down between him, Xue Chong, and the others. It also crushed all the Poisonous Insects that were crawling toward him.","Amidst continuous CRUNCHING sounds, the Poisonous Insects were struck as if by a massive force, their heads exploding as they died.","Seeing the scene before them, Xue Chong and the others stood frozen in place, staring in astonishment at Chen Yi, who was now hundreds of feet away.","\"Is this... Qimen Dunjia?\"","\"Idiot!\" the woman who had spoken earlier cursed. \"This is the fucking worldly manifestation of Chess Dao Perfection!\"","Another burly man stared wide-eyed at their surroundings, asking in a muffled, booming voice, \"Isn’t Chess Dao just a useless trick for scholars? Why does it look so powerful...?\"","\"There are thousands of Dao Realms; how could any of them be useless?\" The charming woman licked her lips, completely unconcerned about the deaths of the Poisonous Insects. Flicking the whip in her hand, she said, \"Everyone, be careful. This ’Dragon Tiger’ is even trickier to handle than the Little Daoist we slaughtered earlier.\"","\"Do you even need to say that?","\"I...\"","These people were considered highly experienced and knowledgeable. Although they were wary and astonished in their hearts, at this moment of life-and-death struggle, they naturally did not want to weaken their own momentum.","On the contrary, Yan Jingchen, who had fallen to the back, frowned as he looked at the motionless Xue Chong and the others:"]},{"number":559,"title":"Chapter 559 - 320: Liu Wu, Domineering!","paragraphs":["\"Why haven’t you made your move yet? What are you waiting for?\"","He hadn’t followed them earlier, so he wasn’t enveloped by the Chessboard Realm. However, given his Cultivation and Technique Realm, he still sensed something amiss, especially with Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism continuously surging around them.","\"What happened to you all?!\"","But no matter what Yan Jingchen said, Xue Chong and the rest stood completely frozen in place, as if their souls had been stripped away. Sensing trouble, Yan Jingchen glanced at Chen Yi, who was equally motionless, and prepared to step forward to investigate.","Right at that moment, several piercing whistles tore through the air from the direction of the Prefecture City.","\"Yan Jingchen!\" Pei Ze laughed loudly. \"It really is you!\"","As the laughter echoed all around, a chorus of HISSING accompanied it. RUSTLING sounds rapidly approached from the distance, though no figures could be seen. Within moments, Pei Ze, Zhu Fangling, and Li Yunjun landed nearby, standing shoulder to shoulder.","Yan Jingchen turned his head to look. After a brief assessment, he frowned slightly. \"It’s you?","\"Who were you from the Mountain Race again?\"","A cold sneer appeared on Pei Ze’s gaunt face. \"Cut the bullshit. I slaughtered so many of your disciples back then. How could you possibly forget?\"","Yan Jingchen’s expression darkened at those words. \"Pei Ze!","\"My Five Poison Sect also killed hundreds of your Mountain Race members. If I remember correctly, I was the one who killed your two sons!\"","Pei Ze’s eyes instantly turned venomous. He clapped his hands, and a glossy black centipede darted out from his body, spitting a mouthful of venom at Yan Jingchen.","\"I thought you died a long time ago. I never expected you to shed that skin of yours and fake your death to escape.","\"Today, we’ll settle all our scores, old and new!\"","Without a moment’s hesitation, he charged straight at Yan Jingchen. Beside him, Zhu Fangling and Li Yunjun followed closely.","Yan Jingchen furrowed his brows. No longer able to check on Xue Chong and the others, he took a deep breath and met Pei Ze’s charge.","\"I should be the one saying that!","\"You people from the Mountain Race caused my Five Poison Sect’s vitality to suffer greatly. How could I ever let you off!\"","The four of them immediately engaged in a fierce battle. Relying on his slightly higher Cultivation, Yan Jingchen ignored several Gu Insects. Furthermore, as he fought, the highly toxic poison spreading from his body forced Pei Ze and the others to act with caution. Taking on three opponents at once, he wasn’t at a disadvantage in the slightest.","However, Pei Ze, Zhu Fangling, and Li Yunjun were in no rush for a quick victory. The three formed a triangular formation around Yan Jingchen. Fist and Foot, Blades and swords all struck out in unison. With every move, several Gu Insects were scattered into the surroundings, their sizes so miniscule they were practically invisible.","Yan Jingchen seemed to sense this and snorted coldly. \"Thirty years have passed, yet your Mountain Race hasn’t changed a bit. You still use the same old tricks.","\"Your White Jade Skill has certainly become much more formidable through your Cultivation, though.","\"However...\"","Pei Ze met his clawing strike, blocking horizontally with a gaunt arm as hard as steel. \"That’s all it amounts to!\"","BANG!","Pei Ze was sent flying backward, several gashes sliced into his arm. Seeing this, Zhu Fangling and Li Yunjun evaded Yan Jingchen’s claws, attacking high and low to keep him pinned down.","In an instant, their desperate, life-and-death struggle caused Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism to roar ceaselessly. Earth-Splitting trenches tore through the ground one after another, boulders shattered, and trees were reduced to fine powder.","In the distance, Pei Qian and Lan Yanni watched the scene unfold but were in no hurry to intervene. Instead, they directed their gazes toward Chen Yi.","Compared to the brutal siege of Yan Jingchen by Pei Ze’s trio, the situation on Chen Yi’s side was much more bizarre.","\"Brother, what is ’Dragon Tiger’ doing?\" Lan Yanni asked.","Pei Qian observed for a moment and shook his head slightly. \"I don’t know either.\"","He could only tell that something was happening on Chen Yi’s side, but he couldn’t see any visible anomalies.","\"Then what should we do?\"","\"Let’s wait a bit longer. We’ll clear the surrounding highly toxic poison first.\"","\"Alright...\"","What they didn’t know was that Chen Yi, who was currently facing Xue Chong and the others alone, appeared to be standing completely still, but in reality, they had already clashed for several rounds. Furthermore, Xue Chong and the others were covered in wounds of varying sizes, with blood flowing freely.","In contrast, Chen Yi remained standing by the side of the chessboard, watching them from afar as he calmly placed chess pieces onto the board one by one. With the arrival of the Mountain Race, he no longer needed to risk his life in close combat. Enhanced by the Chess Dao, Xue Chong and the others, who merely had Cultivations in the Third and Fourth Grade Realm, were simply no match for him.","\"If your Technique hasn’t reached Perfection, you are ultimately just ants.\"","Xue Chong watched another chess piece transform into a small hill and plummet toward them. He cursed with a venomous expression, \"If we don’t break this damn Chess Dao, we’re all going to die here!\"","\"Liu Wu’s Chess Dao... is too overbearing. It’s too difficult...\""]},{"number":560,"title":"Chapter 560 - 321: Go Down and Face Your Punishment","paragraphs":["\"Tyrannical Dao?\" Chen Yi wanted to laugh a little. How could a bunch of Evil Demonic Dao, who hid in the dark to murder commoners, understand what the \"Tyrannical Dao\" was? After all, it still contained the word \"Dao.\"","However, Chen Yi also knew why they felt that way. It was all because their Heart Spirits were intimidated by the Illusion Realm that had evolved in the Zhou surroundings.","The human body contained three Seas of Qi: the Dantian, the Chest, and the Yintang. While it seemed they were all for guiding, gathering, and storing Qi, there were actually subtle differences—namely, the three elements of Essence, Qi, and God. The Dantian stored Essence, the Chest strengthened Qi, and the Yintang nourished God. Martial Arts followed this order, using True Essence from the bottom up to Step by step fill one’s own Essence, Qi, and God until achieving Dao Perfection.","But the Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting learned by scholars was not like this. In other words, when scholars Cultivated their moral character and nurtured their nature, what they nourished was their own \"God.\" This was also the reason why Chen Yi could resist Du Cang’s Black Magic Secret Skill using the Chess Dao. Speaking solely of \"God,\" once a scholar’s Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting reached Dao Perfection, they could borrow the power of Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism to do things that ordinary people, or even Martial Artists, could not.","Just like how the Chess Dao could evolve heaven and earth, deducing people or events. Just like how the Painting Dao could mix the false with the genuine; the people painted would transition from illusion to solidity, appearing entirely real. Therefore, when Chen Yi used the Chess Dao to capture the Heart Spirits of Xue Chong and the others, he was suppressing them with absolute \"God.\" Although the Chess Dao was not as lethal as Du Cang’s Black Magic Secret Skill, it was enough to heavily injure Xue Chong. As for the Poisonous Insects invading from all around... such mindless creatures would have their heads crushed by \"God\" with Yi-ease.","While watching the outside slaughter between Yan Jingchen, Pei Ze, and the others, Chen Yi unhurriedly continued to place his pieces. Every white piece tossed onto the chessboard would trigger transformations in this heaven and earth. Storms, lightning, landslides, and more. Xue Chong was battered and exhausted by this series of changes. Even though he was certain that they weren’t truly injured, the pain felt entirely real. Furthermore, with every new wound that appeared on his body, he could perceive his own weakening. It was not a weakening of his True Essence Cultivation, but a growing heaviness in his body and a sense of powerlessness in connecting with and manipulating Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism.","\"Liu Wu!","\"The Shu State Jianghu widely rumors that you are a figure on par with Xiao Jinghong, yet to think you can’t even fight us head-on!\"","Chen Yi glanced at him. \"Noisy!\"","He tossed out another chess piece from his hand, linking it with the dozens of white pieces from earlier to act as a General encircling several Heizi within. The next moment, a two-horned Jiao Dragon darted out from the chessboard. Its thick, sturdy body coiled as it hovered in midair. Its golden eyes, devoid of any emotion, stared coldly at Xue Chong and his group.","Too lazy to waste more words on these people, Chen Yi pointed with One Finger. The Jiao Dragon immediately dove toward Xue Chong and the others, the dense, misty luster around its Zhou body softly illuminating the surroundings.","Seeing this, Xue Chong’s serpent-like face turned so gloomy and cold that it looked as if it might drip blood. The charming woman beside him Transferred her position and shoved him. \"Dodge!\"","The rest of the group moved in unified Steps. But after the Jiao Dragon flew past, countless bits of Scale Armor shed from within the luster surrounding its Zhou body. Even if Xue Chong and the others dodged its fatal strike, their bodies were pierced by the closely trailing scales. One piece after another, they poked dozens—even hundreds—of bloody holes into their bodies.","Even so, they still did not dissipate or die.","Xue Chong and the others looked down at themselves and revealed miserable smiles.","\"What a formidable Chess Dao. I admit defeat.\"","To think their Five Poison Sect had rampaged across the Jianghu for hundreds of years, relying entirely on the Poison Skills they Cultivated and the Poisonous Insects they refined. Yet here, facing Chen Yi, not only were their Poison Skills completely ineffective, but even those Poisonous Insects they had painstakingly poured their blood and sweat into were utterly useless. They were like toddlers who had just learned to walk, left with no choice but to suffer endless torment within this chessboard.","That woman had lost her former charm; more than half of her face had been sliced off by the Jiao Dragon Scale Armor. It was a bloody, mangled mess. However, her eyes still glared fiercely at Chen Yi.","\"No matter how high your Chess Dao Realm is, it is still useless in Martial Arts slaughter! If our Cultivation had broken through to the Upper Three Grades, this Chess Dao of yours would be nothing but a Blinding Technique!\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi paused. With a wave of his hand, he dispersed the Jiao Dragon. He stood tall, leapt onto the chessboard, and said in a flat tone:","\"When your Five Poison Sect laid plans in the Shu State to murder those refugees, did you ever consider that they had no Cultivation, or that their Cultivation and Realm were lower than yours?","\"If they had Martial Arts to protect themselves, even if they couldn’t avoid the plague poison, they could have held on a little longer. But now...","\"They have to fight for their lives against King Yama!\"","Chen Yi’s gaze swept over Xue Chong and the others one by one, as if looking at a few ants.","\"You wouldn’t understand the principle of ’do not do to others what you do not want done to yourself’ even if I explained it. You might as well roll down to the underworld and suffer your punishment.\"","As his voice fell, the surrounding mountains, rivers, and forests suddenly dissipated. Looking again, he and Xue Chong’s group were still standing in their original spots. The sounds of Yan Jingchen, Pei Ze, and a third person fighting in the distance drifted over.","Compared to Chen Yi’s calmness, Xue Chong and the others—who had just emerged from the chessboard world—no longer possessed their previous ferocity. Instead, they withered away at a speed visible to the naked eye. Their bodies hunched over, barely able to remain standing. Even if they could still mobilize the True Essence in their bodies and connect with Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, their auras were already extremely weak. Of all their Cultivation and Techniques, not even one-tenth remained.","Xue Chong and his group looked at Chen Yi not far away, abruptly grit their teeth, and yelled, \"Sect Leader, be careful! He...\"","But before they could finish speaking, Chen Yi had already moved. The distance of a hundred feet was crossed in the blink of an eye. The Long Spear was like a crescent moon, bending into a bow as it swept out horizontally.","\"Quickly...\"","\"Dodge...\"","As Xue Chong and the others stared at the sudden flare of golden light, their faces were instantly overcome with absolute terror."]},{"number":561,"title":"Chapter 561 - 321: Roll Down Below and Suffer Your Punishment","paragraphs":["Faced with this spear thrust, even if they wanted to dodge, it was impossible. They could only watch helplessly as the golden light swept across their bodies.","With a single thrust of the spear, eleven top experts of the Five Poison Sect were decapitated!","Noticing the commotion behind him, Yan Jingchen forced Pei Ze and the other two back with a single palm strike and turned his head to look.","He saw heads flying into the air almost simultaneously, smashing against the mountain rocks before rolling to his feet.","Blood sprayed from the headless corpses as they slowly collapsed to the ground.","THUD, THUD, THUD rang out incessantly.","The battlefield fell dead silent.","Pei Ze stopped Zhu Fangling and Li Yunjun from rushing forward. While circulating his Cultivation Technique to restore his True Essence, he looked at Chen Yi in awe.","\"A formidable youth. Truly a formidable youth.\"","They had originally thought that even if the people from the Mountain Race couldn’t wipe out the Five Poison Sect completely, they could at least drive them out of Shu State once again.","Little did they expect that before they could even fully engage, the majority of the Five Poison Sect members who came to Shu State on this trip would already be dead or injured.","Moreover, those who died were among the top existences in the Five Poison Sect in terms of Cultivation and Technique.","Pei Qian felt much the same. Looking at the calm Chen Yi in the distance, he couldn’t help but think of Pei Guanli.","If this man could become the son-in-law of the Mountain Race, it would actually be quite acceptable.","Lan Yanni didn’t look at Chen Yi; instead, she stared at the corpses of Xue Chong and the others, licking her lips.","\"Brother, do you think brother-in-law ’Dragon Tiger’ would mind if I asked him for one or two corpses?\"","The bodies of the Five Poison Sect members contained highly toxic substances, making them rare materials for Refining Gu.","Naturally, her eyes burned with greed.","Pei Qian cast her a sideways glance. \"Brother-in-law?\"","Lan Yanni chuckled twice and said in a sweet, naive tone, \"Sister Guanli’s husband is naturally my brother-in-law.\"","\"You... go ask our brother-in-law later and see if he can spare a few more corpses...\"","\"Will do!\"","With Xue Chong and the others dead, some were naturally joyous, while others... felt pure hatred.","Yan Jingchen stared blankly at the corpses scattered across the ground, as if completely unable to believe his eyes.","These were the Five Poison Sect members he had painstakingly trained over the past thirty years.","Xue Chong was at the Middle Fourth Grade in Cultivation and excelled at controlling snakes. He was in charge of Snake Valley within the sect, and his Snake Palm Cultivation Technique had reached Great Success.","The charming woman, Shi Lanxu, was at the Upper Fourth Grade. She practiced with a special Weapon—the Long Whip—and was exceptionally skilled at refining Poison.","As for the burly man...","Looking at the several Altar Masters and Elders of the Five Poison Sect, Yan Jingchen’s jade-like face grew increasingly calm.","After a long while, Yan Jingchen finally looked at Chen Yi. He unexpectedly revealed a faint smile and shook his head, saying, \"I must admit, I’m getting old.","\"Even if I were to fight them, I couldn’t have defeated their combined forces in such a short time, let alone kill every single one of them.\"","\"Speaking of which,\" Yan Jingchen paused for a few breaths before asking with a smile, \"I suppose Your Excellency ’Dragon Tiger’ must practice other Cultivation Techniques as well?","\"Let me guess. The Soul-Catching Skill?","\"Probably not. Soul-Capturing and Thought Extraction is similar to Poshisu Country’s Black Magic. Even if they were no match for it when joining hands, they wouldn’t have ended up in such a miserable state.","\"The Buddhist Sect’s Vajra Evil-Passing shouldn’t be it either; you don’t have that sandalwood scent on you.","\"The Daoist Sect...\"","After guessing one by one, Yan Jingchen gave up and shook his head. \"Having not walked the Jianghu for a long time, I have indeed underestimated the people of this world.\"","Chen Yi looked at him quietly, the killing intent in his eyes undiminished.","If he hadn’t noticed the plague poison appearing in Shu State this time, the number of dead and injured civilians would have been immeasurable.","How could he feel any pity for Yan Jingchen?","Scum of the Evil Demonic Dao like him completely deserved death!","Yan Jingchen was naturally aware of the current situation. He let out a self-deprecating laugh as the aura around his body inexplicably surged and skyrocketed.","Without any visible movement from him, the mountain rocks beneath his feet shattered ring by ring.","Following that, large swaths of poisonous fog drifted out from his cuffs, blending with the Poison Power previously released by the White Jade Skill to transform into a mass of pitch-black mist.","It didn’t look like Poisonous Miasma; instead, it appeared more like liquid ink.","Not only that, as Yan Jingchen erupted with power, his imposing aura climbed to its peak, stirring Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism around him to form hiltless daggers suspended in midair.","He looked at Chen Yi, then at Pei Ze’s group of three on the other side, the smile on his face growing wider.","\"I have roamed the Jianghu unhindered for decades and experienced countless events, both big and small.","\"I’ve fallen from the mountain peak to the bottom of the valley, and by relying on sheer resilience, I climbed from the bottom of the valley back to the peak. Do you really think I’d be frightened by this little display of yours?","\"Pei Ze, didn’t you want to avenge your deceased son? I am right here! Come on!\"","Looking like a madman, Yan Jingchen’s hair and beard billowed without wind. After shouting a few times, his gaze fell on Chen Yi.","\"And you, ’Dragon Tiger’! Attack me together!","\"If I don’t die today, you and the people around you will never know peace!\"","Chen Yi remained noncommittal, simply glancing at Pei Ze’s trio opposite him, as well as Pei Qian and Lan Yanni hiding in the dark.","After a moment of thought, he gestured for them to step back a little before carrying his Long Spear and walking toward Yan Jingchen.","\"I have no interest in your grudge against the Mountain Race, and I originally didn’t plan on attacking your Five Poison Sect. But alas...","\"You all insisted on seeking your own doom.","\"Yan Fusha was like this, and so are you. You’ve even gone further, intending to poison the common people of Shu State.","\"For such deeds...\"","As Chen Yi spoke, he took a step into the area enveloped by Yan Jingchen’s Fist Intent.","Black and white colors covered his body, casting him in an interplay of light and dark, while his figure inexplicably elongated by a few inches.","The next moment, his figure vanished abruptly.","Yan Jingchen seemed prepared for this, crossing his claws in front of his chest.","CLANG!","The tip of the Long Spear, dyed golden, struck against his twin claw blades.","A massive surge of force erupted.","Yan Jingchen’s body was uncontrollably pushed backward.","The smile on his face froze. He stared in astonishment at Chen Yi, who brandished the Long Spear and thrust again. \"Your Power...\"","Something wasn’t right!","Chen Yi’s Cultivation was only at the Fourth Grade Realm!","Even with Spear Dao Perfection, Great Success in Fist Dao, and Great Success in Step Dao, he could jump one major realm at most.","As for himself, he was already an Upper Three Grades Martial Artist thirty years ago.","Although he hadn’t broken through to the First Grade Realm now, he wasn’t far off.","Coupled with the surrounding Poison Power and Fist Intent, he should have been vastly stronger than Chen Yi.","Yet the current situation was the exact opposite.","At this thought, an idea suddenly popped into Yan Jingchen’s mind, nearly shattering his resolve to fight to the death.","Could it be that this Liu Wu also possessed the Martial Arts·Body?","Or some kind of Horizontal Cultivation Technique?","If not, how could his physical strength be so terrifying?","\"You... how could your talent...\"","Before he could finish speaking, Chen Yi pressed his advantage mercilessly. After thrusting his spear, he leaped into midair.","The Long Spear pointed straight toward the heavens.","Dark clouds gathered in the previously clear night sky.","Lightning flashed and thunder rumbled within the clouds.","In less than two breaths, a deafening thunderclap exploded, followed by a bolt of silvery-white lightning descending from the sky to strike the Long Spear.","Even Chen Yi’s body faintly crackled with electrical sparks.","Yan Jingchen frowned slightly, but his reaction was not slow. He immediately scattered a cloud of toxic powder to obscure his figure and appearance.","At the same time, the hiltless daggers that had condensed in midair began to plummet.","They shot toward Chen Yi one after another.","The whistling sound of them tearing through the air echoed across the mountain forest.","Chen Yi remained unmoved, his gaze fixed entirely on Yan Jingchen.","Only when the daggers were close did he step forward.","His entire person turned into a blur of black shadow, threading through the gaps between the daggers like he was navigating a maze.","Moving forward one moment and retreating the next.","He dodged left and right, evading all the blades.","Meanwhile, the Long Spear in his hand remained wreathed in golden Spear Intent and electrical sparks, acting like a divine Weapon as it swept aside the surrounding daggers.","Yan Jingchen naturally wouldn’t just sit and wait for death. Watching Chen Yi steadily approaching, a victorious smirk crept onto his face.","Immediately, he spread his arms and lifted the pitch-black mass above him, then violently thrust his hands outward.","In the blink of an eye, the inky mass of poisonous fog split into two halves and surged toward Chen Yi, aiming to entangle him.","\"I’ve cultivated for decades. My Poison Power will kill even Upper Three Grades Martial Artists upon contact!","\"Let’s see how... Hmm?\"","But before Yan Jingchen could celebrate for long, he saw a streak of white fluorescent light zip past.","When he looked again, the fluorescent light was already blocking the path of the poisonous fog.","Despite its incredibly tiny body, it showed no fear of the toxic mist and dove right into it.","Yan Jingchen was shocked and infuriated. \"The Mountain Race’s Gu King?!\"","That bee-like Gu Insect was none other than Granny Shan’s Gu Insect, which he had seen thirty years ago.","It was as if it had been refined specifically to counter their Five Poison Sect, capable of devouring any poisonous substance.","No matter how much he roared, that glowing white \"bee\" still devoured the massive, hill-sized cloud of poisonous fog entirely.","It took only three breaths.","Naturally, Chen Yi wouldn’t let this opportunity slip by. Ceasing the Wandering Dragon and Phoenix Step Technique, he switched to the Meteor Butterfly Step.","His body moved with the spear, arriving in the blink of an eye.","—Dragon-Falling!"]},{"number":562,"title":"Chapter 562 - 322: Another Celestial Tier!","paragraphs":["The long spear thrust out.","A Thunder Dragon fell from the sky.","Its two antler-like horns pointed obliquely at the firmament, and its massive draconic mouth was wide open, faintly holding a Dragon Ball within.","It was dazzling, its imposing might astonishing.","On the other hand, Yan Jingchen seemed completely terrified. He remained utterly motionless with his head tilted back, staring straight at the Thunder Dragon.","More accurately, he was looking at the \"bee\" that had devoured his Evil Poisonous Power.","A faint murmur could be heard. \"Beyond Wumeng Mountain, the Thunder Dragon descends upon the world...\"","BOOM!","CRACKLE!","The Thunder Dragon crashed heavily onto Yan Jingchen, sending electric sparks flying in all directions.","The solid Spear Intent hidden within splashed outward, shattering rocks and turning the surrounding trees to ash. When it landed on the Chishui River, the water exploded violently, sending fish and shrimp flipping into the air.","A long while passed.","The deafening noise gradually subsided.","The pervasive poisonous miasma slowly dissipated, leaving the scent of soil and vegetation to grow increasingly dense.","Chen Yi hovered in midair, looking down.","Yan Jingchen stood quietly, his head raised to meet his gaze.","Pei Ze, Li Yunjun, and the others had long since retreated several miles away. Alongside Pei Qian and Lan Yanni, they stared blankly at the utterly devastated battlefield, too stunned to speak.","Even Zhang Dabao and his group in the distance firmly held onto their frightened horses and camels, gazing over.","\"As expected of... the Boss...\" Liu Lang leaned against the wheel rut of a carriage, a hint of envy in his eyes.","Although his Cultivation and Technique were weaker than those of Chen Yi and Yan Jingchen, the fluctuations of Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism in the surroundings were so massive that he could clearly feel them.","The Spear Dao was like a rainbow, the Fist Dao like a blade.","Even watching from a distance, the golden and white glows stung his eyes, bringing tears to them.","Hearing the voice, Zhang Dabao turned his head belatedly. \"Brother Liu, you’re awake! Are you feeling bet—huh? Why are you crying?","\"Don’t tell me... the Boss avenged you, and you’re moved to tears?\"","Liu Lang shot him a sideways glance and cursed, \"Screw you! I’m just... I’m just...\"","As an expert who had achieved Great Success in Saber Dao—no, more accurately, someone who had half a foot into the Perfection Realm—he found it hard to tell the truth.","Otherwise, wouldn’t a Martial Arts idiot like Zhang Dabao bombard him with idiotic questions?","\"You’re right, I’m very touched! The Boss, he... Anyway, a true man dies for his confidant,\" Liu Lang said with a wooden expression. \"From now on, alive, I belong to Hundred Herbs Hall; dead, I’ll be a ghost of Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","Liu Lang said all this with a stiff face, but when Zhang Dabao and the others heard it, they found absolutely nothing wrong with it.","They felt sincere admiration.","\"The boss is right. One look and you can tell our Boss is meant for great things. Following him, even if we don’t soar to great heights, this life will at least be worth it.\" Jin Peng was quite young and had not yet reached adulthood, but he understood perfectly well what a massive sensation his recent deeds would cause if they spread.","In a word—from now on, their names would be renowned in the Jianghu.","\"It’s a pity that Eldest Senior Sister and Senior Sister Shen have to guard the Xiao Family, otherwise...\"","\"Shut your trap! Did you forget Senior Brother Xue’s instructions?\" someone scolded. \"If Eldest Senior Sister finds out what we’ve been up to, won’t she skin us alive? We must keep our mouths shut and remain tight-lipped, or else...\"","\"Right, right, right...\"","Their side was lively and boisterous because, in their eyes, Chen Yi killing the current Five Poison Sect Leader, Yan Jingchen, with a single thrust of his spear was the epitome of formidable power.","However, from Chen Yi’s perspective, he had merely scored an easy victory.","Or rather, Yan Jingchen was much weaker than he had imagined.","With a Second Grade Realm Cultivation, Perfection in Fist Dao, coupled with all those poisonous insects and poison... logically speaking, he shouldn’t be this weak.","Even though Chen Yi currently possessed a Fourth Grade Cultivation, with his Spear Dao and Body Dao at Perfection, and his Step Dao and Fist Dao at Great Success, he should theoretically only be able to bridge the gap of two major realms.","It was absolutely impossible for him to slay Yan Jingchen this effortlessly.","Chen Yi looked at the Gu Insect hovering in midair. He wondered if it was responsible.","When the Dragon-slaying Spear had descended earlier, he could see that Yan Jingchen was frozen in place, seemingly suppressed by the pressure of Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism.","He waited another moment, but Yan Jingchen remained entirely silent and motionless.","Pei Ze, Pei Qian, and the others were just about to step forward, but Chen Yi raised a hand first, signaling them to stop.","\"Stand back.\"","Pei Ze’s expression slightly shifted. He glanced at Yan Jingchen and stretched out his arms to block Pei Qian and the others.","\"Third Granduncle?\"","\"Listen to him.\"","Pei Qian nodded and waved his hand, recalling the Gu Insect \"bee\" that was flapping its wings in midair.","Chen Yi offered no explanation. A crystalline glint flashed in his eyes as he looked at Yan Jingchen.","Under the Qi Observation Skill, the truth was laid bare.","Yan Jingchen’s aura had indeed completely dissipated. The True Essence within his three major Qi Sea Acupoints was slowly escaping and returning to heaven and earth.","His physical body had likewise crumbled under that spear strike. His internal organs were damaged to varying degrees, his meridians were shattered inch by inch, and his flesh and blood were riddled with residual Spear Intent.","He was as dead as one could possibly be.","Yet, Chen Yi still felt that something was amiss. Therefore, he simply stared at Yan Jingchen’s \"corpse\" without uttering a single word.","One breath, two breaths... fifteen minutes, thirty minutes...","He was certain—Yan Jingchen wasn’t dead!","If he were dead, with so much time having passed, Chen Yi would have obtained his Opportunity by now.","\"Faking his death?\" Chen Yi murmured.","He flicked his wrist and thrust his spear.","A golden light condensed into a straight line, piercing through Yan Jingchen’s chest and shattering his heart.","Even so, Yan Jingchen remained standing in place, utterly unmoving.","A smile tugged at the corner of Chen Yi’s lips. Holding the spear single-handedly, he thrust it several times in quick succession.","Streaks of Spear Intent consecutively pulverized Yan Jingchen’s bodily shell. In the blink of an eye, he was devoid of his four limbs, and even more than half of his chest was gone.","Looking at the faint aura residing within that perfectly intact head, Chen Yi sneered. \"Still planning to keep up the act?","\"This doesn’t seem like the behavior expected of a Sect Leader.\"","\"Sigh...\"","Reduced to a Human Pig, Yan Jingchen lay among the dirt and crushed stones. He let out a long sigh as life returned to his dull, lifeless eyes.","\"How did you see through this old man’s ’Golden Cicada Shell Escape Skill’?\"","He had utilized this Skill primarily because the prior devouring of his Evil Poisonous Power by the Gu Insect had caused him to suffer a severe backlash, forcing him to take that spear strike head-on."]},{"number":563,"title":"Chapter 563 - 322: Another Celestial Tier!","paragraphs":["Second, he also harbored a stroke of luck, wanting to find a chance to ambush Chen Yi. Who knew he would be seen through from the very beginning.","Chen Yi naturally didn’t know his thoughts. He shook his head and said, \"Even if I couldn’t tell, given the Mountain Race’s hatred for your Five Poison Sect, how could they not make foolproof preparations?\"","Pei Ze, Pei Qian, and the others finally understood his intentions. Especially Pei Ze. He glared at Yan Jingchen, who had attempted to fake his death to escape, and squeezed a curse through his teeth: \"Gui’Er!\"","No wonder Yan Jingchen, who had clearly been confirmed dead back then, managed to survive. It turned out he was hiding such a Technique. However, despite his anger, Chen Yi’s words just now had hit the nail on the head. Even if he hadn’t known earlier that Yan Jingchen wanted to fake his death to escape, he had already made up his mind this time to grind him into ashes to console the souls of his two sons in heaven.","Pei Qian, Li Yunjun, and the others didn’t say anything. Only Lan Yanni loudly cursed the Gui’Er for being shameless. If Chen Yi and Pei Ze hadn’t been here, anyone else might have actually fallen for Yan Jingchen’s trick.","Chen Yi looked at Yan Jingchen and flashed to his side. Under the Qi Observation Skill, he could see that after Yan Jingchen woke up, the True Essence within his Forehead Acupoint Sea of Qi was rapidly circulating. In addition, some minute things were spreading along with the True Essence, like tiny, invisible bugs roaming through his meridians.","In just two breaths, the wounds on Yan Jingchen’s body healed slightly, and the flesh, blood, and bones of his severed limbs were writhing and growing back together. Chen Yi observed for a moment, raising his eyebrows as he asked, \"Are these Poisonous Insects?\"","Without waiting for Yan Jingchen to answer, Chen Yi thrust his spear into the wound on his chest, tearing out a chunk of flesh and blood when he pulled it out. But strangely, the moment the flesh separated from the body, the tiny bugs attached to it instantly lost their life force.","Watching his actions, the severe pain wracking his body made Yan Jingchen’s expression twist hideously. He gritted his teeth and said, \"Don’t waste your energy.","\"How could I let anyone else seize the treasures I’ve refined?\"","\"True.\" Chen Yi was just about to smash his head with a spear strike when he suddenly thought of something and asked, \"Whose idea was it for you all to come here?\"","Yan Jingchen snorted coldly and turned his head away. \"If you want to kill me or torture me, do as you please!\"","\"Kill you?","\"Originally, I planned to end you with one strike of my spear, but now I’ve changed my mind.\"","Chen Yi waved at Pei Ze and the others while saying, \"Even if you don’t speak, I know the person who sent you here is Liu Hong.","\"He must have planted some people in the grain store. He knew the grain store was going to trade grain with someone tonight, which is why he had you make a move.\"","The hateful look on Yan Jingchen’s face froze. \"How did you know?\"","\"Not just here, but the one who ordered you to poison the citizens of the Prefecture City is also him, right?\" After Chen Yi finished speaking to himself, he thrust his spear again and again into the wounds on Yan Jingchen’s limbs. Chunks of newly grown flesh were sent flying, causing all the tiny bugs on them to perish.","But he didn’t touch Yan Jingchen’s chest, nor did he use Silver Needles to seal his meridians and acupoints, allowing the flesh and organs in his chest to fully repair themselves.","Yan Jingchen mostly saw through his intentions and growled with a sinister expression, \"If I live, you and the people behind you will all die!\"","Chen Yi continued his actions noncommittally. Only when Pei Ze and the others arrived did he say, \"I have great use for this person. I wonder if you could help me keep an eye on him for now?\"","Pei Ze was just about to agree, but upon seeing the anomalies on Yan Jingchen’s body, he turned to Pei Qian next to him and said, \"You decide.\"","Pei Qian knew full well the grudge between him and Yan Jingchen. After a moment of thought, he said, \"Since you have spoken, we naturally cannot refuse.","\"It’s just that given his current condition, if we keep him alive, I’m afraid...\"","Chen Yi understood his meaning and nodded. \"Wait a moment.\"","Pei Qian and the others naturally had no objections.","A short while later.","Once the injuries on Yan Jingchen’s chest had recovered, Chen Yi flicked out a few Silver Needles, sealing the three great Seas of Qi at his Chest, Forehead Acupoint, and Dantian. They then saw that all the tiny Poisonous Insects that had previously been moving incessantly died off.","Seeing this, Chen Yi verified his suspicions. Without stopping his hands, he threw out Silver Needles one after another, sealing the acupoints on the front and back of Yan Jingchen’s body.","Yan Jingchen glared at him with pure hatred. \"Even if I become a ghost, I won’t let you off!\"","Chen Yi glanced at him. \"I believe you won’t have that Opportunity.\"","Right then, Jin Guang shone brilliantly—","[Rejected Yan Jingchen leading the Five Poison Sect to attack Liu Lang and the others; captured Yan Jingchen alive, slayed more than half of the Five Poison Sect members...]","[Reward: Hundred Flowers Palm grade upgraded to Celestial Tier, Opportunity +282.]","[Evaluation: Arrived on the scene, reputation established, handled the situation, performance commendable.]","Chen Yi took a glance, then used his spear to fling Yan Jingchen into Pei Ze’s hands, saying, \"There should still be some Five Poison Sect members left in the Prefecture City. I’ll trouble you all to clean them up as well.\"","Pei Ze grabbed Yan Jingchen by the head with one hand and grinned savagely. \"Rest assured, my young friend. With their Sect Leader dealt with, the rest are nothing to fear.\"","Pei Qian took a look at Yan Jingchen and silently put away the buzzing and fluttering Gu Insect. He had brought a supreme treasure of the Mountain Race down the mountain this time, originally intending to use it to slaughter the Five Poison Sect. He hadn’t expected that before it was even his turn to strike, the person in front of him would already wipe out more than half of the Five Poison Sect members.","A moment later.","Lan Yanni pointed at the corpses on the ground and said, \"Brother, can I take them away as well?\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. \"Brother?\"","\"You’re the lover my Sister Guanli fancies, so calling you my brother isn’t a stretch, right?\"","Chen Yi couldn’t help but laugh. This girl probably didn’t know that Pei Guanli also called him her brother. However, he didn’t explain further. He simply agreed, letting Lan Yanni dispose of the corpses as she pleased.","\"Thank you, Brother.\"","Pei Qian looked at the delighted Lan Yanni, then his gaze fell on Chen Yi. He coughed, \"Sister’s... cough, cough...\""]},{"number":564,"title":"Chapter 564 - 322: Another Celestial Tier!","paragraphs":["\"Well, the matter is urgent. We shall return to the Prefecture City first.\"","Unlike the young Lan Yanni, Pei Ze really couldn’t bring himself to say the word \"brother-in-law.\"","Naturally, Chen Yi guessed as much. He chuckled and nodded. \"Thank you for your trouble.\"","\"You’re too polite...\"","After Pei Ze and the others left with Yan Jingchen and the corpses, Chen Yi walked over to Zhang Dabao and his group.","He glanced over them one by one, then rapidly waved his hands, executing the Controlling Needle with Qi technique. Streaks of silver needles landed on the injured, rapidly healing their wounds.","Only Liu Lang, the most heavily injured of the bunch, remained weakly leaning against the cart wheel, his expression full of eager anticipation. To his surprise, after Chen Yi finished treating the others, he actually put the silver needles away as if he had completely forgotten about him.","\"The refugees outside the East City Gate are a major concern. Take advantage of the dark and transport a portion of the grain to Lin Village first,\" Chen Yi instructed.","Zhang Dabao, Jin Peng, and the others nodded in acknowledgment.","Chen Yi gave a few more instructions and turned to leave.","Unable to hold back any longer, Liu Lang hastily called out, \"Boss, Boss, what about me? I... I’m still injured...\"","Chen Yi stopped and turned his head to look at him, a look of sudden realization dawning on his face. \"I almost forgot.\"","Liu Lang chuckled. \"You’re a busy man, Boss. No rush...\"","Before he could finish, Chen Yi vanished in a flash. \"Since that’s the case, just endure it for now.","\"Don’t worry, you won’t die.\"","The smile on Liu Lang’s face froze. He stared blankly at the silhouette that disappeared in the blink of an eye, completely caught off guard.","After a long while, he turned to Zhang Dabao and asked blankly, \"Did I offend the boss in some way?\"","Zhang Dabao tried hard to suppress his laughter, his body trembling slightly. \"Probably... not?\"","\"Then, then why didn’t he heal me? I almost died at the hands of those old poisonous freaks just now!\"","\"Don’t overthink it, Brother Liu. Perhaps the boss is tempering you,\" Zhang Dabao replied.","\"Tempering? He’s tempering me? Damn it, I’ve never experienced the ’tempering’ of having more than half of my meridians severed!\"","\"Well, now you have.\"","\"You son of a...\"","A few moments later, Chen Yi arrived at the Chishui Riverbank.","Tonight, he had only seen Yan Jingchen and his group ambushing Liu Lang’s party, but he hadn’t come across Lin Zhenghong’s location. Therefore, he had followed the cart tracks all the way here.","Just as expected, he found the ground littered with corpses, and among them was Lin Zhenghong.","Chen Yi scanned the area. After confirming there were no survivors, he stood by the Chishui River and gazed in the direction of the Prefecture City.","\"People from the Liu Family?\" he suddenly chuckled after some thought.","The corpses here showed no traces of Poison Power. Instead, they were pierced by crossbow arrows originating from the military garrison. Clearly, someone else had murdered Lin Zhenghong. However, the Liu Family had come to hijack the convoy, but whatever they were after was destined to elude them.","\"Trying to get something for nothing?","\"Heh, too late!\"","Not long after, Chen Yi sneaked into the Prefecture City, only to find that more than half of the city was brightly lit and ablaze with lights. Faintly, a cacophony of noises drifted over.","\"Hurry, open the door!\"","\"Officers, what... what are you doing? It’s the middle of the night... Do you know my master’s identity?\"","\"I don’t care about your identity! This is a matter of life and death, so get out of the way!\"","Similar scenes were playing out all over the Prefecture City. Some cooperated, while others resisted. The clamor, arguments, and shouting soon dissolved into panic and terror, mixed with the faint sounds of crying. The commotion was easily comparable to the time when Xiao Wan’er was kidnapped by Du Cang.","The City Guard Army, the Government Office officials, and even the soldiers stationed outside the city had all been mobilized. Everyone was fully armed, their faces covered with water-soaked cloth strips. Additionally, the physicians from the city’s Medicine Halls had been forcibly conscripted, ordered to prepare medicinal herbs or follow the government officials to various parts of the city.","Seeing this, Chen Yi knew that Elder Master Xiao had made his move.","\"Alas, water can keep a boat afloat, but it can also overturn it...\" he muttered.","Such a simple truth, yet there were always people who failed to understand it. It would have been one thing if they simply didn’t understand, but they even attempted to poison an entire region just to satisfy their own selfish desires.","Their crimes were punishable by death!"]},{"number":565,"title":"Chapter 565 - 323: Oh No, the Son-in-Law is Dying!","paragraphs":["The night was late, but far from peaceful.","When Chen Yi returned to Spring Lotus Garden, there was already some clamor outside. Armored Warriors brought several Physicians, fanning out from the central courtyard to the surrounding ones. They checked and questioned everyone one by one, instructing them to boil medicinal herbs.","Actually, there was no need for such trouble. Those infected by the plague poison would fall into a deep slumber within an hour. They would look as though they had been poisoned, their lips and teeth turning dark purple. However, the Xiao Family was a large clan after all. With people constantly coming and going from the estate, it was hard to guarantee that no hidden dangers would slip through the cracks.","Chen Yi naturally didn’t dwell on it, leaving the Old Master to worry about it. After changing into a light, casual robe, he headed straight to the study to wait, without waking Xiao Wuge and Xiaodie. He lit the oil lamp, poured some water, and ground the ink. Sitting at the desk, Chen Yi’s face was illuminated by the candlelight, a contemplative look in his eyes.","Although the actions of Liu Hong and the Five Poison Sect had stirred up the Prefecture City both inside and out, they had also exposed more flaws. The gathering of refugees, the rising grain prices, the plague poison, Xinglin Hall, the conflicts involving the Jing State Liu Family, the Peacock King Banner, the Barbarian Race...","Stringing all these incidents together, Chen Yi drew a few conclusions—to throw the Shu State into chaos!","To some extent, Liu Hong’s schemes shared the same goal as the White Tiger Guard’s layout in the Shu State; both aimed to throw the Shu State into turmoil. However, the former was far more audacious and unscrupulous. The latter was much more subtle, operating without a sound. They often used a seemingly insignificant incident to fulfill a certain condition and push things forward step by step. In other words, they advanced steadily, calculating every step.","It was like a Chess Master using the world as their chessboard, placing a piece in the Shu State to leverage a corner of the game. This inevitably gave Chen Yi a sense of familiarity. This was exactly how he operated: strategizing before acting. While others calculated three steps ahead, he calculated ten. Even if he occasionally miscalculated—like with Du Cang, or the sudden attack by the Five Poison Sect—most of his plans still came to fruition.","\"The White Tiger Guard... Pavilion Master?\" Chen Yi couldn’t help but think of that enigmatic Pavilion Master of the White Tiger Guard.","Many of the things the White Tiger Guard did indeed left no traces, but they couldn’t prevent some of their people from being too careless. Like Liu Si’er probing him in Tonglin Town—it was clumsy. Ge the Third hid the deepest, yet he was forced to flee for silver coins. Xiao Dongchen was too selfish, merely using the White Tiger Guard to seek profit for the second branch. Cui Qingwu clearly had no real dedication to the White Tiger Guard; she acted too much like a pampered young lady, obeying only in name but not in spirit.","If Chen Yi were the White Tiger Guard Pavilion Master, he figured he wouldn’t entrust Cui Qingwu with any heavy responsibilities either. Comparing them all, among the White Tiger Guard members he had encountered, only three were qualified.","One was Uncle Gui, who had died accidentally. He hid the deepest, never showing off his abilities. The second was Lou Yuxue. She hid in the Bright Moon Building and did a lot for the White Tiger Guard; otherwise, she couldn’t have been promoted to Golden Banner Officer. The last person was \"General.\"","Although Chen Yi didn’t know how many Golden Banner Officers there were in the White Tiger Guard, it wasn’t hard to gauge the caliber of the others based on General. Whether in terms of bearing, tactics, intellect, or Cultivation, they were all commendable, with no obvious weaknesses. Had Chen Yi not grasped a lot of information and seized the initiative, given the White Tiger Guard’s capabilities, it would have been almost impossible for him to turn the tables. He would only have been dragged along like a marionette by the White Tiger Guard, and ultimately, a Fledgling like him would hardly have met a good end.","From this, it wasn’t hard for Chen Yi to see the formidable nature of the White Tiger Guard Pavilion Master.","\"Playing chess... Could he also be someone accomplished in the Chess Dao?\" Chen Yi made a few guesses, and the chessboard in his mind began to move once again.","Beneath the chessboard formed by illusory mist, the Nine States and Three Prefectures of the Great Wei could be faintly seen. Even though only the Shu State was somewhat clear at the moment, he already felt like Zhuge Kongming during his Longzhong Dialog. In this world, the Wei Dynasty reigned supreme. To the north lay the untamed wilderness, to the south the Barbarian Race, to the east the Pirate Wokou, and to the west the Buddha Country. Surrounded by a pack of wolves, dark currents surged within. In short, the world was on the brink of chaos.","After a moment of thought, Chen Yi picked up a few Heizi from the chessboard, crushing them into flying ash in his grip. His gaze then focused solely on the few Heizi in the Shu State’s corner of the board. Liu Hong, Zhu Hao, and the rest.","\"The schemes Liu Hong planned align with the White Tiger Guard’s goals... Hmm, it should be a temporary alignment. Like two people walking together for a short distance before going their separate ways,\" Chen Yi pondered. \"Their destinations should be the same, so over at the Imperial Court...\"","Chen Yi vaguely understood. It must be that the Capital Prefecture was preparing for some major event, which ended up dragging a lot of people into it. The game between these various factions was complex and intricate. Those caught in the middle, like the Xiao Family, probably couldn’t see it clearly.","\"So this is just the prelude. Or perhaps... some kind of probe? Whether it succeeds or fails might affect the outcome of that major event?\" he wondered.","Chen Yi didn’t know for sure, but he was clear on one thing—the Shu State would not descend into chaos, nor could it!","\"The Shu State cannot fall into chaos. The Xiao Family has to be the stabilizing anchor, and it can only be done by the Xiao Family,\" he reasoned. \"It’s time for the Old Master to make a decision. If he doesn’t make a move, Liu Hong’s merit for this matter will likely vanish. In that case... the White Tiger Guard Pavilion Master’s layout is truly far-reaching...\"","Chen Yi shook his head, unrolled a sheet of Yunsong Paper, and lowered his brush, writing a few words as smoothly as flowing water.","\"In the end, Liu Hong is just a chess piece. And one tucked away in a corner, fancying himself smart,\" Chen Yi mused. \"However, he has indeed brought a lot of trouble to the Xiao Family.\"","Sometimes, grudges formed just that inexplicably. Like how the Xiao Family flourished for two hundred years, only to suddenly decline, like a tiger falling onto the plains. Surrounded by a pack of wolves, they naturally became a target.","Without the Xiao Family, there would be others to take over the Dingyuan Army. It could be the Liu Family, Noble Families of the Shu State, or other Nobles of the Great Wei Dynasty. It had nothing to do with right or wrong; it was all driven by human nature and profit.","Thinking of this, Chen Yi stopped his brush and looked at the two lines written in Cursive Script on the Yunsong Paper:"]},{"number":566,"title":"Chapter 566 - 323: Oh No, the Son-in-Law Is Dying!","paragraphs":["\"Its rise is sudden, its fall is equally swift.\"","Even without connecting to Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, these ten characters still carried a lingering charm. However, what was even more profound than the calligraphy was the meaning they conveyed. The cycle of prosperity and decline was the ultimate Dao.","Chen Yi examined the writing for a moment before picking up his Wolf Hair Brush. \"I’ve done so much. It’s time I take a few days of rest,\" he thought with a secret smile.","He dropped the brush.","SPLAT.","Drops of ink splattered, ruining more than half of the calligraphy piece. Following this, Chen Yi leaned back into his chair. His breathing grew weak, and his lips took on a faint purplish-blue hue.","He wondered who would still be able to recognize him as \"Liu Wu\" now!","A short while later.","Voices echoed from outside the Spring Lotus Garden. Wang Lixing had brought people to the wooden building and shouted a few times. Xiaodie, who was a light sleeper, woke up. Once she clearly heard the words from below, she hurriedly got dressed. She first went to Chen Yi’s wing, and upon finding it empty, she quickly rushed to wake Xiao Wuge.","Hearing that a plague had broken out, Xiao Wuge sobered up instantly and began throwing on his clothes.","Xiaodie quickly helped him tidy up and said, \"Mr. Chen isn’t in his wing. He should be in the study. I’ll go inform him.\"","Xiao Wuge kept his small face stern and waved his hand. \"Hurry, go. Chen Yi also went out of the city yesterday, I hope he didn’t... pah, pah, pah. Chen Yi will definitely be fine.\"","Without waiting for a response, Xiaodie trotted downstairs. She let out a breath of relief when she saw the candlelight glowing inside the study.","\"Mr. Chen! Mr. Chen, the Armored Warriors in the estate...\"","The moment she pushed the door open, Xiaodie saw Chen Yi slumped back in his chair. She froze in sheer terror. A moment later, she ran out the door in tears.","\"This is terrible! Mr. Chen... Mr. Chen is dying!\"","Wang Li Xing and the others were stunned. Once they processed her words, they immediately rushed into the wooden building. \"What happened to Mr. Chen?\"","\"Mr. Chen... boohoo... Mr. Chen has... he’s been infected by the plague toxin...\"","Inside the Qingjing Residence.","Elder Master Xiao sat imposing and bold like a grand Blade in his Grandmaster’s Chair. With one hand resting on his knee and the other draped over the back of the chair, his eyes, restored with God-like vitality, stared intently out the door. He had been like this ever since \"Liu Wu\" paid a visit. He didn’t dare to relax for even a moment; his heart was even heavier than when Xiao Wan’er had been abducted.","Yes, it was heavy. It wasn’t mere worry or annoyance.","Elder Master Xiao couldn’t figure one thing out—why did it have to come to this? Even if the Xiao Family’s decline was considered a sin, those people could have just bullied, harmed, or ostracized him. Why did they have to drag the citizens of the Prefecture City down with them?","A plague toxin.","A plague toxin!","Beside him, Xiao Jing didn’t even dare to breathe too loudly. It had been a very long time since he last saw the Elder Master look like this. It was just like five years ago at Mengshui Pass.","Xiao Xuanshuo sat straight in his wheelchair, his hands resting naturally on the armrests. His Fang Zheng face was full of anger. After a long silence, he couldn’t help but ask, \"Father, how long do you plan to endure this?\"","Elder Master Xiao stiffened slightly. \"We wait.\"","One short word. Nothing more needed to be said.","Xiao Xuanshuo’s jaw clenched, clearly grinding his teeth. \"If ’Dragon Tiger’ hadn’t come to report tonight, your eldest granddaughter and Chen Yi would both be in mortal danger. That is a plague toxin! A plague toxin!\"","Having a military background, he had naturally seen scenes of battlefields littered with corpses. But that was in war, where armies fought each other. The dead died on their feet, fighting with fierce bravery.","A plague toxin was different. If one died, a whole household was infected. If a household died, a whole crowd was infected. If no treatment Method could be found, let alone the hundreds of thousands of citizens in the Prefecture City, even the neighboring villages and towns would be in mortal danger.","Elder Master Xiao glanced at him from the corner of his eye and remained silent for a moment before saying, \"Liu Wu has already told us the Method to resolve the plague toxin. For now, saving the citizens is our top priority. Time is tight; the Government Office and the Guard Army cannot be thrown into chaos.\"","Even though he knew the plague toxin was likely orchestrated by Liu Hong, he still had to endure it for the sake of the people. The Governor’s Office controlled the allocation of money and grain in Shu State. If Liu Hong was eliminated, it would take at least five days for the Imperial Court to arrange a replacement.","They couldn’t afford to waste that kind of time. Not to mention, even if he didn’t do it for the citizens, he had to consider himself and the Xiao Family. Weighed down by heavy thoughts, Elder Master Xiao felt somewhat hesitant and indecisive.","Hearing this, Xiao Xuanshuo sighed. He silently wheeled himself toward the door, clearly disappointed.","However, before he could leave, Elder Master Xiao seemed to make up his mind and suddenly spoke up. \"Xuanshuo, make a trip to the Capital Prefecture for me!\"","Xiao Xuanshuo paused in surprise, then was overjoyed. \"Father, you’ve finally thought it through.\"","Elder Master Xiao grunted in affirmation. Looking at him, he said, \"I will personally write a memorial later. You must present it to the Holy Emperor and let the Holy Emperor make the final decision.\"","Although he lacked concrete evidence to bring down Liu Hong right now, the clues he had on hand were enough to get things started. Even if it merely planted a seed of doubt in the Holy Emperor’s mind, causing him to send an imperial envoy to investigate, or if the White Tiger Guard stepped in to dig deeper, the trail would undoubtedly lead back to Liu Hong.","The Peacock King Banner, the Barbarian Prince, the Five Poison Sect, the Ji State Trading Company... Any one of these was enough to strip Liu Hong of his Official’s Hat.","Xiao Xuanshuo agreed repeatedly and asked, \"Then what about here in Shu State...\"","Elder Master Xiao glared at him and scoffed. \"I am not dead yet. A little wind and waves won’t capsize the great ship of Shu State.\"","With Liu Wu’s warning and the Method to break the plague toxin, if he still couldn’t keep Shu State safe, then he, the Duke Dingyuan, might as well die early.","Xiao Xuanshuo chuckled sheepishly. Just as he was about to speak, panicked footsteps echoed from outside the door. Third Steward Lu Guan rushed over in a hurry. Ignoring all formalities, he shouted, \"Elder Master, this is bad! Mr. Chen, he... he...\"","\"What happened to him?\"","\"He seems to have been infected by the plague toxin! Right now... right now, he’s already unconscious! Elder Master, you...\"","Elder Master Xiao’s brows furrowed tightly. He immediately stood up and ordered, \"Quick, lock down the Spring Lotus Garden! Tell Wan’er and the others not to leave the Jiaxing Garden either. We absolutely cannot let the plague toxin spread!\"","\"Yes, yes...\" Lu Guan didn’t dare to hesitate. He Transferred his path and sprinted away.","After he left, Elder Master Xiao slammed a heavy Punch onto the table.","SMASH.","Wood splinters flew into the air.","\"Liu Hong, you old thief! Even death would be too good for you!\"","South Street, the Liu Family.","Compared to the noisy clamor outside, it was far too quiet here. Amidst the bright lights, dozens—perhaps over a hundred—Guards dressed in blue tunics surrounded the area, guarding every courtyard.","In a pavilion deep within the backyard, Liu Hong looked up at the bright moon in the night sky, his face devoid of any expression. Behind him, Liu Taoyao stood dumbstruck, his eyes locked onto the chest on the stone table. Inside the open chest lay hundreds of scattered sheets of paper. The words \"ten thousand taels\" could faintly be seen on them.","\"This is impossible, Father. This is impossible...\" Liu Taoyao muttered. \"I clearly took this chest from Lin Zhenghong’s hands. How... how could this be? How could those silver notes be fake?\"","Liu Taoyao clearly couldn’t accept the reality that ten million taels worth of silver notes had turned into waste paper. He was even more baffled as to how this had happened.","Liu Hong didn’t respond to his words; his gaze simply shifted uncertainly. Compared to those silver coins, he cared much more about the sudden changes in the Shu State Prefecture City.","\"It’s too early,\" Liu Hong said.","Hearing his voice, Liu Taoyao asked, \"What? Father, what’s too early?\"","Liu Hong paused and glanced at him. He then sat on the stone stool opposite his son, his expression uncharacteristically grim.","\"The plague toxin. It was discovered far too early. Almost as soon as it began to spread, it was noticed by... the Xiao Family. Their response was extremely swift. The Government Office, the City Guard Army, the citizens, and the Jianghu People all learned about it.\"","\"Father, isn’t it better to discover such a formidable plague toxin as early as possible?\"","\"Do you know who orchestrated this plague toxin?\"","\"I... I do not know.\"","\"It was me.\"","\"Wha—\" Liu Taoyao stared at him blankly. \"Father, you... you did this?\"","Even though he knew his own father wasn’t a good person and secretly colluded with the Peacock King Banner and the Barbarian Race, he had no idea about the plague toxin.","Liu Hong nodded. \"It was my doing... along with the Five Poison Sect.\"","The only reason he hadn’t mentioned it was because his scheming with the Five Poison Sect was ultimately aimed at the Jing State Liu Family. To prevent them from noticing, he had acted with great caution and hidden behind the scenes. But now, there was no way to keep it hidden any longer.","Liu Taoyao asked in confusion, \"Why would you...\"","Liu Hong shook his head. \"I cannot tell you the reason. But you must firmly remember what I am about to say next.\"","\"Father, please... speak.\"","\"Take advantage of the chaos inside and outside the Prefecture City tonight. You will take your men and leave Shu State.\"","Caught completely off guard, Liu Taoyao forgot all about the silver notes and asked, \"Father, do you have a task for me to do?\"","\"I am telling you to take your men and flee! Go as far away as possible, and never return to the Great Wei Dynasty in this lifetime!\"","\"Why?!\"","Looking at his eldest son, a faint smile appeared on Liu Hong’s face as he sighed. \"One wrong Step, and the entire game is lost.\"","If the plague toxin being discovered by the Xiao Family was the only issue, it wouldn’t be so bad. The critical problem was that the silver notes Liu Taoyao brought back were fake. No matter how foolish Liu Hong was, he knew he had been outplayed this time. It wasn’t just him; perhaps the Five Poison Sect hadn’t succeeded either. Whoever was hiding in the shadows had completely and utterly destroyed almost all of his meticulously laid plans.","How could he not prepare an escape route?","Still unable to understand, Liu Taoyao stammered, \"B-but Father...\"","Liu Hong raised his hand to cut him off. \"Do not ask anything. Listen to me and leave right now!\" he said sternly.","However, just as his words fell, a voice echoed from nearby.","\"Lord Liu, where exactly are you sending your noble son...\""]},{"number":567,"title":"Chapter 567 - 324: A Sudden Wind Rises, Frost Covers the City","paragraphs":["The intruder was dressed entirely in black. He wore a bronze mask of an archaic design, its edges speckled with verdigris rust.","The only visible features were a pair of clear, bright eyes that carried a hint of mockery, reflecting the figures of Liu Hong and his son.","Liu Taoyao recovered from his shock, stood up, and unsheathed the long sword at his waist. Pointing it directly at the intruder, he demanded, \"Who are you to dare trespass into the Liu family’s home?\"","In contrast, Liu Hong shed his previous solemnity, revealing a look of surprise. His gaze became subtly complex—a mixture of dejection, panic, and relief, among other emotions.","The intruder glanced at Liu Taoyao and let out a scoff. \"They say a tiger father begets no dog son, but from what I see, that’s not always true.\" He shifted his gaze to Liu Hong. \"What do you say, Lord Liu?\"","Just as Liu Taoyao was about to speak again, Liu Hong abruptly cut in. \"Yao’er, remember what I just told you. Leave now.\"","\"Father, but he...\"","\"He is an old friend of mine. This has nothing to do with you. Go!\"","Seeing his father’s stern expression, Liu Taoyao froze for a moment. He then cast a wary glance at the man in the bronze mask, sheathed his long sword, and left in a hurry.","Though his mind was swirling with questions, years of receiving Liu Hong’s teachings made it clear to him that something major was unfolding. He would simply have to wait until he was away from here to find another opportunity to investigate the situation in Shu State.","The bronze-masked intruder did not stop him. He waited quietly until Liu Taoyao was far away before taking a seat opposite Liu Hong. \"Lord Liu is a smart man. You should know that it was no easy feat for me to make this trip here.\"","Liu Hong nodded in understanding, his tone laced with bitterness. \"I ask for nothing else, only that you spare my son’s life.\"","The intruder smiled and shook his head. \"Lord Liu, we have known each other for years. You should know my temperament. Whatever the Lord commands, I execute.\"","Hearing this, Liu Hong fell silent for a moment. He took a deep breath, and his demeanor recovered a fraction of its former dignity. He was still the Governor of Shu State. \"Song Jinjian, there’s no need to beat around the bush. Tell me, what did that lord send you to Shu State for?\"","The intruder, Song Jinjian, smiled and nodded. \"Now this is the Liu Hong, the Lord Liu, that I know.","\"However, even if you hadn’t asked, I would still have to properly complete the task the Lord entrusted to me.\"","Pausing briefly, his eyes turned serious. \"The Lord wants you to do nothing more. Just wait obediently for the Holy Emperor’s decree.\"","\"The Holy Emperor’s... decree?\" Liu Hong tipped his head back and burst into laughter, as if he had just heard the greatest joke in the world, though his voice carried a faint undercurrent of sorrow.","A few moments later, his laughter subsided. He looked at Song Jinjian across from him, a mocking expression on his face. \"Over all these years, I’ve done so much for him, only to end up with such a fate. Isn’t he afraid that I’ll fight to the bitter end and drag him down with me?\"","Unsurprised by his reaction, Song Jinjian shook his head. \"This is precisely one of the reasons the Lord sent me here.","\"Lord Liu, the Lord is not a heartless man. Otherwise, he wouldn’t have pushed so hard to make you the Governor of Shu State in the first place.","\"You should be well aware that this was a mutual agreement, not something the Lord forced upon you.\"","After speaking, Song Jinjian raised his hand. A guard of the Liu family, dressed in green, briskly walked over, serving a jug of wine, two cups, two pairs of chopsticks, and four plates of cold sliced meat.","\"I came in such a hurry that I haven’t eaten all day. You don’t mind me borrowing your estate’s cook, do you, Lord Liu?\"","Liu Hong caught a glimpse of the retreating guard from the corner of his eye and silently took the wine jug, filling both their cups.","Seeing this, Song Jinjian smiled and shook his head. \"Don’t worry, Lord Liu. This wine is also from your estate. It’s not poisoned wine bestowed by the Lord.\"","Despite having his thoughts read, Liu Hong’s expression remained unchanged. He raised his cup and said, \"Please.\"","Song Jinjian said no more, lifting his own cup to clink against his.","CLINK.","The two of them downed their drinks in one gulp.","Setting down his cup, Song Jinjian’s gaze turned solemn. \"Do you remember the first time we drank together and shared our thoughts?","\"Back then, I saw that you were ambitious and deeply calculating. Naturally, the Lord saw it too.","\"But His Excellency didn’t think it was a bad thing. He even told me that capable people are never content to trail behind others.","\"Because of this, I’ve kept those words to heart all these years and never been overly harsh on you.","\"And, of course, you didn’t let down my expectations; you executed several tasks exceptionally well.\"","He paused for a moment before abruptly changing the subject. \"So why did you bungle things so spectacularly this time?\"","Meeting his gaze, Liu Hong calmly replied, \"Someone got in the way.\"","\"Oh? And who might this person be?\"","\"’Dragon Tiger’ Liu Wu.\"","\"Liu Wu? One of the Jianghu people?\"","Song Jinjian pondered for a moment before letting out a mocking laugh. \"Lord Liu, you might as well be completely frank. It will make it easier for me to put in a good word for you when I return to report to the Lord.\"","Liu Hong simply stared at him with a placid expression, offering no response.","Understanding his intentions, Song Jinjian sighed. \"Although the Lord hasn’t said much, the disaster you’ve caused this time is far too grave. His Excellency has no way to protect you.\"","\"A disaster I caused?\" A cold sneer tugged at the corners of Liu Hong’s mouth. \"Heh. His Excellency truly thinks highly of me.\"","\"Whether he thinks highly of you or not is His Excellency’s business,\" Song Jinjian said noncommittally. \"I’ll only ask you one thing. Do you still want your eldest son to leave Shu State alive?\"","Liu Hong gave a straightforward \"I do,\" before adding, \"And I want him to stay by your side.\"","\"Me?\" Song Jinjian pointed at himself, somewhat surprised. \"Has Lord Liu lost his mind?","\"I am a nameless nobody. Wouldn’t having your eldest son follow me completely ruin his future?\"","Liu Hong shook his head. \"I only ask that he preserves the very last bloodline for the Jing State Liu family.\"","\"Oh? What makes you so certain that something will happen to the Liu family?\"","\"If the Liu family were safe, with that lord’s cunning, even if he couldn’t protect me, he wouldn’t just sit idly by.\"","Hearing this, Song Jinjian smiled and uttered two words: \"What a pity.\""]},{"number":568,"title":"Chapter 568 - 324: Sudden Winds Rise, Frost Covers the City","paragraphs":["\"Losing a Grand General like you, I must say it is a pity on behalf of the Lord.\"","After some thought, he still did not agree. \"Whether your eldest son can stay by my side is not up to you, nor is it up to me.\"","Liu Hong understood that he was referring to the \"Lord,\" so he nodded. After organizing his thoughts, he recounted everything that had recently happened in Shu State exactly as it occurred.","\"...Tonight, just as the plague began to spread, the Xiao Family took action and even produced a Medical prescription to treat it. This should be Liu Wu’s doing.\"","Song Jinjian’s eyes lit up slightly. \"In that case, this ’Dragon Tiger’ does indeed have some skill.\"","Liu Hong hummed in agreement and pointed at the chest on the nearby stone stool. \"Not just that. He schemed against the people from the Ji State Trading Company, making them give away a million piculs of grain, only to get a pile of waste paper in return.\"","Song Jinjian glanced at the fake silver notes in the chest and chuckled involuntarily. \"You didn’t lose unjustly.","\"From Lv Jiunan to Asutai, then to Du Cang and the Five Poison Sect, even the Ji State Trading Company was completely outsmarted by him.","\"No wonder you handled this long-planned matter so poorly.\"","Liu Hong refilled their cups but didn’t toast. He took a sip on his own and said, \"It is destiny.","\"Before tonight, I had many complaints about His Lordship, so I planned to risk my life one last time. Unfortunately, I lost everything.\"","After finishing his wine, Song Jinjian’s hand paused as he set down the cup. He sighed and said, \"It’s not just you.","\"The failure of this plot has extremely far-reaching consequences, and the Lord is suffering an endless headache because of it.","\"However, since things have come to this, even he has no other choice but to try his best to salvage the situation.\"","Liu Hong fell slightly silent. After downing the wine in his cup, he asked, \"When will the Holy Emperor’s decree arrive?\"","\"In three to five days at the shortest, or eleven to twelve days at the longest.\"","\"Ten days... I’m afraid the Xiao Family won’t be able to hold back anymore.\"","\"The Xiao Family?\" Song Jinjian shook his head and sighed. \"The most troublesome part is the Xiao Family.","\"Originally, according to the Lord’s plan, the Xiao Family would certainly be eradicated from Shu State after this. What would follow next is the fight for the position of commander-in-chief of the Dingyuan Army.\"","Liu Hong nodded silently. \"Now that the Xiao Family has freed themselves, trying to put them to death again will be difficult.\"","Song Jinjian glanced at him. \"Not necessarily.\"","\"Oh? Does His Lordship have another plan?\"","\"Forgive me, Lord Liu. I don’t know either, but...","\"But there is one thing I can tell you. The Holy Emperor wishes to become an unparalleled sovereign who outshines all throughout history, and his greatest hope is to march south and conquer the Barbarian Race.\"","\"What about the north?\"","\"Those barbarians have been constantly crusaded against by past dynasties. Why would the Holy Emperor take them seriously?\"","Liu Hong understood clearly in his heart. \"Thus, I can An Xin and go on my way.\"","Song Jinjian paused, then poured two cups of wine again. Raising his cup with both hands, he offered a toast and said, \"Rest assured, Lord Liu. The Lord will certainly not forget your hard work.\"","Liu Hong returned the toast. \"In that case, I will entrust my son to you, Mr. Song.\"","Song Jinjian looked at him in silence for a moment, then nodded, saying, \"I will give it a try.\"","He continued to ask, \"Liu Taoyao at least has some quick-witted intelligence, but your second son...\"","Without waiting for him to finish, Liu Hong lowered his head slightly. \"Let him accompany me to the underworld on the same Dao.\"","Hearing this, Song Jinjian knew he had already made his choice.","\"Before coming here, the Lord instructed me to act according to the circumstances, but he somewhat underestimated you, Lord Liu.","\"Speak. Aside from Liu Taoyao, do you have any other unfulfilled wishes? If it’s within my power, I will definitely accomplish them on your behalf.\"","Hearing this, Liu Hong initially wanted to shake his head and say no, but he suddenly remembered someone. \"If it is convenient for you, bring Liu Zhaoxue along with you as well.\"","\"Oh? The daughter of the first branch?\"","\"Yes, Zhaoxue is intelligent. She definitely won’t disappoint you.\"","Song Jinjian gave him a deep look and agreed with a smile. \"It’s just adding an extra pair of chopsticks anyway.\"","Liu Hong remained silent.","Seeing this, Song Jinjian said no more. He stood up, patted his shoulder, and walked outside. \"Alright, I should go do some real business now. If I have caused any offense, I hope Lord Liu can forgive me.\"","\"Please go ahead...\"","Not long after.","The Cyan-clothed Guards inside and outside the Liu Family quietly changed faces, along with all those Maids and servants. From the inside out, not a single one escaped. Although Liu Hong didn’t see it with his own eyes, he figured it should naturally be this way. A person without any use value was worse than a dog. Not to mention those who were meant to be dogs in the first place?","Liu Hong looked at the cold minced meat on the table. He picked up his chopsticks, grabbed two pieces of meat, and chewed them slowly in his mouth, feeling somewhat like a hero reaching the twilight of his life. He knew very well that with Song Jinjian’s arrival in Shu State, both he and the Jing State Liu Family had no way out. Even if His Lordship didn’t make a move, he still couldn’t escape death. It was just a matter of sooner or later.","Was he unwilling to accept this? Liu Hong was naturally unwilling. He thought back carefully and didn’t feel he had taken a wrong Step anywhere. Piece by piece, event by event, everything had gone according to his expectations. Yet, the outcome was far from satisfactory.","\"If not for ’Dragon Tiger,’ the Xiao Family would have been doomed.","\"’Dragon Tiger’ Liu Wu... I will be waiting for you in the underworld!\"","Just then, Liu Taofang ran outside the pavilion and shouted with a look of terror, \"Father, Father, something happened!\"","Liu Hong’s expression remained unchanged. \"Sit down and talk.\"","How could Liu Taofang sit down? He spoke in a panicked tone, \"Father, something huge has truly happened in the manor!","\"Just now, the Maids in my courtyard were all replaced! I—I don’t recognize a single one of them...\"","Liu Hong raised a hand to interrupt, saying, \"I ordered them to be replaced.\"","Liu Taofang froze for a moment before his face relaxed. He sat across from him and asked in confusion, \"Father, why did you suddenly replace everyone? You scared me to death.\"","Liu Hong didn’t explain, only telling him to pour the wine.","Liu Taofang didn’t hesitate in the slightest. He poured him a cup of wine, poured one for himself, and downed it with a smack of his lips.","\"Father, I saw my elder brother leading people away in a hurry just now. Did something happen?\"","\"A plague broke out in the city. I asked him to go to the Government Office to help out.\""]},{"number":569,"title":"Chapter 569 - 324: Sudden Winds Arise, Frost Covers the City","paragraphs":["\"Oh, oh? How... how did the plague...\"","Before Liu Taofang could finish his sentence, his entire body stiffened at the table. His eyes turned pitch black, and blood oozed from his eyes, ears, nose, and mouth. Within just two breaths, he lost all signs of life.","Liu Hong watched him quietly, his facial muscles twitching slightly, as if he didn’t know whether to laugh or cry.","After a long while, he finally picked up his cup, finished his wine, and got up to walk outside.","Whether it was because of the silvery moonlight cascading down or some other reason, Liu Hong’s black hair appeared completely silver-white.","A faint song echoed through the air.","\"Once the torches burned red, a sudden wind brought frost over the entire city, and the bells of the Horse Gang rang...\"","Song Jinjian revealed his figure from a corner, silently watching him disappear around the bend.","\"Liu Wu...","\"How dare you ruin the Lord’s grand plan? I cannot let you live!\"","***","Between 3:00 AM and 5:00 AM, before the sky had brightened, the clamor within the Prefecture City continued. The commoners dared not go outside, while the government officials went from door to door, occasionally plastering a seal on the outside of a house.","Although the Wandering Martial Artists who had come here were panicked, they relied on their Martial Arts Cultivation and had some degree of confidence. However, they too dared not run around recklessly. They could only squeeze into inns and taverns, complaining bitterly.","\"It’s truly bizarre.\"","\"Ever since we arrived in Shu State, there hasn’t been a single day of peace.\"","\"Tell me about it.\"","\"Horse bandits, the Barbarian Race, soaring grain prices, the plague, and refugees on top of that... Do you guys think Immortal Bai might have issued another prophecy?\"","\"Damn it, that’s it! It has to be him!\"","\"Stop talking nonsense. No one has even seen Immortal Bai, how could it be him?\"","\"Why not!\"","\"Have you forgotten who we’re here for?\"","\"Immor—\"","It was unclear who started it, but a rumor soon began to spread throughout the Prefecture City. The rumor claimed that Immortal Bai had secretly arrived in Shu State and issued a prophecy for someone with a poor destiny, which in turn triggered these numerous incidents. Surprisingly, quite a few people actually believed it, and Liu Zhaoxue was one of them.","She suddenly remembered the fortune-telling she had received outside the East Market a few days ago. The more she thought about it, the more convinced she became that the person who read her fortune was Immortal Bai.","\"Bones of gold and jade, a heart of orchids...","\"The phoenix is noble and aloof, drinking only morning dew and eating only bamboo seeds. Thus, its standards are exceptionally high, making it prone to feelings of loneliness.\"","This prophecy wasn’t considered incredibly profound, and Liu Zhaoxue herself felt a sense of loneliness, finding herself entirely out of place within the Jing State Liu Family and the lands of Shu State. She didn’t think she was the person mentioned in the rumors, but she knew someone who was—Ling’er.","With these thoughts in mind, Liu Zhaoxue scanned Xinglin Hall on South Street but couldn’t spot Ling’er anywhere. Just as she was about to continue her search, she suddenly saw several figures dressed in Mountain Race clothing outside the Medicine Hall. Not far from them was the very person she was looking for—Ling’er of the Five Poison Sect. However, it was glaringly obvious that the Maid who usually feigned compliance by her side was now completely devoid of life.","Liu Zhaoxue’s beautiful eyes widened in shock. She covered her mouth, too terrified to make a single move. The people of the Mountain Race had actually come to seek revenge at a time like this!","Pei Ze noticed her gaze and cast a sidelong glance at her. A cruel smile was the only expression that surfaced on his gaunt face before he turned and left. Here in Shu State, when the Mountain Race took action, no one dared to stand in their way. Let alone Jianghu People, how many within the Government Office would be blind enough to interfere at such a time?","Liu Zhaoxue only snapped back to reality after waiting for them to walk far away. She hastily led her people back to the house to pack their belongings. To her surprise, just as she finished packing, she heard a hoarse voice behind her.","\"Liu Zhaoxue?\"","\"You...\"","Before Liu Zhaoxue could react, she felt a sharp pain in the back of her neck and fainted.","\"Consider yourself lucky. From now on, you’ll be staying by my side...\"","As the voice faded, the guest room was left completely empty, with only a glimmer of light shining in from the east. It was neither bright nor warm.","***","Two days later.","Chen Yi slowly \"woke up,\" calling out weakly with a hoarse voice, \"Xiaodie, Xiaodie...\"","Xiaodie, who had been sound asleep by the window, jolted awake. Upon seeing Chen Yi’s eyes open, she abruptly stood up and ran outside.","\"Mr. Chen is awake!\"","\"Miss! Miss! Mr. Chen is awake!\"","Chen Yi turned his head to watch her run off. He couldn’t help but blink, thinking to himself, \"If I don’t wake up soon, my ears will fall off from your constant nagging.\"","Thanks to feigning illness this time, he managed to discover Xiaodie’s little secret.","He thought, \"’The Biography of the Second Son-in-Law of the Marquis’s Mansion’... What a terrible title. Even ’The Legend of Mr. Qingzhou’ would have been better...\""]},{"number":570,"title":"Chapter 570 - 325: Slaughter Them All","paragraphs":["Two days was enough time to change many things.","The grain shops in the East and West Markets closed down and suspended business. At first, rumors spread that they had disregarded the lives of the common people, which led to an angry mob swarming them. Indeed, no grain was found. The storefronts were completely smashed to pieces, along with the staff, accountants, and Shopkeepers inside. After the Government Office inspected the scene, seeing no hope of catching the culprits, they made excuses about having other matters to attend to, openly and secretly cursing that those shops deserved it.","However, the people of the Prefecture City could not go without grain, nor could the refugees outside the city be ignored. Ultimately, the Governor’s Office and the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office opened their granaries. A portion of the grain was distributed into the grain market, sold at the price of one tael of silver per stone. The larger portion was used for disaster relief.","But after discovering that a benevolent family outside the Prefecture City had already distributed one stone of grain to each refugee, the people from the Government Office changed their minds. They directly sent the grain to Guang’an County and other areas downstream of the Chishui River.","With this two-pronged approach, the commoners inside and outside the Prefecture City were all praising Left Governor Liu Hong, calling him a just and uncorrupt official. By extension, Prefect Liu Si also received much praise, which caused him to act with lightning speed and decisiveness over the past two days. After all, for every good deed he accomplished, he could earn a higher evaluation on his merit record at the end of the year: disaster relief, preventing the spread of the plague, and tracking down the murderers of Lin Zhenghong and others, as well as the culprits who plundered a million stones of grain.","Of course, several Thousand Households of the Imprisonment Department also secretly received some ambiguous orders.","\"Those people in the grain shops died under bizarre circumstances, and the grain disappeared just as strangely. There must be hidden secrets involved. The investigation is far too difficult, so we might as well put it on hold for now.\"","Anyone who could rise to the rank of Thousand Households in the Imprisonment Department was exceptionally shrewd. Naturally, they understood Lord Prefect’s intentions and all went to help the government officials handle the plague first.","What was the reason? There were quite a few fools in the Imprisonment Department who asked this question, such as the single-minded Fang Hongxiu. Out of helplessness, the other Thousand Households could only point toward the east for her.","\"The west just lost a million stones of grain, and the refugees in the east received a hundred thousand stones in a single day. Who do you think took it?\"","Fang Hongxiu and the others finally understood. The Government Office was being generous at others’ expense, planning to send away the refugees first before catching the culprits.","\"Aren’t the superiors afraid they’ll run away?\"","\"If they run, they run... Hundred Households Fang, you know that many Jianghu People have died in the city recently, right?\"","\"I’ve heard. Word is that it’s the Five Poison Sect... Do the superiors mean the Mountain Race took it...?\"","\"I didn’t say anything. Just go do what you need to do.\"","Fang Hongxiu understood perfectly. If it was the Mountain Race, it would indeed be difficult for the Imprisonment Department to continue the investigation. Even if that entire million stones of grain went into Wumeng Mountain, the Government Office could only turn a blind eye. After all, when the people of the Mountain Race plundered the grain, they did not forget to lend a hand to rescue the refugees, resolving the crisis for the Government Office.","Who would be so tired of living as to go to Wumeng Mountain to stir up trouble with the Mountain Race? Moreover, this matter was a messy account to begin with. The grain shops hoarded their grain, waiting for the highest bidder, which caused public resentment to brew. Having their grain stolen could be considered bringing trouble upon themselves. It wouldn’t be an exaggeration to say it was beautifully executed.","Fang Hongxiu’s Heart Spirit relaxed, and she led her people to hurry toward the Xiao family’s mansion.","\"The Xiao family has truly been plagued by bad luck recently.\"","\"The eldest daughter of the Xiao family just escaped danger and is still in shock, and now that live-in son-in-law has also met with an accident. As luck would have it, he contracted the plague.\"","\"You can say that again. Sigh...\"","After a meticulous screening of everyone inside and outside the Prefecture City, there were only about a hundred people who had contracted the plague. Aside from Yuan Hao, the rest were fed medicinal soup and strictly forbidden from going out.","Because Chen Yi had \"fallen ill,\" the entire Marquis’s Mansion was also implicated. Not only were Xiao Wuge and Xiaodie in the Spring Lotus Garden barred from leaving, but Xiao Wan’er and the others at the Jiaxing Garden who had been outside the city were also ordered to be grounded. The entire Marquis’s Mansion was in a state of extreme panic. Even though the Old Master repeatedly assured them that the plague could be cured, until Chen Yi fully recovered, everyone in the other courtyards turned pale at the mere mention of the Spring Lotus Garden.","Fortunately, the threshold of the Xiao family’s mansion was high enough. They didn’t need to have people from the Government Office standing guard outside every day like the others infected with the plague. They only needed to report on Chen Yi’s current condition every hour—whether his illness had improved or worsened, and whether anyone else in the mansion had been infected.","Therefore, for the past two days, Xiaodie became the busiest person. She had to serve Xiao Wuge, take care of Chen Yi, and frequently traverse the courtyards to pass along the situation here to the people outside the garden. She was thoroughly exhausted.","Seeing this, Xiao Wan’er felt a twinge of fond reproach in her heart. Naturally, she didn’t believe that Chen Yi would contract any plague. Even if the hundreds of people in the Marquis’s Mansion were all infected, Chen Yi wouldn’t be. On the contrary, he was highly likely to cure everyone before they could even get infected.","\"This bad guy is always doing things that catch people by ’surprise.’ Huatang saw it clearly when she grounded him back then...\" she thought.","Fortunately, Xiao Wan’er knew that Chen Yi must have his reasons for doing this, so she felt An Xin staying inside the Jiaxing Garden. While comforting Xie Tingyun, Shen Huatang, and the others, she kept an eye on the movements at the Spring Lotus Garden. As a result, the moment Xiaodie called out a few times, Xiao Wan’er couldn’t wait and immediately led her people to the Spring Lotus Garden.","Xiao Wuge, who had stepped out of another wooden building a step ahead, saw her and grinned happily. \"Wan’er, Chen Yi is awake. Can I leave the wooden building now too?\"","Xiao Wan’er gave a gentle murmur of agreement. Feigning joy, she took his hand and walked toward the wing room where Chen Yi was staying. When she pushed open the door to the wing room, she saw Chen Yi’s \"sickly\" appearance and immediately covered her mouth with a laugh. Her expression was a charming mix of joy and playfulness, and her laughter was ethereal.","Chen Yi leaned against the bed, turning his head to look at her. Knowing in his heart that she was aware he was faking his illness, he coughed and asked, \"Wan’er, why are you laughing?\"","Xiao Wan’er’s smile faltered. She gave him a reproachful eye roll, then walked over and sat down beside his bed."]},{"number":571,"title":"Chapter 571 - 325: Slaughter Them All","paragraphs":["\"Chen Yi, you’ve finally woken up. I’m happy for... my sister.\"","Xiao Wuge suspected nothing. THUMP THUMP THUMP! He came running over and threw himself onto the bed. \"Chen Yi, you’ve finally woken up! I was scared to death.\"","\"Scared to death? More like you cried from being scared, didn’t you?\"","\"N-no, I didn’t. It wasn’t me, it was Sister Xiaodie who cried. She even said you were dying.\"","Xiaodie let out a startled gasp and explained, her face flushed red, \"That day, I went to the study and saw Mr. Chen unconscious. I-I was just a little worried...\"","Chen Yi, naturally aware of all this, waved his hand and said, \"It’s alright now.\" Then, he gave Xiao Wan’er a look.","Xiao Wan’er understood and sent the others away. She also asked Xiao Wuge to bring the news to Elder Master Xiao, before she finally traced a few words on his palm.","[What was the reason this time?]","Chen Yi glanced at Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang, who were guarding outside the door. He first smiled and thanked her, then opened her palm. His finger lightly traced a few times, leaving clear strokes.","[I resolved some matters and wanted to rest for a couple of days.]","[You... you could have just told me if you wanted to rest. Why fake an illness and make people worry?]","[It was a bit rushed...]","Perhaps because she had experienced this a few times, Xiao Wan’er cooperated with increasing proficiency. While they verbally discussed the situation in Prefecture City, they traced words on each other’s palms to share their secrets.","The gentle autumn afternoon sun shone down, casting a bright glow on the two of them. The \"sickly\" scholar and the delicate, breathtakingly beautiful woman complemented each other perfectly, creating quite the picturesque scene.","Listening to the soft murmurs inside, Xie Tingyun didn’t notice anything unusual, so she began conversing silently with Shen Huatang. Her lips parted and closed several times to form a question: \"Junior Sister, do you think it’s necessary for us to stand guard outside for something like this?\" Unfortunately, she wasn’t well-read enough to quote an idiom about a guilty conscience protesting too much, so she could only ask bluntly.","Shen Huatang stood quietly by the door. She glanced at her, then turned her head to look at the room behind them, replying silently, \"Eldest Miss and Mr. Chen are not what you think.\"","\"Why wouldn’t they be? Earlier, they...\"","\"If they were, you and I would be the first to suffer.\"","Xie Tingyun fell into deep thought after understanding her words. Stroking the Long Sword at her waist, she silently mouthed, \"Junior Sister, if we tell General Jinghong about this, could we redeem ourselves?\"","Shen Huatang glared at her with a hint of exasperation. \"Shut up!\"","Xie Tingyun closed her mouth resentfully. \"It was just a joke. Why take it so seriously?\"","Amidst her grumbling, her curiosity continued to grow. At the same time, she harbored a doubt. If Eldest Miss and Mr. Chen really were having an affair, what would Second Miss do? She’d probably do exactly what her junior sister said—slaughter them both...","Naturally, Chen Yi didn’t see the silent banter between the two martial sisters outside the door. Through their casual chat, he learned about the situation in Prefecture City from Xiao Wan’er. His expression remained unchanged, but inwardly, he frowned.","Liu Hong’s reaction was all wrong! Logically speaking, with Yan Jingchen and the members of the Five Poison Sect missing, Liu Hong should be pacing like a cat on a hot tin roof right now. But according to Xiao Wan’er, not only was Liu Hong acting completely unfazed, he had also handled several matters in Shu State beautifully—disaster relief, epidemic prevention, placating the commoners, and so on. In just two days, the situation in Shu State had undergone an earth-shattering transformation. It was as if nothing had ever happened.","Elder Master Xiao’s response was equally strange. He had holed up in the estate, never stepping foot outside. He hadn’t directly seized Liu Hong and executed him before reporting it, as Chen Yi had hoped. It truly left him somewhat puzzled. Could an unexpected variable have come into play?","Xiao Wan’er didn’t understand all this. Seeing his silence, she took his hand and wrote a few words to ask:","[Is anything wrong?]","She couldn’t involve herself too deeply in these affairs, but she still hoped to offer whatever meager assistance she could.","Chen Yi shook his head slightly. Holding her hand, he considered his wording, their palms unconsciously rubbing together. Xiao Wan’er’s pretty face grew increasingly flushed. She endured it for a moment, but seeing him continue like this, she couldn’t help but lightly swat him. Snapping out of his daze, Chen Yi smiled under her reproachful gaze.","[It seems everything has been resolved.]","Chen Yi pondered carefully and formed a few speculations. Elder Master Xiao should have already made a move and was simply waiting for conclusive news. And Liu Hong’s reaction seemed very much like he had resigned himself to his fate. He didn’t know if the White Tiger Guard had taken action, or if...","Pushing these thoughts aside and planning to ask someone about it later, Chen Yi smiled and said, \"Is there any news from Madam?\"","Xiao Wan’er pulled her hand back and lowered her head slightly. \"There’s no news from my sister yet.\"","Seeing her demeanor, Chen Yi guessed what she was thinking and took her hand back without leaving room for argument. Xiao Wan’er struggled slightly but failed to pull free, so she let him hold it, though her expression inevitably became somewhat complicated.","However, upon seeing the next few words Chen Yi traced on her palm, her expression instantly morphed into anxious embarrassment. Letting out a startled gasp, she reached out and pinched him a few times, which made Chen Yi burst into laughter with a mischievous wink. Her face completely flushed, Xiao Wan’er glared at him reproachfully and mouthed wordlessly, \"That phrase... you are not allowed to say it again. Never again.\"","Chen Yi nodded, entirely amenable, his eyes still fixed on her face. Xiao Wan’er couldn’t resist gently swatting him again. \"Y-you get some rest. I’ll head back to Jiaxing Garden.\" With that, she hurriedly stood up and walked out, not even waiting for Chen Yi to reply.","Chen Yi chuckled in spite of himself. He figured he could be quite wicked at times, always coming up with devious little tricks to coax a smile out of people. But in truth, he hadn’t said anything inappropriate just now. Just one single line.","Jade Steps and Jade Trees—someone like you is rare in this world.","Another two days passed.","After confirming that the epidemic hadn’t spread and that all infected individuals had fully recovered, the Government Office posted a public notice."]},{"number":572,"title":"Chapter 572 - 325: Kill Them All","paragraphs":["The commoners in the Prefecture City had all returned to their daily lives. However, because grain prices had stabilized, those who had hoarded grain earlier were filled with regret, while those who hadn’t were naturally somewhat smug. They completely forgot the miserable state they were in just a few days ago.","Some rejoiced while others worried. Chen Yi was naturally among those who rejoiced. Over the past two days, Wang Ji had visited once, bringing him quite a bit of news. He had confirmed that Liu Hong seemed to have accepted his fate; it was said his hair had turned white overnight.","\"Liu Zhaoxue has disappeared, the Five Poison Sect in Xinglin Hall has been purged, and Liu Hong’s eldest and second sons are also nowhere to be found.","\"Coupled with that old fox’s recent behavior, everything points to a massive upheaval on his end.\"","Although Chen Yi didn’t know who was responsible, given his understanding of Liu Hong, the truth behind this matter was definitely not simple. Think about it: how could someone so deeply calculating do absolutely nothing in the face of his current predicament? When things were this abnormal, something was definitely amiss.","Thinking about this, Chen Yi remained completely unbothered, sitting by the pond and holding his newly bought fishing rod to fish. There was nothing he could do. Thanks to that \"plague poison,\" he had been ordered by the Old Master to rest peacefully at home.","Chen Yi was more than happy to enjoy the leisure. Especially since Xiao Wuge was Cultivating Martial Arts in the Martial Arts Arena, no one was beside him catching fish every now and then to ruin his peace.","However, these good days came to an abrupt halt with the arrival of Li Huai’gu.","\"Brother Qingzhou.\"","\"Brother Huai’gu.\"","After exchanging a few pleasantries, Chen Yi saw Li Huai’gu’s haggard expression and couldn’t help but ask with a smile, \"Brother Huai’gu, you made a special trip here despite your busy schedule. Is there something important?\"","Li Huai’gu smiled bitterly and cupped his hands. \"I can’t hide anything from you, Brother Qingzhou.\" He sighed and said, \"I don’t know what happened, but Lord Liu has barely been involved in the affairs of the Government Office over the past two days.","\"Lord Yang went to ask him a few times but couldn’t get a clear answer.","\"But the Governor’s Office has a lot of matters to handle, and someone eventually has to do the work.\"","Li Huai’gu rambled on for a while before finally explaining his purpose for coming. \"I wonder if Brother Qingzhou has been in contact with Brother Yunfan lately?\"","Chen Yi paused slightly. \"My brother?\"","Li Huai’gu nodded helplessly. \"Brother Yunfan hasn’t come to duty at the Government Office for several days.","\"I went to Tingyu Pavilion to ask, and they said Brother Yunfan has fallen ill and closed his doors to all visitors.","\"I figured that since Brother Qingzhou and Brother Yunfan have a deep relationship...\"","Chen Yi understood. After a brief thought, he roughly had some guesses. Chen Yunfan had obtained the evidence of Commander-in-Chief Zhu Hao’s crimes. Not showing his face at this time likely meant he was no longer in the Prefecture City. However, Chen Yi also didn’t know where Chen Yunfan would go, nor what method he would use to bring down Zhu Hao.","Thinking this, Chen Yi shook his head and said, \"I don’t know either. But I’ll send someone over to ask. Brother Huai’gu, you just need to wait for my news.\"","Li Huai’gu cupped his hands in thanks and hurried away without staying any longer.","Watching him leave, Chen Yi lost the mood to continue fishing, so he called Xiaodie over to brew a pot of tea. As he drank, he looked up at the clouds in the sky, inevitably falling into a daze. The White Tiger Guard also had schemes regarding Chen Yunfan... Judging from the current situation, Chen Yunfan was valued by the White Tiger Guard even more than he, the \"Fledgling,\" was.","\"All along, I seem to have overlooked something,\" he thought.","\"Chen Yunfan isn’t just an Assistant Governor to the Governor of Shu State; he is also the eldest young master of the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family.","\"If he was chosen by the White Tiger Guard... would the Chen Family just sit idly by?\"","Chen Yi didn’t think the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family would treat Chen Yunfan the same way they treated him. Especially considering the status and positions of Chen Xuanji and Chen Xuandu in the Imperial Court. Thinking deeper, could his status as the \"Fledgling\" also have been tacitly approved by the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family?","\"The White Tiger Guard, the Chen Family... the Imperial Court... me, Chen Yunfan...\" he pondered.","The chessboard in Chen Yi’s mind shifted, silent and unnoticed, making him feel like an Immortal seated in the heavens, looking down upon the Nine State and Three Prefectures of the Great Wei Dynasty.","\"If the Chen Family tacitly approved, I’m afraid the original host’s marriage into the Xiao Family... might have hidden motives behind it...\"","Thinking up to this point, in the right corner of the chessboard, on the intersecting lines representing Jiangnan Prefecture, a few Heizi quietly emerged. A few names faintly appeared: Chen Xuanji, Chen Xuandu, Cui Yu, Lin Zhong...","Chen Yi’s gaze shifted northward toward Guangyuan County, as if crossing thousands of miles to see where the Capital Commandery was located.","\"It seems it’s necessary to interact more with my brother,\" he mused."]},{"number":573,"title":"Chapter 573 - 326: Even Closer Than a Biological Father","paragraphs":["Compared to the tranquil brightness and cool breezes of Spring Lotus Garden, Tingyu Pavilion appeared much more elegant and quiet. The late autumn air was crisp. Fallen leaves and petals were scattered across the flagstone path, while various flowers still bloomed vibrantly on either side, vying for attention.","Chen Yunfan wore a pure white long gown with a loose sash. His hair was untied, cascading down his back as he slowly practiced his sword forms. Amidst the graceful movements, a faint but sharp killing intent lingered. He was, of course, unaware that Chen Yi was plotting to get closer to him. He only knew that a massive upheaval was about to strike Shu State. Because of this, he had closed his doors to visitors, planning to head out later to avoid drawing attention to his actions.","He had already presented Lv Jiunan’s corpse, along with the evidence of Shu State Vice Commander-in-Chief Zhu Hao’s crimes, to the Shu State Inspector General, Tang Zixing. First, he didn’t trust the Governor’s Office or the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office. Second, sending the items directly to the Capital Prefecture would make it difficult to explain his source of information. After mulling it over, Tang Zixing became his best option.","By using the Inspectorate Office to deliver the suspect and the evidence to the Capital Prefecture, he would avoid becoming a target of public criticism, no matter how the Holy Emperor investigated and ruled afterward. Although the Inspectorate Office would take the lion’s share of the credit, Chen Yunfan deduced that his own portion wouldn’t be small either. He refused to believe that the White Tiger Guard, having handed him such a massive gift, would let a mere Inspectorate Office derail their entire scheme. If his deduction was wrong, all the better; he would simply continue working at the Governor’s Office. With a restless colleague like Li Huai’gu around, he could still enjoy a leisurely life.","\"Born to high gates and red doors against my will, I wander the world with a sword, a flute, and a jug of wine.\"","Lin Zhong grinned in amusement. The Young Master’s Sword Dao was on the verge of reaching the Perfection Realm, yet his poetry remained as stagnant as ever. However, Lin Zhong had a rough idea of what was on Chen Yunfan’s mind and didn’t dare provoke him right now. After all, it was only natural for a Young Master of the Noble Families to throw a bit of a temper tantrum upon discovering that everything he possessed had been prearranged by others. Lin Zhong could only hope that Chen Yunfan would eventually figure things out for himself and use the likes of Lv Jiunan and Zhu Hao as stepping stones to soar to the heavens.","Beside them, Chun Ying stood perfectly straight. The tray in her hands held a teacup, a sweat towel, and various pastries. Since that day, she had become extremely careful—not out of fear, but by strictly adhering to her proper place. She suddenly realized that despite serving by Chen Yunfan’s side for years, she had never truly understood the Eldest Young Master of the Chen Family. She had originally thought he simply disliked the constraints of rules, acted unconventionally, and was inherently callous. Now, she recognized that was merely a facade. Beneath that exterior was a deeply passionate and authentic man who could be driven by his emotions. He had hidden this so well that even Chun Ying, a White-robed Minister herself, had misjudged him. As a result, she was forced to change her strategy, lest she face the only other outcome: being banished back to the White-robed Minister organization. Fortunately, there was still room to maneuver, and she had plenty of time.","Not long after.","Chen Yunfan sheathed his long sword and walked straight toward his room. Passing by Chun Ying, he didn’t even spare her a glance, though he did pick up the towel to wipe his face. Only after taking a few steps did he speak with his back to them, \"Chun Ying, go boil some hot water and help me change.\"","Chun Ying replied affirmatively and silently followed behind him.","Lin Zhong watched the two walk away, rubbing the stubble on his chin thoughtfully.","\"The Young Master’s temperament really seems to have changed. Sigh, I hope the Master’s decision was right...\"","Inside the room.","Chen Yunfan sat bare-chested in the wooden bathtub, his eyes closed as he let Chun Ying pour in the scalding hot water. Bucket after bucket was poured until the water level rose past his chest. Chun Ying then scattered some flower petals over the surface before wiping the sweat from her nose and forehead. \"Young Master, it’s ready,\" she said softly.","Chen Yunfan grunted an acknowledgment, his eyes still closed.","Chun Ying was just about to leave when she heard him ask, \"Is there a reply from my father yet?\"","Chun Ying replied with a slight hesitation, \"Not yet.","\"Rest assured, Young Master, the White-robed Minister wouldn’t dare neglect your orders.\"","\"It better be.\"","Chen Yunfan opened his eyes and glanced at her, asking in a flat tone, \"What about the Inspectorate Office?\"","Chun Ying lowered her eyes submissively and said, \"Ning Yu is still keeping watch there. The moment there’s news, he’ll come report it immediately.","\"However, judging by the time, there should be news from the Capital Prefecture soon.\"","Chen Yunfan withdrew his gaze. Staring at the scenery outside the window, his expression remained placid. \"The sooner there’s a result, the sooner I can go to the Government Office.\"","Hearing this, Chun Ying bit her lip, not daring to offer advice like she used to. Chen Yunfan guessed what was on her mind but offered no comfort. Until he figured out the overarching schemes of the White-robed Minister, his father, and the White Tiger Guard, he couldn’t relax for a single day. The same went for Chen Yi.","Over the past few days, Chen Yunfan would occasionally recall what he had seen and heard since arriving in Shu State, which helped him understand why Chen Yi was hiding his identity and operating in the shadows. With the White Tiger Guard watching from the dark, and the high-ranking officials of the Shu State Government Office and the Noble Families and Clans stirring up trouble in the open, he would have acted just as cautiously if he were the one who had married into the Xiao Family.","However, understanding was one thing; Chen Yunfan still felt a bit resentful.","This was because, if he asked himself honestly, had he truly been in Chen Yi’s position, he might not... or rather, he definitely wouldn’t have handled things as well as Chen Yi did. This was especially true regarding the events of the past few days in Shu State—the plague and the food crisis. Either issue alone would have him racking his brains in frustration.","Asking him to treat plague victims? What a joke. It would be a miracle if he didn’t get infected himself. Asking him to stabilize grain prices? That wouldn’t work either. Aside from seeking out Liu Hong or asking the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family and Cui Qingwu for help, he would be virtually out of options.","\"Human capability has its limits. It’s much more satisfying to just kill with a single sword thrust...\""]},{"number":574,"title":"Chapter 574 - 326: Closer Than a Biological Father","paragraphs":["His hands were tied.","As the Assistant Governor of the Governor’s Office, Chen Yunfan was bound by strict rules and regulations. A single misstep could trigger a chain reaction, unlike Chen Yi, who could simply wash his hands of the matter. Even though he knew Zhu Hao was colluding with the enemy and committing treason, he still had to act within the rules. He couldn’t just run off to Guangyuan County and slaughter Zhu Hao.","After a moment of silence, Chen Yunfan stood up and gestured. Chun Ying understood immediately. She dried his body, served him as he changed into a clean brocade robe, and fastened his belt. As Chen Yunfan let her attend to him, he looked into the Copper Mirror and asked, \"How many times has Li Huai’gu been here?\"","\"To answer you, Young Master, Advisor Li has been here four times over the past two days,\" she replied.","\"Four times? It seems there is quite a lot of official business at the Governor’s Office.\"","Hearing this, Chun Ying paused. She shot a quick glance at him and gathered her courage to say, \"Young Master, there have been significant changes within the office.\"","Chen Yunfan cast a sidelong glance at her, staring until she lowered her head again, before he snorted. \"I thought you, the White-robed Minister, were planning to go back.\"","\"This servant... wouldn’t dare.\"","\"I hope you truly wouldn’t dare.\" Chen Yunfan straightened his brocade robe and walked out. \"Tell me, what changes happened at the Government Office?\" he asked as he walked.","\"Liu Hong seems to have run into trouble.\"","\"Oh?\"","Seeing that he was interested, Chun Ying quickly continued, \"Rumor has it that his hair turned white overnight. He looks several times older than before, as if his very spirit and energy have been drained out of him.","\"And...\"","After hearing about what had transpired within the Government Office, Chen Yunfan furrowed his brows. \"He ran into trouble? The Jing State Liu Family is still standing, and Consort Liu is still around. How could he possibly run into trouble?\"","Chun Ying nodded in agreement. \"You are right, Young Master. There is indeed something wrong with Liu Hong, but as the Governor of Shu State, he holds a Second Grade rank. Ordinary charges brought against him would have almost no impact. Just like when Liu Wen used the Bright Moon Building to burn the summer grain in the Three Towns. After the conflict between the Liu Family and the Xiao Family, the Holy Emperor merely gave both sides a slap on the wrist.\"","\"Your people haven’t sent back any news?\"","\"Not yet...\"","Chen Yunfan gave a slight nod and stepped outside to stretch his body. \"Since Liu Hong ignores political affairs, Lord Yang is left to handle the heavy workload within the Governor’s Office. No wonder Li Huai’gu has visited so many times.\"","It was obvious that Li Huai’gu wanted him to return to work at the Government Office. Chen Yunfan muttered a few words under his breath about how lucky he was.","Just as he was about to ask Chun Ying to brew some tea in the pavilion, he heard Niu Mountain’s voice from outside the door.","\"Young Master, someone is here to visit...\"","Without even thinking, Chen Yunfan interrupted, \"I won’t see them.\"","Niu Mountain finished his sentence anyway, \"...Miss Cui.\"","Chen Yunfan froze and glared at him in silence.","Chun Ying and Lin Zhong silently lowered their heads, though the corners of their mouths curled up slightly.","Niu Mountain scratched his head, finally realizing what had happened, and gave a foolish smile. \"Forgive me, Young Master. I spoke too slowly.\"","Chen Yunfan rolled his eyes, too lazy to bicker with the blockhead. He simply waved his hand. \"Go ask Qingwu.\"","Niu Mountain gave a prompt sound of acknowledgment and trotted off, his footsteps THUMPING against the ground.","A short while later, he ran back from the rear courtyard to the front yard, THUDDING along the way, leading a middle-aged man in blue clothes.","Chen Yunfan sized up the newcomer and raised an eyebrow. He wondered, \"Why would he come to Shu State?\"","Lin Zhong and Chun Ying also recognized the man. They exchanged a glance, both feeling somewhat surprised.","Song Jinjian was one of the resident retainers and Tributors of the Qinghe Cui Family. He was once a famous Swordsman in Jiangnan Prefecture, known for upholding justice and possessing excellent character. At the age of twenty-one, he had broken through to the Third Grade Realm after wiping out a band of Wokou in Taizhou County. Jianghu People believed he would soon possess the strength to challenge figures like the \"Monarch Xue Jian\" Lone Immortal Ye. However, contrary to expectations, he chose to retire at the height of his career and became a Tributor for the Cui Family.","As the group observed him, Song Jinjian naturally noticed them as well and bowed from a distance. \"I greet Young Master Chen and Commander Lin.\"","Chen Yunfan pursed his lips and waved his hand, gesturing for him to head toward the rear courtyard.","Song Jinjian clasped his fists and followed Niu Mountain straight to the back.","Watching his retreating figure, Chen Yunfan secretly guessed the purpose of his visit. After much thought, he could only surmise that Song Jinjian was here to pass on a message for the Cui Family. Was it to ask Cui Qingwu to return to the family, or...","Feeling slightly displeased, Chen Yunfan flicked his sleeves, turned around, and walked back to his side room, losing the leisurely mood to drink tea.","Chun Ying nudged Lin Zhong before following behind Chen Yunfan. Lin Zhong understood the unspoken cue. He remained where he was, gazing toward the rear courtyard, and cocked his ear to listen.","It didn’t take long before the sound of Song Jinjian and Cui Qingwu’s conversation drifted over.","\"Uncle Song, what brings you here?\"","\"Eldest Miss, the Lord asked me to inquire when you will be returning to Qinghe.\"","\"My father?\"","\"Before the end of the year, perhaps...\"","Lin Zhong couldn’t catch the rest of the conversation clearly, but he knew that Cui Qingwu’s return to the Qinghe Cui Family was not far off. He retracted his gaze, looked at Chen Yunfan in the side room, and sighed as he shook his head. \"The marriage alliance between the Chen Family and the Cui Family was single-handedly arranged by the Master and Madam. The Young Master is probably...\"","Going to accept his fate?","Perhaps.","Just as Lin Zhong was about to go report this, his ears twitched, and he immediately looked toward the front yard.","Ning Yu arrived in a hurry. \"Where is the Young Master?\"","Lin Zhong pointed behind him. \"Inside.\"","Ning Yu muttered an apology and hurriedly ran into the side room. He was just about to report when Chun Ying, acting quickly, made a hand gesture to warn him that walls have ears.","Ning Yu understood. He went to the study, fetched some paper and a brush, and wrote down a few words.","[The Holy Emperor’s decree has arrived at Guangyuan County. Zhu Hao defied the decree and attempted to flee. He was beheaded with a single sword strike by Xiao Jinghong.]","After reading the message, Chen Yunfan froze for a moment. \"Xiao... hmm... She’s in Guangyuan? When did she go there?\"","Ning Yu shook his head to indicate he didn’t know.","Chun Ying pondered for a moment and wrote a few words on the paper. \"It was likely after the chaos in the Xiao Family a few days ago. At that time, ’Dragon Tiger’ Liu Wu killed ’Jackal’ Du Cang, which might have made the Xiao Family aware of Zhu Hao’s transaction with the Peacock King Banner.\"","Chen Yunfan nodded in sudden realization. That made sense.","The evidence of Zhu Hao’s crimes in his possession was ostensibly an arrangement given to him by the White Tiger Guard. However, the person who delivered the letter was Chen Yi. Given his understanding of Chen Yi, if his brother had caught wind of the news, how could he not have tipped off the Xiao Family? In that case, Xiao Jinghong’s appearance in Guangyuan made perfect sense.","Having figured everything out, a smile emerged on Chen Yunfan’s face. \"This is getting interesting.\"","One piece of merit split three ways. He truly wanted to see what the White Tiger Guard’s reaction would be upon hearing the news. If they still managed to arrange an official position for him as a Deputy Commander out of this, then he would just have to accept it.","\"Damn it. If that actually happens, the Emperor is either senile or a fool,\" he muttered to himself. \"Treating me better than my own father? In their dreams.\"","Chen Yunfan murmured under his breath, looking in the direction of Guangyuan County with a smile occasionally creeping onto his face. His sister-in-law showing up there was truly an unexpected delight.","***","Although Guangyuan was technically a county seat, the city was not small by any means. Located at the junction of Shu State, Jing State, and You State, it was the strategic chokepoint of Shu State and saw a massive influx of traveling merchants. Consequently, many people settled down here to make a living.","The Cao Gang, the Horse Gang, the Salt Gang, and Wandering Martial Artists from all walks of life converged here, making the local situation incredibly complex. Often, even the local Noble Families with long-standing heritages would find themselves bogged down, tiptoeing around their own affairs for fear of offending one faction or another.","However, none of this mattered in Xiao Jinghong’s eyes.","To her, they were nothing more than an unpresentable motley crew. The gap between them and the Wind and Rain Tower was as vast as heaven and earth, let alone comparing them to the Dingyuan Army.","Yet, while she could afford to ignore those extraneous individuals, she could not ignore the Shu State Capital Commandery. This was especially true after she had personally killed Zhu Hao. Even though the Holy Emperor had issued a decree to apprehend Zhu Hao, it was still highly inappropriate for her to have executed him outright.","But since the deed was done, Xiao Jinghong maintained her composure, waiting quietly in the Capital Commandery for news from the Capital Prefecture.","Beside her stood Xiao Xuanshuo, who had accompanied the imperial decree’s delegation. Although he was dissatisfied with many members of the Xiao Family, he genuinely approved of his niece, Xiao Jinghong, from the bottom of his heart. As a result, he was currently recounting the events from the Prefecture City with a smile.","\"...When I headed to the Capital Prefecture, my father had already ordered someone to notify the Government Office to deal with the plague poison, so there shouldn’t be any major issues.\"","Xiao Jinghong gave a slight nod. \"You just said the news came from that Liu Wu?\" she mused. \"He returned to Shu State?\"","Xiao Xuanshuo hummed in affirmation. \"I heard that before the plague poison could spread, he noticed it and produced a prescription to cure it after making a diagnosis. If it weren’t for him, the Prefecture City would likely be in absolute chaos by now.\"","Xiao Jinghong gazed thoughtfully toward the Prefecture City. \"What a coincidence.\"","When she was in the Prefecture City, Liu Wu was nowhere to be found. Only a few days after she left the city, not only had Liu Wu returned, but he had also stepped in to resolve a massive crisis.","After some thought, Xiao Jinghong dismissed her suspicions and chalked it up to coincidence. After all, other than sharing a similar moniker, she and Liu Wu had never interacted before. She couldn’t think of any reason why Liu Wu would deliberately avoid her.","\"Aside from the decree regarding Zhu Hao, did the Holy Emperor issue any others this time?\" she asked.","Xiao Xuanshuo smiled and nodded. \"I can’t hide anything from you. The Holy Emperor has also issued a decree to punish Liu Hong...\""]},{"number":575,"title":"Chapter 575 - 327: A First Grade Official!","paragraphs":["It was to be expected that Liu Hong would be punished.","Xiao Jinghong was not surprised by this outcome. What surprised her was that the Holy Emperor had issued a decree of punishment based solely on a single memorial from her grandfather. It seemed far too direct.","According to the laws of the Imperial Court, convicting a Second-Grade Officer required an investigation by an imperial envoy, a trial by the Nine Ministers, and a final ruling by the Holy Emperor. None of these steps could be skipped. Furthermore, Liu Hong had committed the severe crime of treason and colluding with the enemy. At the very least, they needed to figure out who his accomplices were and whether he had any remaining factions.","Take Zhu Hao, for example. He had illegally sold ironware to Poshisu Country through the Ji State Trading Company. The evidence was clear, and his crimes warranted death, which meant the people of the Ji State Trading Company also had to be arrested and brought to justice. The same logic applied here.","Liu Hong had been in Shu State for many years, and his power was deeply entrenched. Every family and faction he had contacted needed to be investigated to prevent anyone from slipping through the cracks.","As Xiao Jinghong thought about this, the look in her eyes softened slightly.","Liu Hong’s conviction was a good thing for both the Xiao Family and Shu State. As for the members of other Noble Families, without Liu Hong shielding them on the front lines, the Xiao Family’s influence would eventually uproot them one by one. Moreover, with Zhu Hao brought to justice, life would be much easier for the Xiao Family and the Dingyuan Army in the future.","After a moment of silence, Xiao Xuanshuo smiled and said, \"From what Eunuch Feng implied, the Holy Emperor flew into a rage during the court assembly the day before yesterday.","\"Even Celestial Minister Cui Mao was reprimanded for poor supervision and failing to promptly discover the circumstances of the Foreign Officials.","\"He brought up issues like embezzling public funds, collusion between officials and merchants, dereliction of duty, and treason. His words were harsh, leaving the Courtiers on pins and needles.\"","\"And then?\" Xiao Jinghong asked.","Seeing her interest, Xiao Xuanshuo lowered his voice and continued, \"Using the cases of Liu Hong and Zhu Hao as a pretext, the Holy Emperor seems intent on initiating a series of reforms.","\"He plans to tighten the control over Salt Tokens, while also bringing tea and porcelain under state monopoly. Furthermore, he wants to audit agricultural estates...\"","Hearing this, the look in Xiao Jinghong’s eyes shifted slightly beneath her partial armor.","The trade of salt and iron was a crucial source of silver coins for the border Commandant’s Office, especially the Salt Tokens. Salt Merchants would hand over grain to the Capital Commandery in exchange for an equivalent amount of Salt Tokens. They would then use the tokens to withdraw salt and sell it in designated areas.","The rules and regulations were strict. Even so, the salt trade was an incredibly profitable business, yielding margins several times higher than grain or medicinal herbs. Naturally, this bred a great deal of corruption.","Even without conducting an investigation, Xiao Jinghong knew that Zhu Hao and his associates extorted no less than a hundred thousand silver coins from the Salt Merchants every year.","If tea and porcelain were added to the monopoly, the national treasury and imperial coffers would indeed see a significant increase in silver, but it would also breed even more corrupt individuals.","And then there was the auditing of agricultural estates...","Across the Great Wei Nine State and Three Prefectures, there were countless Noble Families and Clans. Which family could claim they had never concealed their land holdings?","Even in Tonglin Town, the Xiao Family’s fief, people reclaimed wastelands for farming every year. The total agricultural land had increased by an unknown, massive amount compared to two hundred years ago. If all of this was accurately calculated, the grain tax the Xiao Family would have to pay each year would be no small sum.","Of course, since the Xiao Family was farming within their own fief, having extra land wouldn’t result in punishment. However, the amount of land swallowed up by some Noble Families was simply too egregious. It wasn’t just single households being absorbed; entire villages were being annexed, and such occurrences were all too common.","\"I assume there is a lot of opposition?\"","\"You are absolutely right, Niece Jinghong. As soon as the topic was broached, many ministers immediately jumped out in opposition.\" Xiao Xuanshuo said with a sneer, \"They are terrified that the Holy Emperor will uncover their own family’s hidden estates, threatening their generational inheritance.","\"However, the Holy Emperor didn’t fly into a rage over this. Instead, he simply said he would consider it. Those Courtiers had wanted to continue arguing to dissuade him, but they were interrupted by another matter.\"","At this point, Xiao Xuanshuo’s expression turned serious. \"Chen Xuanji has returned.\"","Hearing the name, Xiao Jinghong paused slightly, searching her memory. \"My husband’s father? The current Patriarch of the Chen Family who was sent as an envoy to the Buddha Country?\"","Xiao Xuanshuo nodded. \"That’s him.","\"He returned to the Capital Prefecture right in the middle of the court assembly. The Holy Emperor actually paused the assembly and personally led officials to welcome him. It shows just how deeply he values him.","\"But that wasn’t all. After receiving Chen Xuanji, the Holy Emperor brought him straight into the ongoing assembly. After asking a few questions, he immediately issued a decree to reward him.\"","Xiao Xuanshuo looked at Xiao Jinghong and said in a deep voice, \"Chen Xuanji was promoted to the First Grade. He has been appointed as one of the Nine Ministers—the Minister of War.\"","\"Minister of War?\"","This time, Xiao Jinghong was truly taken aback.","Before being dispatched to the Western Continent Buddha Country, Chen Xuanji was the Governor of Jiangnan Prefecture. His qualifications and talents were indeed sufficient for a promotion to the Nine Ministers. What surprised her, however, was that he was made the Minister of War—a position that oversaw the promotions of all military officers and the distribution of military armaments throughout the world.","\"Then... what about Lord Luo?\"","Knowing she was referring to the former Minister of War, Luo Yong, Xiao Xuanshuo shook his head slightly. \"He retired and returned to his hometown.\"","\"By the Holy Emperor’s intention?\"","\"It was likely a mutual decision discussed between him and the Holy Emperor prior to that day, but the announcement was delayed until Chen Xuanji’s return to the Imperial Court.\"","Xiao Jinghong nodded in understanding. That made sense.","After a moment of thought, she added, \"If I recall correctly, Chen Xuandu is currently the Right Minister of the Governor’s Office in the Northern State?\"","\"Indeed. The Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family is truly illustrious, currently basking in the Holy Emperor’s profound favor.\"","Xiao Xuanshuo couldn’t help but think of their own family. Compared to the Chen Family, the difference was like night and day.","Chen Xuanji was now one of the Nine Ministers, Chen Xuandu held a Second Grade post managing a state’s administration, and the Chen Family’s eldest son, Chen Yunfan, currently served as the Assistant Governor of the Shu State Governor’s Office...","At this thought, Xiao Xuanshuo’s expression grew a bit solemn. With a hint of hesitation, he said, \"Niece Jinghong, there is something I’m not sure if I should say...\"","Xiao Jinghong glanced at him. She could roughly guess what he was going to say, so she simply shook her head and replied in an even tone, \"Let’s talk about it after we get back.\"","Seeing her response, Xiao Xuanshuo sighed inwardly and said no more.","The Chen Family was illustrious now, while the Xiao Family was in decline. Even though Chen Yi was currently just a live-in son-in-law of the Xiao Family, there was no guarantee that the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family wouldn’t use some underhanded means to influence the Xiao Family through him."]},{"number":576,"title":"Chapter 576 - 327: First Grade Official!","paragraphs":["Just then, footsteps sounded from outside the hall.","Xiao Xuanshuo sat upright and attentive, while Xiao Jinghong turned her head to look.","It was Li Fu, the Governor of Shu State. His appearance was ordinary, not particularly outstanding, and his posture was not considered tall or straight. But wearing his crimson Official Robe, complete with an Official Hat and Jade Belt, he carried a certain imposing aura as he strode in.","Li Fu entered the hall and took the seat of honor. Xiao Xuanshuo cupped his hands in greeting, but Xiao Jinghong remained seated, unmoving.","Li Fu waved his hand, signaling Xiao Xuanshuo to dispense with the formalities. His gaze fell on Xiao Jinghong, and he shook his head with a smile. \"General Xiao, you have truly put Mr. Li in a difficult position this time.\"","Xiao Jinghong remained unmoved. \"What difficulties does the Commander face?\" she asked calmly.","\"Zhu Hao defied the imperial decree and attempted to assassinate the envoy to flee Shu State. If I hadn’t intervened, your troubles would be even greater.\"","Li Fu’s smile remained unchanged. \"Troublesome as it may be, there was still a chance to have Zhu Hao confess the truth and give up his accomplices. Now that he’s dead, neither Eunuch Feng nor I can easily report back to the Holy Emperor.\"","\"That is between you and Eunuch Feng. It has nothing to do with me.\"","\"...General Xiao is as straightforward as ever.\"","Xiao Jinghong cast him a glance, her tone dropping a couple of degrees. \"Commander, there is no need to pin the blame on me and strike first. The man may be dead, but the matter remains. The delays in provisions and military equipment for the Dingyuan Army, as well as the grain tax issue—does the Capital Commandery not plan to give me an explanation?\"","Li Fu’s smile froze. \"General Xiao, you exaggerate. This matter...\"","\"Does the Commander want to claim ignorance?\"","\"...No.\"","Faced with Xiao Jinghong’s aggressiveness, Li Fu shook his head somewhat helplessly. \"Once we thoroughly investigate the actions of Zhu Hao and his accomplices, Mr. Li will certainly report to the Minister of War, Luo... Lord Chen,\" he said sternly. \"He will then report it to the Holy Emperor for a final decision.\"","Xiao Jinghong still felt dissatisfied. She spat out a few more words, \"Salt and iron operations.\"","Li Fu frowned slightly. \"What does General Xiao mean by this?\"","\"The Commander asks when he already knows the answer. Zhu Hao was in charge of the salt and iron revenues; how could he not have lined his own pockets?\"","\"So General Xiao intends to investigate this to the bitter end?\"","Upon hearing this, Xiao Jinghong looked straight at him. \"Does the Commander not intend to investigate it thoroughly?\" she asked, her eyes sharp.","Meeting her gaze, Li Fu’s expression flickered uncertainly, seemingly putting him in a difficult spot.","Xiao Xuanshuo sat perfectly still with his eyes downcast, but his ears caught every single word of their conversation. He couldn’t help but marvel at Xiao Jinghong’s words. Over the past five years, the Xiao Family and the Dingyuan Army had suffered countless overt and covert suppressions from the Capital Commandery. Now that Zhu Hao was dead, it was indeed time to settle some scores.","After a long time, Li Fu withdrew his gaze, picked up the teacup from the table, and took a sip. \"General Xiao has been in Shu State for many years and should be clear about the situation here, just like in Guangyuan...\" he said, carefully weighing his words.","Before he could finish, Xiao Jinghong interrupted, \"Forgive me, Commander, but I have spent most of my time in the army and know little about matters outside.\"","\"...\"","Hearing this, Li Fu set down his teacup and shook his head with a bitter smile. \"I promise you, not a single one of the silver coins embezzled by Zhu Hao and his accomplices will be missing.\" Seeing that Xiao Jinghong remained silent, he gritted his teeth slightly and continued, \"A portion of it will be allocated to the soldiers of the Three Towns. Is General Xiao satisfied?\"","Xiao Jinghong stared at him for a few breaths before looking away. \"Then we shall do as the Commander suggests,\" she said calmly.","She was not a stubborn person; achieving her goal was enough. Moreover, she was well aware of the complex and deeply rooted factions within Guangyuan County, where the Capital Commandery was located. Especially those Salt Merchants—who knew how many interests and people were tied up behind them. Unless absolutely necessary, Xiao Jinghong did not want to push things to the absolute extreme for now, lest it worsen the Xiao Family’s already dire situation.","Li Fu, however, grumbled inwardly, \"What do you mean, ’as the Commander suggests’? It was clearly your idea.\"","Though he thought this, he didn’t show a hint of it on his face. \"Then regarding the matter of Zhu Hao’s death...\"","\"Handle it according to the laws and regulations. I will bear the full responsibility.\"","Upon hearing this, Li Fu finally managed a smile. \"That is good. Then General Xiao, why not wait a moment today? Mr. Li has arranged a banquet in the city...\"","Unexpectedly, Xiao Jinghong stood up directly. \"There is no need. It’s rare for me to visit Guangyuan, and I need to pay a visit to the Fu Family. If Eunuch Feng is ready to depart, I trouble the Commander to send someone to the Fu Family to notify us.\"","\"Alright...\"","As Li Fu watched Xiao Jinghong and Xiao Xuanshuo walk away, the smile on his face slowly dissipated. After sitting quietly for a moment, he sighed, muttered something to himself about women being narrow-minded, then stood up and walked toward the outer wing room.","After straightening his clothes, he pushed open the door. \"Eunuch Feng.\"","Feng Erbao stood in the room, looking at a Painting on the wall. Beside him were several older eunuchs and two Guards in Armor. Hearing the sound, Feng Erbao turned around with a gentle smile. \"Commander Li, have you handled the matter with General Xiao?\"","Li Fu nodded. \"Just as you expected. General Xiao believes she is not at fault and refuses to bow her head.\"","Feng Erbao’s eyelids twitched, his smile stiffening slightly. After a moment, he waved his hand and laughed. \"No matter, no matter. General Xiao also meant well. If it weren’t for her stepping in to help, and that thief Zhu Hao had actually escaped, neither you nor I could bear the responsibility.\"","\"With you saying so, Mr. Li can rest easy.\"","\"You are too kind...\"","They chatted idly for a few sentences. Li Fu looked around. Seeing that Feng Erbao signaled for him to speak frankly, he asked, \"Could you speak plainly? How did the Holy Emperor... how did His Majesty trace this to Zhu Hao? Was it a memorial written by Xiao Xuanshuo... or the Xiao Family?\"","Feng Erbao cast him a sideways glance. \"What is Commander Li worried about?\"","\"I dare not hide it from you. As Commander, Mr. Li has been lax in disciplining his subordinates. To have alarmed the Holy Emperor makes me truly ashamed.\"","\"If that is all, Commander Li can put his mind at ease,\" Feng Erbao said. \"The Imperial Family is not showing favor to the Xiao Family. Someone else submitted a memorial to him.\"","\"Oh? May I ask who in Shu State it was?\"","\"The Inspector General, Tang Zixing, and... Chen Yunfan.\"","Li Fu suddenly realized. \"So it was Lord Tang. That explains it.\" He paused, then added, \"Chen Yunfan... The name sounds familiar...\"","Feng Erbao wore a half-smile. \"The eldest son of the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family.\"","Li Fu’s brows furrowed imperceptibly. \"The son of Minister of War, Lord Chen... Thank you for the guidance, Eunuch.\"","\"It’s hardly guidance. Even if I didn’t tell you, you would find out about this matter in a few days.\"","\"You are too polite...\"","***","As night approached, Xiao Jinghong and Xiao Xuanshuo left the Fu Family and headed toward the Capital Commandery. Along the way, Xiao Jinghong was somewhat silent. Xiao Xuanshuo’s mood was similar to hers; both found the current situation of the Fu Family difficult to accept.","Originally, due to Fu Wanqing, the Fu Family had an extremely close relationship with the Xiao Family and enjoyed boundless glory in Guangyuan County. However, after the news of Xiao Fengchun and Fu Wanqing dying in battle arrived, the Fu Family’s situation mirrored that of the Xiao Family, steadily declining. By now, the Fu Family was almost unable to sustain itself.","\"Jinghong, once we return, Second Uncle will go discuss this with Father. We will definitely figure out a way to look after the Fu Family.\"","Xiao Jinghong murmured an agreement and was about to speak when, out of the corner of her eye, she noticed a storefront at a nearby street intersection. Outside the newly opened shop, quite a few scholars were gathered, pointing and talking about the signboard above the door.","\"The three characters for Hundred Herbs Hall are written with vigorous and flowing strokes, elegant and unbridled. They are indeed more pleasing to the eye than Wei Qing’s Style.\"","\"This must be the ’Cursive Script’ spreading from the Prefecture City?\"","\"Seeing it in person is better than hearing about its fame. It truly has unique qualities.\"","\"Of course! Mr. Qingzhou’s Cursive Script has already reached the Perfection Realm. Even if this signboard is just a rubbing and doesn’t fully display his Calligraphy Dao realm, it’s still beyond what anyone else can compare to.\"","\"Rather than marveling at it here, we’d be better off finding some paper and brushes to trace it. Perhaps we could learn a fraction of Mr. Qingzhou’s mastery in Cursive Script.\"","\"You’re right...\"","Listening to their discussion, Xiao Jinghong’s gaze fell on the three characters for Hundred Herbs Hall. She naturally recognized Chen Yi’s handwriting, and the corners of her mouth couldn’t help but curve into a slight smile. Her husband was not in Guangyuan, yet there was news of him even here. This feeling... was quite fascinating.","After watching for a moment, Xiao Jinghong snapped back to her senses and thoughtfully studied the bustling Hundred Herbs Hall. \"Second Uncle, I remember Grandfather saying that the expansion of the Hundred Herbs Hall was a collaboration with our Xiao Family?\"","Xiao Xuanshuo nodded. \"Yes...\" He quickly realized her implication and asked in slight surprise, \"You mean...\"","Xiao Jinghong nodded slightly and pointed at the Hundred Herbs Hall. \"Let the Fu Family take charge of the Hundred Herbs Hall’s matters here in Guangyuan County.\"","The Xiao Family wasn’t short on the silver coins earned from one county like Guangyuan, but the Fu Family was. Rather than letting the other Noble Families here profit from it, choosing the Fu Family was much more suitable.","Catching on, Xiao Xuanshuo agreed. \"When we get back, I will go discuss it with your grandfather and Wan’er.\"","\"Yes. Eldest Sister is currently managing the estate’s account books, so we definitely should let her know.\"","Of course, Xiao Jinghong didn’t think Xiao Wan’er would refuse. Having said this, she looked at the characters for \"Hundred Herbs Hall\" once more, yearning to return home. \"Let’s go. It’s time to return to the Prefecture City...\""]},{"number":577,"title":"Chapter 577 - 328: Swordsman Chen Qingzhou","paragraphs":["Chen Yi naturally did not know Xiao Jinghong’s movements. But he knew that within two or three days, Xiao Jinghong would inevitably return.","The reason was simple. Liu Hong’s hair had turned white overnight, and he no longer involved himself in government affairs; he was already like a grasshopper in late autumn—he wouldn’t be jumping around for much longer. Zhu Hao’s situation was much the same. Furthermore, the Capital Prefecture was closer to Guangyuan County. If the Imperial Court sent people to Shu State, their first stop would definitely be Guangyuan. Once the dust settled in Guangyuan, Xiao Jinghong would return to Shu State to oversee the Xiao Family and prevent Liu Hong from launching a counterattack.","The only thing Chen Yi wasn’t sure about was who would get the credit for bringing down Zhu Hao.","\"I figure there’s a higher possibility that my elder brother Chen Yunfan will take the top credit.","\"After all, Madam is now the Commander-in-Chief of the Dingyuan Army. She can’t be promoted any further and will, at most, receive some dispensable rewards.\"","Chen Yi saw through it all clearly, so he An Xined and went about his own business.","During the day, he played chess, played the zither, painted, fished, and read books. At night, he cultivated the Four Symbols Skill and various Martial Arts Techniques. His gains were not small. Although the Four Symbols Skill he cultivated was merely an Earth-rank Technique, with the enhancement of the Perfection Realm Martial Arts·Body, his Cultivation progress was still not slow. However, after his Cultivation reached the Fourth Grade Realm, it was no longer a simple accumulation of True Essence, but also involved the \"God\"—the enhancement of the Four Symbols Divine Position at his Forehead Acupoint.","The time required for a breakthrough exceeded that of the past. It took him about half a month to elevate by a minor realm. Whether he was satisfied or not, Chen Yi didn’t think too much about it. He just needed to put in more effort while Xiao Jinghong was away.","Fortunately, his Technique Cultivation was not constrained by his Cultivation Technique. It could be described as advancing a thousand miles in a single day.","The Big Spear Pile Skill, Black Tortoise Concealment Technique, and Four Symbols Skill were all cultivated to Perfection. After completely absorbing the Spear Dao Profound Mysteries of the Perfection Realm, the Celestial Tier Dragon-Falling Spear Spear Technique had also been cultivated to the Perfect Level. Although the Mountain Shattering Fist had reached the Celestial Tier, it was limited by his Great Success Fist Dao and had not progressed further, remaining at the Mastery Level. The Celestial Tier Hundred Flowers Palm, Wandering Dragon and Phoenix, Meteor Butterfly Step, Brocade Spring Saber Technique, and others were the same.","Among the Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting and Medicine Dao, only the Chess Dao remained, requiring him to find time to play chess and absorb its Profound Mysteries. Calculating carefully, aside from reading, cultivating the Four Symbols Skill, and fishing every day, the hours Chen Yi spent on Techniques were not considered much.","Late at night, inside the Purple Bamboo Forest.","After Chen Yi finished cultivating various Techniques and didn’t encounter any Opportunity for an epiphany, he checked the light screen:","[Opportunity: 346]","Chen Yi glanced at the remaining Opportunity and revealed a thoughtful expression.","\"Now that both my Martial Arts and Techniques have reached a point where they can progress no further, it’s time to cultivate another Technique.\"","For anyone else, biting off more than one could chew was a universal truth. But Chen Yi was different. With Opportunity by his side, the path of \"more skills do not weigh one down\" was more suitable for him. Especially when it came to Martial Arts. The more Techniques he cultivated and the profounder his Realm, not only could he achieve comprehensive mastery by understanding one thing, but it could also make his Dao Realm even deeper.","Once his Cultivation broke through to the Upper Three Grades, he could use \"God\" to steal more of Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism to enhance the power of his Techniques. It just so happened that Chen Yi currently had another Technique suitable for Cultivation on hand: the Celestial Flower Flying Sword Technique.","\"Swordsmanship, Sword Dao...","\"Madam is known for her ’Spear and Sword Dual Mastery.’ This will actually complement her husband quite well.\"","Chen Yi chuckled a couple of times, then waved his hand to cut down a section of Purple Bamboo, and began cultivating the Celestial Flower Flying Sword Technique.","After practicing a set of moves, a notification appeared.","[Studying Swordsmanship·Celestial Flying Flower (Profound Tier) successful, Level: Initial Insight]","[Martial Arts·Sword: pre-entry-level 0/1 (points can be added)]","Without much hesitation, Chen Yi continued to consume Opportunity to elevate his Sword Dao to Great Success. As the Profound Mysteries flooded his mind, he also took the chance to elevate his Zither Dao to the Great Success Realm. At this point, all of his Technique Dao Realms had reached Great Success and above.","Chen Yi didn’t pay attention to the Zither Dao; he only roughly browsed through the Sword Dao Profound Mysteries before continuing to cultivate his Swordsmanship by the moonlight.","Half an hour, an hour...","In less than two hours, he had cultivated the Celestial Flower Flying Sword Technique to the Mastery Level. It couldn’t be described as anything but fast.","Chen Yi let out a light breath, his eyes falling on the pond not far away, and the Purple Bamboo in his hand slightly trembled. A phantom shadow slashed across ten zhang, and a faint Sword Qi bloomed, sinking into the pond water.","SPLASH, SPLASH, SPLASH...","Golden Carps, startled, leaped out of the water, staring at Chen Yi with wide fish eyes before splashing back into the pond one by one.","How should that look be described? It was roughly like the look in Chen Yi’s eyes when he was previously abducted by Liu Jing—as if looking at an idiot.","\"...\"","Chen Yi instantly shattered the Purple Bamboo in his hand, muttering words about roasting, stewing, and braising them sooner or later, and turned to head back to the wooden building.","Before he even reached his wing room, a chilling wind suddenly began to howl. There was a faint RUMBLE in the night sky.","Chen Yi stopped in his tracks, looked up, and slightly raised his eyebrows. \"It’s going to rain.\"","As if in response to his words, a thunderbolt tore through the night, illuminating his figure. Bean-sized raindrops subsequently fell.","Before long, a PATTER of raindrops resounded throughout the courtyard. Those Golden Carps also joined in the fun, occasionally leaping out of the water to spit water in Chen Yi’s direction. Chen Yi just pretended not to see them, standing under the eaves to watch the night rain for a while. The yellowed lanterns fluttered in the wind, their shadows tangling with one another. Amidst the clamor, a sense of tranquility could be seen.","Just as he was lost in thought, a line of large golden characters floated past Chen Yi’s eyes:","[Daily Intelligence·Profound-rank Middle Grade: 9:00 PM, West Market tailor shop. Hidden Guard General, Lady Tiger, Simurgh Phoenix, and others exchange intelligence. A small amount of Opportunity can be obtained.]","Chen Yi glanced at it, retracted his Heart Spirit, turned around to return to his wing room, and continued to cultivate the Four Symbols Skill.","\"If nothing unexpected happens, the White Tiger Guard should be about to make their move...\"","...","It had been a while since it last rained in Shu State. When it suddenly started, the rain was torrential, and the temperature sharply dropped a few degrees along with it.","With every Autumn Rain comes a chill. The commoners in the city all changed into autumn clothing, and some with weak and cold constitutions even put on winter clothes.","Xiaodie was naturally no exception."]},{"number":578,"title":"Chapter 578 - 328: Swordsman Chen Qingzhou","paragraphs":["Early in the morning, she also brought out the thick clothes that had been freshly washed and sun-dried, helping Xiao Wuge change into them.","\"Young Master, if you feel restricted during your Martial Arts practice, take off your outer coat. But remember to put it back on before coming back, so you don’t catch a cold...\"","Xiaodie reminded him over and over again until Xiao Wuge really couldn’t help but say he had memorized it all, which finally made her stop talking.","After Xiao Wuge was neatly dressed, the two walked out of the wooden building one after the other. Wang Lixing had already been waiting outside for a long time. Xiao Wuge ducked under the Oil Paper Umbrella Wang Lixing held up, waved at Xiaodie, and followed him toward the Martial Arts Arena.","Xiaodie watched them walk away. Looking at the heavy rain outside, she knew she couldn’t sweep the courtyard or do laundry today, so she decided to only clean the two wooden buildings. She didn’t know when Xiao Jinghong would return, but she would always meticulously do the tasks she was supposed to do. Up and down, inside and out, she wiped everything spotless, not even sparing the nooks and crannies.","It wasn’t that she was deliberately meticulous. When she first entered the Marquis’s Mansion as a child, the butler of the mansion had taught her to do it this way. However, very few people completed their tasks as meticulously as she did. Xiaodie certainly didn’t think doing this was anything praiseworthy. To her, this courtyard was her home, her everything. What was wrong with being thorough when cleaning her own home? Besides, the master of this courtyard treated her well. Returning a favor with gratitude—that was essentially what it came down to.","After busying herself for nearly an hour, Xiaodie glanced at the wing where Chen Yi stayed, grabbed an Oil Paper Umbrella, and jogged to the back kitchen. She hadn’t forgotten that there was game meat in the mansion today. It wasn’t that she was being a glutton again. With the Annual Examination approaching, Xiao Wan’er had specifically instructed her, \"Chen Yi has been studying hard lately, so we need to give him some nourishing food.\"","Xiaodie naturally remembered this well. She passed through several residences, arrived at the back kitchen, picked up the already packed food box, and carefully made her way back, Returning Spring Lotus Garden. Along the way, whenever she encountered a Maid or a Household Servant, she would smile, greet them, and exchange a few quiet words. Some of it was trivial gossip from within the mansion, while other bits were rumors from the outside.","\"Sister Xiaodie, did you hear? Many Jianghu People arrived in the Prefecture City today. They are all very, very formidable masters.\"","\"Really? How formidable?\"","\"It is said that they came from other State Capitals, and there is no shortage of outstanding figures among the younger generation.\"","Xiaodie blinked and asked with feigned surprise, \"Why would they come here instead of going to the heartland of the Central Plains?\"","\"That I don’t know.\"","\"I’m guessing it has something to do with that Immortal Bai, just like the Wandering Martial Artists who rushed over a few days ago.\"","Xiaodie let out an \"oh\" of realization. She silently memorized this information before continuing to chat with other maids and household servants. Before long, all sorts of news from inside and outside the Marquis’s Mansion had reached her ears. Only then did Xiaodie run back to the Spring Lotus Garden, thoroughly satisfied.","She arrived under the eaves of the wooden building, shook the rainwater off her Oil Paper Umbrella, closed it tight, and hung it aside. Then, she carried the food box into the living room. The dishes were laid out on the dining table one by one. Just as she was about to go wake Chen Yi, she heard footsteps approaching.","\"Ah, you’re up?\" she asked.","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. He walked over to the table, sat down, and invited her to eat with him. \"With the rain pouring so heavily, how could I keep sleeping?\"","Xiaodie looked outside. After making sure no one was coming, she sat down beside him and chuckled, babbling about wanting to fetch thick clothes for him and so on. Chen Yi realized this belatedly. He looked at his brocade clothes and said, \"It won’t be too late to change into them later.\"","With his Martial Arts cultivation, summer and winter felt the same to him. However, in the eyes of outsiders, he was still a frail scholar, so he had to do things that fit his identity.","Xiaodie didn’t insist. She started chattering away about the things she had just heard. Things like how many Wandering Martial Artists had arrived in the Prefecture City, all of whom were formidable experts of the younger generation. The prices of grain and medicinal herbs were stabilizing, and the local commoners were all talking about thanking the Lord Governor for his kindness, even mentioning writing a ten-thousand-people petition for him. She also mentioned that the refugees outside the city had been escorted back to their hometowns by the government officials.","Chen Yi listened in silence. He wondered what expressions those commoners would have when they learned of Liu Hong’s heinous crimes, unable to suppress an inner sneer. He figured that however much gratitude they felt now, that was exactly how much hatred they would harbor toward Liu Hong later.","At first, the increasing number of Wandering Martial Artists in the city hadn’t piqued his interest. Wherever people were, there was the Jianghu. They had legs, so it wasn’t surprising if they ran off to the Shu State on any given day. Besides, Immortal Bai had indeed already arrived in the Shu State, and...","Chen Yi suddenly remembered something—the Swordsman he had encountered the day he killed Du Cang.","He wondered, \"Could it be because of him?\"","If the news of that Swordsman dueling with Immortal Bai spread, it would indeed likely attract some Wandering Martial Artists. However, judging from that Swordsman’s words, there was a certain threshold to watching his duel with Immortal Bai.","Chen Yi pondered for a moment and decided to find someone tonight to ask about that Swordsman’s identity. Someone capable of fighting it out with Immortal Bai obviously wouldn’t be a nameless nobody.","They chatted a bit more. After finishing breakfast, Chen Yi went to the study, picked up a classic text, and started reading. The rainy weather made the room dim. Lighting a few oil lamps and reading to the rhythmic pitter-patter of the rain held its own unique charm.","However, Chen Yi read extremely fast. \"Reading ten lines at a glance\" wasn’t enough to describe it; \"reading ten pages at a glance\" was more accurate. FLIP FLIP FLIP. The rustling sound of turning pages echoed continuously. If it weren’t for his successful Cultivation, which had gradually enhanced his God intent to the point where he almost possessed a photographic memory, flipping through the pages like this would definitely be a waste of effort. Fortunately, the moment he finished reading a book, its entire contents were etched into his mind.","Soon, an hour passed. Chen Yi put down the book and massaged the bridge of his nose, recalling the classics he had just read one by one.","\"Policy essays, critiques of current affairs...","\"The Annual Examination will likely be the same as before. It won’t test the classics, history, or the words of the Saints, but will instead draw questions from national affairs, government decrees, and current events...\"","Now that he had a general understanding of the Annual Examination, Chen Yi decided not to read any more past exam questions or policy essays. It was nothing more than a test of his understanding of current events and government decrees. Writing down the framework of a solution would be enough. Whether he scored well depended on three things: first, the Academic Administrator’s preferences; second, whether his citations from the classics were appropriate; and third, whether his \"solutions\" were practical. Giving an answer that missed the mark completely would obviously lead to a poor grade.","Chen Yi looked at the sky and was about to head out to the Tingyu Pavilion to investigate, when he heard faint voices coming from outside the garden. He looked toward the sound, a smile inevitably appearing on his face.","\"What a coincidence.\"","The arrival was none other than Chen Yunfan. Besides him, Cui Qingwu and the others followed along. However, Chen Yunfan and Cui Qingwu parted ways outside the courtyard. One came to the Spring Lotus Garden, while the other went to the Jiaxing Garden.","Chen Yunfan led Lin Zhong into the Spring Lotus Garden, loudly calling out, asking where everyone was and demanding they come out to welcome him. His boisterous shouting prompted Xiaodie to hurriedly come out and check.","Upon seeing her, Chen Yunfan smiled and asked, \"Where is Chen Yi?\"","Xiaodie naturally recognized him. She bowed and greeted, \"Chen Yi is reading in the study. Please wait a moment.\"","Before she could turn around and report back to the wooden building, Chen Yi had already appeared in the living room. He waved at Chen Yunfan and Lin Zhong, then instructed Xiaodie to brew some tea. Chen Yunfan exchanged a meaningful glance with Lin Zhong and walked into the living room with a smile.","While looking around, he feigned casualness and asked, \"I heard Brother Yi fell terribly ill a few days ago?\"","Chen Yunfan deliberately emphasized the word \"terribly.\" Others might not be clear on the matter, but he knew exactly how formidable Chen Yi was. Let alone a mere plague toxin, even bizarre poisons that made Jianghu People pale at the mention of them would be useless against Chen Yi.","Catching the underlying implication in his words, Chen Yi invited them to sit and smiled. \"The Physician in the mansion treated me in time, so there are no major issues anymore.\"","He paused, looked at Lin Zhong, and showed a hint of reminiscence on his face. Feigning sudden realization, he asked, \"Uncle Zhong?\"","Lin Zhong nodded, smiling as he bowed. \"Lin Zhong greets Young Master Yi.\"","Chen Yi waved his hand, signaling him not to be so polite. After the two sat down, he finally asked, \"When did Uncle Zhong arrive in the Shu State?\"","\"A few days ago. The matriarch of the mansion was worried about the Eldest Young Master, so she dispatched me to come and visit him.\"","\"So, does that mean you will be heading back soon?\"","\"Probably not. The Eldest Young Master has some matters here that require my assistance. He has already written a letter back to inform the matriarch...\"","As Lin Zhong said this, he seamlessly kept his eyes fixed on Chen Yi the moment he mentioned the matriarch. It was as if he wanted to see if there was any unusual change in Chen Yi’s expression. When he noticed that Chen Yi maintained a constant smile on his face, Lin Zhong couldn’t help but mutter in his heart.","He thought that it was exactly as the master had said—Young Master Yi had indeed changed compared to before. Such bearing was truly extraordinary.","Chen Yunfan, however, ignored all of this. Seeing that the two had finished speaking, he immediately said, \"I came this time because I have an earth-shattering matter to tell Brother Yi...\""]},{"number":579,"title":"Chapter 579 - 329: Brilliant as the Galaxy!","paragraphs":["The massive news Chen Yunfan spoke of was none other than the fact that Chen Xuanji had returned to Great Wei.","\"A few days ago, Father traveled day and night to return to Capital Prefecture. That very day, the Emperor appointed him as the Minister of War, in charge of the world’s military forces and ordnance deployment.\"","\"Minister of War?\"","Recently, Chen Yi had read many books and gained a better understanding of the situation within the Imperial Court.","The Nine Ministers were the Minister of Heaven, Minister of Earth, Minister of Rites, Minister of War, Minister of Justice, Minister of Works, Minister of Supervision, Counselor, and Minister of Ceremony.","Among them, the Minister of Heaven oversaw the appointment, dismissal, and performance evaluation of officials.","The Minister of Earth managed the national treasury’s funds and provisions, handling matters like the country’s salt and iron monopolies, as well as tax supervision.","The Minister of Rites governed the imperial examinations, sacrifices, protocol, and Academic Administrators. Institutions like the Imperial Academy and Honglu Temple all fell under his jurisdiction.","The Minister of War, head of the military officials, controlled their promotions and the distribution of ordnance. Under his command were departments such as the Armory Department and the Courier Service Department.","The Minister of Justice oversaw the judicial system, supervising the Imprisonment Department and the Prison Department.","The Minister of Works managed construction and craftsmanship. The Minister of Supervision controlled the Inspectorate Office of each state. The Counselor oversaw the Stargazing Pavilion, using celestial phenomena to determine national policies. The Minister of Ceremony managed royal affairs...","The Nine Ministers held equal rank, each performing their respective duties as First Grade officials.","Besides them, there were Dukes, Marquis Wus, the Nobility, and the four divisions of the Secretariat—of which the White Tiger Guard was one.","Chen Yunfan nodded and took a letter from his sleeve. \"Mother wrote a letter. Do you want to read it?\"","Seeing his mischievous smile, Chen Yi knew he was testing him. He smiled and shook his head.","\"I won’t read a letter written to my older brother.\"","Lin Zhong had tested him earlier, and now Chen Yunfan was doing the same. Did they really want to know his attitude toward the Chen Family’s matriarch, Cui Yu, that badly?","Heh.","Why would he have any obvious feelings toward a stranger?","Chen Yunfan froze for a moment. Upon realizing his intention, he laughingly called him sly. \"Mother didn’t say much in the letter. She just told me to behave myself in Shu State.\"","Chen Yi casually agreed, \"As she should.\"","\"Besides that, there’s one more thing. Can you guess what it is?\"","\"Just tell me, Brother.\"","\"How boring.\"","Chen Yunfan put the letter away, no longer keeping him in suspense. \"After Father took up the post of Minister of War, according to custom, he must first inspect the Border Towns of the Nine States.","\"In other words, he’ll be arriving in Shu State in a few days.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow, his hand pausing as he lifted his teacup. \"Father... is coming to Shu State?\"","Chen Yunfan tilted his head back and chuckled, \"I offered to let you read it just now, but you refused. Regretting it now, aren’t you?\"","Seeing Chen Yi take a sip of tea, completely unmoved, he found it dull and snorted.","\"Shu State is the southern gateway of the Great Wei Dynasty, and the Three Towns of the Dingyuan Army are the most crucial of the key strongholds. Whether for public or private reasons, Father should make a trip here to understand the situation.","\"Not to mention that both I... and you are in Shu State.\"","While his mind raced with countless thoughts, Chen Yi calmly replied, \"That doesn’t have much to do with me.\"","\"What? After marrying into the Xiao Family, do you plan to cut all ties with the family?\"","\"According to our dynasty’s customs, when a man marries into his wife’s family, his original family will usually remove his name from their genealogy.","\"Even if they don’t, I’ll still be labeled ’married out.’ My future descendants will have no ties to the Chen Family.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yunfan and Lin Zhong exchanged a glance and couldn’t help but fall silent.","Chen Yi observed their expressions, set down his teacup, and asked with a light smile, \"If you have something to say, Brother, you might as well speak plainly.","\"Did the family order me to do something?\"","Realizing he couldn’t hide it from him, Chen Yunfan shook his head helplessly. \"Mother wants you and me to go see Father, to see if he needs us to wait on him.\"","\"Wait on him?\"","Chen Yi laughed involuntarily. \"Father is one of the Nine Ministers of Great Wei. He’ll be surrounded by attendants wherever he goes. Why would he need me to serve him?\"","Chen Yunfan hesitated, looking as if he wanted to say more.","Seeing this, Lin Zhong stood up, cupped his fists in a salute, and said, \"Young Master Yi, there’s no need to belittle yourself.","\"You are now the world-renowned Mr. Qingzhou. I imagine the Master would also like to see you.\"","Chen Yi glanced at him, then turned his head to signal Xiaodie to pour more tea.","Whether he was being neglected or not, how could he not know?","Previously, when Chen Xuanji replied to Chen Yunfan, he had also written a letter to Chen Yi, claiming he had already punished Cui Yu and so on.","Between the lines, he had shown the utmost care and concern.","Although Chen Yi didn’t reject the people of the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family, he had developed a certain level of wariness toward them.","Especially after learning that Chen Xuanji had taken the post of Minister of War, his suspicions became even more certain.","He and Chen Yunfan had been targeted by the White Tiger Guard. The Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family had to be aware of it—at the very least, Chen Xuanji and Chen Xuandu definitely were.","Chen Yi even suspected that the mastermind behind arranging his marriage into the Xiao Family wasn’t the matriarch Cui Yu, but the Patriarch—his father, Chen Xuanji.","Otherwise, with his past talent and learning, even if he didn’t become a king or prime minister, passing the imperial examinations wouldn’t have been a difficult task.","There was another suspicious point.","After Chen Xuanji left and he was imprisoned by Cui Yu, not a single clan elder from the Chen Family showed their face.","This didn’t match the memories in Chen Yi’s mind, nor did it make logical sense.","Thinking of this, Chen Yi made a decision.","\"Since Father is coming, both out of familial duty and common sense, I should go and pay my respects.\"","Hearing this, a smile returned to Chen Yunfan’s face as he teasingly scolded, \"Brother Yi, you said so much just now, I really thought you didn’t want to see Father.\"","Chen Yi looked at Lin Zhong, who had sat back down, and smiled subtly.","\"It’s good to see him. I’ll let Father see that I’m living very well in the Xiao Family now. I’m sure he’ll be pleased.\"","If it really was Chen Xuanji’s idea, then his half a year of idle life in the Xiao Family had probably already deviated from Chen Xuanji’s original intention.","But what did that have to do with him?","He was now just a live-in son-in-law of the Xiao Family, Xiao Jinghong’s husband, an Instructor who taught people calligraphy, and nothing more.","If the Chen Family wanted to use him to plot against the Xiao Family, they were dreaming!","Unaware of the underlying complexities, Chen Yunfan picked up his teacup to moisten his throat and said, \"Both you and I haven’t seen Father in a long time. I wonder if his temper has improved at all.\""]},{"number":580,"title":"Chapter 580 - 329: Dazzling as the Galaxy!","paragraphs":["\"Are you afraid, Yunfan?\"","\"Afraid? You must be joking, Brother Yi. I am the dignified Imperial Top Scholar, Assistant Governor of the Governor’s Office, and a role model for all scholars in the world. When Father sees me, he will definitely praise me.\"","\"Is that so?\" Chen Yi replied with a hint of doubt in his tone. \"Yunfan, what exactly do you think Father will praise you for?\"","\"Naturally, he’ll praise me for...\" Chen Yunfan froze. The absurd things he had done in Shu State recently instantly flashed through his mind, and his heart tightened for no reason.","Despite his inner misgivings, he remained stubborn. \"...for my outstanding talent and my diligent governance and love for... Alas, anyway, Father will definitely not scold me this time.\"","He figured that would be highly unlikely. Chun Ying had been handling all the government affairs, leaving him with little to do. The few times he did go out on official business, he had made mistakes. Add to that this recent incident...","Chen Yunfan seemed to have thought of something. The smile returned to his face, and he said with absolute certainty, \"If you don’t believe me, Brother Yi, how about we make a bet?\"","Seeing the smile on his face, Chen Yi shook his head and refused without a second thought.","Chen Yunfan’s face darkened, and he snorted, \"Are you afraid?\"","\"I’m afraid.\"","\"If you’re not afraid... Huh?\"","\"Brother Yi, you really are, really...\" Chen Yunfan wanted to punch him.","Chen Yi ignored him, picking up his teacup to take a sip. Based on his understanding of Chen Yunfan, the latter would never act so cocky without a certain degree of confidence. He guessed that the clues provided by the White Tiger Guard had yielded results. Had Zhu Hao been caught? If so, Mrs. Chen should be returning to the manor tomorrow.","Seeing Chen Yi’s silence, Chen Yunfan grew furious. Especially when he thought of all the things Chen Yi had done while hiding his identity, he almost couldn’t resist exposing him right then and there. After holding back for a good while, he finally took a deep breath and squeezed out a smile. \"The Annual Examination is approaching. How is your preparation coming along, Brother Yi?\"","Chen Yi replied casually, \"Adequate enough to pass, though perhaps not the absolute best.\"","\"Oh? Don’t you want to achieve a first-grade result?\"","\"There’s no need...\"","Chen Yunfan found him incredibly boring, seeing how impervious he was to any prodding.","Lin Zhong, standing nearby, listened extremely carefully, his gaze darting back and forth between the two. He finally understood the meaning behind the words Chun Ying had told him earlier—the young master did indeed treat Young Master Yi differently. They could generally be considered a fine example of brotherly harmony. It just seemed that Young Master Yi was still brooding over his past marriage into the Xiao Family as a live-in son-in-law. On this point, Lin Zhong was powerless to offer any comfort. He merely made a silent note of it so he could relay the information back to the Chen Family.","After a few more words of idle chatter, Chen Yunfan’s good mood had mostly vanished. Suppressing his frustration, he planned to properly settle the score with Chen Yi once he achieved Sword Dao Perfection.","Chen Yi naturally didn’t know what he was thinking, and even if he did, he probably wouldn’t care too much. Now that he had achieved Perfection in two Daos and Great Success in several others, his cultivation was roughly on par with Chen Yunfan’s. He truly had nothing to fear.","Seeing that it was getting late, Chen Yi instructed Xiaodie to go to Jiaxing Garden to ask about lunch. After Xiaodie left, Chen Yi invited Chen Yunfan and Lin Zhong to sit in the study. Lin Zhong declined, claiming that a mere martial artist like himself had no business there. Chen Yi and Chen Yunfan then headed to the study together.","At a glance, Chen Yunfan spotted the \"Song of the Water Melody: Mid-Autumn\" hanging behind the desk and the Flying Heaven Illusion Realm beneath the study’s crossbeam. Unable to resist, he stepped closer.","\"Is this the Immortal Palace that appeared by the Quchi on the night of the Mid-Autumn Festival?\"","Without waiting for Chen Yi’s reply, Chen Yunfan took down the calligraphy scroll. As he examined the Cursive Script on it and observed the bizarre sights of the Immortal Palace Illusion Realm, he clicked his tongue in marvel.","\"Brother Yi, your Calligraphy Dao truly has outstanding merits. No wonder Hundred Herbs Hall’s business boomed so much after they acquired your calligraphy.","\"Qingwu told me about it several times, but I never went to see it. Today...\"","Before he could finish his sentence, Chen Yunfan’s eyes darted around, and he immediately rolled up the calligraphy scroll and tucked it into his sleeve. The Immortal Palace Illusion Realm vanished.","Chen Yunfan looked at Chen Yi with a beaming smile. \"I’ll take this scroll back to study and observe. You don’t mind, do you, Brother Yi?\"","Chen Yi glared at him in exasperation. \"You’re just acting innocent after getting a good deal.\"","He had already tucked it away; what was the point of asking now? However, Chen Yi didn’t care much about a single calligraphy scroll. With his Martial Arts Cultivation, he could write eighty to a hundred scrolls at any given time.","Chen Yunfan was in an excellent mood. After looking around, his gaze sharpened, fixating on a few paintings hanging on another wall. The mountains, rivers, lakes, and seas depicted in them were majestic and brilliant like a galaxy, clearly indicating that the painting skills had entered the Dao. But that was secondary; Chen Yunfan’s eyes were locked on the signatures in the bottom left corners of those paintings—Chen Yi, Chen Qingzhou.","Painting Dao... Minor Success?","Chen Yunfan’s good mood evaporated instantly. He silently cursed, wondering just how many of Brother Yi’s Techniques had entered the Dao Realm. Calligraphy Dao, Painting Dao, Medical Dao, Martial Arts Spear, Punch, and Step—just the ones Chen Yunfan knew about amounted to six Daos. Was he even human?","Chen Yunfan grumbled incessantly in his heart, but on the surface, he feigned calmness and asked, \"Brother Yi, you’ve also achieved some success in painting?\"","Seeing that he had noticed, Chen Yi didn’t bother hiding it. \"Calligraphy and painting are interconnected. It’s not difficult.\"","He had to be kidding. It was true that calligraphy and painting shared the same origins, but Chen Yunfan had never seen many scholars who achieved success in both Daos. However, he didn’t voice his disbelief. Instead, he pointed at the Ancient Zither in the corner and asked, \"How are your zither skills?\"","\"I play rarely, so my achievements are limited.\"","\"Is that so? What about the Chess Dao?\"","Chen Yi smiled and replied that he usually just played chess with Xiao Wuge, so his chess skills hadn’t improved much.","Chen Yunfan didn’t believe him and dragged him over to set up a game. Unable to decline, Chen Yi played a match with him.","Of course, he couldn’t use his full strength. More accurately, he didn’t even use a tenth of his chess skills. Even so, after a little over a hundred moves, Chen Yunfan still surrendered and conceded defeat.","\"Let’s play another game.\"","\"Brother Yi, how could you place your piece there?\"","\"That doesn’t count, that doesn’t count...\"","As they played on, Chen Yunfan’s face flushed with alternating shades of green and red. He clutched a Heizi hesitantly.","\"Brother Yi, your Chess Dao... has achieved success?\"","Even if he wasn’t particularly skilled at the Chess Dao, his chess skills were still leagues above other scholars. However, no matter how brilliantly he played, he would ultimately lose by a margin of exactly two points. No more, no less—just two points. Once or twice was fine, but it happened every single time. Even a fool would realize that Chen Yi wasn’t using his full strength.","Chen Yi smiled and shook his head. Tossing his chess piece down, he said, \"Chess skill doesn’t represent the Chess Dao, but rather...\" He pointed to his own head. \"...here.\"","\"There, that...\"","As Chen Yunfan finally processed the insult, his face darkened, and he cursed under his breath a few times. \"Sooner or later, I will show you how formidable I truly am!\"","Chen Yi gathered the chess pieces and the board, then stood up with a smile. \"Yunfan, it’s time for lunch.\"","Xiaodie had already come to report earlier that Xiao Wan’er had prepared lunch at Jiaxing Garden and was waiting for them.","Chen Yunfan remained indignant, muttering to himself about Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting, as well as martial arts, medicine, and how someone wasn’t human. Naturally, he felt a bit disgruntled. Although his Sword Dao had one foot in the Perfection Realm, it still needed some time to fully cross the threshold. Compared to Chen Yi’s progress, the difference was like night and day.","With these thoughts in mind, Chen Yunfan said with a tinge of jealousy, \"Brother Yi, if Father knew of your current achievements, he would definitely be very gratified.\"","Chen Yi nodded noncommittally. He led him out of the study, called out to Lin Zhong, and opened his Oil Paper Umbrella as they headed toward Jiaxing Garden.","Chen Yunfan let Lin Zhong hold the umbrella for him as he followed behind Chen Yi, rambling incessantly. \"Did you receive guidance from someone back home, Brother Yi? That must be it. The uncles and elders in the clan thought so highly of you; how could they have just allowed Mother to imprison you?\"","Chen Yi couldn’t help but laugh. \"Couldn’t it just be that my talent is peerless?\"","Chen Yunfan wanted to say no, but when he thought of all the Techniques Chen Yi possessed that had entered the Dao Realm, the words naturally caught in his throat.","His feelings were somewhat complicated. After a moment of silence, as they arrived at Jiaxing Garden, Chen Yunfan let out a long breath and changed the subject. \"Mother said in her letter that Old Four and Old Liu have already set out to come here. When the time comes, you’ll come with me to welcome them.\"","Old Four Chen He, and Old Liu Chen Yu?","Chen Yi didn’t break his stride. He glanced sideways at him and said with a smile, \"Of course.\"","He guessed this was the idea of the First Mrs. Chen of the Chen Family, wanting the brothers to see Chen Xuanji sooner.","\"When will Father come to Shu State?\"","\"I don’t know the exact date. I only know he should finish inspecting all the Border Towns before the end of the year.\"","\"I see...\"","Chen Yi silently made a mental note of it, then withdrew his thoughts and joined Xiao Wan’er, Chen Yunfan, Cui Qingwu, and the others for the meal.","During the meal, the conversation mostly revolved around the Medical Dao Academy and the recent situation in Shu State, which wasn’t particularly novel.","On the other side, however, the atmosphere among Lin Zhong, Xie Tingyun, Shen Huatang, and the others was much livelier. Perhaps because they all practiced Martial Arts, their casual chat centered on recent major events in the Jianghu. However, it was mostly Lin Zhong doing the talking; Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang had stayed in the Xiao Family and hadn’t left Shu State for a long time, so they didn’t know much about Jianghu affairs.","\"Lately, rumors have been spreading wildly in the Jianghu about Immortal Bai coming to Shu State. I heard someone found out the reason.\"","\"He really came to Shu State?\"","\"What’s the reason?\"","\"Rumor has it that Immortal Bai...\" Lin Zhong paused, speaking with feigned mystery. \"...had a duel with a peerless expert in Shu State.\"","\"GASP!\"","Xie Tingyun first drew a sharp breath, then asked with excitement written all over his face, \"Really?\"","\"It’s not certain yet, but over the past two days, quite a few Upper Three Grades experts have already arrived in Shu State. It’s highly likely to be true...\""]},{"number":581,"title":"Chapter 581 - 330: Don’t Blame Your Brother for Being Unrighteous","paragraphs":["\"A peerless master...\"","Xie Tingyun’s eyes sparkled, inadvertently revealing a touch of envy.","In the literary world, there is no undisputed first; in the martial world, no one settles for second. There was not a single practitioner of Martial Arts who didn’t want to stand at the absolute peak, and Xie Tingyun naturally wanted to as well. Immortal Bai was the highest mountain of them all. He had stood in the Jianghu for decades, looking down upon all heroes. Even if one couldn’t defeat him, being able to stand opposite him and exchange a move or two in this life was something many dreamed of.","\"If only Immortal Bai were truly going to spar with someone in Shu State,\" Xie Tingyun said. \"And it’d be best if it were a Swordsman.\"","For no other reason than this: if a Swordsman were to duel Immortal Bai, for a martial artist practicing the Sword Dao like Xie Tingyun, it would be equivalent to watching a martial demonstration. If the Opportunity arose, she might achieve an epiphany and advance in her Sword Dao. Shen Huatang, on the other hand, remained quite calm. Her Martial Arts Cultivation and Technique Realm were too low; even if she went to watch Immortal Bai duel, she wouldn’t be able to comprehend anything.","Xiaodie, Juan’er, and Cui’er needed even less explanation—it sounded like incomprehensible scripture to them. Only Huan’er and Chun Ying smiled without speaking.","Lin Zhong took in everyone’s expressions and shook his head. \"When figures of that level spar, it is both an Opportunity and a test for the bystanders.\"","Xie Tingyun paused in the middle of picking up food with her chopsticks, her face falling. \"You’re right.\"","She had been taking things for granted. Although her Martial Arts Cultivation and Technique Realm were considered respectable in the Jianghu, earning her the title of Fairy Tingyun, her aptitude would never catch the eye of a figure like Immortal Bai upon closer reflection. Let alone watching from the sidelines, even gazing from a distance was an extravagant hope. Moreover, when experts of that Realm sparred, those without sufficient skill wouldn’t even be able to withstand the shockwaves of their clash if they got too close. They would die without even knowing how.","\"I heard that before figures of that level duel, they each choose a rising star of comparable strength to spar with?\"","Lin Zhong smiled and nodded. \"There is indeed such a custom.","\"For instance, several years ago, before the two seniors, Sword Master and Sword Ghost, dueled, they each selected someone.","\"Senior Sword Master chose his Closed-door Disciple. Although she was just a child, she had already entered the path of the Sword Dao.","\"The Jianghu People all say that her future achievements will definitely rival those of the Sword Master...\"","After giving this brief explanation, Lin Zhong shifted his attention to Chen Yunfan in the inner room. Xie Tingyun, however, grew even more interested and pulled Shen Huatang into enthusiastic chatter.","At the dining table in the inner hall of the wooden building.","Chen Yunfan had naturally heard Lin Zhong’s words. Although he wasn’t interested in lofty figures like Immortal Bai, he could at least use this matter as a conversation topic—especially in front of Chen Yi. Thus, taking advantage of a lull in the chat between Xiao Wan’er and Cui Qingwu, Chen Yunfan raised his teacup to Chen Yi with a smile. \"Brother Yi, have you heard the true reason Immortal Bai came to Shu State?\"","Chen Yi had naturally also heard the conversation between Lin Zhong, Xie Tingyun, and the others. \"What is it?\" he asked casually.","Seeing Chen Yi’s clueless expression, Chen Yunfan smiled and said, \"An expert is going to duel Immortal Bai in Shu State.\"","\"I see...\"","\"If you are interested when the time comes, Brother Yi, I will take you to watch it.\"","\"No thanks. It’s best if I keep a respectful distance from Immortal figures like that.\"","Chen Yunfan smiled. \"I almost forgot that you are a bit frail, Brother Yi. For a duel between experts of that caliber, it would probably be difficult for you to get close.\"","\"You’re right, Brother. But... aren’t you a scholar as well?\"","Chen Yi really didn’t want to reveal the truth and leave Chen Yunfan with nowhere to hide his face. Not only did he know the reason for Immortal Bai’s visit, but he also knew that the person dueling him was a Swordsman. Chen Yunfan wasn’t annoyed; instead, he was delighted, the smile in his eyes becoming even more pronounced.","\"Oh, Brother Yi,\" Chen Yunfan thought, \"you think you know my background, but little do you know that I am well aware of yours. Trying to put on an act with me here? You’re still a bit too green.\"","\"You make a good point, Brother Yi. I was being inconsiderate...\"","Chen Yi glanced at him and set down his bowl and chopsticks. \"Are you not busy with official duties today, Brother? Yesterday, Brother Huai’gu came to our door and mentioned that you hadn’t gone to work at the Government Office for some time. He also said you were sick. Is that true?\"","Chen Yunfan’s smile stiffened. Catching a glimpse of Cui Qingwu’s half-smile out of the corner of his eye, he inexplicably felt a surge of panic. \"Brother Yi, are you remembering it wrong?\"","\"Oh? Perhaps I am.\"","Noticing his gaze, Chen Yi looked at Xiao Wan’er beside him and asked with a smile, \"Have the refugees outside the Prefecture City been evacuated?\"","Xiao Wan’er didn’t understand his intention but nodded cooperatively. \"They left yesterday. I heard that under the coordination of the Governor’s Office and the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office, they gradually dispersed after everyone received rations for their return journey.\"","\"And the grain prices, I remember they’ve dropped quite a bit as well,\" Chen Yi added.","\"Cui’er was just saying this morning that a picul of refined grain is now less than one tael of silver,\" Xiao Wan’er replied. \"Many commoners who bought grain a few days ago were so furious that they went to the grain shops to argue.\"","\"Did the Governor’s Office step in to mediate?\"","\"I heard it was Lord Yang, Yang Ye, and Third Scorer Li who went...\"","Hearing this, Chen Yunfan’s mouth twitched, and he let out a dry laugh. \"Is that so? I didn’t expect so much to happen while I was away from the Government Office, heh heh.\"","Cui Qingwu shot him a reproachful look before leaning close to Xiao Wan’er. \"Sister Wan’er, I have to return home for the New Year holidays. Why don’t we travel to Tonglin together sometime later?\"","Xiao Wan’er instinctively looked at Chen Yi. Seeing him give a slight nod, she smiled and agreed.","\"I wonder how many renowned doctors will come in response to the invitations we sent out earlier,\" Xiao Wan’er mused.","\"Don’t worry, Sister Wan’er. Even if those people don’t come, our Cui Family can still find suitable candidates for the dean.\"","\"That would be wonderful, but...\"","Seeing the two women change the subject, Chen Yunfan breathed a sigh of relief and couldn’t help but glare at Chen Yi.","\"Brother Yi,\" he thought, \"if you’re going to be ruthless, don’t blame me for being unjust.\""]},{"number":582,"title":"Chapter 582 - 330: Don’t Blame Your Brother for Being Unjust","paragraphs":["\"I just heard Brother Yi say he isn’t confident about the Annual Examination?\"","\"Then you need to study harder. Don’t carelessly lose your scholarly rank and make a laughingstock of yourself before the whole world.\"","Chen Yi paused. Out of the corner of his eye, he glanced at Xiao Wan’er beside him. Guessing Chen Yunfan’s intention, he feigned complete confidence and replied, \"It’s just a policy essay.\"","Xiao Wan’er observed his expression. Seeing no sign of falsehood, she held back her urge to give him any further admonitions.","\"Little Sister Qingwu, how about we wait until the dean of the Medical Dao Academy is chosen before heading to Tonglin?\"","\"Alright...\"","They chatted and laughed until they finished lunch.","Holding their umbrellas, Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er respectively saw off Chen Yunfan and Cui Qingwu, with Lin Zhong and the others following behind. The rain grew heavier, beating against the umbrellas with endless PATTER PATTER sounds that masked everyone’s footsteps. Even their conversation became muffled and hard to hear clearly.","Seeing that Cui Qingwu’s attention was elsewhere, Chen Yunfan turned his head to Chen Yi and gritted his teeth. \"Brother Yi, you just had to touch a sore spot and embarrass me!\"","\"Right back at you,\" Chen Yi chuckled, keeping his voice down as he glanced at Xiao Wan’er.","\"Hmph. Thanks to you, I’ll be going to the Government Office to work this afternoon.\"","\"As you should.\"","Chen Yunfan snorted and turned to board the carriage. Just before entering the cabin, he looked back and reminded him, \"Don’t forget to come with me to welcome Father, Old Four, and Old Liu when they arrive in Shu State.\"","Chen Yi held up his Oil Paper Umbrella. \"Rest assured. Just like when you came to Shu State that day, didn’t I also go outside the North City Gate to welcome you?\"","Chen Yunfan hesitated before saying, \"Father is coming with great fanfare this time. You... forget it, forget it. I’ll notify you when the time comes.\"","Chen Yi nodded in agreement, watching him and Cui Qingwu enter the carriage.","Lin Zhong waited for Huan’er and Chun Ying to step inside before sitting directly on the driver’s seat. Gripping the reins, he bid them farewell and drove away. Ning Yu and Niu Mountain, on the other hand, walked back on foot.","Chen Yi waved, watching them leave. Xiao Wan’er did the same.","Chen Yi was just about to take Xiaodie back to Spring Lotus Garden when he heard Xiao Wan’er ask, \"Are you not confident about the Annual Examination, Chen Yi?\"","He paused his steps. Silently cursing Chen Yunfan for being a blabbermouth, his verbal response was pleasant. \"I am fully confident.\"","Xiao Wan’er smiled. \"Then I’m relieved.","\"The Annual Examination is different from other matters; you cannot afford to be careless. If you were to lose your scholarly rank, it would inevitably cause some trouble in the future. Let alone outsiders, even the students at your academy would probably...\"","Chen Yi quickly agreed. \"Don’t worry, don’t worry, I understand. Don’t you know my capabilities, Wan’er?\"","Catching the underlying implication of his words, Xiao Wan’er gave him a reproachful look and turned to walk back to the wooden building. It wasn’t that she didn’t know his abilities; she was simply worried that he wouldn’t put in his best effort out of indifference or his easygoing nature.","Watching her walk away, Chen Yi tossed his umbrella to Xiaodie. He leisurely took shelter beneath it and said, \"Let’s go back and read.\"","Standing on her tiptoes to hold the umbrella for him, Xiaodie covered her mouth and giggled. \"Mr. Chen, Ms. Xiao is right. The Annual Examination is immensely important. You shouldn’t treat it so casually.\"","Chen Yi pursed his lips. \"Casual or not, it’s just an Annual Examination.\"","More often than not, talented and capable people who worked hard to improve themselves did not necessarily achieve good results. If hard work always paid off, there wouldn’t be so many unfulfilled ambitions and regrets in the world. Naturally, Chen Yi wouldn’t bother explaining this aloud. He would only curse Chen Yunfan a few more times in his heart for being such a loose-lipped meddler.","Coincidentally, at this very moment, Chen Yunfan was cursing Chen Yi in the exact same manner. While grumbling to himself, he had to deal with Cui Qingwu’s relentless, coaxing verbal attacks.","\"Brother Yunfan, you’ve been practicing Martial Arts so diligently lately. It must be very tiring.\"","\"It’s not tiring, not at all...\"","\"Not tiring? Then why haven’t you been going to work at the Government Office, Brother Yunfan?\"","\"There are some matters...\"","\"What matters? Let’s hear them.\"","\"Well, this...\"","\"Are Ning Yu and Niu Mountain not doing their best? Or is it Chun Ying...\"","Seeing a fine layer of sweat suddenly bead on Chun Ying’s forehead, Chen Yunfan held back a laugh and said, \"None of them. Ahem... I’ll go to the Government Office to work this afternoon...\"","Cui Qingwu wasn’t truly blaming him, either. Upon hearing this, she smiled and nodded. \"Brother Yunfan, Uncle Chen is coming to Shu State. It’s best if you put on a good performance for the time being.\"","\"You’re right, Qingwu...\"","Feeling helpless, Chen Yunfan alighted alone when the carriage passed by the Governor’s Office and watched Lin Zhong drive away.","He thought, \"Brother Yi, oh, Brother Yi, just you wait!\"","Grimacing with a headache, Chen Yunfan smoothed out his clothes and walked into the Governor’s Office. When the government officials at the entrance saw him, they looked slightly peculiar, but they were quick to salute. \"Lord Chen.\"","Chen Yunfan nodded and made his way to the inner hall, sitting down in his relatively spacious Assistant Governor’s office.","In the adjacent room, Li Huai’gu heard the noise and looked up. Once he realized who it was, he let out a sigh of relief. He rubbed his aching shoulders, stared at the mountain of ledgers on his desk, and muttered, \"He’s finally here.\"","Instantly re-energized, Li Huai’gu scooped up a stack of ledgers from his desk and practically jogged into Chen Yunfan’s office.","THUD.","Exactly thirty ledgers were spread out in front of Chen Yunfan.","\"I’ll leave these to you, Brother Yunfan.\"","Staring at the pile of administrative affairs, Chen Yunfan’s eye twitched. \"Brother Huai’gu, these...\"","Guessing what he was about to say, Li Huai’gu interrupted, \"When you weren’t at the Government Office before, Lord Yang ordered me to handle things in your stead. Now that you’re back, I’ll have to trouble you to take care of these matters.\"","\"This many?\" Chen Yunfan flipped through them briefly. Suddenly, his gaze sharpened as he pointed to one of the ledgers near the bottom. \"The Annual Examination? Isn’t this Lord Liu’s...\"","He caught himself, realizing that something truly must have happened to Liu Hong.","Assuming he was still in the dark, Li Huai’gu made a shushing gesture and pointed toward the deep end of the corridor outside the door. \"Starting the day before yesterday, Lord Liu has been staying behind closed doors. At present, all matters are being handled by Lord Yang. Furthermore...\"","A short while later, after getting up to speed on the Government Office’s current situation, Chen Yunfan realized that Chun Ying’s report yesterday had been rather conservative. Not only was Liu Hong no longer involving himself in the Government Office’s affairs, but his temperament seemed to have changed completely.","It was as if... he was waiting to die.","Chen Yunfan recalled the recent events: the grain stores, the Five Poison Sect, the Mountain Race, the disaster refugees, the plague... and Chen Yi.","He wondered, \"Did Brother Yi find some leverage against Liu Hong?\"","It was highly likely. Liu Hong and the Jing State Liu Family backing him had been continuously targeting the Xiao family, so it was only natural for Brother Yi to take action against him. However, based on his understanding of Liu Hong, the man shouldn’t just be sitting idly by as a sitting duck in such a situation.","Unless...","Thinking of certain rumors he had once heard, Chen Yunfan frowned inwardly. Aside from the Jing State Liu Family and Consort Liu, Liu Hong had another massive backer behind him. It was just that even with the combined power of the Chen family and the White-robed Minister, they hadn’t been able to uncover that person’s identity.","He thought, \"Someone capable of making Liu Hong concede defeat and lie low... The Nine Ministers, or...\"","A few figures surfaced in Chen Yunfan’s mind, giving him some vague suspicions. Naturally, he wouldn’t share these thoughts with Li Huai’gu. He simply accepted the administrative tasks and began reviewing them with a bitter expression.","\"Settling the refugees cost one million stones of money and grain...\"","\"Providing relief to the Three Counties of Guang’an cost...\"","\"The merchants rumored to have died on the Ancient Tea-Horse Road have returned... Hmm?\"","Chen Yunfan looked thoughtfully at the ledger in his hands, his gaze involuntarily turning toward the direction of the Xiao family’s residence. Previously, when rumors spread that people flying the Peacock King Banner had arrived at the Ancient Tea-Horse Road, he had genuinely thought King Landu was that audacious.","Looking at it now... the truly audacious one was his Brother Yi.","At this thought, a complex expression appeared on Chen Yunfan’s face.","\"It seems Brother Yi already considers himself a part of the Xiao family,\" he thought. \"Who knows if Father coming to Shu State will be a good thing or a bad thing... Mother, the family made a mistake with those arrangements...\"","Shortly before 9:00 PM.","Chen Yi quietly left the Xiao family’s residence and headed straight for the West Market. Using the rain as cover, he hid his tracks along the way and soon slipped into the residence behind the tailor shop.","Compared to his previous visits, however, he was much more cautious this time. There was no other reason; along the way, he had detected the auras of no fewer than four Upper Three Grades Martial Arts experts. This was far more than before.","He thought, \"It seems the news of the duel between Immortal Bai and that person has already spread. I wonder if that man leaked it himself or if it was someone else.\"","Recalling the Swordsman he had seen that night and the words he had spoken, Chen Yi gave a slight purse of his lips.","\"So much for ’having the qualifications to come watch the battle,’\" he continued thinking. \"Now that the news has spread and so many Jianghu People have gathered, I highly doubt you’ll actually drive them away when the time comes.\"","Even as he thought this, Chen Yi didn’t genuinely believe the man was incapable of doing so. He figured that even without lifting a finger, that man could probably dissuade numerous unqualified Wandering Martial Artists from watching with just a single sentence. With these thoughts in mind, Chen Yi concealed his aura and silenced his breathing, focusing intently on any sounds coming from the tailor shop.","Not long after, the General’s voice drifted over from that direction.","\"The Pavilion Master has ordered us to immediately move out and capture Liu Hong’s accomplices...\""]},{"number":583,"title":"Chapter 583 - 331: Reversed Moon Sword!","paragraphs":["The General lowered his voice while concentrating on the sounds outside the house.","With his Cultivation, let alone ordinary people, even Jianghu People of similar Cultivation could hardly escape his detection.","Hearing only the torrential rain outside, he continued, \"The Holy Emperor is furious. Not just Liu Hong, but the entire Jing State Liu Family has been uprooted.\"","Lou Yuxue and Cui Qingwu exchanged a glance, both feeling somewhat surprised.","\"Has Consort Liu fallen out of favor?\"","The General looked at them, rendered speechless. He clearly hadn’t expected this to be their first thought.","\"Lord Pavilion Master didn’t mention it. However... with the Liu Family meeting such an end, even if Consort Liu remains in favor, she will likely become estranged from the Holy Emperor in the future.\"","\"That makes sense.\"","Lou Yuxue nodded thoughtfully, then asked, \"My Lord, if we make a move to capture people now, won’t it alert Liu Hong?\"","Cui Qingwu chimed in, \"Liu Hong is wildly ambitious. If he senses any unusual activity around him, who’s to say he won’t lash out in desperation?\"","The General smiled and shook his head. \"He should have already made his choice.\"","\"Are you referring to what he’s done recently...\"","\"That should be correct.","\"These days, he has stayed secluded inside the Governor’s Office behind closed doors. Everything seems fine at his home on the surface, but in reality, there are some strange movements.\"","The General directed his gaze toward the Governor’s Office on South Street, sighing slightly. \"Both of his sons are gone.\"","\"Did they flee in advance?\"","\"The eldest, Liu Taoyao, most likely fled. The second, Liu Taofang... is presumed dead.\"","The General withdrew his gaze. Looking at the secret letter in his hand, he said something that shocked Lou Yuxue and Cui Qingwu: \"The Iron Banner Officers I recently planted in the Liu Family have all lost contact since the night the plague poison appeared. They are probably dead as well.\"","Lou Yuxue and Cui Qingwu frowned slightly. \"Were they discovered?\"","The General put away the secret letter, shook his head, and then nodded. \"Maybe yes, maybe no.","\"In short, a massive upheaval has occurred within the Liu Family.\"","He really couldn’t describe the exact situation.","But last night, when he went to investigate the Liu Family, he noticed before even getting close that the people inside the estate seemed completely devoid of life.","Although they looked like living people from a distance, upon closer inspection, their auras were as fragile as the elderly on death’s door.","Extremely faint.","But before he could get any closer, the General sensed a sharp, overbearing aura lunging straight at him.","Without a second of delay, he retreated immediately, fleeing from the Liu Family’s location.","Even now, the General still felt a lingering fear—as if a Long Sword were suspended right above his head.","Lou Yuxue, naturally unaware of all this, pondered for a moment and said, \"Since Lord Pavilion Master sent a letter with instructions, shall we make our move tonight?\"","Hearing this, Cui Qingwu glanced at her but kept her inner reluctance to herself.","The General observed their expressions and nodded. \"We act tonight.","\"However, we must prioritize.","\"The one closest to Liu Hong is the Vice Envoy of the Inspectorate Office, Ye Jingxiao. Lord Pavilion Master specifically instructed in his letter—he must be captured alive.\"","\"Ye Jingxiao...\"","Lou Yuxue recalled, \"If I remember correctly, he previously wrote a memorial based on baseless rumors regarding the burning of the summer grain in the Three Towns.\"","The General said, \"It is him.","\"At that time, rumors spread in Shu State that the Xiao Family had orchestrated an inside job. On the surface, thugs went to burn the summer grain, but in reality, the Xiao Family secretly sold the grain.","\"When Hawk first arrived in Guangyuan, he even had someone investigate him, but it was delayed due to other matters.\"","Lou Yuxue was also aware of what happened after the summer grain incident in the Three Towns. \"I didn’t expect Liu Hong to be the one behind Ye Jingxiao. I thought he belonged to the Ji State Trading Company.\"","Before the General could speak, Cui Qingwu scoffed, \"It’s obvious.","\"With Liu Hong being such a crafty old fox, he definitely plotted against the Ji State Trading Company long ago, just like with this plague poison.","\"From the news we’ve gathered so far, Liu Hong probably intends to use those refugees to his advantage.","\"Think about it. If the plague poison hadn’t been resolved, what kind of situation would the entire Prefecture City be in?\"","Lou Yuxue ignored her provocative tone and pondered, \"First a food shortage, then the threat of the plague poison. If I were those refugees, I’m afraid...\"","A touch of coldness appeared on the General’s face. \"They would take desperate risks.","\"Even if those refugees didn’t want to, with Liu Hong’s methods, he has many ways to force their hands.","\"Fortunately, things didn’t reach that point, or else we would all be punished by the Pavilion Master.\"","Lou Yuxue hummed in agreement as a figure surfaced in her mind.","Once again, it was his handiwork—\"Dragon Tiger\" Liu Wu.","Even though Lou Yuxue knew Liu Wu did all of that for the Xiao Family, he inadvertently did the White Tiger Guard a massive favor.","Rebellion was unlike plague poison or natural disasters; it was a major event that would cause an uproar throughout the Great Wei Dynasty.","Setting aside whether troops would be deployed, the White Tiger Guards scattered across various regions would be the first to bear the brunt of the punishment.","Especially in Shu State Prefecture City.","With so many Banner Officers hidden everywhere, not only had they failed to stop Liu Hong’s scheme, but they also hadn’t even noticed it.","If she were the Pavilion Master, she would have condemned everyone too.","Cui Qingwu seemed to read her mind, saying pointedly, \"That Liu Wu’s skills are truly impressive.","\"I heard most of the Five Poison Sect experts died at his hands that night, and even Yan Jingchen was no exception.\"","The General paused, his expression softening slightly. He smiled and said, \"I suppose that must be the case.","\"Otherwise, with the temperament of the Mountain Race, why would they hide and sneak around?\"","Cui Qingwu didn’t know much about the Mountain Race. Hearing this, she asked, \"Lord General, Yan Jingchen’s Cultivation shouldn’t be low. How did he compare to Du Cang?\"","The General thought for a moment. \"They were evenly matched.\"","Before Cui Qingwu could ask further, he continued, \"Even though Yan Jingchen’s Cultivation was slightly higher than Du Cang’s, his Fist Dao relied entirely on Poison Power to win.","\"However, the Witchcraft of the Mountain Race perfectly counters Poison Power, which is exactly why the Five Poison Sect was hunted to extinction by the Mountain Race back then.\""]},{"number":584,"title":"Chapter 584 - 331: Reversed Moon Sword!","paragraphs":["\"The reason Du Cang and Yan Jingchen are considered equals in strength is actually because the Black Magic Secret Skill Du Cang cultivated is a Technique that specifically targets a Martial Artist’s ’God’.","\"Ordinary Jianghu people have almost no chance of survival when they encounter him. The only exception is...","\"Liu Wu is a freak.\"","Not just an exception, but a freak. General’s evaluation of Liu Wu also represented his apprehension toward the man. First, it was due to the Pavilion Master’s high regard for Liu Wu, and second, because Liu Wu’s recent life-and-death battles were truly eye-catching. General even suspected that Liu Wu was some old monster who hadn’t appeared in the world for a long time. Every time he made a move, he would use something new, rendering him completely fathomless.","Upon hearing this, Cui Qingwu felt a sense of sudden realization. She recalled the scene of her first encounter with Liu Wu—she had fought him and even emerged victorious. Compared to the current \"Dragon Tiger\", that encounter felt like an illusion. She wondered how, in such a short period, Liu Wu’s Cultivation could progress so rapidly. Or perhaps the person she initially met was not the same Liu Wu as now?","Cui Qingwu couldn’t figure out the reason, nor was she willing to believe in Liu Wu’s Martial Arts talent, so she had to drop the matter. Her remaining days in Shu State were numbered; she hoped she would have a chance to clarify this matter in time. Ignoring these thoughts, she moved past the brief interlude and straightforwardly asked about the identities of Liu Hong’s other accomplices.","\"Sun Zhiguang of the Sun family... and others, as well as Zhu Hao’s younger brother, Zhu Lingchuan, who is Mr. Lingchuan of Guiyun Academy!\"","Lou Yuxue blanked slightly. \"He is also Liu Hong’s man?\"","General hummed in affirmation. \"Not only is he Liu Hong’s man, but he is also one of his strategists.\"","\"Why... why would he be so close to Liu Hong? Logically, he should be helping Zhu Hao more.\"","\"We’ll only know the answer to that after we capture and interrogate him.\"","\"And what about Zhu Hao? He...\"","Before Lou Yuxue could finish, General raised his hand and interrupted, \"There’s no need to pay much attention to his side. He’s already a dead man.\"","To him, whether Liu Hong died or not was secondary, but Zhu Hao had to die.","\"These are the people for now. Later, using the authority of the White Tiger Guard, I will have the Imprisonment Department cooperate. The two of you will take South Street as the boundary and act separately, one heading south and the other north.\"","\"Understood.\"","Just as Chen Yi and Lou Yuxue thought the meeting was over, General continued. \"There are two more things I need to remind you about.\"","\"Please speak, my lord,\" Lou Yuxue said.","\"The newly appointed Minister of War, Chen Xuanji, is about to inspect the Border Towns around the world. He will arrive in Shu State in a few days. By then, we need to purge the state of any riffraff.\"","Lou Yuxue opened her mouth to ask a question, but Cui Qingwu beat her to it. \"Chen Xuanji? Uncle Chen returned from the Western Regions?\"","General smiled and nodded. \"It’s said he just returned three days ago. The Holy Emperor welcomed him personally and issued an edict at the court assembly, appointing Lord Chen as the Minister of War. The Pavilion Master specifically instructed us to ensure that Shu State remains stable for a while, lest we disturb that lord.\"","Cui Qingwu’s face revealed a hint of surprise, clearly not having expected this.","Lou Yuxue, on the other hand, thought of two other matters. She hesitated before saying, \"My lord, this subordinate has a question, though I am unsure if I should ask.\"","General glanced at Cui Qingwu and chuckled softly. \"You want to ask about the Chen family’s two young masters?\"","\"Yes... Chen Xuanji is now the Minister of War. If he learns of our schemes against his two nephews, wouldn’t we offend him?\"","\"Offend? What do you mean by offend?","\"The White Tiger Guard is loyal only to the Holy Emperor. As for other courtiers... even the Nine Ministers are not allowed to interfere in our affairs.","\"So what if we offend him?","\"Does he really think the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family can stand against the White Tiger Guard?\"","Hearing this, Lou Yuxue fell silent and tactfully closed her mouth. She had assumed that the Lord Pavilion Master had informed Chen Xuanji of the schemes against the two Chen family young masters. Now, it seemed things were far more complicated than she had thought.","Cui Qingwu had naturally realized this as well, but she didn’t care whether Chen Xuanji knew or not. Rather, she wanted to know what the White Tiger Guard—or the Holy Emperor—was truly plotting against Chen Yunfan. Previously, she had indeed hoped to help Chen Yunfan rise rapidly in rank to silence the wagging tongues in her family, which was why she joined the White Tiger Guard. But as of today, she increasingly felt that their scheme involving Chen Yunfan was far from simple. Under these circumstances, how could she dare to continue?","Seeing their silence, General waved his hand, gesturing for Cui Qingwu to leave first while keeping Lou Yuxue behind. Cui Qingwu looked at the two of them but didn’t pry, simply turning around and walking out of the tailor shop.","Once everything quieted down, the voices inside the tailor shop became faint, barely audible. Chen Yi turned his ear to listen for a moment, silently taking a few steps forward before he could finally hear the conversation.","\"...forgive me.\"","\"Since it’s the Pavilion Master’s instruction, there’s no need for you to act like this, my lord. It doesn’t matter if this subordinate waits a bit longer.\"","General chuckled a few times. \"That is good.","\"Chen Xuanji’s arrival is of great significance. The Three Towns Dingyuan Army, the Xiao family, and even Mengshui Pass should all be taking this seriously.","\"Whether the White Tiger Guard’s years of planning in Shu State will bear fruit also rests on Chen Xuanji.\"","Lou Yuxue stared blankly. \"Him?\"","\"The Lord Pavilion Master stated this in his secret letter. We only need to act according to orders for now; there is no need to ask too much.\"","\"Understood.\"","General sized up Lou Yuxue, the smile on his face widening. \"However, there is one thing I can tell you in advance.","\"Although the Lord Pavilion Master asked you to temporarily remain in Shu State, he also mentioned his future arrangements for you.","\"Jiangnan Prefecture.\"","Lou Yuxue’s body trembled, her pupils constricting slightly as she asked urgently, \"My lord, regarding Jiangnan Prefecture...\"","General raised a hand with a reassuring smile. \"Rest assured, since the Lord Pavilion Master has said so, he must have arranged everything.","\"Even if Jiangnan Prefecture already has one Jade Banner Officer and two Golden Banner Officers overseeing it, you don’t need to worry too much. You only need to take care of the affairs of the Bright Moon Building.\"","\"Are you saying... the Pavilion Master has a way to make this subordinate an Elder of the Bright Moon Building in Jiangnan Prefecture?\" Lou Yuxue asked hesitantly.","General shook his head slightly. \"I don’t know.\" With that, he stood up. \"You shouldn’t overthink it. Just wait for the Lord Pavilion Master’s orders.\"","\"Understood...\"","Not long after, General and Lou Yuxue departed separately, using the rainy night as cover to head straight for some of the noble families within the Prefecture City.","Chen Yi waited quietly in place until several lines of golden text floated before his eyes:","[Witnessed the Hidden Guard General and others receiving a secret letter. Reward: \"Reversed Moon Sword\" [Profound Tier], Opportunity +28.]","[Review: People arrived, voices were heard, but the scene was unseen...]","Upon reading this, Chen Yi finally let out a breath and quietly left the estate to return to the Xiao family. The night’s harvest was bountiful. The White Tiger Guard had already begun moving to apprehend Liu Hong’s accomplices, and it looked like the Jing State Liu Family was about to suffer a disaster. Mr. Lingchuan was indeed Liu Hong’s man, and before Xiao Jinghong could even interrogate him, the White Tiger Guard was going to take him down.","Furthermore, Chen Xuanji’s arrival in Shu State was deeply related to the White Tiger Guard’s schemes—even if General hadn’t explicitly said so. And lastly, Lou Yuxue was heading to Jiangnan Prefecture... Golden Banner Officer...","Thinking of this, a smile curled at the corners of Chen Yi’s mouth. It was a good thing Lady Tiger was leaving. At the very least, it indicated that the White Tiger Guard’s schemes in Shu State should be coming to a close. By then, as a live-in son-in-law, he would finally be able to enjoy some leisurely days.","Just as he was thinking this, Chen Yi paused mid-step. Another string of golden text flashed before his eyes:","[Daily Intelligence · Profound-rank Top Grade: At three quarters past Noon, Governor of Shu State Liu Hong will visit Duke Dingyuan Xiao Yuan. Reward: A small amount of Opportunity can be obtained.]","Hm?","Chen Yi’s brows furrowed instinctively as he gazed in the direction of the Governor’s Office. Liu Hong was going to see the old patriarch? Why? Especially right after his accomplices were being apprehended by the White Tiger Guard...","Various thoughts flashed through Chen Yi’s mind, only to be rejected one by one. He wondered, \"Mutual destruction? A humble apology? Neither seems likely...\"","Based on Chen Yi’s understanding of Liu Hong, sitting out waiting for doom was indeed not in his nature. It was just that with his Liu family members and accomplices either dead or captured, what could he possibly change by going out to see the old patriarch at a time like this?","DRIP DROP.","Rainwater pattered all around in the gloomy darkness, as if the night stretched endlessly into every corner. Meanwhile, on the chessboard in Chen Yi’s mind, Liu Hong and all the chess pieces connected to him were rising and falling.","After a long time, Chen Yi finally let out a heavy sigh, a hint of helplessness crossing his face. \"As expected of someone who could climb to the position of Governor of Shu State. He truly has some courage.\"","There were not many choices left for Liu Hong. The old patriarch was in good health, his Cultivation had mostly recovered, and he had no fear of assassination by Liu Hong. At the same time, the Xiao family was already in an invincible position; there was no need for them to make a move against Liu Hong when they could just watch from the sidelines.","The old patriarch knew this well. Naturally, Liu Hong knew this too. Therefore, he only had one path left to take..."]},{"number":585,"title":"Chapter 585 - 332: The Emperor’s Mind is Hard to Guess!","paragraphs":["The Chess Dao’s deduction was not omnipotent. It relied on using the \"known\" to calculate the \"unknown,\" rather than relying on abstract and mystical fortune-telling. Therefore, while Chen Yi could figure out many things, there were just as many he couldn’t predict.","For instance, Yan Fusha of the Five Poison Sect suddenly abducting Pei Guanli. Or \"Jackal\" Du Cang tracking his scent to the Xiao family’s home and subsequently kidnapping Xiao Wan’er. Or Liu Hong setting up a grand scheme involving the disaster refugees.","Chen Yi could, at most, deduce that Liu Hong was plotting something major, but he couldn’t figure out exactly what it was. He simply lacked the necessary clues.","However, regarding Liu Hong’s visit to the Xiao family’s home tomorrow, Chen Yi could roughly guess his intentions. The reason was simple. Currently, Liu Hong had no path left to take other than death or fleeing. For him to visit the Xiao family under such circumstances, it definitely wasn’t to offer himself up to be mocked and humiliated by Elder Master Xiao. That didn’t match Liu Hong’s temperament.","After mulling it over, only one option remained: finding a way to land a punch on the Xiao family. It wouldn’t do much physical harm, but the insult...","Chen Yi tipped up his bamboo hat, gazing at the several Government Offices in the distance on South Street. Rain fell like a curtain. Outside the offices, flickering torchlights dotted the darkness. Through the gloom, he could faintly make out dozens of Imprisonment Officers wearing raincoats and bamboo hats setting out into the night. General, Lady Tiger, and Simurgh Phoenix wore golden and silver tiger-patterned masks, each leading a squad of Imprisonment Officers to strike at various parts of the Prefecture City.","The sound of splashing footsteps echoed in quick succession. Chen Yi retracted his gaze and shook his head thoughtfully.","\"Liu Hong is indeed at the end of his rope and powerless to salvage the situation, but for him to have risen to the position of Governor of Shu State, his character and tactics are evident,\" Chen Yi murmured.","Therefore, the punch Liu Hong intended to throw at the Xiao family tomorrow would be no child’s play; it was bound to be calculated. Whether it was a hidden scheme or an overt plot was hard to judge. But Chen Yi was certain of one thing: Liu Hong was prepared to die.","He thought, \"They say ’when a man is near death, his words are meant well’?","\"Heh, that depends entirely on the person.\"","Chen Yi’s gaze swept over the myriad twinkling lights of the city before he silently returned to the Xiao family’s home. Compared to when he left earlier, the return trip took a bit longer, as he deliberately bypassed several Martial Artists whose Cultivation was clearly in the Upper Three Grades. Moreover, he wiped away some traces within the Purple Bamboo Forest to prevent certain individuals from noticing them upon their return.","Approaching the hour of the Ox, Chen Yi finally returned to his wing room. He changed into a lightweight long gown and sat cross-legged on the bed to cultivate the Four Symbols Skill.","Five days had passed since he broke through to the Fourth Grade, and his Cultivation had improved significantly. The \"God\" within his Forehead Acupoint grew stronger as his True Essence circulated, wrapping in thin strands around the Four Divine Positions. This not only heightened Chen Yi’s five senses but also made the Spiritual Power possessed by the Four Divine Positions increasingly formidable.","However, not long after entering a meditative state, his heart suddenly skipped a beat. He quickly snapped awake and laid down flat on the bed. The Black Tortoise Concealment Technique rapidly retracted all of his aura, simultaneously smoothing out the slightly disturbed Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism around him.","Faint snoring soon followed.","Just as Chen Yi settled everything, a beautiful silhouette descended from the north, stepping on a long sword. It was none other than Xiao Jinghong, returning from Guangyuan County. She merely cast a glance in the direction of the Spring Lotus Garden before dropping straight down into the Qingjing Residence.","Naturally, the entire Xiao Mansion was alerted by her arrival. Without needing orders, dozens of Armored Warriors took up posts around the Qingjing Residence.","Mr. Liu Si’er stood guard near the Martial Arts Arena, staring straight toward the front courtyard. Xiao Jinghong had returned right after the chaos in Shu State subsided. He couldn’t help but wonder how much of those events had to do with her. And then there was the Old Marquis...","A myriad of thoughts churned in Mr. Liu Si’er’s mind, but he didn’t dare avert his gaze, standing as still as a statue.","Inside the Qingjing Residence.","Elder Master Xiao had naturally been alerted as well. Throwing on an outer coat, he leaned on his cane and made his way to the main hall to take a seat. Xiao Jinghong was already waiting there. She bowed and greeted, \"Jinghong pays her respects to Grandfather.\"","Elder Master Xiao looked her over, then smiled and waved his hand for her to sit. \"There’s no need for such formalities among family. Are things settled over in Guangyuan?\"","After taking a seat, Xiao Jinghong replied concisely, \"Zhu Hao tried to run, so I killed him with a single sword strike.\"","\"You killed him?\" Elder Master Xiao looked at her with a hint of surprise. \"Tell me the details.\"","Xiao Jinghong gave a nod of affirmation and proceeded to recount the sequence of events. At the end, she said, \"Death is like a lamp going out. Li Fu originally intended to pin all the blame on Zhu Hao, but I refused.\"","After hearing the whole story, Elder Master Xiao sighed. \"You did the right thing.\"","However, he didn’t say anything further. His thick knuckles tapped against the back of his chair as he clearly pondered the repercussions of the matter.","Xiao Jinghong naturally understood that killing Zhu Hao had far-reaching consequences and that keeping him alive would have been more beneficial to the Xiao family. But doing so would have left her spirit unsettled. Choosing the lesser of two evils, it was better to kill him and end it all once and for all.","A moment later.","Elder Master Xiao looked at her and asked a few more questions, mostly regarding her opinions on Li Fu and the people from the Capital Prefecture.","Xiao Jinghong answered them one by one. \"There are numerous loopholes in the Capital Commandery’s management of salt and iron, especially regarding the embezzlement of the Dingyuan Army’s funds and provisions.","\"I believe that even though this matter involves a large number of people, that is still no excuse for Li Fu to try and downplay the matter.\"","Elder Master Xiao nodded slightly. \"It is understandable for Li Fu to think that way.","\"The situation in Guangyuan County is complex. As the Commander-in-Chief, he inherently needs to balance all factions and prioritize stability.\"","He paused, shifting the conversation. \"However, our Xiao family cannot be the ones to take a step back.","\"Zhu Hao had previously sinned against the Dingyuan Army. Now that he is dead, the people backing him must provide an explanation.","\"The only trouble is that Feng Erbao was also present at the scene. If the message he passes on to the Holy Emperor is biased...\"","Xiao Jinghong understood his meaning and said, \"If it is, then so be it.\"","Elder Master Xiao’s gaze sharpened slightly. \"Is that what you think?\"","Without backing down in the slightest, Xiao Jinghong looked straight at him. \"I believe the Holy Emperor should already be aware of the situation in Shu State. In fact, he might even...\""]},{"number":586,"title":"Chapter 586 - 332: The Emperor’s Mind Is Hard to Guess!","paragraphs":["\"Whether Eunuch Feng speaks of it or not, it will not affect the Holy Emperor’s view of Shu State or my Xiao Family.\"","Seeing Elder Master Xiao remain silent, she softened her tone and continued. \"Forgive me, Grandfather. I misspoke.","\"However, it is an undeniable fact that I have been hindered at every turn within the Dingyuan Army over the years. It is also a fact that the Holy Emperor and the court officials have remained entirely indifferent.\"","Hearing this, Elder Master Xiao looked at her with a slightly complex expression.","After a long silence, he retracted his gaze, relaxed his posture, and leaned back in his chair. A gratified smile returned to his face. \"Jinghong, you have grown so much over these years.\"","Xiao Jinghong lowered her head slightly and said softly, \"I just do not want to fail the spirits of my father and mother in heaven.\"","If Xiao Fengchun and Fu Wanqing hadn’t died in battle, why would she have enlisted in the army to prop up the massive Xiao Family?","After all, a person’s actions and thoughts were dictated by their position.","Since Xiao Jinghong had become the Commander-in-Chief of the Dingyuan Army, she could not afford to treat her duties like child’s play.","In the past, out of consideration for Elder Master Xiao’s feelings toward the Imperial Court and the Holy Emperor, she had made far too many concessions.","Now, she realized that doing so only encouraged outsiders to push their luck. Therefore, she was no longer willing to yield.","Moreover, even if not for herself, she had to consider the future of the Xiao Family, the Dingyuan Army, and Shu State.","Elder Master Xiao naturally understood all of this. Smiling, he shook his head. \"Liu Wu was right earlier. I have stayed secluded in the mansion for too long, always seeking compromise and stability. In doing so, I’ve chilled the hearts of many old comrades.\"","Xiao Jinghong looked at him. \"Grandfather, I didn’t—\"","Raising a hand to interrupt her, Elder Master Xiao said, \"I am not blaming you. On the contrary, you did the right thing.","\"In truth, when I had your second uncle take the memorial to the Capital Prefecture this time, aside from dealing with Liu Hong and Zhu Hao, it was also to test the Holy Emperor’s attitude toward our Xiao Family. And now...\"","His smile widened as he continued. \"Now, it seems the Holy Emperor has not forgotten our Xiao Family.\"","Xiao Jinghong paused. She wanted to say something, but upon seeing the look on her grandfather’s face, she simply nodded in silence.","Seeing this, Elder Master Xiao sighed inwardly.","How could he not know what Xiao Jinghong was thinking? How could he not understand the root cause of the Xiao Family’s current predicament?","But the Holy Emperor’s heart was difficult to fathom.","Often, the more one did, the more mistakes one made, ultimately leading to even more troublesome situations.","This was especially true now that their Xiao Family was steadily declining—at least compared to those in the north.","Instead, he hoped the Holy Emperor would remember the Xiao Family’s two centuries of toil in guarding the nation’s borders. He hoped the emperor would consider the family’s decline and the emptiness of Shu State, and shift his gaze toward the north.","Otherwise, even if the entire Xiao Family sacrificed themselves, how far beyond Mengshui Pass could they possibly conquer?","Were the Barbarian Race really that easy to kill?","His thoughts swirling, Elder Master Xiao kept his expression neutral and asked, \"What about Liu Hong?\"","Xiao Jinghong replied with a slightly heavy tone, \"Tomorrow afternoon, after Eunuch Feng’s carriage arrives at the Prefecture City, he will read the decree and apprehend him.\"","A hint of relief flashed through Elder Master Xiao’s eyes. \"That is good.","\"Once Liu Hong falls, the network of people he has gathered will lose their core. They will scatter and disperse, never to pose a real threat again.","\"It’s just that...\"","Elder Master Xiao looked toward the north and sighed. \"I wonder who the Holy Emperor will appoint to the position of Governor of Shu State.\"","Xiao Jinghong nodded, though she could not guess the candidate either.","Of course, in her opinion, the best candidate was Yang Ye.","That way, the Xiao Family would enjoy at least a year or two of peace.","Xiao Jinghong exhaled softly. She was just about to stand and announce her return to Feng Erbao’s carriage when she heard urgent footsteps approaching from outside the hall.","She immediately settled back into her seat.","A moment later, Xiao Jing’s figure appeared in the hall. Upon seeing Xiao Jinghong sitting to the side, he only paused for a second before dropping to one knee to report. \"Marquis, General. Something has happened in the Prefecture City tonight.\"","Elder Master Xiao exchanged a glance with Xiao Jinghong and asked deeply, \"What happened?\"","\"The White Tiger Guard has appeared. They are leading men from the Imprisonment Department to arrest people all over the city.\"","\"The White Tiger Guard? Who are they arresting?\"","\"The Sun Family, the Zhu Family...\"","Xiao Jing rattled off a few names in quick succession, unable to suppress his excitement. \"Even Ye Jingxiao, the Vice Inspector General of the Inspectorate Office, was taken down by someone wearing a golden mask!\"","Xiao Jinghong nodded in realization. \"The White Tiger Guard. A Golden Banner Officer.\"","A smile spread across Elder Master Xiao’s face. \"If the White Tiger Guard is making a move, they must have received word from the Capital Prefecture.","\"Liu Hong, Liu Gongmo—this time, you are doomed!\"","As soon as he finished speaking, he raised his hand slightly and ordered, \"Xiao Jing, go back out and continue monitoring the situation. Make absolutely sure to find out the specific identities and reasons behind these arrests.","\"This time, I will make every single one of those families cough up what they’ve swallowed.\"","Although he normally disdained kicking a man while he was down, the people surrounding Liu Hong were all scheming villains who wanted to tear the Xiao Family apart.","Toward such people, Elder Master Xiao naturally wouldn’t show any mercy.","Xiao Jing accepted the order and departed.","Xiao Jinghong then stood up to take her leave. \"Before nightfall, Eunuch Feng sent word that he has matters to discuss early tomorrow morning. I shall return first and enter the city with them.\"","Elder Master Xiao smiled and nodded. \"Very well.","\"Tomorrow, when Feng Erbao reads the decree condemning Liu Hong, your presence by his side will further intimidate anyone harboring malicious intentions toward our Xiao Family.\"","Xiao Jinghong bowed in respect before vanishing, leaving the Xiao Family mansion once again.","However, as she flew near the edge of the Prefecture City, her eyes subconsciously drifted toward the Spring Lotus Garden.","It was as if she could pierce through the heavy curtains of rain and the obstructing houses to see a figure with a gentle face.","She figured that once the dust settled on Liu Hong’s matter, Shu State would find peace...","Before she could finish her thought, Xiao Jinghong frowned, suddenly remembering something else—another pressing matter was fast approaching.","She wondered if it would bring trouble.","But after a moment of careful thought, her brow relaxed. Tearing through the curtain of rain, she headed straight toward the North City.","With Immortal Bai present, even if there was trouble, she was confident she could resolve it.","Elder Master Xiao, of course, was unaware of all this.","However, having received several pieces of good news tonight, he was smiling more joyously than he had in a long time.","Coupled with his recently robust health, he summoned the servants and ordered them to prepare some wine, meat, and dishes.","He then began to drink and eat by himself.","Meanwhile, in the Spring Lotus Garden, Chen Yi quietly opened his eyes. Looking toward the north, a helpless expression crossed his face.","His Madam leaping about high in the sky was truly a bit startling.","He had thought that since it was already late into the night, Xiao Jinghong wouldn’t return. He hadn’t expected her to come back so quickly.","If his Cultivation hadn’t reached the Fourth Grade, allowing him to comprehend the wondrous uses of \"God\", he really might not have been able to detect Xiao Jinghong’s arrival in advance.","Thinking this, Chen Yi rolled over, closed his eyes, and went to sleep.","Cultivation was out of the question now.","Who knew if his Madam would pull a surprise return?","The next morning.","The rain had lessened significantly, but the sky remained densely packed with dark clouds.","A chilling wind blew fiercely, filling the air with a howling WHOOSH.","Perhaps the cold wind was too clamorous, carrying the rumors within the Prefecture City to every corner along with it.","In the streets and alleys, most people were discussing last night’s events.","Things like who from which family was arrested by the Government Office, who was an official, and who was connected to whom.","Even the Wandering Martial Artists who had just arrived in Shu State joined in the commotion, cursing the corrupt officials to death with great interest.","Amidst the hubbub, some people asked for the reasons behind the arrests, but no one could provide a clear explanation.","Because of this, some people became agitated.","\"Mr. Lingchuan from Guiyun Academy was also arrested?\"","\"Why would he be arrested? Is it because of his older brother?\"","\"It’s highly likely.\"","\"Although the Zhu Family is a prestigious clan, Mr. Lingchuan has never involved himself in the family’s internal affairs. He only teaches at the academy.\"","\"He must have been implicated...\"","If the common folk believed this, how could the scholars of Guiyun Academy think otherwise?","Therefore, early in the morning, many scholars rushed to the academy to seek verification or ask for help.","Mr. Yue Ming was equally alarmed.","However, having weathered many storms, he wasn’t about to be swept up by the students’ panic. His attitude remained relatively cautious.","Mr. Zhuo Ying initially planned to do the same, but upon seeing an increasing number of students arriving, he had no choice but to visit Mr. Yue Ming’s residence.","\"Dean, this matter is of grave importance. It’s best if we clarify the reasons as soon as possible.","\"Moreover, with the Annual Examination approaching, it’s truly detrimental to disturb the students’ Heart Spirit at this critical juncture.\"","Mr. Yue Ming hummed in agreement and pondered, \"We definitely need to clarify things, but who should we ask...\"","Pausing for a moment, he came up with an idea. \"I will go find Lord Yang. As the Governor, he should have some information.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying’s expression relaxed. \"Then I’ll make a trip to the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office.\"","Standing up, Mr. Yue Ming said, \"The Imprisonment Department is indeed worth visiting. Also...\"","He looked at a few of the students gathered outside the door and added, \"Have someone go look for Qingzhou as well.\"","\"Qingzhou?\" Mr. Zhuo Ying asked.","\"He has been studying at the Marquis’s Mansion recently. I fear he might be unaware of this matter.","\"Even if he doesn’t know, that old fool Xiao Yuan definitely will...\""]},{"number":587,"title":"Chapter 587 - 333: Saving the Collapsing Edifice","paragraphs":["After coming to an agreement, Mr. Yue Ming and Mr. Zhuo Ying went their separate ways. One went to the Governor’s Office, while the other headed to the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office. They also instructed Ma Guan to visit the Xiao Family’s residence to see Chen Yi. The three of them, accompanied by the rest of the academy’s scholars, marched out of Guiyun Academy in a grand procession.","Under the overcast sky, the crowd surged like a river, heading straight south along Kangning Street. A few people branched off at the intersection of Chuansi Street. The remaining group split into two factions at South Street, taking up positions outside the Governor’s Office and the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office. Naturally, more scholars arrived after hearing the news. They mingled with the unaware commoners, all trying to pry into what exactly had happened the night before.","Annoyed beyond endurance, Liu Si—who couldn’t risk exposing the existence of the White Tiger Guard—ordered the Imprisonment Department to step forward and handle the situation. Several Thousand Households of the Imprisonment Department were equally troubled. After passing the buck back and forth, the task ultimately fell onto Fang Hongxiu’s shoulders.","She straightened her official robes and rested a hand on the hilt of her blade. Stepping outside the Government Office with a solemn expression, she swept her gaze over the crowd and announced sternly, \"This is a restricted area of the Government Office. All unauthorized personnel must step back at once!\"","The four Imprisonment Officers who accompanied her looked astonished. Turning their heads to look at her, they were left somewhat speechless.","\"Lord Hundred Households is truly as brave as ever...\"","She was indeed brave. However, the surrounding scholars were even fiercer.","A teacher from Guiyun Academy stepped out from the crowd. Cupping his hands in a salute, he raised his voice, \"Mr. Lingchuan of our Guiyun Academy has been arrested and brought to the Imprisonment Department. Dare I ask, what law has he broken?\"","\"That is classified. No comment!\"","\"Then how dare you arrest him?\"","\"We have conclusive evidence!\"","\"What evidence?\"","\"No comment...\"","Facing over a hundred scholars entirely on her own, Fang Hongxiu didn’t take a single step back. Her only response remained a steadfast \"No comment.\"","The teacher grew somewhat irritated. \"If you do not give us a proper explanation today, we will not leave!\"","\"That’s right, we’re not leaving!\"","\"We’d like to see just what your Imprisonment Department is capable of...\"","Hearing this, Fang Hongxiu furrowed her brow tightly. Her fingers tightened around her blade’s hilt; clearly, these people were annoying her to no end. Yet, she couldn’t afford to lose her temper. Most of the scholars present held official degrees and were backed by influential families. Any slight injury or mishap would bring her considerable trouble. Left with no choice, Fang Hongxiu could only try to stall for time, inwardly cursing those Lords Thousand Households to hell and back.","Meanwhile, the situation outside the Governor’s Office was far better. Although Chen Yunfan was dressed in his official robe, he lacked the slightest self-awareness expected of an Assistant Governor of the Governor’s Office. Sitting on the steps by the entrance, he casually chatted and joked with the people around him.","\"Everyone here has read the teachings of the sages. Surely you’ve heard of ’see no evil’ and ’speak no evil,’ right? Keep quiet. You’ll have your answers once your teachers come out.\"","\"Lord Assistant Governor, could you tell us what exactly happened?\"","\"What happened? I am in the dark as well.\"","\"Then why did you come out...\"","Chen Yunfan waved his hand and said with a smile, \"The air inside the Government Office is too stuffy. I just came out for some fresh air.\"","\"This...\"","\"No ’this’ or ’that.’ Either disperse now and go back to your respective homes, or wait quietly for news.\"","Chen Yunfan couldn’t care less about why these people were here; he only knew that staying outside was much better than handling official duties inside the Government Office. Of course, he also couldn’t tell these scholars the truth. At least, not before the dust had settled. If certain people caught wind of it and ended up running away or dying by accident, it would cause unnecessary trouble for the people in the Government Office.","While dealing with the noisy crowd, Chen Yunfan occasionally cast a glance back at the Governor’s Office. In truth, he was somewhat gloating. Unlike Zhu Hao, Liu Hong was the Governor of Shu State; his intellect, political maneuvers, and family background were all leaps and bounds ahead of Zhu Hao’s. Zhu Hao’s downfall was purely his own stupidity—carelessly letting the White Tiger Guard find evidence of his crimes. Liu Hong, on the other hand, had his claws and fangs systematically shattered one by one by Brother Yi. To have such a perfect advantage ruined by a single person meant he deserved his fate.","What Chen Yunfan found most amusing, however, was that Liu Hong would likely go to his grave without ever knowing \"Liu Wu’s\" true identity. How could he not find it entertaining that Liu Hong would die with such lingering grievances?","Just as Chen Yunfan was pondering this, a calm voice rang out from behind him.","\"Assistant Governor Chen.\"","Hmm?","Chen Yunfan turned to look, his pupils suddenly shrinking. He saw Liu Hong standing at the top edge of the steps outside the Governor’s Office, looking down at him.","That alone wouldn’t have been a big deal. Although Liu Hong was dressed impeccably in his grand red official robe and black jade belt, his posture still somewhat upright, his face was almost unrecognizable. His thick hair, now mostly white, was neatly combed and coiled into a bun at the back of his head, secured with a hairpin. His face was covered in dense wrinkles, radiating sheer old age. Most notably, his eyes were incredibly cloudy, resembling those of a frail old man who had just suffered a severe illness.","While Chen Yunfan was in a daze, a faint smile tugged at Liu Hong’s lips. He looked at him with a half-smile and said, \"Assistant Governor Chen, you are blocking the way.\"","Snapping back to reality, Chen Yunfan stood up and stepped to the side. With a slight bow, he greeted, \"Lord Liu.\"","\"Assistant Governor Chen, being amicable with the people is a good thing, but remember one thing,\" Liu Hong said, tilting his head to look at him. \"You are the Assistant Governor of the Governor’s Office. An official must carry an air of authority. Blind humility and strict adherence to etiquette will only cause the base and petty to look down on you.\"","Chen Yunfan was slightly taken aback. Meeting his gaze, he hesitantly accepted the advice, \"Your Lordship is right to lecture me.\"","Liu Hong smiled and nodded. Clasping his hands behind his back, he walked straight toward the crowd. His emaciated frame radiated a feeble aura, yet it felt as though he carried an immense, unyielding weight. With every step he took, several people directly in his path stepped aside and bowed in respect. In just over a dozen steps, Liu Hong had passed through the crowd, heading toward the East Market.","Among the scholars and commoners gathered outside the Governor’s Office, not a single person dared to clamor and make noise like before. No one even dared to meet his gaze. It was only after Liu Hong had walked far away that these people finally opened their mouths to speak."]},{"number":588,"title":"Chapter 588 - 333: Turning the Tide","paragraphs":["Muted voices drifted over.","\"Lord Liu, the Governor... his aura truly terrifies me...\"","\"Me too.\"","\"For some reason, when he just looked over, I felt like all my strength was drained. I could barely stand...\"","Whether they were scholars or commoners, none could compare to Liu Hong, whose mastery over his qi was absolute. Chen Yunfan watched Liu Hong walking slowly in the distance through the rain, a slightly strange expression on his face.","He was certain that Liu Hong’s sharpness was even more piercing today than ever before, despite his visible old age. That kind of aura he had only seen in three people: the Chen Family Patriarch Chen Xuanji, Chen Xuandu, and the Cui Family Patriarch, the current Celestial Minister Cui Mao.","The former two possessed a calm composure, while the latter was like a solitary boat on a boundless sea—tranquil and completely undisturbed. But Liu Hong... he exuded pure disdain. It was as if there was no longer anyone or anything in this world worthy of his attention. His entire being radiated an unbridled arrogance, which starkly contrasted his peaceful demeanor from just moments ago.","Chen Yunfan watched thoughtfully as Liu Hong walked away. Retracting his gaze, he ignored the scholars and turned to walk into the Governor’s Office. He immediately saw Li Huai’gu walking briskly toward him. Without even stopping to greet him, Li Huai’gu tried to bypass him and head out.","Chen Yunfan grabbed him. \"Brother Huai’gu, where are you going?\"","Li Huai’gu tried to shake off his hand, but forget breaking free—he couldn’t even lift his arm. He looked at Chen Yunfan in astonishment and said urgently, \"I have urgent business. Please let me go, Brother Yunfan.\"","\"Are you going to chase after Lord Liu?\"","\"Yes... Uh, how did you know?\"","Chen Yunfan let go of his hand. Instead of answering, he pointed toward the East Market and said, \"Lord Liu went that way. Hurry up and go.\"","Li Huai’gu rubbed his wrist and, without asking any more questions, hurried off in the direction he had pointed. Chen Yunfan glanced at him and then went straight to where Yang Ye was. He also wanted to figure out the reason behind Liu Hong’s unusual behavior.","After bypassing two side rooms, Chen Yunfan arrived at the inner hall and vaguely heard the voices of Yang Ye and Mr. Yue Ming inside.","\"...Liu Gongmo probably already knows that something has happened,\" Yang Ye’s voice drifted out.","\"I didn’t expect that arresting so many people last night would actually be tied to him,\" Mr. Yue Ming sighed. \"Lingchuan... what a pity...\"","\"Those who commit many injustices are doomed to destroy themselves,\" Yang Ye replied. \"During the Mid-Autumn Poetry Gathering, I already noticed something off between Liu Gongmo and Zhu Lingchuan. Do you remember?\"","Mr. Yue Ming recalled for a moment and slowly nodded. \"That night, there were teachers from academies in other State Capitals. During their verbal sparring, Lingchuan intentionally or unintentionally spoke up for Liu Gongmo a few times.\"","Yang Ye sighed, \"Looking back now, there were signs early on.\" He looked toward the door and paused slightly when he saw Chen Yunfan. Gesturing for him to come in, he continued, \"I wonder what he went out for.\"","Chen Yunfan walked straight into the hall, greeted them one by one, and sat to the side, acting as if he was just there to listen.","Mr. Yue Ming glanced at him and said, \"Let him be. Whether he’s fleeing or just strolling, we can’t stop him.\"","Yang Ye nodded silently.","Confused, Chen Yunfan saw them fall silent and couldn’t help but ask, \"What did Lord Liu say just before he left?\"","Yang Ye hesitated slightly, nodded, and sighed. \"He did say something, but it was incomprehensible.","\"He said that to establish oneself, one must be ruthless. That was where he lost; otherwise, he wouldn’t have ended up in this situation today.\"","Chen Yunfan was puzzled. \"Ruthless?\"","Mr. Yue Ming added, \"Liu Gongmo also said that the younger generation is formidable, but I don’t know who he was referring to.\"","The name Chen Yi popped into Chen Yunfan’s mind. He frowned slightly and asked, \"Where is Liu Hong going?\"","Yang Ye and Mr. Yue Ming shook their heads. \"We don’t know...\"","Hearing this, Chen Yunfan’s expression darkened slightly. However, his feet seemed rooted to the ground; he didn’t get up to run out of the Governor’s Office to chase after Liu Hong. He knew very well that if Liu Hong really wanted to plot against Chen Yi, he would only be digging his own grave.","\"Brother Yi, oh Brother Yi, I’m waiting to watch a good show. Don’t disappoint me,\" he thought.","In truth, no one could guess Liu Hong’s intentions. Even he himself seemed to be wandering aimlessly. After coming out of the Governor’s Office, Liu Hong walked eastward and turned south at the alley entrance at the end of the East Market.","The rain was continuous, and the cold wind howled, but he looked as if he was enjoying it, unhurriedly passing through the crowd and weaving through the streets and alleys. Occasionally, when he saw people bowing in greeting, Liu Hong would just nod in response without stopping. But if he saw something interesting, he would pause to watch for a while. He would even chat with commoners like an ordinary old man, talking about the past and discussing recent hardships.","\"Grain prices won’t rise anymore. The Government Office will naturally keep an eye on those grain merchants...\"","\"The end of the year is approaching. Wishing you peace and health...\"","\"Your boy is cut out for studying. If you lack the money to support him, I have some broken silver here. It will at least let him attend a private school for a year...\"","When Li Huai’gu finally found Liu Hong, he saw him pulling out a few pieces of silver and handing them to an old woman. As if sensing his presence, Liu Hong patted the child’s head while waving to Li Huai’gu.","After Li Huai’gu caught up, Liu Hong clasped his hands behind his back and walked west. Even when standing in South City Yanhua Lane, Liu Hong wore an appreciative expression, much like a traveler. He walked around, taking in the sights.","Li Huai’gu fell half a step behind, following him closely.","It wasn’t until the two bypassed the Spring Rain Building and turned north that Liu Hong finally spoke. \"Ever since I was promoted to Governor, I haven’t had the leisure to carefully look at this city.","\"It’s not that I didn’t want to, but my eyes were always looking forward and upward. It became difficult to lower my head and look at what was right beneath my feet.\"","Li Huai’gu was slightly taken aback, unsure of what to say.","Liu Hong ignored him and continued speaking to himself, \"Like you, I was the third-ranking scholar in the imperial examinations during the fifth year of the Anhe era.\""]},{"number":589,"title":"Chapter 589 - 333: Turning the Tide","paragraphs":["\"I was twenty-seven then. In the blink of an eye, sixteen years have passed. I traveled from Capital Prefecture to Ji State, and then back from Ji State to Shu State. It took me twelve full years just to secure the position of Governor.\"","Looking at the gradually lowering rooftops of the houses on both sides, Liu Hong said with deep emotion, \"It seems fast, a stroke of good fortune, but in reality, I am far behind certain people.","\"Let’s not talk about those far away, but look closer, like Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion.","\"Xiao Fengchun is a mere martial artist, yet relying purely on his birth and bloodline, he easily secured the position of Marquis Wu.","\"He could effortlessly obtain what the rest of us strive for our entire lives, while our lifelong efforts are often in vain.","\"How is that fair?\"","Although his words contained complaints, Liu Hong’s tone remained unchanged, as if he were merely recounting a very ordinary matter.","\"Therefore, since arriving in Shu State, I have had no eyes for anyone else. My sole aim has been to be the ’number one’ among my peers.","\"Even more so, to erase the gap between Jing State Liu Family and the Xiao Family.","\"Unfortunately, I have failed...\"","Li Huai’gu felt a deep shock in his heart upon hearing this. This was the first time he had heard Liu Hong’s past in such detail. Even though he had heard snippets before, it was not nearly as shocking as hearing it personally from Liu Hong right now.","Liu Hong seemed to sense his reaction. He turned his head, smiled, and asked, \"Advisor Li, have you established your life’s ambition?\"","Li Huai’gu recovered his wits and hesitated, \"I have studied since I was young, all in order to...\"","Liu Hong raised a hand to interrupt him. \"To save the empire from collapse and rescue the people from suffering?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Heh, I once had that ambition too.\"","Li Huai’gu froze for a moment, looking at him in astonishment.","Liu Hong smiled and withdrew his gaze. He stopped on Chuansi Street, looked east toward the Xiao Family, and asked, \"But have you ever thought about how many commoners actually need saving during a prosperous era of peace? If the empire isn’t collapsing, how much of your capability can you actually put to use?","\"Even if you compare yourself to the sages and capable ministers of the past, you can only bow down to the trivial matters of the marketplace.","\"This is the ultimate destination for scholars like us.\"","As Liu Hong spoke, he walked toward the Xiao Family, the smile in his voice disappearing little by little.","\"Advisor Li, come. Follow me and bear witness for me.\"","Li Huai’gu watched him walk forward with steady steps, but his own feet felt as if they had been filled with lead. It wasn’t until Liu Hong had walked over a hundred feet away that he gritted his teeth and followed. In his heart, however, he continuously denied Liu Hong’s earlier words.","Scholars in a prosperous era could still be capable ministers; they could still act for the common people and protect a region. A chaotic era... To hell with a chaotic era! When Li Huai’gu was young, he had experienced the invasion of the Barbarian Race. He had seen nine out of ten houses left empty, and he had seen the white mourning silk hung in front of every residence in the alleys. If one were to deliberately do things contrary to the supreme principles of the sages just to display their talents and rival the ancient sages of the past, they would be worse than animals.","Naturally, Liu Hong didn’t care about Li Huai’gu’s thoughts. Upon arriving outside the Xiao Family, he straightened his robes and called out clearly toward the vermilion gates, \"Liu Hong of the Governor’s Office has come to visit Marquis Xiao.\"","The voice carried inside the gates. Without hesitation, Third Steward Lu Guan hurriedly opened the main doors, cupped his hands, and said, \"Lord Liu.\"","Liu Hong smiled and nodded. \"Please announce my arrival.\"","\"Please wait a moment, Lord Liu. I’ll go right now...\"","A short while later, Elder Master Xiao’s voice rang out from inside Qingjing Residence.","\"Invite him in.\"","Receiving the order, Lu Guan went to the front courtyard and led Liu Hong and Li Huai’gu all the way toward Qingjing Residence. Along the way, the Armored Warriors and servants all wore solemn expressions. Liu Hong turned a blind eye to this, walking in front with a composed look.","The pattering rain had unknowingly grown a bit heavier, beating against the roof tiles of the corridor. The PIT-PAT sound echoed endlessly.","Inside Spring Lotus Garden.","Chen Yi had already sensed this. He turned his head to look over, a smile tugging at the corners of his lips. \"This one came... quite early.\""]},{"number":590,"title":"Chapter 590 - 334: Reigning Supreme","paragraphs":["Coincidentally, Xiaodie hurried over, saying that the Eldest Miss had already prepared the meal.","Chen Yi nodded, signaling her to go ahead. He withdrew his gaze and looked at Ma Guan and the others sitting in front of him, saying with a smile,","\"I truly know nothing about Mr. Lingchuan’s situation.\"","Ma Guan hesitated, wanting to ask further, but he heard Chen Yi say, \"However, there’s no need for you all to worry.","\"Perhaps by the time you return to the academy, Mr. Yue Ming and Mr. Zhuo Ying will have already brought back some news.\"","Beside Ma Guan, Tang Ye asked, \"Sir, do you think the Government Office might have wrongfully arrested Mr. Lingchuan?\"","Chen Yi couldn’t help but laugh. Shaking his head, he said, \"I’ve been busy preparing for the Annual Examination lately. Where would I find the time to overthink this?\"","Seeing Ma Guan, Tang Ye, and the others hesitate to speak, he stood up and said, \"You cannot judge some people just by their surface appearances, just as you cannot judge some matters merely by right or wrong.","\"I won’t comment on what kind of person Mr. Lingchuan is, nor whether he broke the law, but I believe the Shu State Government Office wouldn’t act without grounds.","\"Especially against a tutor of our Guiyun Academy.\"","Ma Guan opened his mouth. \"Sir, are you saying Lingchuan...\"","Chen Yi glared at him, interrupting his words, and said in an exasperated tone, \"Perhaps the people from the Government Office merely invited Mr. Lingchuan over to ask a few questions.\"","This was already a highly perfunctory response.","He truly had no good impression of Zhu Lingchuan—what was there to say about someone who associated with Liu Hong?","But since Ma Guan, Tang Ye, and the others had come with earnest hearts, it wasn’t appropriate for him to reveal the harsh truth and make these students see Zhu Lingchuan’s true colors.","Offering a single phrase distinguishing between surface and reality, right and wrong, was his limit.","Chen Yi said no more, waving his hand to signal Ma Guan, Tang Ye, and the others to follow him out of the wooden building.","\"The Annual Examination is approaching. Don’t let these matters affect your grades. If you miss the upcoming Prefecture Examination because of this, I believe even Mr. Lingchuan would regret it upon finding out.\"","Ma Guan, Tang Ye, and the others exchanged glances before bowing in respect. \"Sorry for disturbing you, sir. We will take our leave now.\"","Chen Yi hummed in acknowledgment, quietly watching them walk away. His gaze then crossed a distance of hundreds of feet, landing inside the Qingjing Residence.","There, Liu Hong and Li Huai’gu had already been led into the Qingjing Residence by Lu Guan and arrived in the main hall.","The rain PATTERED incessantly, SPLASHING water onto the bluestone slabs of the courtyard.","The accumulated rainwater carried scattered fallen leaves and petals, flowing toward the lower stone troughs before merging into the pond.","The crisp and chaotic sound disturbed the surrounding quietude.","Chen Yi calculated the hour. It was three quarters past Noon, so he slightly lifted the restrictions of his Black Tortoise Concealment Technique.","Wisps of True Essence leveraged Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, gathering it to his ears.","Elder Master Xiao’s voice could be heard clearly.","\"Liu Gongmo, coming to find me right before your death, do you have something to say?\"","The corners of Chen Yi’s mouth curled up slightly. The elder ultimately couldn’t suppress his anger.","Such aggressiveness truly didn’t resemble a victor who had gained the upper hand. Instead, it made him seem like someone whose lingering fury hadn’t dissipated—a person who had swallowed a bitter loss and remained resentful.","As for Liu Hong...","He seemed to have long anticipated that the elder would know about this matter. Without waiting for an invitation, he sat down on the Grandmaster’s Chair beside the elder.","Then, waving his hand to gesture for the somewhat stunned and surprised Li Huai’gu to sit, he nodded and said, \"I have some words that I must get off my chest. I hope Marquis Xiao can forgive me.\"","Elder Master Xiao remained noncommittal. Resting his hands on the back of his chair, with the cane he had leaned on for five years placed by his feet, he glanced at Li Huai’gu and snorted, \"I thought that with your great capabilities, Liu Gongmo, and having done such massive deeds, you had completely disregarded my Xiao Family.\"","Seeing the two prominent figures of Shu State looking over, Li Huai’gu’s forehead instantly broke out in sweat. He quickly suppressed his shock and carefully sat in a seat near the hall’s entrance.","He couldn’t help but be shocked.","Liu Hong was about to die?","How could the life of a Second-Grade Officer of the current dynasty just vanish like that?","Li Huai’gu recalled Liu Hong’s earlier actions of roaming the streets and alleys, as well as the words he had spoken. A faint realization dawned in his heart.","What Marquis Xiao said must be true. Liu Hong, Governor Liu, was truly going to die.","The reason... perhaps it had something to do with what Liu Hong had said earlier...","Did he want to be a capable minister in chaotic times, one who could save the nation from collapse and rescue the people from disaster?","No.","He probably wanted to be a ruthless overlord of troubled times.","If that were the case, how could Liu Hong not die?","After a moment of silence, Elder Master Xiao glanced at the sky outside the door and sneered, \"Liu Gongmo, you don’t have much time left.\"","Xiao Jinghong had come to tell him last night that Feng Erbao would arrive at the Prefecture City today with the Holy Emperor’s decree.","Calculating the hour, they should be arriving at the Prefecture City any moment now.","Although Liu Hong didn’t know when the people from the Capital Prefecture would arrive, it wasn’t hard for him to deduce some outcomes from the arrest of Zhu Lingchuan and the others last night.","Either today or tomorrow, when the Holy Emperor’s decree arrived, he would be taken to the Capital Prefecture.","Moreover, he also knew that it was absolutely impossible for him to return to the Capital Prefecture safely.","Those people would not let him live.","The smile on Liu Hong’s face remained. Glancing at the cane from the corner of his eye, he smiled and said, \"Congratulations, Marquis Xiao.\"","\"Congratulations?\"","\"Marquis Xiao’s robust health is a blessing for Shu State and a fortune for the Great Wei. How could I not offer you my congratulations?\"","Elder Master Xiao turned his head to look at him. \"Spit it out.\"","He truly didn’t want to waste words with a dying man, much less bother pretending.","But seeing Liu Hong’s hair, which seemed to have turned white overnight, and his greatly aged face, he held back his impending outburst of temper.","Liu Hong chuckled and said, \"Marquis Xiao has misunderstood.","\"It’s true that I came this time with some things to say, but don’t you have anything you want to ask me, Marquis Xiao?\"","Elder Master Xiao frowned and glared at him, clenching his thick fists. His anger was clearly surging.","\"Do you really think I don’t know about the things you’ve done?","\"Colluding with the Barbarian Race, conspiring with the Ji State Trading Company to smuggle ironware, and instructing the Five Poison Sect to poison the disaster refugees with the intent to harm the entire region...\""]},{"number":591,"title":"Chapter 591 - 334: Claiming Hegemony","paragraphs":["\"Item by item, case by case, it’s enough for you and everyone in the Jing State Liu Family’s nine generations to lose their heads!\"","Li Huai’gu was dumbfounded. What was he hearing? He doubted his own ears.","Colluding with the Barbarian Race, illegally selling military weapons, spreading the epidemic poison... Liu Hong did all these things? The Governor of Shu State did this?","Liu Hong’s expression remained unchanged. He nodded, then shook his head, saying, \"Marquis Xiao is mostly correct, but there are some errors and omissions.","\"The person secretly selling ironware and ore was Zhu Hao of the Capital Commandery. I merely added fuel to the flames.","\"Colluding with the Barbarian Race... If Marquis Xiao is referring to Asutai, the youngest son of the Barbarian Race’s Left King Mu Hage, then you should be thanking me instead.\"","Elder Master Xiao laughed out of extreme anger. \"You let him go, and you expect this old man to thank you?","\"What a joke!\"","Liu Hong nodded solemnly. \"The person who let him go wasn’t me, but someone else.","\"It was ’Dragon Tiger’ Liu Wu.","\"The very same Liu Wu who has repeatedly helped your Xiao Family.\"","Elder Master Xiao frowned slightly, looking at him with icy eyes. \"Are you courting death?\"","Seeing his expression, Liu Hong knew the Marquis thought he was sowing discord, so he patiently explained, \"It was indeed the work of the ’Dragon Tiger.’","\"In fact, after the barbarian slave uprising in the East Market, several of my subordinates did take Asutai away.","\"But before they could transfer him out, that Liu Wu beat us to it and snatched him away.","\"After that, a long time passed. It wasn’t until the day before your Eldest Miss met with a mishap that he delivered Asutai to me.\"","Seeing that Elder Master Xiao didn’t interrupt, Liu Hong continued, \"Later, when Liu Wu went to rescue Miss Wan’er, he brought Lv Jiunan along.","\"At that time, Lv Jiunan wasn’t dead yet.\"","Hearing this, Elder Master Xiao couldn’t help but recall the night Xiao Wan’er had her accident, when Liu Wu appeared at the Qingjing Residence. That day, Liu Wu had produced some evidence directly pointing at Liu Hong—claiming he was colluding with the Barbarian Race, the Poshisu Country, and others.","So, Liu Wu had interrogated Asutai and Lv Jiunan to get all this? But why did he let Asutai go?","Seeming to guess his thoughts, Liu Hong smiled and said, \"Why did Liu Wu return the person to me?","\"The reason is quite simple.","\"He wanted to use this to solidify the suspicion that I was connected to the Barbarian Race, forcing me to take a desperate risk.\"","Pausing for a moment, a trace of bitterness finally appeared on Liu Hong’s face. \"The reality was just as he calculated. I panicked.","\"Anxious to succeed and eager to cover everything up, I had the Five Poison Sect make a move, which coincidentally aligned with the arrival of the refugees from Guang’an County and other areas.","\"Who could have known that the outcome... would backfire so completely.","\"Not only was the epidemic poison neutralized by Liu Wu, but even my arrangements against the Ji State Trading Company were seen through one by one. In the end, I lost everything.\"","During these recent days, Liu Hong hadn’t attended to Government Office affairs. He had dedicated all his mind to finding out the reason why his plans had failed. He wanted to know where things went wrong and where someone had found a loophole to exploit.","After much deliberation, he surprisingly discovered that the situation had taken a sharp downturn after the Mid-Autumn Festival. More accurately, it started after Lv Jiunan arrived in Shu State, and Liu Taofang was framed by Lin Huai’an of the Ji State Trading Company.","That was the first time in all these years that Liu Hong had acted without regard for the bigger picture, all to clear away hidden dangers for his own son. As a result, it left a fatal hidden danger for himself.","Lin Huai’an’s death had directly affected Zhu Hao’s trade with King Landu, causing internal problems within the Ji State Trading Company. Lin Zhenghong, who replaced him, lacked the brains, finesse, and seniority to maintain the situation in Shu State, allowing Liu Wu to exploit the gaps. Then Lv Jiunan, Asutai, Du Cang, Zeng Zhifeng, and the Five Poison Sect suffered accidents one after another, leading to the complete collapse of an otherwise excellent situation.","When Liu Hong figured all this out, besides lamenting that he wasn’t ruthless enough, he also attributed it to the Xiao Family’s good luck. If Liu Wu hadn’t intervened, how could his years of planning have failed?","And then there were those incompetent bunglers on the Ancient Tea-Horse Road—the horse bandits. If they hadn’t abducted Asutai and brought him to Shu State, forcing Lv Jiunan to personally come to Shu State, how could the subsequent events have happened?","Listening to Liu Hong’s words, Li Huai’gu’s face no longer showed shock, but extreme horror. He looked at Liu Hong in disbelief, never expecting that this Governor—a high-ranking Imperial Court official holding absolute power in Shu State—would commit such wicked deeds.","Li Huai’gu stood up abruptly and questioned, \"Wh-why?","\"Liu, Liu Hong, Liu Gongmo, wh-why did you do all that?!","\"Do you know, do you have any idea how many people would have died if you had succeeded?!\"","Liu Hong paused upon hearing this, turned his head to look at him, and said noncommittally, \"Have you forgotten what I just told you?","\"People of our generation achieve greatness in times of turmoil and chaos. Otherwise, living a mediocre life, one is nothing more than a dog in times of peace.","\"What I did was merely add fuel to the fire in Shu State, burning a hole so those foreign enemies could find an opportunity to strike.","\"That way, both I and Marquis Xiao would have a place to unleash our abilities.\"","Finishing his sentence, Liu Hong paused and looked at Li Huai’gu with a half-smile. \"And you, the Third Place Scholar, would also have the chance to showcase your talents, wouldn’t you?\"","Li Huai’gu’s face instantly flushed red. \"No, incorrect, that’s not it!","\"This is simply twisted logic and heresy!","\"You... you are committing high treason!","\"To think you call yourself a scholar, bah! I-I am ashamed to be associated with you!\"","Being cursed at like this, Liu Hong’s expression actually became even more tranquil. He didn’t bother to explain further, turning instead to Elder Master Xiao.","\"Actually, aside from these, I have done a few other major things.\"","Elder Master Xiao’s expression was equally ugly. The way he looked at Liu Hong was like looking at a madman. He hadn’t planned to waste any more words on him, intending to just let him die."]},{"number":592,"title":"Chapter 592 - 334: Claiming Supremacy","paragraphs":["Unexpectedly, Liu Hong’s next words shattered Elder Master Xiao’s remaining composure.","\"The thing I am most proud of happened five years ago, during the Barbarian Race’s invasion.\" Liu Hong looked at Elder Master Xiao, a smug smirk surfacing on his face. \"I was the one who leaked Xiao Fengchun’s location to the Barbarian Race!\"","Elder Master Xiao froze. His anger dissipated significantly, replaced by sheer disbelief, as if he doubted his own ears. \"W-what did you say?\"","\"Did Marquis Xiao not hear me? I will repeat it.","\"Back then, when Xiao Fengchun successfully led the iron cavalry to raid the Barbarian Race’s supplies, I was the one who tipped them off, drawing their...\"","Before Liu Hong could finish, a fist the size of a bowl loomed in his vision and smashed into his face.","BAM.","Liu Hong was sent flying backward, crashing heavily against the wall.","Before he could even react, fists rained down on his face and body, one punch after another.","Had Elder Master Xiao not retained a shred of rationality and refrained from using his True Essence, those few punches alone would have been enough to blow Liu Hong’s head clean off.","\"Why?!","\"Why did you do this?!","\"Speak!\"","Li Huai’gu watched the scene unfold, completely at a loss. Unable to step forward and intervene, he could only watch helplessly as Elder Master Xiao battered Liu Hong with punch after punch.","At that moment, Xiao Shen arrived.","Seeing the situation in the hall, he hurriedly rushed forward to hold Elder Master Xiao back. \"Brother, Brother, stop! Stop!\"","\"Scram!\"","Elder Master Xiao flung his arm, tossing Xiao Shen aside. Just as he was about to resume his beating, Xiao Shen cried out in pain.","\"Brother, the imperial court has sent people!","\"Jinghong is bringing them here right now. They said they’re here to announce an imperial decree condemning Liu Hong. You... you can’t hit him anymore!","\"If you beat him to death, you... you...\"","Elder Master Xiao delivered two more punches. His eyes were bloodshot and his face was flushed with fury. One hand still maintained a death grip on Liu Hong’s neck, pinning him against the wall.","\"Speak! Who ordered you to do this?!\"","Liu Hong’s already aged face was now battered beyond recognition. Blood seeped from the corners of his mouth and the bridge of his nose, his eye sockets were bruised and purple, and his entire face was severely swollen.","Yet, he was still smiling. Coughing weakly, he gasped, \"N-no one ordered me. Heh...","\"Marquis Xiao, you are Marquis Xiao... Your son was also Marquis Xiao. But I, Liu Hong, am merely... merely from the third branch of the Jing State Liu Family...","\"If it weren’t for... for my diligent studying, I could never have hoped to even measure up to the Xiao Family’s prestige in my entire life.","\"Ever since I arrived in Shu State, I knew very well that Shu State belonged to the Xiao Family. If Xiao Fengchun was still alive, even if I became the Governor, I would still have to act according to the Xiao Family’s whims...\"","Elder Master Xiao panted heavily, his fists clenching and unclenching.","He absolutely refused to believe that his son had died for such a ridiculous reason.","What did he mean, Shu State belonged to the Xiao Family?","What did he mean, act according to the Xiao Family’s whims?","The Xiao Family had guarded the borders of Great Wei for two hundred years. Every generation had shed blood and died on the battlefield. They had never once thought of ruling over Shu State as kings.","Why was it that, in the eyes of people like Liu Hong, it had become the Xiao Family’s fault?","No matter how consumed by rage Elder Master Xiao was, the impending arrival of the envoys from the Capital Prefecture forced him to suppress his urge to kill Liu Hong.","\"Liu Gongmo, you and the Liu Family will pay the price for what you’ve done!\"","With that, Elder Master Xiao was about to release his grip, but Liu Hong suddenly grabbed his hand and softly uttered a name.","\"Marquis Xiao, did you know that General... General Fu, she didn’t...\"","Elder Master Xiao’s eyes widened sharply. He slammed a fist into Liu Hong’s abdomen, forcing the rest of his words back down his throat.","\"Shut up!","\"If you dare leak another word, I will kill you!\"","Liu Hong clutched his stomach with both hands, coughing incessantly. His face flushed completely red, yet he struggled to speak.","\"Hehe... Marquis Xiao knows about the Barbarian Race... Hehe... Fu... Fu...\"","Elder Master Xiao threw another punch.","But Liu Hong continued to speak.","Simultaneously, footsteps approached from outside the Qingjing Residence behind them. Among them was none other than Xiao Jinghong.","\"Marquis Xiao, Fu...\"","Before he could finish, a resounding BAM echoed through the air.","Blood splattered.","Unable to tolerate it any longer, Elder Master Xiao drove his fist straight through Liu Hong’s chest, pinning him to the wall as crimson stained the surface behind him.","Despite such a fatal blow, Liu Hong showed no signs of agony in his final moments. Instead, he forced out a smile, as if his scheme had finally succeeded.","\"Heh... hehe... Thank... thank you, Marquis Xiao...\"","As blood bubbled from his lips, Liu Hong could no longer speak. Yet, he mustered his very last ounce of strength to trace a few words onto Elder Master Xiao’s wrist.","Reading the words, Elder Master Xiao’s expression changed drastically once more. He clenched his fist and struck out again.","At the same time, a voice rang out from behind him.","\"Marquis Xiao, wait...\""]},{"number":593,"title":"Chapter 593 - 335: Liu Wu Is Light...","paragraphs":["BANG!","A deafening crash echoed from the Qingjing Residence.","Instantly, the entire courtyard fell dead silent.","Even the chilly, late-autumn rain seemed to lose its momentum, falling soundlessly into the yard.","Chen Yi held his Oil Paper Umbrella and headed toward the Jiaxing Garden. His expression remained calm and indifferent, as if he hadn’t heard the commotion at all.","He remained unfazed even as two lines of glowing golden text drifted across his vision.","[Witnessed Shu State’s Duke Dingyuan, Xiao Yuan, kill Governor Liu Hong with a Punch. Reward: \"Essentials of Qi Min\", Opportunity +42.]","[Evaluation: Person arrived, sound heard, scene unseen...]","Chen Yi glanced at the text. Instead of worry, a smile crept onto his face.","\"Well played, Liu Hong,\" Chen Yi murmured softly. \"Even in death, you managed to force the Xiao Family into a dilemma. You certainly had some brains. Now Elder Master Xiao... and Madam, are probably going to have a massive headache.\"","Outside the main hall of the Qingjing Residence, Feng Erbao stood wearing a round-collared scarlet silk robe. A solitary crane was embroidered on his chest, and a gold-inlaid Jade Belt encircled his waist. In his hand, he held a Duster pointing directly into the hall.","Beside him stood Xiao Jinghong, dressed in her usual casual attire—a long green robe tightly secured by a waistband. Her customary Long Sword, Qing Feng, hung by her side.","Although her eyes flickered with a hint of surprise, she maintained a relatively calm expression as she took in the bloody scene inside the hall.","The surrounding imperial envoys, eunuchs, and Forbidden Palace Guards from the Imperial City all shared Feng Erbao’s reaction—a chaotic mix of sheer shock and panic.","Inside the main hall.","The furious glare had yet to fade from Elder Master Xiao’s face after he had shattered Liu Hong’s head with a single Punch. He took a few heavy breaths before managing to regain some composure.","Once settled, he swung his arm and tossed Liu Hong’s lifeless body out the door. The corpse rolled to a halt right at Feng Erbao’s feet.","Feng Erbao glanced at the murderous Elder Master Xiao, then down at Liu Hong’s corpse. His face turned livid as he slowly retracted his Duster, resting it against the crook of his arm.","\"Marquis Xiao, Liu Hong was explicitly requested by the Holy Emperor to be escorted back to the Capital Prefecture. Acting so recklessly truly puts me in a difficult position,\" Feng Erbao said.","Elder Master Xiao turned around and shot him a sideways glance. Pulling a handkerchief from his sleeve to wipe the foul blood from his hands, he declared sternly, \"Liu Hong colluded with the enemy and betrayed his country without a shred of remorse. He deserved this death. However, for the sake of our many years protecting Shu State together, I went out of my way to send him off. It spared him a fate worse than death.\"","Feng Erbao’s lips trembled as he processed the words, visibly enraged.","\"Marquis Xiao, I will report exactly what transpired today to the Holy Emperor. You had best watch your step!\"","With that, Feng Erbao cast a sidelong glance at Xiao Jinghong, let out a cold snort, and flicked his sleeves before turning on his heel and storming out of the Qingjing Residence.","The remaining eunuchs scrambled forward to hoist Liu Hong’s corpse and hurried after him. Someone even carefully bypassed Elder Master Xiao to scrape some flesh and blood off the blood-splattered wall inside the hall to take with them.","In a matter of moments, only four people were left in the Qingjing Residence: Elder Master Xiao, Xiao Shen, Xiao Jinghong, and the still-stunned Li Huai’gu.","Outside, a large crowd from the Xiao Family had rushed over, but they were all held back by the Armored Guards.","A brief moment of silence fell over the room.","Li Huai’gu finally snapped out of his daze. With a conflicted expression, he bowed respectfully to Elder Master Xiao and Xiao Jinghong one by one.","\"Marquis, General, I will take my leave now.\"","As he stepped toward the door, he met Xiao Jinghong’s gaze and hesitated for a second before adding, \"If necessary, I can step forward to testify to the Marquis’s claims.\"","Xiao Jinghong gave a slight nod and waved Lu Guan over, gesturing for him to escort Li Huai’gu out. She then stepped into the hall. Her eyes swept across the crimson mess before landing on Xiao Shen.","\"Third Grandfather, I must trouble you to placate the people waiting outside.\"","Clutching his chest, Xiao Shen looked at her as if he wanted to say something, but held his tongue. Instead, he pointed at Elder Master Xiao behind her and quickly exited the Qingjing Residence.","Although he was the Chief Steward of the Xiao Family’s third branch, the true authority within the Marquis’s Mansion lay solely with Elder Master Xiao and Xiao Jinghong. There were certain matters and conversations he was better off not knowing or hearing.","It did not take long for the commotion outside the Qingjing Residence to quiet down as well.","Only then did Xiao Jinghong step forward to help her grandfather to a seat. She then sat in the chair beside him, her back as straight as Liu Hong’s had once been, and looked at him.","\"Grandfather, you killed Liu Hong, and I killed Zhu Hao. Both of the guilty ministers the Holy Emperor demanded have died by our hands. I fear complications will soon arise,\" she said.","She didn’t bother asking Elder Master Xiao for his reasons. In truth, the moment Xiao Jinghong stood outside and heard Liu Hong confess that he was the one who leaked the information about Xiao Fengchun and Fu Wanqing being in the Barbarian Race territories, murderous intent had surged within her own heart.","She had never expected that Liu Hong’s collusion with the Barbarian Race and the Poshisu Country had begun during the great war five years ago. He was the very culprit who had caused her parents to die in battle.","Even if Elder Master Xiao hadn’t killed him, Xiao Jinghong would have found an opportunity to do it herself.","But Liu Hong was already dead. No matter how much Xiao Jinghong wanted to grind his bones to dust, the chance was gone.","Elder Master Xiao leaned back in his chair, his face entirely void of emotion. \"If complications arise... then let them.\"","He was fully aware of the precarious position his actions had placed the Xiao Family in. But he had his reasons—reasons that made killing Liu Hong an absolute necessity.","Causing the deaths of the Xiao Family’s Fengchun and Fu Wanqing was only part of it. Liu Hong’s attempt to reveal that Fu Wanqing was still alive and trapped among the Barbarian Race was the main factor that solidified Elder Master Xiao’s resolve.","If Xiao Jinghong found out her mother was still alive in this world, the consequences would be tens, if not hundreds, of times worse than their current predicament.","Elder Master Xiao stared at the tiny specks of crimson still clinging to his hands. After a moment of thought, he asked in a deep voice, \"How many days until the Wu Mountain Mutual Market is completed?\"","Xiao Jinghong paused slightly before replying calmly, \"Ten days at the shortest, half a month at the longest. It will definitely be finished by then.\"","\"Good,\" he said. \"You no longer need to go to the Mutual Market. I will have the Third Master take men to keep an eye on things there. Shortly after this, you will head straight out to inspect the Three Towns.\"","Xiao Jinghong was not an indecisive person. She gave a firm nod in agreement.","\"The new Minister of War is about to inspect the Border Towns across the realm. It is the perfect time for me to head to the Iron Wall, Profound Armor, and Cang Lang Three Towns.\""]},{"number":594,"title":"Chapter 594 - 335: Liu Wu Is Light...","paragraphs":["Elder Master Xiao’s expression softened slightly, though his tone grew increasingly serious. Turning his head to look at her, he said,","\"Liu Hong died by my hands, and you killed Zhu Hao. It remains to be seen whether the Holy Emperor will fly into a rage and punish us, but the Xiao Family can no longer remain as we were before.","\"Regardless of what the Xiao Family was like in the past, after today, in the eyes of others in Shu State and even the Nine State and Three Prefectures, our actions over the past five years will be seen as nothing but a disguise.","\"Furthermore, Feng Erbao already knows that I am in good health. From now on, they will never view the Xiao Family the way they used to.\"","Pausing for a moment, the elder master sighed. \"I actually hope the Holy Emperor punishes us.\"","As the old adage goes, the dogs that truly bite don’t bark.","The Xiao Family’s successive killings of Zhu Hao and Liu Hong would lead the other Noble Families and Court Officials to believe they had merely been lying dormant, feigning weakness. Those who had previously looked down upon or sympathized with the Xiao Family would inevitably change their tune.","Xiao Jinghong understood his meaning. \"The Holy Emperor’s will is unfathomable. Please rest assured, Grandfather; I will not pin my hopes on that.\"","If the Holy Emperor punished them, it meant the Xiao Family still had a chance. However, if the Holy Emperor simply praised the killing or remained entirely indifferent, that would spell a true crisis for the Xiao Family.","Elder Master Xiao gave an affirmative grunt, his expression easing. He watched the torrential rain pouring outside the main hall, his palm rubbing against the back of his chair.","\"From now on, whether it’s thunderous fury or heavenly grace, I will have to shoulder it all. The Xiao Family... no longer has any way out.\"","It wouldn’t be a matter of simply enduring it or acting powerless and helpless as they had before. They had to be formidable. It had to be just like the Xiao Family from five years ago—one family with two Marquises, guarded by several Martial Artists of the Upper Three Grades.","Within Shu State, apart from the Mountain Race, no one dared to provoke the Xiao Family’s fierce majesty.","However, while outsiders remained oblivious, Elder Master Xiao knew full well that the Xiao Family of today genuinely lacked its former strength. They were merely a paper tiger—strong on the outside but hollow within.","Xiao Jinghong was naturally aware of this as well. Thus, when the elder master told her to head to the Three Towns immediately, she agreed without a moment’s hesitation.","\"If you need anything, Grandfather, just send word.\"","\"I know.\" Elder Master Xiao paused as if recalling something, changing the subject. \"Earlier, you mentioned you were going to look for those people. How is that going?\"","Xiao Jinghong shook her head. \"I haven’t found an opportunity yet, but... I should have a lead by the fifteenth of next month.\"","\"The fifteenth?\"","\"Yes. Monarch Xue Jian has challenged Immortal Bai to a duel upstream of the Chishui River. I will go there to watch the battle.\"","\"Monarch Xue Jian... Lone Immortal Ye?\"","Elder Master Xiao had heard this name before; he knew he was one of the foremost Swordsmen in the Jianghu. As for Immortal Bai, the name was legendary to him. Before he succeeded to the Marquis Position of Duke Dingyuan, he had actually met Immortal Bai once.","\"Both of these men have been renowned throughout the Great Wei for years. Their strength and status are transcendent. It’s no wonder their clash will draw out the Jianghu People.\"","Despite saying so, the elder master genuinely held no favorable impression of people like Immortal Bai. The saying that martial artists used their strength to break the law was no empty talk.","Thinking of all the Wandering Martial Artists she had encountered along the way, Xiao Jinghong considered for a moment before saying, \"Shu State is currently swarming with all sorts of characters. It would be best to have a few more experts guarding the estate. I will transfer some personnel from the military over shortly.\"","Hearing this, Elder Master Xiao subconsciously pulled his sleeves together to cover the bloodstains and nodded. \"Not too many.\"","\"I understand.\" Xiao Jinghong recalled a minor matter. \"Grandfather, there’s one more thing. My mother...\"","Before she could finish, Elder Master Xiao’s expression shifted slightly. \"Don’t listen to the nonsensical babble of outsiders!\"","Xiao Jinghong hesitated, somewhat bewildered. \"Grandfather, the Fu Family is currently facing a difficult situation. I simply wanted them to take charge of the Hundred Herbs Hall’s affairs in Guangyuan County.\"","Elder Master Xiao froze slightly. Upon realizing his mistake, he coughed and turned his head away. \"Oh, that... I was already planning to do just that. Just now, I thought you were going to bring up something else.\"","\"Something else?\"","\"It’s nothing...\" Elder Master Xiao vaguely brushed the topic aside.","Xiao Jinghong didn’t pry any further. Since she hadn’t clearly heard what Liu Hong said earlier, she naturally wouldn’t connect the matter to Fu Wanqing.","Their discussion concluded.","Just as Xiao Jinghong was about to stand up and head for the Three Towns, she heard Elder Master Xiao say, \"There’s no rush. It won’t be too late to leave after lunch.\"","\"Hmm?\"","\"Your husband is currently eating in Wan’er’s courtyard. Go over and join them before you leave.\"","Seeing his solemn tone, Xiao Jinghong felt a bit puzzled but nodded in agreement anyway, heading straight for the backyard.","After everyone had left, Elder Master Xiao sat in silence for a moment before pulling back his cuff with one hand, looking at the faintly bloodstained characters written on it.","\"Liu Wu is Qing... zhou?\"","Even though the final character \"zhou\" wasn’t completely finished, the elder master could easily deduce it from its outline.","Qingzhou. Chen Qingzhou. Chen Yi.","Elder Master Xiao was somewhat uncertain. He carefully recalled Chen Yi’s actions and daily behavior since arriving at the Xiao Family, but he hadn’t noticed any anomalies. If Chen Yi was indeed Liu Wu, how could he possibly have achieved success in the Calligraphy Dao, Martial Arts, Medical Dao, and Fist Dao?","Even calling him \"master of both the pen and the sword\" felt like a derogatory understatement. Let alone mastering four different Daos, even if he were just an ordinary master of both the pen and the sword, how could the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family ever bear to let Chen Yi marry into the Xiao Family?","\"Are there truly such outstanding talents in this world?\"","Thinking back to when Chen Yi was infected with the plague toxin a few days ago, Elder Master Xiao felt even more convinced deep down that this was just another one of Liu Hong’s schemes. By making a move to kill Liu Hong this time, he had already fallen into Liu Hong’s trap, forcing him to forcefully bear the weight of the Xiao Family with nowhere to rest and recuperate as before.","After pondering the matter over and over, although Elder Master Xiao was certain that Chen Yi and Chen Yu were not the same person, he still intended to look into it.","\"I must investigate it, just for peace of mind...\"","Meanwhile, Xiao Jinghong arrived at Jiaxing Garden. Hearing the cheerful conversations and laughter of Chen Yi, Xiao Wan’er, and the others inside, the corners of her lips unconsciously curled up into a smile."]},{"number":595,"title":"Chapter 595 - 335: Liu Wu Is Light...","paragraphs":["Although her mood was far from good because of the incident with Liu Hong, seeing the backyard as peaceful as ever brought her a sliver of comfort.","\"Is this how Father felt when he returned from his deployments?\" Xiao Jinghong wondered, feeling a sense of empathy. With light steps, she entered the living room.","\"Second Miss.\"","\"General.\"","Juan’er, Xiaodie, Shen Huatang, and the others by the door noticed her first and rose to bow.","Xiao Jinghong waved a hand, gesturing for them to sit. Then, before Xiao Wan’er and Chen Yi could even get up, she took a seat next to Chen Yi and asked in a slightly relaxed tone, \"Eldest Sister, Husband, did I arrive in time?\"","\"Just in time. We’re starting to get hungry.\" Chen Yi turned to look at her and nodded with a smile. \"Madam, please wait a moment.\"","He instructed Xiaodie to fetch a bowl and chopsticks, then served Xiao Jinghong a bowl of rice. Taking advantage of the moment, Xiao Wan’er fell into her usual routine, chatting with Xiao Jinghong with sisterly concern.","\"Are the matters in Guangyuan resolved?\"","\"Yes, they’re resolved.\"","\"Then you should be able to take a few days off to rest. No need to rush out again.\"","Taking the bowl from Chen Yi, Xiao Jinghong replied apologetically, \"I’m afraid I have to disappoint you, Eldest Sister. After lunch, I must set off to inspect the New Army in the Three Towns.\"","Xiao Wan’er instinctively glanced at Chen Yi. Seeing him simply listening to their conversation with a gentle smile, she decided not to press the issue.","Chen Yi naturally knew everything that had just transpired, but he could only feign ignorance, chatting and laughing with Xiao Jinghong. Their conversation mostly revolved around his recent preparations for the Annual Examination and a few major events that had occurred in the Prefecture City. Intentionally or not, Chen Yi revealed that he had been feeling unwell, having contracted the plague toxin.","Catching on, Xiao Wan’er chimed in from the side, \"Don’t worry, Second Sister. Your husband’s health is fine now.\"","Xiao Jinghong furrowed her brows at first. She didn’t let her guard down until she confirmed that Chen Yi’s complexion was indeed rosy and healthy.","\"Husband, you are now a tutor at Guiyun Academy. You don’t have to do everything yourself. Just leave some tasks to the servants in the mansion.\" She paused, then looked at Xiao Wan’er and added, \"You too, Eldest Sister.\"","In her eyes, the two people beside her were both physically frail, so there was no harm in giving them a few extra reminders. Chen Yi readily agreed to her advice, but Xiao Wan’er’s Heart Spirit was somewhat conflicted.","On one hand, she had to cover for Chen Yi; knowing his illness was fake, she couldn’t let the truth slip. On the other hand, harboring a sense of guilt toward Xiao Jinghong made her chest feel tight and uncomfortable.","Fortunately, true to her word, Xiao Jinghong didn’t linger after lunch and directly left the Marquis’s Mansion. Beneath her guilt, Xiao Wan’er felt a wave of relief.","It wasn’t until then that someone in the mansion came to report what had happened at the Qingjing Residence.","Xiao Wan’er was momentarily stunned. \"Grandfather killed... the Lord Governor? And he did it right in front of the imperial envoy? This...\"","Chen Yi had anticipated this, so he offered a few words of comfort. \"The Old Master must have his reasons for doing so. Besides, if there was real danger, Madam would have warned us just now.\"","Xiao Wan’er thought about it and nodded hesitantly. The logic was sound, and the situation was what it was, but there wasn’t much she could do. Rather than worrying, it was better to focus on doing her own work well.","After chatting for a bit longer, they parted ways.","Chen Yi took Xiaodie with him, Returning Spring Lotus Garden.","Xiaodie patted her budding chest and said, \"Young Master, I didn’t expect Liu... Liu Hong to be so wicked, actually colluding with the enemy.\"","Seeing Chen Yi’s calm expression, she asked in confusion, \"He was so wicked, so why is the Eldest Miss worried that the Old Master killed him? Isn’t this a good thing?\"","Chen Yi chuckled. \"Of course it’s a good thing, but we do need to take preventative measures...\"","Liu Hong dying by the Old Master’s hands would have a profound impact. However, no matter how one looked at it, it wasn’t a bad thing.","The Xiao Family had been showing weakness for far too long."]},{"number":596,"title":"Chapter 596 - 336: Mountains and Rivers Ask Not of the 4 Seasons!","paragraphs":["Showing weakness. Being weak. Whether subjective or objective, the Xiao Family would inevitably attract covetous eyes and endless trouble.","Just like the Jing State Liu Family and the Zhu Family—where Zhu Hao and Zhu Lingchuan belonged—attacking the Xiao Family openly and in secret. Just like the Shu State Governor’s Office, the Capital Commandery, and the Inspectorate Office, pretending to comply but secretly undermining the Xiao Family in matters big and small. Even the majority of the Court Officials over in the Capital Prefecture did not stand on the Xiao Family’s side.","Chen Yi had a vague idea of the reasons behind this, but he was still missing the main factor. Or rather, he had always overlooked the thoughts of one person—the reigning Holy Emperor.","In this world, after all, imperial power was mandated by heaven. The Holy Emperor reigned supreme in the Imperial City, overlooking the world, and a single word from him could determine the life and death of all people. So, did the Xiao Family’s current predicament have anything to do with the Monarch in the Imperial City of the Capital Prefecture?","The answer was self-evident.","If he stood on the Xiao Family’s side, even if he only spoke a word of justice, the Xiao Family’s situation would be much better than it was right now. In this light, it made perfect sense that the White Tiger Guard was scheming against Shu State, intentionally or unintentionally creating disputes to cause trouble for the Xiao Family. Chen Yi even figured out the reason why he and Chen Yunfan were targeted by the White Tiger Guard.","—To manipulate the Xiao Family through his hands.","—To control Shu State through Chen Yunfan.","\"A person as proud and knowledgeable as ’me,’ suppressed for five long years, finally breaking free. Even if ’I’ am just a live-in son-in-law, I would probably treat this as a lifesaving straw, wouldn’t I?\" Chen Yi thought silently. He would, definitely.","\"So I became the ’Fledgling,’ which is why in the very beginning, the White Tiger Guard was so eager for me to gain a firm foothold in the Xiao Family,\" Chen Yi mused.","\"It was only after I became an Instructor at Guiyun Academy, leading the White Tiger Guard to mistakenly believe I had started scheming to take over the Xiao Family, that they finally laid low.","\"As such, Ge the Third’s departure was not for that sum of silver, nor was it out of fear of his identity being exposed. It was simply an inevitable retreat after accomplishing his mission.","\"But later...","\"Heh, the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family and the White Tiger Guard should both be Blades in the hands of the reigning Holy Emperor. My brother and I are the double-edged tip of that Blade.","\"The one far away in the Capital Prefecture gripped the hilt, stabbing it straight into the land of Shu State.","\"This game of chess... is truly majestic and imposing.\"","A hint of a smile tugged at the corners of Chen Yi’s mouth, yet his eyes remained exceptionally calm. Specks of fluorescent light flickered in his pupils, like chess pieces dancing across a board. As the stars shifted and swapped places, a few inconspicuous little pieces appeared on the board. They were far from the cluster in the bottom-left corner that represented the southwestern Shu State, yet a single piece was enough to establish dominance, looking like a giant ruling its own domain.","The first sat at the \"Tianyuan\" center point—the current Holy Emperor of the Great Wei Dynasty, along with his court ministers.","The second occupied the bottom-right corner representing the southeast. This piece represented the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family.","The third, occupying the star point in the top-left corner, represented the Ji State Trading Company.","The fourth consisted of several pieces in the top-right star point, distinct in black and white as if two armies were facing off against each other, though no specific names were assigned to them.","Aside from these, a few scattered pieces orbited around these star points. There was the elder Sun Fu who had traveled far to Jinling, Duke Qian Zhang Xuan who held the fort in Guangyue Prefecture, as well as the Left King’s son Asutai and Fu Wanqing, who were deep in the heartland of the Barbarian Race. Though scattered, they populated the colossal chessboard in Chen Yi’s mind—one that stretched tens of thousands of miles across the Nine State and Three Prefectures of the Great Wei Dynasty—making it seem less empty.","Chen Yi \"looked\" at the nascent chessboard in his mind. The smile on his face gradually faded, and his gaze shifted to the Spring Lotus Garden.","Under the heavy, overcast sky, a torrential downpour raged. The flowers, plants, and trees withered further under the assault, but the Golden Carp in the pond were unusually active. They thrashed about with a SPLASH, sending water spraying in all directions.","\"Mountains and rivers never ask for the seasons; their flourishing and withering are left to fate,\" Chen Yi murmured in his heart.","He broke into a smile again, turned his head to look at Xiaodie, and said, \"Prepare some tea and snacks. Your Young Master is going to make final preparations for the Annual Examination.\"","Xiaodie naturally nodded in compliance. Seeing the smile on Chen Yi’s face, she also relaxed. \"Young Master, if you say the Master is fine, then he will definitely be fine. Hehe.\"","Chen Yi patted her and scolded jokingly, \"I’m not an Immortal. How would I know so much?\"","At best, he was a half-immortal. A half-immortal? Tsk, wasn’t that title much more interesting than \"Dragon Tiger\"?","After the two returned to the wooden building, Chen Yi dried himself off and went to the study, grabbing an ancient tome to leaf through. However, his mind was not on the book. He was still sorting out and deducing the matters concerning Shu State and the Xiao Family.","After this incident with Liu Hong, Chen Yi had made some gains after all. And the gains were not small. Aside from figuring out the schemes of the reigning Holy Emperor, the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family, and the White Tiger Guard in Shu State, he had also acquired several other things.","—Provisions, silver coins, the Celestial Sect, and the Xiao Family.","First, there should be about five hundred thousand *shi* of provisions left, hidden in Lin Village by Liu Lang and the others. They were of no use to Chen Yi, so he figured he would find a chance to \"sell\" them to Elder Master Xiao later.","Second was the two million taels of silver coins obtained from the General. It seemed like a lot, but the Hundred Herbs Hall’s upcoming expansion would require money everywhere. With such drastic expenditures, even this amount might be stretched thin. However, it should be enough to support their expenses in Shu State.","Next were the disciples of the Celestial Sect who had joined the Hundred Herbs Hall. After the Five Poison Sect incident, Chen Yi had clearly distinguished who was close and who was distant. He could let Wang Ji arrange their positions according to the situation.","And finally, the Xiao Family.","In fact, the reason Chen Yi had chosen to only watch from the sidelines regarding Liu Hong’s visit to Elder Master Xiao was because he had his own plans. He wanted to use Liu Hong to force Elder Master Xiao into abandoning his tolerant approach—or at the very least, make him stop being so naive as to expect \"others\" to consider their old ties with the Xiao Family.","Otherwise, if the family remained as soft and weak as a toothless tiger, how could he justify lending them a helping hand?"]},{"number":597,"title":"Chapter 597 - 336: Mountains and Rivers Ask Not of the Four Seasons!","paragraphs":["Not to mention \"sheltering\" him and letting him be an idle live-in son-in-law.","The result was obvious. Elder Master Xiao had fallen for Liu Hong’s provocation and killed Liu Hong with his own hands, placing the Xiao Family in an awkward situation. With things as they were, even if he wanted to endure silently, others would no longer give him the chance. He had only one path left: to strengthen the Xiao Family, and to do so by any means necessary. At the very least, he had to return the Xiao Family to the prestige it held five years ago, so that those prying eyes would hesitate before making a move against them.","Since Chen Yi had made his choice, he would also work towards this goal. Thinking of this, Chen Yi slightly raised his head and looked out the window.","The rain formed a dense curtain. Vaguely, a figure sat upright amidst the clouds, holding a Heizi in his hand, about to make a move. Although his face could not be seen clearly, his composed demeanor made it impossible to underestimate him. If Chen Yi’s Chess Dao had not reached Perfection, merely looking directly at that figure might have made his heart grow heavy and his moves hesitant.","Chen Yi wondered, \"I don’t know who ’he’ is. The Holy Emperor, or one of his confidants?\" He had no way of knowing. He only knew that the opponent held countless chess pieces in his hand. Backed by the Holy Emperor, they also had Court Officials, Noble Families, Jianghu Sects, and more at their disposal. The strength of the two sides was fundamentally unequal.","But Chen Yi simply refused to believe in the impossible—whoever made his life uncomfortable, he would skin them alive.","He thought, \"I’d like to see if I, this newly minted Chess Master, can win this game with the half-crippled Xiao Family.\" Pausing for a moment, Chen Yi withdrew his gaze, put down the book in his hand, and sat cross-legged on the Grandmaster’s Chair to cultivate the Four Symbols Skill. \"A Lower Fourth Grade Cultivation is ultimately a bit too weak. I need to break through to the Upper Three Grades Realm as soon as possible...\" he mused.","News of Liu Hong’s death smashed into the Prefecture City like an earth-shattering boulder.","At the Governor’s Office.","Upon returning, Li Huai’gu immediately found Yang Ye to inform him of the matter. Mr. Yue Ming and Chen Yunfan, who had not yet left, were also made aware. Their expressions varied, but all were somewhat conflicted. Yang Ye had been an official for many years, so he naturally understood what Liu Hong’s strange behavior over the past few days signified and had formed his own speculations. He just hadn’t expected Liu Hong to die in such a manner.","Mr. Yue Ming felt much the same. Only Chen Yunfan’s complicated feelings stemmed not from Liu Hong, but from Chen Yi.","Chen Yunfan thought, \"Brother Yi’s scheme succeeded in the end. Liu Hong... why bother?\" Although he had long known how capable Chen Yi was, when the result truly unfolded as he had predicted, he couldn’t help but marvel inwardly. Had he been in Chen Yi’s position, let alone bringing down Liu Hong, merely tracing the clues back to him would have been an impressive feat.","\"Father, since you’re coming to Shu State this time, you must clear Brother Yi’s name. At the very least... at the very least, we can’t let him hold a grudge against our Chen Family...\" he added mentally. He had some confidence in Chen Yi, but the five years Chen Yi had been imprisoned previously were far too miserable. Let alone a peerless genius like Chen Yi, even an ordinary commoner locked up for five years would harbor resentment.","After a moment of silence, Mr. Yue Ming was the first to stand up. \"Since things have come to this, I now understand the root of the matter. I will take my students back to the academy.\"","Yang Ye forced a smile. \"Mr. Yue Ming, I hope you can keep this a secret for now, lest it cause upheaval in Shu State.\"","Mr. Yue Ming nodded, then shook his head. \"Don’t worry, I know what’s at stake.\" He couldn’t possibly tell too many people about such a matter; at most, he would inform a few teachers at the academy. However, he also knew that an incident of this magnitude couldn’t remain hidden forever. In a day or two at most, everyone in Shu State who needed to know would know.","Glancing around, Mr. Yue Ming sighed. \"Fortunately, the Governor’s Office has you holding the fort, old friend.\"","Yang Ye smiled bitterly. \"These old bones will just have to hold out for now.\"","After Mr. Yue Ming left, Yang Ye looked at Chen Yunfan and Li Huai’gu in the hall. He sighed and said, \"Although this matter is significant, it does not affect us.\"","Li Huai’gu glanced at Chen Yunfan. Seeing the latter nodding with an unfazed expression, he hesitated before asking, \"Lord Yang, shall we proceed as usual from now on?\"","\"Proceed as usual,\" Yang Ye nodded. \"That stubborn Old Xiao killing Liu Gongmo indeed has a huge impact. But then again, with people coming from the Capital Prefecture to arrest Liu Gongmo, the outcome is the same for us. The Governor’s Office is destined to be leaderless. For now, let everyone perform their own duties and wait for the Holy Emperor’s decree.\"","Li Huai’gu nodded silently in agreement, the scene he had witnessed at the Qingjing Residence once again surfacing in his mind. He slowly realized the truth—Liu Hong had actively sought death. Li Huai’gu couldn’t help but recall the words Liu Hong had spoken to him on the way to the Xiao Family’s home. After a moment of thought, he recounted the conversation, asking at the end, \"Lord Yang, why do you think Lord... Lord Liu would...\"","Before he could continue, Yang Ye raised a hand to interrupt him, his tone serious. \"Liu Gongmo colluded with the enemy and betrayed the country. In his vain attempt to poison the commoners and plunge Shu State into chaos, he had already become a madman. The thoughts and actions of such a person are different from ordinary people. Huai’gu, what use is there in figuring out his reasons?\"","Chen Yunfan sneered from the side. \"Brother Huai’gu, surely you don’t want the world to fall into chaos as well?\"","Li Huai’gu lowered his head with an awkward smile. \"Lord Yang, Lord Chen, please forgive me. I have no such thoughts. I just don’t understand why Lord Liu wanted to die at Marquis Xiao’s hands.\"","Chen Yunfan shook his head. \"He just wanted to cause trouble for the Xiao Family before his death, nothing more.\"","Yang Ye glanced at him with approval. \"Liu Gongmo knew he would die. Enraging Old Xiao into killing him was nothing more than an attempt to have the Holy Emperor punish the Xiao Family. As for whether the result will go as he wished... that remains unknown.\"","He didn’t state it as a certainty, but inwardly, he hoped the Holy Emperor would be lenient and minimize the matter. Otherwise, if Marquis Xiao were punished, not only would Liu Hong’s dying wish be fulfilled, but it would also cause an uproar among the people of the world. With this in mind, Yang Ye waved his hand. \"Go back to your work.\"","\"Yes, I will take my leave...\"","Just as Mr. Yue Ming had anticipated, news of Liu Hong dying at Elder Master Xiao’s hands quickly reached the ears of those paying attention. For a time, the Prefecture City was in constant upheaval.","Naturally, the Xiao Family reacted the fastest. Led by Xiao Shen and Xiao Xuanshuo, several core members of the Xiao Family were instructed by the Elder Master to leave the Marquis’s Mansion. They successively visited several Noble Families within the Prefecture City, such as the Wan Family, the Sun Family, and the Tang Family.","Although Elder Master Xiao was pedantic, he could still distinguish between what was urgent and what was not. Moreover, since he had been forced to make a choice, he began to act with resolute vigor once again, just as he had when facing the armies of the Barbarian Race and the Poshisu Country. Since someone didn’t want him to continue enduring in silence, his only option was to fight back with all his might. The backup plans and idle chess pieces he had arranged in the past, along with the close associates he had previously ordered to remain silent, all needed to make their moves. He strove to help his Xiao Family recover some of its prestige in a short period of time.","Upon receiving the news, Inspector General Tang Zixing of the Inspectorate Office immediately wrote a memorial and dispatched it to the Capital Prefecture. He didn’t even have time to track down Feng Erbao and the others to finalize the handling of Zhu Hao.","The White Tiger Guard was among the first to learn that something was going to happen to Liu Hong. This outcome naturally surprised General. However, regardless of his own thoughts, this matter needed to be relayed to the Lord Pavilion Master as soon as possible. He quickly wrote a secret letter and dispatched a falcon to fly to the Capital Prefecture.","At the same time, he found Lou Yuxue and Cui Qingwu at the Imprisonment Department and informed them of the situation. \"Liu Hong died unexpectedly. His accomplices must be interrogated and have their confessions signed and thumbprinted as soon as possible. The Pavilion Master needs results.\"","Lou Yuxue readily agreed, knowing in her heart that the dust had finally settled on this matter.","Cui Qingwu, however, frowned and asked, \"What impact will Liu Hong’s death have on Shu State?\" Such an inquiry hit the nail on the head, though deep down, she was merely worried it might affect Chen Yunfan.","General had a rough idea of what was on her mind and shook his head. \"It’s hard to say for now. Let’s wait for the Pavilion Master’s instructions.\" Based on his understanding of the situation in Shu State, he reckoned the Holy Emperor wouldn’t do anything to the Xiao Family. It was just that he couldn’t fathom the Lord Pavilion Master’s intentions. If that man had other schemes, the Xiao Family’s fate would be somewhat miserable.","\"Alright, tell the subordinate Iron Banner Officers to keep a close watch on their respective areas and observe the movements within Shu State.\"","When the waters run shallow, all sorts of unsavory characters reveal themselves. The more chaotic the times, the better the White Tiger Guard could see through an individual, a clan, or a faction. This could also be considered a good thing.","Meanwhile, on the official road in the North City.","Feng Erbao and his entourage, having recently left the city, stopped at a post station to rest. However, Feng Erbao did not stay in his carriage; instead, he ventured alone into the dense forest not far from the station. Looking into the depths of the woods, where only the noisy sound of rain could be heard, he asked in a feminine voice, \"Song Jinjian, did Lord Cui send you here to find me?\""]},{"number":598,"title":"Chapter 598 - 337: I Am Invincible","paragraphs":["Deep within the forest.","Song Jinjian wore a Profound Robe with a Long Sword hanging at his waist, a smile playing on his lips.","His appearance was quite transcendent—fair-skinned and beardless, with slender phoenix eyes beneath sword-like brows. He possessed a truly striking demeanor.","However, when Feng Erbao looked at him, his gaze unconsciously drifted toward the Long Sword at Song Jinjian’s waist.","The Long Sword, named \"Non-Struggle,\" held a resounding reputation in the Jianghu.","Legend had it that it once belonged to a Sword Immortal from the previous dynasty, before an ancestor of the Cui Family chanced upon it.","After Song Jinjian became a Tributor of the Cui Family, the Patriarch gifted Non-Struggle to him, uttering a phrase that later spread far and wide: \"A peerless weapon meeting a worthy master brings out the best in both.\"","Whether the weapon was peerless was undisputed, but whether the master was worthy, Feng Erbao reserved his judgment and couldn’t be bothered to comment.","No matter how high Song Jinjian’s attainment in the Sword Dao was, he was still nothing more than a dog of the Cui Family.","Song Jinjian assessed Feng Erbao before bowing in greeting. \"Please forgive me, Eunuch Feng. My Lord specifically ordered me to present you with a great gift.\"","Feng Erbao reflexively flicked his Duster and asked with a soft, effeminate smile, \"What kind of great gift?\"","Song Jinjian stepped slightly to the side. \"Eunuch Feng, please Step this way.\"","Feng Erbao narrowed his eyes. His pitch-black irises, filling his eye sockets, appeared even more profound in the overcast, dense forest.","About three breaths later, without moving his feet, he said, \"Lead the way.\"","Song Jinjian smiled and nodded. He turned and ventured into the dense forest first, walking away at a brisk pace.","Only after Song Jinjian had gone about a hundred zhang ahead did Feng Erbao cautiously shadow his Steps.","Song Jinjian hadn’t carved out a name for himself in the Jianghu without extraordinary skill; otherwise, he wouldn’t be so highly regarded by the old monsters of the martial world. They claimed that, given time, he would be able to stand shoulder to shoulder with Monarch Xue Jian, Lone Immortal Ye.","However, as the Chief Eunuch serving the Holy Emperor, Feng Erbao had read countless classified reports and secrets. Among them, naturally, was information on Song Jinjian.","His Sword Dao prioritized \"speed\"—vastly different from Monarch Xue Jian, but rather similar to Sword Master Li Wudang. To be precise, the speed of Song Jinjian’s sword bore a God-like resemblance to Li Wudang’s signature Swordsmanship, \"Qing Feng.\"","It boasted the reputation of \"invincible within a hundred zhang.\"","Feng Erbao’s reluctance to follow too closely stemmed from this exact apprehension.","Fortunately, his worries turned out to be unfounded.","After traveling for three miles, Song Jinjian stopped on a tree branch, pointing diagonally downward with a smile. \"Eunuch Feng, look. This is the ’great gift’ I have brought for you.\"","Feng Erbao stopped a hundred zhang away. Through the gaps in the foliage, he could faintly make out a figure leaning against a tree at the spot Song Jinjian was pointing at.","The person’s brocade robes were already soaked by the rain. Water trickled down, pooling on the ground and inexplicably blooming into a puddle of dark red.","Feng Erbao studied the scene for a moment before his brow sharply furrowed. \"Song Jinjian, is your Lord insulting me?\"","He could clearly see that the clothes between the person’s legs were stained with blood, looking just like a little eunuch who had freshly emerged from the palace’s castration room.","How could he not feel humiliated and enraged?","Song Jinjian unhurriedly shook his head, his expression earnest. \"You misunderstand, Eunuch Feng.","\"My Lord ordered me to entrust this person to you, hoping he can serve by your side.\"","\"Oh? Who is he?\"","\"Liu Taoyao.\"","A subtle expression crossed Feng Erbao’s effeminate face. He clearly hadn’t expected it to be this person.","He certainly knew that Liu Taoyao was Liu Hong’s eldest son, but he simply couldn’t fathom why Song... why Lord Cui would do such a thing.","Noticing his confusion, Song Jinjian smiled and explained before Feng Erbao could ask. \"You should be aware of the Holy Emperor’s decree, Eunuch Feng. With the exception of Consort Liu, everyone else in the Jing State Liu Family must die.","\"However, my Lord is one who remembers old ties, and so am I. Since we promised Liu Hong to save his eldest son, we must keep our word.\"","Hearing this, Feng Erbao couldn’t help but cover his mouth and laugh.","His shrill laughter echoed through the dense forest, accompanied by the RUSTLE of rain-battered dead leaves falling to the ground.","\"Song Jinjian, you and your Lord are truly amusing.","\"Even a dog that has bowed and scraped for you all these years deserves a good end, but what about Liu Hong?","\"You actually caused his... caused the Jing State Liu Family’s bloodline to be severed.\"","Song Jinjian gave a noncommittal nod. \"A bad life is better than a good death. He has lost a ’leg’, but perhaps he can still make something of himself.\"","He then looked at Feng Erbao with a serious expression. \"Just like you, Eunuch Feng... hmm... though perhaps he won’t reach your heights, it’s still an acceptable outcome.\"","Feng Erbao’s face stiffened. He stared at the swordsman for a moment before speaking in a soft, dark tone, \"Since it is a request from Lord Cui, I accept.\"","After saying that, he took a step forward but abruptly pulled back. Flicking his Duster, he said, \"If there is nothing else, you may withdraw.\"","Song Jinjian smiled and vanished into the depths of the forest in a blur.","Only when the swordsman’s presence had completely faded did Feng Erbao approach Liu Taoyao, scrutinizing the young man with a dark expression.","\"Cui Mao...\"","The Qinghe Cui Family had passed down its legacy for a thousand years, producing countless brilliant and stunningly talented individuals.","There were Swordsmen and Rangers who roamed the Jianghu unhindered; one had even slaughtered a ten-thousand-strong northern cavalry single-handedly with nothing but a sword.","There was Mr. Da of the academy, whose disciples were spread all across the world.","Even more entered the court as officials. Three of them had reached the position of Chancellor, standing second only to the Emperor and above the masses.","Not to mention the distant past, just looking at the tail end of the previous dynasty’s golden age. An ancestor of the Cui Family had firmly held the position of Chancellor for two decades. Through his own power, he implemented bold and decisive reforms, single-handedly laying down a hundred years of foundation for the previous dynasty’s reign.","Now, in the Great Wei Dynasty, the Cui Family remained active.","It was just that due to their ties with the previous dynasty, successive generations of Emperor Wei harbored aversion toward them. Although they didn’t go so far as to slaughter the Cui Family, they also refused to allow its descendants to enter the core of power.","That was, until today, two hundred years later, when Cui Mao made a meteoric rise.","Passing the exam to become a Scholar at twelve, passing the provincial exam at fifteen, and taking first place in the palace exam at eighteen, he became the youngest Imperial Top Scholar in the history of the Great Wei Dynasty.","His prominence was unmatched.","Many prominent figures in the Capital Prefecture originally thought that, having achieved success at such a young age, Cui Mao would inevitably stray and face setbacks."]},{"number":599,"title":"Chapter 599 - 337: I Am Invincible","paragraphs":["Yet, he languished in obscurity at the Hanlin Academy for six long years, only assuming the role of Fifth-Grade Junior Minister at Honglu Temple at the age of twenty-eight. By forty, he had become the teacher of the current Holy Emperor. Later, on his deathbed, the late Emperor promoted him to Minister of Heaven—the head of the Nine Ministers—to assist the current Holy Emperor.","Twenty years had passed since then.","Twenty years was neither a long nor a short time. However, aside from the Minister of Heaven, the other eight ministers in the Imperial Court had been replaced entirely; some positions had even seen multiple changes. For instance, before Chen Xuanji, the position of Minister of War had been held by Luo Yong, Le Yi, Duanmu Yun, and others.","Thus, Cui Mao’s ability to securely hold the position of Minister of Heaven for two decades was exceptionally remarkable. In other words, his intellect and political maneuvering were far from simple. Otherwise, the current Holy Emperor wouldn’t have praised Cui Mao as the \"Number One Minister of the Great Wei.\"","As Feng Erbao pondered this, his expression gradually calmed. With a flick of his wrist, he tossed out his Duster, sweeping up Liu Taoyao to carry him back to the relay station. Although he was a close attendant to the current Holy Emperor and his absolute loyalty should lie with the Emperor, he clearly understood Cui Mao’s place in His Majesty’s heart. Leaving aside the fact that Liu Hong had already brought doom upon himself, even if there were no reason at all, the current Holy Emperor would not punish Cui Mao for eliminating him.","Feng Erbao knew this very well, so naturally, he wouldn’t wag his tongue out of turn. On the contrary, by leveraging his connection with Cui Mao, he, a Chief Eunuch, might just advance further to become the highest-ranking Chief Eunuch.","A short while later.","The carriages bound for the Capital Prefecture set off once more, galloping north along the official Dao.","Song Jinjian watched the carriages from afar, his palm repeatedly stroking the hilt of his Non-Struggle Sword at his waist. Eventually, he lifted his hand, crossing his arms over his chest as he looked down at the carriages disappearing at the end of the official Dao.","\"Had the Lord not given specific orders, I would have killed that eunuch without a second thought. It would have been a fitting tribute to Liu Gongmo’s spirit in heaven.\" A contemptuous smile tugged at the corners of Song Jinjian’s lips. He turned and waved toward the other side. \"Come out. It’s time for you to hit the road as well.\"","Liu Zhaoxue, her figure concealed beneath a black cloak, stepped forward. Behind her followed Zhao Shichang, similarly dressed entirely in black. She cast a complicated look toward the official Dao to the north, not saying a word.","Zhao Shichang, however, bypassed her without hesitation, dropping to one knee and bowing his head. \"My lord, shall we wait for you in the Capital Prefecture?\"","\"We are not going to the Capital Prefecture,\" Song Jinjian said flatly. \"We are going to Jinling.\"","Though confused, Zhao Shichang readily agreed, rising to his feet and stepping behind a nearby tree.","Song Jinjian’s gaze then fell upon Liu Zhaoxue, a flicker of appreciation flashing in his eyes. But when Liu Zhaoxue looked back at him, his expression reverted to a calm, cold indifference.","\"Have you made up your mind? Are you choosing to stay behind, or will you go to Jinling with Zhao Shichang?\" he asked.","Liu Zhaoxue looked at him, falling into a brief silence. Staying behind meant following by his side. Going to Jinling...","\"The Liu family is no more. What point is there in me going to Jinling?\"","Song Jinjian looked at her noncommittally. \"Don’t you plan to avenge the Jing State Liu Family?\"","\"Avenge them?\" A trace of sorrow flitted across Liu Zhaoxue’s elegant and beautiful face. She shook her head. \"The Holy Emperor passed down the punishment, exterminating the three branches of the Liu family. What ability do I, Zhaoxue, have to seek revenge against the ruler of a nation?","\"Or are you suggesting that I should place the blame on Cui Mao?\"","\"Insolent!\" Before Song Jinjian could speak, Zhao Shichang sharply reprimanded her from the side. \"How dare you address the Lord by his true name?\"","Liu Zhaoxue glanced at him out of the corner of her eye, sneering. \"Are you my Third Uncle’s Staff Officer, or are you a dog of the Cui Family?\"","Zhao Shichang snorted. \"From beginning to end, I have only ever followed the Lord!\"","\"A loyal hound.\"","\"You...\"","Just as Zhao Shichang raised his hand, Song Jinjian thrust out One Finger. A burst of Sword Qi slashed past like the wind.","THUD.","His hand, severed cleanly at the wrist, fell to the base of the tree.","Zhao Shichang snapped back to his senses and immediately dropped to his knees on the branch. \"Please forgive my offense, my lord!\"","Song Jinjian didn’t even spare him a glance. \"Get lost.\"","Ignoring the need to treat his wound, Zhao Shichang leapt down to the base of the tree, grabbed his severed hand, and darted straight toward the north. Dozens of figures clad in black who had been hiding in the surroundings departed along with him.","A short while later.","Song Jinjian looked at Liu Zhaoxue, who was standing with her head bowed in silence, and shook his head. \"Since that is the case, you will stay by my side.\"","Liu Zhaoxue raised her head to look at him, her face returning to its previous coldness. \"Aren’t you afraid I’ll look for an opportunity to kill you?","\"You... you clearly promised Third Uncle that you would keep Liu Taoyao safe. Why did you sever his roots and extinguish the bloodline of our Liu family?\"","Song Jinjian cast a sidelong glance at her, then turned his head to gaze at the dark clouds in the distant night sky.","Deafening thunder shook the heavens as streaks of lightning crashed down, illuminating their figures.","\"Liu Hong committed the heinous crime of treason. The Jing State Liu Family was never meant to have any surviving bloodline. Allowing Liu Taoyao to eke out a miserable existence in this world is already a show of mercy from the Lord.\"","Liu Zhaoxue stared at him. \"What about me, then?\"","\"You are still of great use. For now, your life is spared.\"","Song Jinjian retracted his gaze, a smile touching his handsome face. \"As for whether you will look for a chance to kill me... you are more than welcome to try.","\"But I must remind you—you will only get one chance.\"","Liu Zhaoxue’s eyes were clear. Looking at his smiling face, she gave a nearly imperceptible nod.","Seeing this, Song Jinjian’s smile faded. In a blur of motion, he took her and headed back to the Prefecture City.","\"I will remain in the Shu State until the end of the year.","\"During this time, you should put in the hard work to improve your Cultivation.\"","\"Yes, my lord...\"","Two days later.","News of everything that had transpired in the Shu State reached the Capital Prefecture. To be precise, it reached the White Tiger Guard.","Xuan Xing, dressed in a red robe and wearing a white mask, took the deciphered secret missive and headed straight for a Quiet Chamber near the third floor. He waited for a moment. Hearing no sound from within, he simply slipped the missive through the crack under the door and respectfully took his leave.","Inside the empty, pitch-black Quiet Chamber, a sudden gust of wind blew in from nowhere, sweeping up the secret missive. The letter tumbled through the air twice before slipping back out through the gap under the door. It then silently drifted across two long corridors, finally entering another Quiet Chamber on the opposite side."]},{"number":600,"title":"Chapter 600 - 337: I Am Invincible","paragraphs":["The person wearing the white tiger pattern mask raised a hand to grasp the secret letter, unfurling it with his fingers to read the contents.","[On the night the plague broke out, Fledgling fell seriously ill.]","[Liu Hong was killed by Marquis Xiao with a single punch. Feng Erbao witnessed it with his own eyes and brought the corpse back to the Capital Prefecture.]","[Zhu Hao attempted to flee but was beheaded by Xiao Jinghong with a single sword strike.]","[Liu Hong’s son, Liu Taofang, was found dead in a guest room; the perpetrator remains unknown. Liu Taoyao and Liu Zhaoxue are missing.]","[Song Jinjian has appeared in Shu State, following Simurgh Phoenix.]","[The National Preceptor of Poshisu Country seeks a Closed-door Disciple; the son of King Landu has already set off to present himself.]","[The Barbarian Race shows signs of moving north, which seems to be related to the son of the Left King...]","After finishing the secret letter, the person wearing the white tiger pattern mask fixed his gaze on the very top line.","\"Qingzhou is seriously ill? What a joke.\"","His voice was no longer as deep as before; instead, it carried a hearty, chuckling tone.","He then stood up and walked to the window. Pulling a snow-white falcon from his sleeve, he tied the secret letter to its leg and released it into the air.","The snow-white falcon instantly flapped its wings and soared high into the sky.","The person in the white tiger pattern mask watched as it circled twice in the air before landing somewhere in the eastern part of the Imperial City. A flash of displeasure crossed his dark eyes.","\"Hmph, that dog Chen Xuanji couldn’t even hold out after cowering for five years, forcing me to sit here and rot.","\"Sooner or later, I’ll settle this score with you...\"","He grumbled and cursed for a while before leaning back in the Grandmaster’s Chair, crossing his legs, and leisurely drinking his wine. Between sips, he chewed on a few peanuts, producing loud CRUNCH CRUNCH sounds.","\"At least there’s food and wine. Otherwise, there’s no way I’d let him order me around...\" he muttered, his voice barely audible, as if he were worried about being overheard.","A moment later, only the sound of snoring remained in the Quiet Chamber.","Meanwhile, at the spot where the snow-white falcon had landed—the backyard garden of a sprawling five-courtyard mansion.","After reading the secret letter in his hand, Chen Xuanji paid no mind to Fledgling’s severe illness. Instead, he stared thoughtfully at a line further down.","\"Song Jinjian went to Shu State...\"","Chen Xuanji waved his hand, shattering the secret letter into pieces. Clasping his hands behind his back, he gazed at the plum blossoms in the garden.","He stood in silence for a moment before suddenly breaking into laughter. As he laughed, he looked toward the south.","He wasn’t looking very far, nor was he looking at the south of Great Wei. Rather, he was looking at a residence just one street over—a residence with a plaque hanging by its door that read \"Cui Mansion.\"","\"Old friend, I imagine you must be quite furious that I killed one of your dogs.","\"Although Liu Hong didn’t die directly because of me, it can still be said that he died by the hands of the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family.\"","Chen Xuanji had always been a stern and unsmiling man. Yet at this very moment, he could no longer hold it in, nor did he want to. After playing this game of chess for so long, he had finally glimpsed the tip of that person’s iceberg. How could he not be thrilled?","\"I should have known earlier. If the Ji State Trading Company didn’t have Da Shan behind them, they would never dare to be so unscrupulous.\"","After his laughter subsided, Chen Xuanji pondered for a moment before ordering a carriage to be prepared so he could head to the Imperial Palace to seek an audience with the Holy Emperor.","Shortly after, the carriage left the Chen Mansion and traveled north, coming to a halt outside the Imperial City.","Chen Xuanji stepped out, passing through the heavy city gates and bypassing several majestic grand halls at the front, before arriving at the Imperial Study in the rear.","He waited for the little eunuch guarding the door to go in and announce his arrival. Only then did he smooth out his Crane Patterned Crimson Robe and enter the study.","The eunuch attending inside subsequently took his leave, leaving only Emperor Wei and Chen Xuanji alone in the room. The two men exchanged a glance and, surprisingly, both broke into slight smiles.","Chen Xuanji bowed deeply and offered a respectful salute. \"Holy Emperor...\"","Before he could finish, Emperor Anhe waved his hand. \"Xuanji, dispense with the formalities.","\"Though there is a distinction between us as ruler and minister, we are also old friends of many years.","\"Especially over these past five years, you have stayed by my side at every turn, offering your counsel. It has not been easy for you. Therefore, I grant you the privilege of forgoing the customary bow when you see me.\"","Chen Xuanji looked up at him. No longer declining the honor, he smiled and expressed his gratitude.","Emperor Anhe motioned for him to take a seat. \"You’ve come all this way to see me. Have you received some news from the White Tiger Guard?\"","\"I will not hide it from the Holy Emperor. Over in Shu State...\"","Chen Xuanji selectively relayed the contents of the secret letter, omitting only the part about Song Jinjian’s appearance in Shu State.","Upon hearing this, Emperor Anhe furrowed his brows slightly, a trace of displeasure coloring his expression.","\"Do the Xiao Family grandfather and grandson really have so little regard for me? The two men I specifically requested both died by their hands?\"","Chen Xuanji remained silent, allowing the emperor to vent his anger. He knew very well that Emperor Anhe wasn’t genuinely angry. They were two insignificant figures to begin with; if they died, they died.","Indeed, about half an incense stick of time later.","Emperor Anhe took a sip of tea, looked at him with a smile, and asked, \"With Liu Hong and Zhu Hao dead, can our layout in Shu State be considered complete?\"","He then quickly denied his own question. \"The Xiao Family is still there.","\"Not only are they still there, but they are also free from their restraints.","\"My beloved minister, your strategy of sacrificing the plum tree to save the peach seems to have fallen short of your usual standard.\"","Chen Xuanji’s expression remained perfectly calm. \"The fact that the Xiao Family passed the test is enough to prove that they are temporarily capable of defending Shu State.\"","\"Oh?","\"That matter... do you already have an answer?\"","Meeting Emperor Anhe’s gaze, Chen Xuanji said softly, \"The north.\"","Emperor Anhe’s smile gradually faded at those words. He stared at him for a long while before finally speaking.","\"Why not the south?\"","Chen Xuanji replied, \"At first, I truly hoped the Holy Emperor would launch a southern expedition against the Barbarian Race to project our dynasty’s prestige.","\"I spent five years causing discord between the Royal Family of Poshisu Country and King Landu, and I provoked internal strife within the Barbarian Race, doing everything possible to weaken them.","\"However, the Barbarian Race’s territory is too vast, and they have countless experts among their ranks. Even if we mobilized the entire nation’s strength, it remains uncertain whether we could achieve victory in a single campaign.\"","Emperor Anhe remarked noncommittally, \"Now that chaos has erupted in the south, it will allow the Xiao Family, which already has one foot in the grave, to guard the Southern Border without expending too much effort.\"","\"What the Holy Emperor says is correct.\"","Chen Xuanji raised his hand and pointed toward the north. \"In recent years, due to the border market trade, although the north’s military has grown stronger and their horses sturdier, they have also become immersed in a life of luxury and debauchery.","\"Within two years, I am certain their coffers will be completely hollowed out.","\"When that time comes, even if the Holy Emperor doesn’t launch a northern expedition, they will march south to raid our borders anyway.","\"Rather than waiting passively, it is better for the Holy Emperor to seize the initiative and strike.\"","After hearing this, a hint of eagerness flickered in Emperor Anhe’s eyes, yet he shook his head with a laugh.","\"Xuanji, what a brilliant feint to the east while attacking the west. Even I was almost fooled by you.","\"From the very beginning, you had already made up your mind to have me launch a northern expedition, didn’t you?","\"The reason you sent your two sons south was probably to stabilize the situation in Shu State. Whether the Xiao Family falls or not was never truly important.\"","Chen Xuanji lowered his head slightly. \"I would not dare hide it from the Holy Emperor. I did indeed have such intentions.\"","Seeing this, Emperor Anhe pointed at him and scolded jokingly, \"You... you really hide things deeply.\"","\"I beg the Holy Emperor’s forgiveness.\"","Despite their banter, both men understood the truth—that the affairs of the world were constantly changing. Regardless of Chen Xuanji’s original plans, the fact that the Xiao Family still drew breath was an indisputable reality.","A smile returned to Emperor Anhe’s face, and he waved his hand. \"Forget it, the north is fine too.","\"Over these years, the people at the border markets have ventured deep into the Great Desert Grassland and have already thoroughly scouted the terrain, climate, and water sources there.","\"With a northern expedition, my chances of victory are much greater!\"","After chuckling for a moment, Emperor Anhe then asked, \"But how do you plan to persuade the court ministers?","\"Especially my respected teacher?\"","Chen Xuanji bowed deeply. \"Once the Ji State Trading Company and those Noble Families hit a wall and suffer losses in the south, that person... will naturally nod in agreement.\"","\"The Ji State Trading Company?\"","Emperor Anhe narrowed his eyes slightly, and his smile turned cold.","\"Then proceed according to your thoughts. I shall await your good news!\"","\"Thank you for your approval, Holy Emperor!\"","Shortly after, Chen Xuanji left with long, purposeful strides.","Following his departure, several imperial decrees were issued.","Yang Ye was to temporarily serve as the Governor of Shu State; Duke Dingyuan Xiao Yuan and Dingyuan Army Commander-in-Chief Xiao Jinghong were to be docked three years’ salary; Chen Yunfan of the Shu State Governor’s Office was to be rewarded for his meritorious deed of slaying Lv Jiunan..."]}]);
